अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)
	 1. Joined, combined.
	 2. Gone.
	 3. Spread abroad.
4. Anointed.
 E. अञ्ज to go. and क्त affix.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्तु|अक्तुः
अक्तु f. (क्तुः) Night, (on the authority of the Vedas.)
 E. अञ्ज to go, and
क्तु affix.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रम|अक्रमः
अक्रम m. (मः) Want of order or arrangement, confusion, irregularity.
E. अ priv. and क्रम order.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रान्त|अक्रांत
अक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)
	 1. Unpassed, unsurpassed.
	 2. Unconquered.
(-न्तः) The egg-plant. (Solanum melongena.)
 E. अ neg. and क्रान्त
passed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोध|अक्रोधः
अक्रोध m. (-धः) Dispassionateness, restraint of anger, one of the ten
duties of an ascetic.
	 mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Dispassionate.
 E. अ neg.
and क्रोध anger.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रिय|अक्रियः
अक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)
	 1. Inactive, dull, torpid.
	 2. Abstaining from
religious rites.
	 f. (या) Inactivity, neglect of what ought to be
done.
 E. अ neg. क्रिया act.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रियत्व
अक्रियत्व n. (-त्वं) Inactivity, torpor. त्व added to the preceding. also
अक्रियता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रूर|अक्रूरः
अक्रूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Gentle, not cruel.
	 m. (-रः) The paternal
uncle and friend of KṚṢṆA.
 E. अ neg. क्रूर cruel.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेद्य
अक्लेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)
	 1. Incapable of distress or pain.
	 2. Unfit to be
pained or distressed.
 E. अ neg. क्लेद्य to be pained.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लम
अक्लम m. (-मः) Absence of weariness or fatigue.
 E. अ priv. and क्लम
fatigue.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लान्त|अक्लान्तः
अक्लान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Unwearied.
 E. अ neg. and क्लान्त wearied.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्ट
अक्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Unvexed, not distressed or annoyed.
	 2.
Unwearied, indefatigable.
 E. अ neg. क्लिष्ट wearied.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेश|अक्लेशं|अक्लेशः
अक्लेश m. (-शः) Absence of weariness or vexation.
 E. अ neg. क्लेश
distress.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिका
अक्लिका f. (-का) The indigo plant. (Indigofera tinctoria.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष r. 1st and 3d cl. (अक्षति अक्ष्णति)
	 1. To reach or obtain.
	 2. To
pervade.
	 3. To accumulate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष m. (-क्षः)
	 1. A die, cubic or oblong, for playing with.
	 2. Part of a
car.
	 3. A wheel.
	 4. A car.
	 5. A snake.
	 6. Law suit, legal proceedings
7. Sacred knowledge, 8. The soul.
	 9. A seed of which Rosaries are
made, in which sense it occurs mostly in composition, as Rudrākṣa, Indrākṣa.
10. A Karṣa or weight of sixteen māṣas.
	 11.
A tree bearing a medicinal fruit. (Terminalia belerica.)
	 12. A
proper name, the son of RAVANA.
	 13. A name of GARUḌA.
	 14. A
person born blind.
	 15. Terrestrial latitude.
	 n. (-क्षं)
	 1. An organ of
sense.
	 2. Sea, salt.
	 3. Blue vitriol
 E. अशु to pervade, Uṇādi affix स.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षक|अक्षकः
अक्षक m. (-कः) A tree. (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis, Rox.)
 E. अक्ष Beleric
myrobalan, and क affix: from its resembling that plant; or the
termination being a pleonastic affix, the word may have all the
senses of the preceding: also read अक्षिक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षकर्ण|अक्षकर्णः
अक्षकर्ण n. (-र्णः)
	 1. The hypotenuse, especially of the triangle formed
with the gnomon of a dial and its shadow.
	 2. (In astronomy.)
Argument of the latitude.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षत|अक्षतं|अक्षतः
अक्षत n. (-तं)
	 1. Fried grain, (in this sense it is also used in the mas.
plu. (-ताः)
	 2. A eunuch.
	 3. Whole grain.
	 f. (-ता) A plant, named
also Kankara Sringi.
	 mfn. (-त-ता-तः)
	 1. Uninjured, unhurt.
	 2.
Whole, unbroken.
 E. अ neg. and क्षत torn, broken &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=003-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

