 E. अग्नि and शेखर a crest.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्टुत्
अग्निष्टुत् f. (-ष्टुत्) An expiatory sacrifice.
 E. अग्नि and ष्टु to sacrifice, aff.
क्विप् with तुक् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्टोम|अग्निष्टोमः
अग्निष्टोम m. (-मः) A sacrifice, or rather a series of offerings to fire for
five days to be celebrated in the spring.
 E. अग्नि and लोम oblation,
burnt-offering.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्ठ|अग्निष्ठः
अग्निष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) An iron frying-pan.
	 mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Placed in or on fire.
E. अग्नि and ष्ठ what stays or remains, from स्था to stand.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्वात्त|अग्निष्वात्तः
अग्निष्वात्त m. pl. (-त्ताः) Demigods or Manes to whom funeral oblations
are presented. They are said to be the sons of MARĪCI, and
progenitors especially of the gods.
 E. अग्नि, स्व own, and आत्त
taken, who receive what is offered them by fire as their own.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=006-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

