<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तिका
अत्तिका f. (-का) In theatrical language, an elder sister.
 E. अत्ता a
mother, and कन् affix, who is, as it were, a mother; it is also
written अन्तिका and अर्विका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्वी-त्तृ) A feeder, one who eats.
 E. अद to eat. शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नु|अत्नुः
अत्नु m. (-त्नुः) The sun.
 E. अत to go, क्नु Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्य|अत्यः
अत्य m. (-त्यः) A horse, from the Vedas.
 E. अत to go constantly. यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यजनीय
अत्यजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Not to be abandoned.
 E. अ neg. त्यजनीय to be
abandoned.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्त|अत्यंत|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यन्त mfn. or adv.
	 n. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Much, excessive.
 E. अति beyond, and
अन्त end or boundary.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तकोपन|अत्यन्तकोपनः
अत्यन्तकोपन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Very passionate.
 E. अत्यन्त, and कोपन
passionate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तगामिन्
अत्यन्तगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) What goes much or quickly.
 E. अत्यन्त and
गामिन् who goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसुकुमार|अत्यन्तसुकुमारः
अत्यन्तसुकुमार m. (-रः) A species of grain, (Panicum Italicum.)
 E. अत्यन्त,
and सुकुमार very soft.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्ताभाव|अत्यन्ताभावः
अत्यन्ताभाव m. (-वः) (In logic) absolute negation or nonexistence. E.
अत्यन्त much, अभाव not being.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिक|अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिकः
अत्यन्तिक m. (-कः) One who rambles much, a great rover.
	 mfn. (-कः-की-कं)
Much, exceeding.
 E. अत्यन्त, with ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तीन|अत्यंतीन|अत्यन्तीनः
अत्यन्तीन m. (-नः) One who goes quickly or actively.
 E. अत्यन्त much,
and ईन for गामिन् who goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्ल|अत्यम्लं|अत्यम्लः
अत्यम्ल mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं) Very sour.
	 m. (-म्लः) A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)
f. (-म्ला) Another plant and fruit; a species of citron. See मातुलुङ्गी
E. अति, and अम्ल sour.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्लपर्णी|अत्यम्लपर्ण्णी
अत्यम्लपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A creeper and medicinal plant.
 E. अति excessive, अम्ल
sour; and पर्ण a leaf, with the fem. aff. ङीप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय m. (-यः)
	 1. Death.
	 2. Distress.
	 3. Transgression.
	 4. Vice, fault,
guilt.
	 5. Punishment.
	 6. Going over or beyond.
	 7. Absence.
	 8. Loss,
destruction.
 E. अति beyond, away, इण to go, and अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययित
अत्ययित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Exceeded, surpassed.
	 2. Outraged.
 E. अति
before इण to go, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थ|अत्यर्थं
अत्यर्थ n. adv. or mfn. adj. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Much, excessive.
 E. अति, and अर्थ
substance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यल्प|अत्यल्पं
अत्यल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Very small, very little.
 E. अति very, and अल्प
small.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यष्टी
अत्यष्टी f. (-ष्टी) A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with seventeen
syllables to the line.
 E. अति beyond, अष्टी another metre.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यसम
अत्यसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Very rough, uneven, craggy.
 E. अति, and
असम unequal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याकार|अत्याकारः
अत्याकार m. (-रः) Censure, blame, contempt.
 E. अति and आङ prefixed
to कृ to do, घञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचार|अत्याचारं|अत्याचारः
अत्याचार m. (-रः) Deviating from prescribed observances, contemning
religious and moral laws.
 E. अति, and आचार observance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचारिन्
अत्याचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Transgressing.
 E. अत्याचार, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याज्य|अत्याज्यं
अत्याज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्याः-ज्यं) Not to be abandoned.
 E. अ neg. त्याज्य to be
abandoned.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याशा
अत्याशा f. (-शा) Unreasonable hope or desire.
 E. अति, and आशा hope.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहार
अत्याहार m. (-रः) Excessive food.
 E. अति, and आहार food.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहारिन्
अत्याहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Eating excessively, a glutton, a gorman-
dizer.
 E. अत्याहार, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहित|अत्याहितं
अत्याहित n. (-तं)
	 1. Great dread.
	 2. Desperate or daring action.
 E. अति
with धा to have; आङ prefixed. and the participial क्त; हि is substi-
tuted for धा; what engrosses the mind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ति|अत्युक्तिः
अत्युक्ति f. (-क्तिः)
	 1. Idle or excessive talk.
	 2. Expatiating, enlarging.
	 3. A
figure of rhetoric, description of any thing surprising or extraordi-
nary, hyperbole.
 E. अति, and उक्ति speech.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्था
अत्युक्था f. (-क्था) A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with two
syllables to the line.
 E. अति, and उक्था another kind; it is also
read अत्युक्ता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्कट
अत्युत्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Extreme, exceeding great.
 E. अति, and उत्कट
much.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्कृष्ट
अत्युत्कृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Most excellent, best.
	 2. Most valuable,
precious.
 E. अति, and उत्कृष्ट excellent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूह|अत्यूहः
अत्यूह m. (-हः) A gallinule.
	 f. (-हा) A plant, (Jasminum villosum, Rox,
or in Bengal, Nyctanthes tristis) See शेफालिका.
 E. अति, and ऊह
to reason.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र ind. In this place, here, herein.
 E. त्र being substituted for the
termination of the seventh case of इदम् this.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रप
अत्रप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Shameless, immodest.
 E. अ neg. त्रपा shame.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रभवत्|अत्रभवन्त्
अत्रभवत् mfn. (-वान् वती-वत्) Respectable, venerable, (especially in thea-
tical language.
 E. अत्र here, भू to be and the participial affix शतृ;
being present or principal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रास
अत्रास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Fearless.
 E. अ neg. त्रास fear.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि m. (-त्रिः) The name of one of one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints,
born from the eye of RRAHMĀ, married to ANASŪYĀ, daughter
of KARDAMA MUNI, and the father of DATTA or DATTĀTREYA,
DURVĀSAS and CHANDRA.
 E. अद to eat and त्रिप् Unādi aff. The
correct reading is अत्त्रि, but the word is always written with one त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिजात|अत्रिजातः
अत्रिजात m. (-तः)
	 1. The moon.
	 2. A man of the three first classes. E.
अ neg. त्रि three, and जात born, not thrice born; born twice The
moon, from the eye of ATRI, and from the ocean. The Brahman
&c. from the womb and investiture.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिदृग्ज|अत्रिदृग्जः
अत्रिदृग्ज m. (-जः) A name of CHANDRA or the moon.
 E. अत्रि a saint, दृश्
the eye, and ज born, produced. Born from the eye of ATRI, “a
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">Page016-b+ 60</a>]
flash of light from the eye of ATRI, was received by space, a
goddess, the via lactea personified, who bore SOMA.” The following
and other similar names refer to this legend.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन् m. (-त्री) A muni. See अत्रि,
 E. अद to eat, Unādi aff. त्रिन्;
also अत्रिन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रज|अत्रिनेत्रजः
अत्रिनेत्रज m. (-जः) See अत्रिदृग्ज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत|अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूतः
अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत m. (-तः) See अत्रिदृग्ज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रभू
अत्रिनेत्रभू m. (-भूः) See अत्रिदृग्ज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिभारद्वाजिका
अत्रिभारद्वाजिका m. (-काः) The marriage union of ATRI and BHĀRA-
DWĀJĪ.
 E. अत्रि, and भारद्वाजी; affix वुञ्. implying in this and similar
compounds, union.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुर
अतुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Deliberate, not in haste.
 E. अ neg. तुर for त्वरा haste.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्रि
अत्त्रि m. (-त्त्रिः) A sage. See अत्त्रि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्रिन्
अत्त्रिन् m. (-त्त्री) A sage. See अत्त्रि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ ind. An auspicious and inceptive particle; it serves to introduce
a remark, a question, an affirmation, &c. and corresponds to.
	 1.
After.
	 2. And 3. Now, (inceptive or premising)
	 4. What, (inter-
rogatively)
	 5. All, (comprehensively)
	 6. Therefore, thus, further,
moreover, &c. It also implies doubt or command, and is frequently
redundant.
 E. अर्थ to ask, ड affix, and र is dropped, also अथो.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिम्
अथकिम् ind. A particle of assent, how else, what else, assuredly. अथच
ind. Also.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वण|अथर्वण|अथर्वणः|अथर्व्वणः
अथर्व्वण m. (-णः) A name of ŚIVA.
 E. अथर्ब्ब the name of a Veda, and ण aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वन्|अथर्वन्
अथर्व्वन् (-र्व्वा) 1. A Brahman.
	 2. A name of VASIṢṬHA.
	 n. (र्व्व) The name
of the fourth Veda.
 E. अथ an auspicious particle ऋ to go, and
वनिप aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वणि|अथर्वणि|अथर्वणिः|अथर्व्वणिः
अथर्व्वणि m. (-णिः)
	 1. Brahman versed in the Atharva Veda.
	 2. A
family priest.
 E. अथर्व्व the Veda, and णि aff.
