अनङ्ग|अनंग|अनङ्गं|अनङ्गः
अनङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्ग-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Bodiless, incorporeal.
	 m. (-ङ्गः) A name of KĀMA,
the Hindu deity of love.
	 n. (-ङ्गं)
	 1. Heaven, æther or the atmos-
phere.
	 2. The mind or faculty of reasoning.
 E. अन् neg. and अङ्ग
body; as applicable to KĀMA, it alludes to his having been re-
duced to ashes, by the eye of ŚIVA, for having distributed his
