<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्वेद|अन्तःस्वेदः
अन्तःस्वेद m. (-दः) An elephant.
 E. अन्तर् inner and स्वेद warmth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त|अंत|अन्तं|अन्तः
अन्त mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)
	 1. End, term.
	 2. Final, ultimate, (continuing M. N.
even with a fem. noun.)
	 mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)
	 1. Near.
	 2. Handsome.
m. (-न्त)
	 1. Death.
	 2. A boundary, a limit.
	 3. Certainty, ascertain-
ment.
	 4. A limb, a member.
	 n. (-न्तं) Nature, diposition.
 E. अम to
go, and तन् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तक|अंतक|अन्तकः
अन्तक m. (-कः) A name of YAMA.
 E. अन्त death, and क affix of agency.
YAMA is the king or angel of death.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकर
अन्तकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Causing death, mortal, destructive.
 E. अन्त, and कर
what makes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकाल|अन्तकालः
अन्तकाल m. (-लः) Time of death, death.
 E. अन्त end, and काल
time.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तग|अन्तगः
अन्तग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)
	 1. Dead, departed.
	 2. Traversing, crossing, going
to the end.
 E. अन्त, and ग who goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ततस्
अन्ततस् ind.
	 1. From the end, from the term.
	 2. Similarly, like.
	 3. In
part.
	 4. Lastly, finally.
 E. अन्त, and तस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्|अंतर्
अन्तर् ind. Within, between, amongst.
	 2. To the end.
	 3. Certainly,
very well, a particle of assent.
 E. अन्त end, रा to receive, and
क्विप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर|अंतर|अन्तरं
अन्तर (noun and adverb)
	 n. (-रं)
	 1. Interval, intermediate space.
	 2.
period, term.
	 3. Clothing.
	 4. Covering.
	 5. Difference.
	 6. Snake,
behalf.
	 7. A hole or rent.
	 8. Own, the self.
	 9. Without, except.
	 10.
Without, outside.
	 11. Opportune time.
	 12. Midst, the midst.
	 13.
The supreme soul.
	 14. Like, similar.
	 15. Other.
	 16. (In arithmetic)
Remainder, difference.
 E. अन्त end, and र from रा to obtain, and क
aff. In consulting the meanings of the word, it is to be recollected,
that vocables which are adverbs in English, are often nouns of the
neuter gender in Sanskrit; this word is also a pronoun, in the 3d
and 10th acceptations, when the latter means, without, or out
of, any thing but a house or town: the whole of the interpretations
may be referred to the ideas of, within and without.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरङ्ग|अन्तरंग|अन्तरङ्गः
अन्तरङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)
	 1. Own, belonging to.
	 2. Internal, interior.
	 3.
Of kin.
 E. अन्तर, and ग what goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतम|अंतरतम|अन्तरतमः
अन्तरतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्)
	 1. Immediate, intimate, internal.
	 2. Like,
analogous.
	 m. (-मः) A congenial letter, one of the same class. E.
अन्तर inner, and डतम aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरज्ञ
अन्तरज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Prudent, provident, foreseeing.
 E. अन्तर midst,
and ज्ञ who knows.
