<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषुमत्|अभीषुमन्त्
अभीषुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)
	 1. Splendid, brilliant.
	 2. Enamoured,
amorous.
 E. अभीषु and मतुप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Wished, desired.
	 f. (-ष्टा) A perfume. See रेणुका. E.
अभि repeatedly, and इष्ट wished.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्त|अभुक्तः
अभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)
	 1. Uneaten.
	 2. Unenjoyed, unused, unexpended.
3. One who has not eaten.
	 4. One who has not enjoyed or possessed.
E. अ neg. भुक्त eaten.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)
	 1. Straight, not bent.
