अरुन्तुदत्व
अरुन्तुदत्व n. (-त्वं)
	 1. Infliction of pain.
	 2. Acrimoniousness, causticity. E.
त्व added to the last. Also अरुन्तुदता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धती|अरुंधती
अरुन्धती f. (-ती) The daughter of KARDAMA and wife of VASIṢṬHA,
one of the seven Ṛṣis; she is also one of the Pleiades.
 E. अ neg.
रुध to confine, तन् and ङीप् affixes; who does not confine or hinder
good works. ARUNDHATĪ is considered as pattern of conjugal ex-
cellence, and is invoked at the marriage ceremony by the bridegroom.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीजानि|अरुन्धतीजानिः
अरुन्धतीजानि m. (-निः) VASIṢṬHA, one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints,
and stars in the great bear.
 E. अरुन्धती and जानि from जाया a wife;
whose wife is ARUNDHATĪ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीनाथ|अरुन्धतीनाथः
अरुन्धतीनाथ m. (-थः) A name of VASIṢṬHA, as above.
 E. अरुन्धती and नाथ
a lord or husband.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुश
अरुश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Smooth, liter. or fig.
 E. अ neg. रुश rough.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्क|अरुष्कः
अरुष्क m. (-ष्कः) The marking-nut plant, see the next word.
 E. अरुस् a
sore, and क what makes.
