अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ m. (-र्घः)
	 1. Price, cost.
	 2. Mode of worship or reverence.
	 3. An obla-
tion of various ingredients to a god or Brahman.
 E. अर्घ to cost, or
अर्ह to worship, ह being changed to घ, affix अच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घदान
अर्घदान n. (-नं) Presentation of a respectful offering.
 E. अर्घ, and दान
giving.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घबलाबल
अर्घबलाबल n. (-लं) Rate of price, proper price.
 E. अर्घ, and बल strength,
अबल weakness.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घसंख्यापन
अर्घसंख्यापन n. (-नं) Fixing the price of commodities, appraising, assize.
E. अर्घ, and संख्यापन fixing together with: it is the act of the king or
ruler, in concert with the traders, and should be done once a week
or once a fortnight.
