अर्ज|अर्ज्ज
अर्ज r. 1st cl. (-अर्जति) To earn, to gain or acquire, (commonly used with
उप prefixed.) 10th cl. (अर्जयति)
	 1. The same, and: 2. To work or
manufacture.
	 3. To make or prepare. This root and its derivatives
are also read अर्ज्ज, &c. doubling the consonant after र.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) An acquirer, one who gains or acquires.
	 m. (-कः)
Basil, the white sort, (Ocymum villosum.)
 E. अर्ज to gain, and वुन्
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जन|अर्जनं|अर्ज्जनं
अर्जन n. (-नं) Gain, acquisition of wealth, &c.
 E. अर्ज, and ल्युट् affix, also
written अर्ज्जन.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जित
अर्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gained, acquired.
 E. अर्ज to gain, क्त affix, also
written अर्ज्जित.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन m. (-नः)
	 1. The third of the Pāndavas, the son of INDRA and
friend of KṚṢṆA.
	 2. The name of a king with a thousand arms.
See कार्त्तवीर्य्य.
	 3. A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)
	 4. A peacock.
	 5. The
only son of his mother.
	 6. White, (the colour.)
	 nf. (-नं-नी)
	 1. Grass.
2. Slight inflammation of the conjunctiva or white of the eye.
	 f.
(-नी)
	 1. A cow.
	 2. UṢĀ, the wife of ANIRUDDHA.
	 3. The Karatoyā
river in the north of Bengal.
	 4. A procuress, a bawd.
	 mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)
White.
 E. अर्ज to gain, उनन् Unādi affix, fem. ङीप्, also read अर्ज्जुन.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनक|अर्जुनकः
अर्जुनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Belonging to ARJUNA.
 E. अर्जुन and वुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
