अर्भ|अर्भः
अर्भ mfn. (-र्भः-र्भा-र्भं) Destitute of splendour.
	 m. (-र्भः)
	 1. A child, a pupil.
2. Dew.
	 3. Herbs.
 E. ऋ to go, and भन् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भक|अर्भकः
अर्भक m. (-कः)
	 1. A child, the young of any animal.
	 2. A fool, an idiot.
3. Small, minute.
	 4. Emaciated.
	 5. Like, similar.
 E. ऋध to grow,
वुन् Unādi affix, and भ substituted for ध.
