<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतार|अवतारः
अवतार n. (-रं)
	 1. Descent, especially of a deity from heaven; the appear-
ance of any deity upon earth, but more particularly the incarna-
tions of VIṢṆU in ten principal forms which are well known, viz.
1. The fish.
	 2. The tortoise.
	 3. The boar.
	 4. The man-lion.
	 5. The
dwarf.
	 6. and 7. The two RĀMAS.
	 8. KṚṢṆA.
	 9. BUDDHA and
10. KALKI. A pious or distinguished person, in the language of
respect or flattery, is also called an Avatāra, a descent or incarna-
tion of the deity.
	 2. A Tirtha or sacred place.
	 3. Translation,
translating 4. Descent.
	 5. Crossing.
 E. अव before, तॄ to cross,
affix घञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारण|अवतारणं
अवतारण n. (णं)
	 1. Possession by an evil spirit.
	 2. The ends or border
of a garment.
	 3. Worship, adoration.
	 4. Taking out.
 E. अव, तॄ to
pass, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.
