<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाद|अवसादः
अवसाद m. (-दः)
	 1. Lassitude, want of energy or spirit, especially as
proceeding from doubtful or unsuccessful love.
	 2. Exhaustion,
fatigue.
	 3. In law, badness of a cause.
	 4. End, termination.
 E. अव,
षद to go, to sink, घञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अवसादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Exhausting, wearisome.
	 2. Ending, finish-
ing.
 E. अव before षद to go, &c. causal form, वुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादन|अवसादनं
अवसादन n. (-नं)
	 1. Finishing.
	 2. An escharotic.
	 3. Removing proud flesh
by escharotic applications.
 E. अव before षद to go, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादित
अवसादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Languid, exhausted, faint.
 E. अव, षद to go, क्त
aff.
