अश्वतर|अश्वतरः
अश्वतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Swift, speedy.
	 mf. (-रः-री) A mule.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. One
of the chiefs of the Nagas or serpent race, inhabiting the regions
under the earth.
	 2. A Gandharba or celestial chorister.
	 3. A male
calf.
 E. अश्व and तर from तॄ to pass, to go, affix अप्; or ष्टरच् diminu-
tive aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
