असुर|असुरः
असुर mf. (-रः-रा) An Asura or demon: the Asuras are children of DITI
by KAŚYAPA; they are demons of the first order, and in perpetual
hostility with the gods.
	 m. (-रः) The sun.
	 f. (-रा)
	 1. Night.
	 2. A
zodiacal sign.
	 3. A prostitute.
	 f. (-री)
	 1. Black mustard, (Sinapis
ramosa.)
	 2. The wife of an Asura.
 E. अ neg. and मुर a deity; or अस्
to send, to cast, &c. and उरन् Unādi affix, टाप् and ङीप् for the
fem. or अ neg. and सुरा spirituous liquor, personified as a dam-
sel produced at the churning of the ocean, who was rejected by the
demons and received by the gods.
