अहह
अहह ind. A particle or interjection, as ah! aha! &c. implying: 1.
Surprise: 2. Fatigue: 3. Pain: 4. Pleasure: 5. Calling.
 E. अह
from अहम् I, and ह from हा to abandon: self or pride-abandon-
ment; also अहहा.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहहा
अहहा ind. See the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य्य|अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Not to be stolen or taken away.
	 m. (-र्य्यः) A
mountain.
 E. अ neg. and हार्य्य future part. of हृञ् to take or con-
vey.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य्यत्व|अहार्यत्व
अहार्य्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Security, not being liable to be stolen or taken away.
E. अहार्य्य and त्व affix; also अहार्य्यता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहि|अहिः
अहि m. (-हिः)
	 1. A snake or serpent.
	 2. The sun.
	 3. A traveller.
	 4.
Lead.
	 5. The name of a demon: see वृत्रासुर.
	 6. A name of RĀHU,
the ascending node.
 E. आङ् prefixed to हन् to hurt, इन् Unādi affix;
injuring all or every thing, the आ of आङ् is made short.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसक
अहिंसक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Harmless, innocuous.
 E. अ neg. हिंसक mis-
chievous: so अहिंस्र and अहिंस्रक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसा
अहिंसा f. (-सा) Harmlessness, doing injury to nothing, one of the car-
dinal virtues of most Hindu sects, but particularly of the Baud-
dhas and Jainas.
 E. अ neg. हिंसा hurt.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसित
अहिंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uninjured.
 E. अ neg. हिंसित hurt.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्र|अहिंस्रः
अहिंस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं) Innocuous, innocent, harmless.
	 f. (-स्रा) The name
of a plant, commonly Kurkavali: see कर्कटा.
 E. अ neg. and हिंस्रा in-
jurious: than which there is none more so.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिका
अहिका f. (-का) The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)
 E. अ
neg. and हा to go or abandon, ङिक् and टाप् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिकान्त|अहिकांत|अहिकान्तः
अहिकान्त m. (-न्तः) Air, wind.
 E. अहि a serpent, and कान्त beloved;
snakes being supposed to feed upon air.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिच्छत्र|अहिच्छत्रः
अहिच्छत्र m. (-त्रः)
	 1. The name of a country.
	 2. A milky or thorny
plant: see मेषशृङ्गी.
	 f. (-त्रा)
	 1. Sugar.
	 2. A city.
 E. अहि a snake,
and छत्र a parasol.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिजित्
अहिजित् m. (-जित्)
	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.
	 2. Also of INDRA.
 E. अहि
and जित् who conquers, from जि with क्विप् affix; subduing a demon
in the form of a snake.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहित|अहितः
अहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Hostile, inimical.
	 2. Hurtful, prejudicial.
	 m.
(-तः) An enemy.
	 n. (-तं) Food, &c. contraindicated in a disease.
E. अ neg. and हित friendly, fit, proper.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितकारिन्
अहितकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Adverse, inimical, acting unkindly. E.
अहित unkind, कारिन् acting.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितमनस्
अहितमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Hating, adverse, inimical.
 E. अहित and मनस्
mind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितुण्डिक|अहितुंडिक|अहितुण्डिकः
अहितुण्डिक m. (-कः) A snake-catcher or exhibiter.
 E. अहि and तुण्ड face,
इकन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिद्विष्
अहिद्विष् m. (-द्विट्)
	 1. A name of INDRA.
	 2. GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.
3. A peacock.
	 4. An ichneumon.
 E. अहि and द्विष् who hates, from
द्विष् to hate with क्विप् affix; serpent-hater or enemy.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिनकुलिका
अहिनकुलिका f. (-का) The natural enmity subsisting between a snake
and an ichneumon.
 E. अहि, नकुल a mungoose, वुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिनिर्म्मोक|अहिनिर्मोक|अहिनिर्मोकः
अहिनिर्म्मोक m. (-कः) The slough of a snake.
 E. अहि and निर्म्मोक the
same.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिपति|अहिपतिः
अहिपति m. (-तिः)
	 1. A name of SHESHA, the sovereign of the snakes;
also of VĀSUKI and others.
	 2. Any large serpent.
 E. अहि a snake,
and पति lord; also similar compounds, as अहिनाथः, अहीन्द्रः, अहीशः,
अहीश्वरः, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिपुत्रक|अहिपुत्रकः
अहिपुत्रक m. (-कः) A kind of boat.
 E. अहि and पुत्रक a son, resembling a
snake.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिफेन|अहिफेनं|अहिफेनः
अहिफेन n. (-नं)
	 1. Opium.
	 2. The saliva or venom of a snake.
 E. अहि a
snake, and फेन foam.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिब्रध्न|अहिब्रध्नः
अहिब्रध्न m. (-ध्नः)
	 1. A name of ŚIVA.
	 2. One of the demigods called
RUDRAS.
 E. अहि and ब्रधि to bind, नक् Unādi affix; having his
neck bound with snakes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिब्रध्नदेवता
अहिब्रध्नदेवता f. (-ता) The twenty-sixth constellation.
 E. अहिब्रध्न and देवता
presiding deity.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिभय|अहिभयं
अहिभय n. (-यं) Mistrust or apprehension of treachery.
 E. अहि and भय
fear; fear of a lurking snake as it were.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिभुज्
अहिभुज् m. (-भुक्) GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.
	 2. A peacock.
 E. अहि
and भुज् who eats, from भुज् and क्विप् affix; snake-eater.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिमांशु|अहिमांशुः
अहिमांशु m. (-शुः) The sun.
 E. अ neg. हिम cold, and अंशु a ray; also si-
milar compounds, as अहिमकर, अहिमरुचि, अहिमतेजस्, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिविद्विष्
अहिविद्विष् m. (-द्विट्)
	 1. GARUḌA.
	 2. INDRA.
 E. अहि a snake or VRITRA-
SURA, and विद्विष् foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)
	 1. Possessed of, not deprived of.
	 2. Not out-caste
or vile.
 E. अ neg. हीन deprived of.
	 m. (-नः)
	 1. A large snake, a
serpent.
	 2. A particular sacrifice, one lasting twelve days.
 E. अहि
a snake, and इन superior, or अहन् a day, and ख aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीनवादिन्
अहीनवादिन् m. (-दी) A witness who is not unfit to give evidence.
 E. अ
neg. हीनवादी a defective witness.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीरणि|अहीरणिः
अहीरणि m. (-णिः) A kind of snake, said to be two-headed.
 E. अहि, इर
to move, and अणि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहुत|अहुतः
अहुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unoffered, unsacrificed.
	 2. Uncalled, unsummoned.
 m. (-तः) Religious meditation and prayer, considered as one
of the five great sacraments.
 E. अ neg. हु to sacrifice, or ह्वे to call,
क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहे
अहे ind. A particle implying, 1. Rejection.
	 2. Separation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतु|अहेतुः
अहेतु m. (-तुः) Absence of cause or reason.
 E. अ neg. हेतु cause.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुक
अहेतुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Causeless, groundless.
 E. अ neg. हेतुक having
cause.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुता
अहेतुता f. (-ता) Absence of cause or necessity.
 E. तल् added to अहेतु.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुत्व
अहेतुत्व n. (-त्वं) Absence of reason or cause.
 E. त्व added to अहेतु.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेरु|अहेरुः
अहेरु f. (-रुः) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus:) see शतमूली.
 E. अ neg.
हि to go, and रु affix; immoveable; alluding to the number of its
roots.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहो
अहो ind. A particle and interjection of, 1. Reproach, (fie !)
	 2.
Compassion.
	 3. Regret, (ah ! oh !)
	 4. Calling, (ho ! hola !)
	 5.
Praise, flattery, approbation.
	 6. Fatigue, weariness.
	 7. Surprise,
(ah !)
	 8. Doubt, deliberation, (either, or.)
	 9. Contempt, sneer-
ing.
	 10. An expletive.
 E. अ neg. हा to go, and डो aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहोरात्र m. (-त्रः) A day of twenty-four hours or thirty Muhūrtas, from
sunrise to sunrise.
	 n. or ind. (-त्रम्) Day and night, continually,
always.
 E. अहन् a day, and रात्रि a night.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोवत
अहोवत ind.
	 1. A particle of calling; 2. Of compassion; 3. Of
fatigue.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोही
अहोही ind. In a variegated or wonderful manner.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नाय
अह्नाय ind. Soon, instantly.
 E. अ neg. ह्नाय from ह्नु to take away or
secrete, with घञ् affix, and य substituted for the व to which the
radical त is changed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रीक|अह्रीकः
अह्रीक m. (-कः) A Bauddha mendicant.
 E. अ neg. and ह्रीक bashful.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्वला
अह्वला f. (-ला) The marking nut-plant, (Semecarpus anacardium.)
 E. अ
neg. ह्वे to emulate, and डल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ The second letter of the alphabet, corresponding to A long, as in
far, and written in the Roman character Ā.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ ind.
	 1. A particle of reminiscence, (ah! oh!)
	 2. A conjunction
disjunctive, (but)
	 3. A particle of compassion, (ah! alas!)
	 4.
A conjunction copulative, (and.) This particle remains unaltered
in orthography even before vowels.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ or आङ् A particle, and prefix to words, implying; 1. Diminu-
tion, (a little.)
	 2. Limit inceptive, (from, from thence, or that
time.)
	 3. Limit conclusive, (until, unto, as far as.)
	 4. Prefixed to
verbs it extends or reverses their meaning, as रुह to rise, आरुह
to ascend, to mount, and गम to go, आगम to come.
	 5. In composi-
tion with nouns it forms indeclinables, either crude, as आजानु to
the knee, or with the terminations of the objective or ablative
case, as आसमुद्रं or आसमुद्रात् as far as to the ocean.
	 6. A particle
of menace or of pain, (ah! alas!) this is more correctly written
आस्
 E. आप् to pervade, to obtain, and डाङ् affix, प is dropped.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्
आ or आङ् A particle, and prefix to words, implying; 1. Diminu-
tion, (a little.)
	 2. Limit inceptive, (from, from thence, or that
time.)
	 3. Limit conclusive, (until, unto, as far as.)
	 4. Prefixed to
verbs it extends or reverses their meaning, as रुह to rise, आरुह
to ascend, to mount, and गम to go, आगम to come.
	 5. In composi-
tion with nouns it forms indeclinables, either crude, as आजानु to
the knee, or with the terminations of the objective or ablative
case, as आसमुद्रं or आसमुद्रात् as far as to the ocean.
	 6. A particle
of menace or of pain, (ah! alas!) this is more correctly written
आस्
 E. आप् to pervade, to obtain, and डाङ् affix, प is dropped.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ m. (आः) A name of MAHĀDEVA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ ind. A particle of assent, yes, verily.
 E. अम to go, क्विप् affix, अ be-
comes आ
