आकाश|आकाशं|आकाशः
आकाश mn. (-शः-शं)
	 1. The fifth element, æther, the sky or atmosphere.
2. Brahma as identical with æther.
	 3. Space, vacuity.
 E. आङ्
and काशृ to shine, घञ् affix; every where shining; Akash is the
subtle and æthereal fluid, supposed to fill and pervade the
universe, and to be the peculiar vehicle of life and sound.
