<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या f. (-ख्या) A name or appellation.
 E. ख्या to say, आङ् prefixed, अङ्
and टाप् fem. affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यात|आख्यातं
आख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Said, spoken.
	 2. Called, declared.
	 3. Made
known.
	 4. Inflected, declined, conjugated. E. part. past of आख्या to
say, to speak, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यान|आख्यानं
आख्यान n. (-नं)
	 1. A tale, a legend.
	 2. Saying, declaring.
 E. आङ् before
ख्या to tell, affix ल्युट्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायक|आख्यायकः
आख्यायक m. (-कः) A messenger, a teller, an announcer or relater.
	 f.
(-यिका) A tale, a true or probable story.
 E. आख्या to say, खुल् affix,
य inserted.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्येय
आख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit or proper to be said.
 E. आङ् before ख्या to say,
affix यत्; also आख्यातव्य.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत|आगतं
आगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Arrived, come.
	 2. Received, obtained.
	 3. Living
or residing in.
 E. आङ् before गम् to go, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत्य
आगत्य ind. Having arrived.
 E. आङ् before गम् to go, ल्यप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तव्य|आगंतव्य
आगन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What will come, what is likely to arrive. E.
आङ् and गम् to go, तव्य aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तु|आगंतु|आगन्तुः
आगन्तु mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)
	 1. Coming, arriving.
	 2. Incidental, adventi-
tious.
	 m. (-न्तुः)
	 1. A guest.
	 2. A stranger, a newcomer.
	 3. An
accident, any accidental hurt or wound.
 E. आङ् before गम् to go,
to come, तु affix; म becomes न; also आगान्तु and आगन्तुक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुक|आगंतुक|आगन्तुकं
आगन्तुक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)
	 1. Incidental, adventitious. (as pleasure,
pain, ornament, &c.)
	 2. Stray.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. A stranger, a newcomer.
2. A guest.
 E. आगन्तु and कन् affix, what comes and goes: what is
not inseparably inherent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम|आगमं|आगमः
आगम m. (-मः)
	 1. Arrival, coming, approach.
	 2. A Śāstra or work on
sacred science in general, supposed to be of divine origin.
	 3. A
Tantra or any work inculcating the mystical worship of ŚIVA and
SAKTI.
	 4. A grammatical augment, a syllable or letter inserted in
any part of the radical word.
	 5. Record, title deed, legal title, a
voucher or written testimony, &c.
 E. आङ् before गम् to go, to come,
अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमन|आगमनं
आगमन n. (-नं) Arriving, coming.
 E. आङ् before गम् to go, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनिरपेक्ष
आगमनिरपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Independent of a written voucher or title.
E. आगम and निरपेक्षा disregard.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमय्य
आगमय्य ind. Having explored or discovered.
 E. आङ् before गम् to go,
causal form, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमरहित
आगमरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Devoid of a written title or voucher.
	 2.
Without a Śāstra.
 E. आगम and रहित devoid of.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमसापेक्ष
आगमसापेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) With or supported by legal vouchers. E.
आगम and सापेक्ष regard to.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमापायिन्
आगमापायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Transient, of short duration.
 E. आगम and
अपायिन् separating, going at the time of arrival.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमित|आगमितं
आगमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Read over, perused, studied.
 E. आङ् prefixed to
गम् in the causal form; participial affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्य
आगम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)
	 1. To be approached, accessible.
	 2. To be acquired.
E. आङ् before गम् with यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस् n. (-गः)
	 1. Sin.
	 2. Transgression, offence, fault.
 E. आग substituted
for इण् to go, असुन् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=086-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगाध|आगाधं
आगाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Very deep: see अगाध.
