आदितेय|आदितेयः
आदितेय m. (-यः) A deity, a divinity.
 E. अदिति the mother of the gods.
and ढक् derivative aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य m. (-त्यः)
	 1. A deity in general.
	 2. A deity of a particular class;
the ADITYAS are twelve in number, they are forms of SŪRYA or the
sun, and appear to represent him as distinct in each month of
the year.
	 3. The sun.
 E. अदिति the mother of the gods, and घञ्
derivative aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपुष्पिका
आदित्यपुष्पिका f. (-का) Red swallow wort.
 E. आदित्य the sun, and पुष्पिका
having a flower, the flower of the sun, from its red colour: see
अर्कपुष्पिका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यमण्डल
आदित्यमण्डल n. (-लं) The disc or orb of the sun.
 E. आदित्य and मण्डल a circle.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यसूनु|आदित्यसूनुः
आदित्यसूनु m. (-नुः)
	 1. A name of SUGRĪVA, a monkey king; 2. of YAMA;
3. of SANI or SATURN.
 E. आदित्य the sun, and सूनु a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्व|आदित्वं
आदित्व n. (-त्वं) Priority, precedence.
 E. आदि and त्व added; also आदिता
with तल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सा
आदित्सा f. (-ता) Wish to seize.
 E. आङ् before दा to give, desiderative
from, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सु
आदित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing to take or have.
 E. आङ् before दा
to give, desiderative form, उस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदेव|आदिदेवः
आदिदेव m. (-वः) Name of VIṢṆU or NARAYANA.
 E. आदि the first, and
देव a god, the first god, the creator.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुरुष|आदिपुरुषः
आदिपुरुष m. (-षः) The first male, usually applied to VIṢṆU.
 E. आदि the
first, and पुरुष a man.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभूत|आदिभूतः
आदिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) First born or existent.
	 m. (-तः) BRAHMĀ.
 E. आदि
and भूत been.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) First, prior.
 E. आदि and डिमच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिराज|आदिराजः
आदिराज m. (-जः) The name of a king; also पृथु.
 E. आदि and राजन् a king,
the first king; he was a form of VIṢṆU, and husband of Prithivi
or the earth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवराह|आदिवराहः
आदिवराह m. (-हः) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. आदि and वराह a boar; the
first boar, alluding to VIṢṆU'S avatara or incarnation in that
form; also similar compounds, as आदिशूकरः, आद्यकोलः, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्ट|आदिष्टं|आदिष्टः
आदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Commanded, directed.
	 2. Appointed.
	 3. Ad-
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">Page091-b+ 60</a>]
viced, enjoined.
	 4. Said.
	 n. (-ष्टं) Fragments or leavings of a meal.
E. आङ् before दिश् to point or show, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टिन्
आदिष्टिन् m. (-ष्टी)
	 1. A student, a Brahman in the first order.
	 2. A
penite, one engaged in any expiatory rite.
 E. आदिष्ट what is in-
structed, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनव|आदीनवं|आदीनवः
आदीनव m. (-वः)
	 1. Distress, pain, uneasiness.
	 2. Fault, transgression.
3. An inflictor of distress.
 E. आङ् before दीङ् to decay, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपन|आदीपनं
आदीपन n. (-नं)
	 1. Whitening the wall, floor, or seat, &c. upon festi-
val occasions.
	 2. Embellishing.
	 3. Inflaming, exciting.
 E. आङ्, दीप्
to beautify, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपित
आदीपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Illuminated.
 E. आङ् before दीप् to inflame, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत|आदृतः
आदृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Respectful.
	 2. Respected, honoured, worship-
ped.
	 3. Zealous, diligent.
 E. आङ् before दृञ् to have, and क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत्य|आदृत्यः
आदृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Venerable, respectable.
 E. आङ् before दृ to have,
क्यप् affix; तुक् augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेय
आदेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Receivable, leviable, what may be taken or re-
ceived.
 E. आङ् before दा to give, यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवक
आदेवक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) One who sports or plays.
 E. आङ् before दिन to
sport, वुञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश|आदेशः
आदेश m. (-शः)
	 1. An order, a command.
	 2. Advice, instruction.
	 3. (In
grammar,) A substitute.
	 4. (In astrology,) Event, result, conse-
quence of stellar conjunctions, &c.
 E. आङ् before दिश् to point or
show, घञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिन्
आदेशिन् m. (-शी)
	 1. A commander, a director.
	 2. An astrologer, a for-
tune-teller.
 E. आङ् before दिश to point or show, and णिनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेष्टृ
आदेष्टृ m. (-ष्टा)
	 1. An adviser, a director, a commander.
	 2. An employer
of priests.
 E. आङ् before दिश to show, तृच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)
	 1. First, initial.
	 2. Edible, what is to be or may
be eaten.
	 n. (-द्यं)
	 1. Grain.
	 2. Food.
	 f. (-द्या) A name of DURGĀ. E.
आदि and ण्यत् affix, fem. टाप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यकवि|आद्यकविः
आद्यकवि m. (-विः) A name of VALMIKI, author of the Rāmāyaṇa. E.
आद्य first, and कवि a poet, being the first who wrote Sanskrit verse.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्त
आद्यन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) From the beginning to the end.
	 n. (-न्तं) Be-
ginning and end, first and last.
 E. आदि first, and अन्त last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तवत्|आद्यन्तवन्त्
आद्यन्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Finite, having beginning and end.
 E. आदि
beginning, अन्त end, and मतुप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यमाषक|आद्यमाषकः
आद्यमाषक m. (-कः) A Masha, a weight equal to five Gunja or Retti
seeds, about 17(1/2) grains troy.
 E. आद्य and माषक a Masha, the pri-
mary Masha; also माष and मास.
