आर्य्य|आर्य|आर्यः|आर्य्यः
आर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)
	 1. Of a good family.
	 2. Respectable, venerable.
3. Apposite, proper.
	 4. To be sought or obtained.
	 m. (-र्य्यः)
	 1. A
master, an owner.
	 2. A name of BUDDHA.
	 3. A friend.
	 f. (-र्य्या)
1. A name of PARVATI.
	 2. A kind of metre, measured by feet,
each foot being equal to four short syllables, or two long and two
short; there are seven and a half feet in each verse of the
couplet, equal to thirty and to twenty-seven syllabic instants: the
regular form consists of alternate long and short verses, but it
admits of eighty principal variations.
 E. ऋ to go, ण्यत् affix; also
अर्य्य.
