इन्द्रलोकेश|इन्द्रलोकेशः
इन्द्रलोकेश m. (-शः)
	 1. INDRA.
	 2. A guest, hospitality to whom secures
paradise.
 E. इन्द्रलोक and ईश lord.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणिका
इन्द्रवारुणिका f. (-का) Colocynth, a wild bitter gourd, (Cucumis colo-
cynthis.)
 E. कन् added to इन्द्रवारुणी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणी
इन्द्रवारुणी f. (-णी) See the preceding.
 E. इन्द्र and वरुण the two deities so
called, affixes अण् and ङीप्; the favourite plant of INDRA and
VARUṆA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृक्ष|इन्द्रवृक्षः
इन्द्रवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A kind of fir: see देवदारु.
 E. इन्द्र for any god, वृक्ष a tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रव्रत
इन्द्रव्रत n. (-तं) One of the duties of a king, to distribute gratification,
as INDRA pours down rain.
 E. इन्द्र and व्रत observance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृद्धा
इन्द्रवृद्धा f. (-द्धा) A sore, an ulcer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशक्ति|इन्द्रशक्तिः
इन्द्रशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) INDRĀṆĪ, the wife or personified energy of INDRA. E.
इन्द्र and शक्ति power.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसावर्णि|इन्द्रसावर्णिः
इन्द्रसावर्णि m. (-र्णिः) The last of the fourteen Menus.
 E. इन्द्र and सावर्णि the son of the sun.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुत|इन्द्रसुतः
इन्द्रसुत m. (-तः) The monkey king BALI.
 E. इन्द्र and सुत a son; the son
of INDRA: the epithet is also applied to ARJUNA and JAYANTA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरस|इन्द्रसुरसः
इन्द्रसुरस m. (-सः) A shrub, the leaves of which are used in discutient
applications, (Vitex negundo;) also सिन्दुवार.
 E. इन्द्र best, सु good,
and रस juice; whose juice is excellent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरिस|इन्द्रसुरिसः
इन्द्रसुरिस m. (-सः) See the preceding. E. As before, the pen. being changed to इ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसूनु|इन्द्रसूनुः
इन्द्रसूनु m. (-नुः) The son of INDRA: see इन्द्रसुत
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राग्निधूम|इन्द्राग्निधूमः
इन्द्राग्निधूम m. (-मः) Frost.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणिका|इंद्राणिका
इन्द्राणिका f. (-का) Vitex negundo: see इन्द्रसुरस.
 E. कन् added to the next word.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणी|इंद्राणी
इन्द्राणी f. (-णी)
	 1. The wife of INDRA.
	 2. A plant, (Vitex negundo:) see
the preceding.
 E. इन्द्र, ङीष् affix, and आनुक् augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रानुज|इन्द्रानुजः
इन्द्रानुज m. (-जः) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. इन्द्र and अनुज younger born:
the younger brother of INDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रायुध|इन्द्रायुधं|इन्द्रायुधः
इन्द्रायुध m. (-धः) The rainbow.
	 f. (-धा) A kind of leech of various tints
on the back.
 E. इन्द्र and आयुध a weapon; INDRA'S weapon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रारि|इन्द्रारिः
इन्द्रारि m. (-रिः) An Asura or demon.
 E. इन्द्र and अरि an enemy.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रावरज|इन्द्रावरजः
इन्द्रावरज m. (-जः) VIṢṆU.
 E. इन्द्र and अवरज after-born: the younger
brother of INDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राशन|इन्द्राशनः
इन्द्राशन m. (-नः)
	 1. Hemp, dried and chewed.
	 2. The shrub which bears
the seed used as a jeweller's weight, (Abrus precatorius.)
 E. इन्द्र
and अशन food: the food of INDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रासन
इन्द्रासन n. (-नं)
	 1. The throne of INDRA.
	 2. Any throne.
 E. इन्द्र and असन
a seat.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय n. (-यं)
	 1. An organ of sense divided into three classes, Jananendri-
yas, Karmendriyas, and Antarindriyas, or organs of percep-
tion and action, and the internal organs; the first are the eye, ear,
nose, tongue, and skin; the second, the organ of speech or larynx,
hand, foot, anus, and parts of generation; the last are, Manas
the mind or organ of thought; Buddhi the organ of apprehension;
Ahankara the organ of selfishness; and Chitta the heart or organ
of feeling.
	 2. Semen virile.
	 mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Done, seen, given, &c.
by INDRA.
 E. इन्द्र the soul or self, and इयच् affix, deriv. irr. what is
with difficulty restrained by the soul, or इन्द्र the deity, and घ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियगोचर|इन्द्रियगोचरः
इन्द्रियगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Perceptible, capable of being ascertained by
the senses.
 E. इन्द्रिय and गोचर perceptible.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियग्राम|इन्द्रियग्रामः
इन्द्रियग्राम m. (-मः) The senses or organs of sense collectively.
 E. इन्द्रिय
and ग्राम here, assemblage.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियज्ञान
इन्द्रियज्ञान n. (-नं) The faculty of perception, sense, consciousness. E.
इन्द्रिय and ज्ञान knowledge.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियनिग्रह|इन्द्रियनिग्रहः
इन्द्रियनिग्रह m. (-हः) Restraining the organs of sense.
 E. इन्द्रिय and
निग्रह restraint.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबुद्धि|इन्द्रियबुद्धिः
इन्द्रियबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Perception, the exercise of any sense, the faculty of
any organ.
 E. इन्द्रिय and बुद्धि knowledge.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबोधन
इन्द्रियबोधन n. (-नं) Any excitement of sense, an object of perception, a
stimulus, &c.
 E. इन्द्रिय and बोधन waking.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवर्ग|इन्द्रियवर्गः
इन्द्रियवर्ग m. (-र्गः) the organs of sense collectively.
 E. इन्द्रिय and वर्ग a class.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति|इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्तिः
इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Erroneous or vicious perception.
 E. इन्द्रिय and
विप्रतिपत्ति perversion.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियस्वाप|इन्द्रियस्वापः
इन्द्रियस्वाप m. (-पः)
	 1. Unconsciousness, insensibility.
	 2. The end of the
world.
 E. इन्द्रिय and स्वाप sleep.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियागोचर
इन्द्रियागोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Imperceptible.
 E. इन्द्रिय and अगोचर im-
perceptible.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियायतन|इन्द्रियायतनं
इन्द्रियायतन n. (-नं) The body.
 E. इन्द्रिय and आयतन a mansion: the resi-
dence of the senses.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियार्थ|इन्द्रियार्थः
इन्द्रियार्थ m. (-र्थः) An object of sense, as sound, smell, &c.
 E. इन्द्रिय and
अर्थ an object.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियासङ्ग|इन्द्रियासङ्गः
इन्द्रियासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Stoicism, philosophy, detachment from sensual
objects.
 E. इन्द्रिय and असङ्ग detachment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=109-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रेज्य|इन्द्रेज्यः
