<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सन
ईप्सन n. (-नं) Desiring, wishing to obtain.
 E. आप् to obtain, desiderative
form, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired.
 E. आप् to obtain, desiderative
form, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desirous, wishing to get or obtain.
 E. आप् to ob-
tain, desiderative form, उस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर|ईरः
ईर r. 2nd cl. (ईर्त्ते)
	 1. To go.
	 2. To shake. r. 1st and 10th cls. (ईरति,
ईरयति)
	 1. To go.
	 2. To throw or direct, to drive or force on; with
उत् prefixed, to say or speak; with प्र, to send, to make to go;
with सम्, to go like the wind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईयिवस्
ईयिवस् mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वस्)
	 1. Gone, having gone.
	 2. Having obtained.
E. ईण् to go, क्वसु aff. form irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)
	 1. Desert.
	 2. Saline and barren (soil.)
 E. ऋ to go,
and इरन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरित|ईरितं
ईरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Sent, dispatched.
	 2. Said, uttered.
	 3. Gone.
4. Made.
 E. ईर् to send, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिताकूत
ईरिताकूत n. (-तं) Declared purpose or intention.
 E. ईरित and आकूत
purpose.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य
ईर्क्ष्य r. 1st cl. (ईर्क्ष्यति) To envy, to feel impatient at another's
prosperity.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म्म|ईर्म|ईर्मः
ईर्म्म n. (-र्म्मं) A sore or wound.
 E. ईर् to send, and मक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्य्या|ईर्या
ईर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Wandering about as a religious mendicant.
 E. ईर् to go,
affix क्यप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्व्वारु|ईर्वारु|ईर्वारुः|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्व्वारु m. (-रुः) A cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus;) also ईर्व्वालु and
ईर्व्वारु, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा f. (-र्षा) Impatience, envy of another's success; more properly read ईर्ष्या.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्षालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Impatient of another's success, envious.
 E. ईर्षा
and आलुच् affix: see ईर्ष्यालु.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षित
ईर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Envied.
	 n. (-तं) Envy.
 E. ईर्षा and इतच् affix, or
ईर्ष् with क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य r. 1st. cl. (ईर्ष्यति) To envy.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्यं) Envious, envying.
	 f. (-र्ष्या)
	 1. Envy or impatience
of another's success.
	 2. Spite, malice.
 E. ईर्ष्य to envy, and अच् and
टाप affixes; also, but according to the best writers, inaccurately
written ईर्षा.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Envious, envying.
 E. ईर्ष्य and वुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यमाण
ईर्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Envying, envious.
 E. ईर्ष्य and शानच् aff.
