औष्ट्रक|औष्ट्रकं
औष्ट्रक n. (-कं) A herd of camels.
 E. उष्ट्र a camel, and वुञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्म्य|औष्म्यं
औष्म्य n. (-ष्म्यं) Heat, warmth.
 E. उष्म warm, यञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क The first consonant of the Nagari Alphabet, and the first of the
guttural letters, corresponding to K or C in can, designated by
the latter in Sir. WM. JONES'S system, but in this work by the
former.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क m. (-कः)
	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.
	 2. Of VIṢṆU.
	 3. Of KĀMADEVA.
4. Of fire.
	 5. Air or wind.
	 6. A title of YAMA.
	 7. The sun.
	 8. The
soul.
	 9. A clever or dexterous man.
	 10. A king, a prince.
	 11. A
knot or joint.
	 12. A peacock.
	 13. The mind.
	 14. The body.
	 15.
Time.
	 16. Wealth, property.
	 17. Sound.
	 18. Light, splendor.
	 n.
(कं)
	 1. The head.
	 2. Water.
	 3. Pleasure, happiness.
	 4. Hair.
	 5. A
head of hair. pron.
	 mfn. (-कः-का-किम्) Who or what: see किम्.
 E. कै
to sound, or कच् to shine, &c. affix ड.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्य
कंय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Happy.
 E. कं happiness, यस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्यु
कंय्यु mfn. (-य्युः-य्युः-य्यु) Happy, prosperous.
 E. कं happiness and युस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंश|कंशः
कंश m. (-शः) A goblet: see कंस.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस|कंसं|कंसः
कंस m. (-सः) A proper name; KANSA king of Mathura the uncle and
enemy of KṚṢṆA, by whom he was slain; as the foe of the
deity, he is considered an Asura or demon.
	 mn. (-सः-सं)
	 1. A goblet,
a drinking vessel; also कंश and कांस्य.
	 2. A metal, tutanag or
white copper; also bell metal.
	 3. A measure.
 E. कमु to desire, स
Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसक|कंसकं
कंसक n. (-कं) A mineral substance, (a salt of iron?) used as an appli-
cation to the eyes: see पुष्पकासीस.
 E. कंस, and क affix of similarity;
of similar white colour.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकार|कंसकारः
कंसकार m. (-रः) A worker in pewter or white brass.
 E. कंस and कार who
makes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसजित्
कंसजित् m. (-जित्) A title of KṚṢṆA.
 E. कंस, and जित् who conquers.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसहन्
कंसहन् m. (-हा) A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.
 E. हन् from हन to
kill; the destroyer of KANSA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसाराति|कंसारातिः
कंसाराति m. (-तिः) KṚṢṆA, or VIṢṆU in that character.
 E. कंस, and
अराति an enemy, the foe of KANSA; hence also कंसारि and other
similar epithets: see the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारि|कंसारिः
कंसारि m. (-रिः) See the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसास्थि
कंसास्थि n. (-स्थि) Tutanag, white copper, any alloy of tin and copper. E.
कंस white metal, and अस्थि bone, fig. substance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसिक
कंसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of bellmetal, &c.
 E. कंस, and ठन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीय
कंसीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit for or relating to a cup.
 E. कंस, and छ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसोद्भवा
कंसोद्भवा f. (-वा) A fragrant earth: see तुवरी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक
कक r. 1st cl. (ककते)
	 1. To be proud.
	 2. To be unsteady.
	 3. To be
thirsty. (इ) ककि (कंकते) To go.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककन्द|ककंदः|ककन्दः
ककन्द m. (-न्दः) Gold.
 E. कनी to shine, affix द, and the initial repeated.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुञ्जल|ककुंजल|ककुंजलः|ककुञ्जलः
ककुञ्जल m. (-लः) A bird, the Chataka.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुत्स्थ|ककुत्स्थः
ककुत्स्थ m. (-स्थः) A prince, the grandson of IKSHWAKU, and ancestor
of RAMA.
 E. ककुद् an emblem of royalty, and स्थ who resides.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद् f. (-त्) or ककुद mn. (-दः-दं)
	 1. The hump on the shoulders of the
Indian bull.
	 2. An ensign or symbol of royalty, as the white
parasol, &c.
	 3. Chief, pre-eminent.
	 4. The peak or summit of a
mountain.
 E. क happiness, कु to sound, affixes क्विप् and तुक्; त
becomes द; or with a final vowel, taking an additional affix अच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मत्|ककुद्मन्त्
ककुद्मत् m. (-द्मान्)
	 1. A bull.
	 2. A mountain.
	 f. (-द्मती) The hip and lions.
E. ककुद् a bull's hump, &c. affix मतुप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिकन्या
ककुद्मिकन्या f. (-न्या) A river.
 E. ककुद्मिन् a mountain, कन्या a daughter.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिन्
ककुद्मिन् mfn. (-द्मी-द्मिनी-द्मि)
	 1. Peaked.
	 2. Humped.
	 m. (-द्मी)
	 1. A moun-
tain.
	 2. A bull.
 E. ककुद, and मिनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुन्दर|ककुंदर|ककुंदरं|ककुन्दरं
ककुन्दर n. (-रं) The cavities of the loins: see कुकुन्दर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ् f. (-प)
	 1. Space, region or quarter, as east, west, &c.
	 2. Beauty,
splendor.
	 3. Unornamented hair, or the hair hanging down as a
tail.
	 4. A wreath of Champaka flowers.
	 5. A Rāgiṇī or personified
mode of music.
	 6. A Śāstra or sacred treatise.
 E. क wind, स्कुभ् to
spread, क्विप् affix and the स is dropped; or कक् to be proud,
उभ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ m. (-भः)
	 1. A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna, Rox.)
	 2. A part of a lute,
the belly, a wooden vessel covered with leather placed under its
neck to render the sound deeper, or a crooked piece of wood at
the end of the lute.
	 3. One of the Ragas or personified musical
modes.
	 f. (-भा)
	 1. Space, region, quarter: see ककुभ् 2. One of the
Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.
 E. ककुभ् space, and
अच् affix; or क wind, स्कुभ् to spread, क affix and स rejected, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभादनी
ककुभादनी f. (-नी) A kind of perfume: see नली.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककेरुक|ककेरुकः
ककेरुक m. (-कः) A worm in the stomach.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क
कक्क r. 1st cl. (कक्कति) To laugh.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोल|कक्कोलः
कक्कोल m. (-लः) A perfume, a plant bearing a berry, the inner part of
which is a waxy and arometic substance.
	 n. (-लं) The berry, possibly
the fruit of the Cocculus Indicus.
 E. कक् to be proud, with क्विप्
affix, कुल् to accumulate, अच् affix; also with कन् added कक्कोलक
mn. (-कः-कं.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख
कक्ख(ए) r. 1st cl. (कक्खति) To laugh, to laugh at, to deride; see खक्ख.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Hard, solid.
	 f. (-टी) chalk.
 E. कक्ख to deride,
अटन् affix, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष्; also खक्खट.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटपत्रक|कक्खटपत्रकः
कक्खटपत्रक m. (-कः) A plant of the fibres of which a kind of rope is
made, (Corchorus olitorius, Rox.)
 E. कक्खट hard, पत्र a leaf, and
कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्व
कक्व r. 1st cl. (कक्वति) To laugh.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष|कक्षः
कक्ष m. (-क्षः)
	 1. The armpit.
	 2. A spreading creeper, a climbing plant.
3. Grass.
	 4. Dry grass.
	 5. A wood, a forest.
	 6. A forest of dead
trees, a dry wood.
	 7. A private or inner chamber or part of a
house.
	 8. Sin.
	 9. A buffalo.
	 10. The side or flank.
	 11. (In astro-
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">Page146-b+ 60</a>]
nomy,) The orbit of a planet, or the circle anciently termed a
deferent.
	 12. A gate.
	 13. The beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia bele-
rica.)
	 mf. (-क्षः-क्षा)
	 1. A wall.
	 2. The end of the lower garment, which
after the cloth is carried round the body, is brought up behind,
and tucked into the waistband.
	 f. (-क्षा)
	 1. An elephant's rope, the
string round his neck, also his girth.
	 2. A woman's girdle or zone.
3. An enclosure, a part or division of an edifice.
	 4. A part of a car.
5. Objection or reply in argument.
	 6. Similarity, parity.
	 7. Emula-
tion, rivalship.
	 8. The jeweller's weight, the Retti.
	 9. Painful boils
in the armpit, side, shoulder, &c.
	 n. (-क्षं) A constellation, a star:
see कक्ष्या, कच्छ, काञ्चि, &c.
 E. कष् to hurt or kill, स Uṇādi affix,
fem. टाप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षरुहा
कक्षरुहा f. (-हा) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)
 E. कक्ष an enclosure, and
रुह what grows.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशाय|कक्षशायः
कक्षशाय m. (-यः) A dog.
 E. कक्ष an inner room, शाय who sleeps.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षान्तर|कक्षांतर
कक्षान्तर n. (-रं) The inner or private apartment.
 E. कक्ष and अन्तर
interior.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षापट|कक्षापटः
कक्षापट m. (-टः) A cloth passed between the legs to cover the privities.
E. कक्षा a girdle, and पट a cloth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षावेक्षक|कक्षावेक्षकः
कक्षावेक्षक m. (-कः)
	 1. A doorkeeper.
	 2. A guard of the queen's apart-
ments.
	 3. Keeper of royal garden.
	 4. A painter.
	 5. A poet.
	 6. A
debauchee.
	 7. Eagerness of feeling, strength of sentiment.
 E. कक्षा
an enclosure, and अवेक्ष to see, वुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीवत्|कक्षीवन्त्
कक्षीवत् m. (-वान्) The name of a saint.
 E. कक्षा a reply, and मतुप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षोत्था
कक्षोत्था f. (-त्था) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्य|कक्ष्यं
कक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) The cup or receptacle of a balance.
	 f. (-क्ष्या)
	 1. The girth
of an elephant, of rope or leather.
	 2. A woman's girdle or zone.
	 3.
The enclosure of an edifice; that is, either the wall, &c. so enclos-
ing, or the court or chamber constituting the enclosure.
	 4. The
inner apartment of a palace.
	 5. Similarity.
	 6. Effort, exertion.
	 7.
An upper garment.
	 8. A shrub, yielding the black and red berry,
that serves as a jeweller's weight; the Ratti or Gunga, (Abrus
precatorius.)
 E. कक्ष the flank, &c. यत् affix; see कक्ष.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख
कख r. 1st cl. (ए) कखे (कखति) To laugh, to laugh at or deride; also
कक्ख and खक्ख q. v.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या f. (-ख्या) An enclosure, a division of a large building: see कक्ष्या. E.
कख् to deride, यत् aff. and टाप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कग
कग r. 1st cl. (ए) कगे (कगति) To perform any action: the meaning of
this root is not given in many lists, from its application being
indefinitely various.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्क|कंक|कंकः|कङ्कः
कङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)
	 1. A heron.
	 2. YAMA or death.
	 3. A false or pretended
Brahman.
	 4. A title of YUDISHṬHIRA, from his assuming the dis-
guise of a Brahman.
	 5. A man of the second or military tribe.
	 6.
One of the eighteen divisions of the continent.
	 7. The brother of
KANSA.
	 8. A kind of mango.
	 f. (-ङ्का)
	 1. A daughter of UGRASENA.
2. A sort of sandal.
 E. ककि to go, अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कट|कंकट|कंकटः|कङ्कटः
कङ्कट m. (-टः) Mail, defensive armour.
 E. ककि to go, Uṇādi affix अटन्,
and with कन् added कङ्कटक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कटेरी
कङ्कटेरी f. (-री) Turmerick.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कण|कंकण|कंकणं|कङ्कणं|कंकणः|कङ्कणः
कङ्कण mn. (-णः-णं)
	 1. A bracelet or ornament of the wrist.
	 2. A string
or ribband tied round the wrist.
	 3. An ornament or trinket.
	 4. A
crest.
	 f. (-णी) A small bell or tinkling ornament; also किङ्किणी and
कङ्कणीका.
 E. कं happily, agreeably, कण् to sound, or the reiterative
form of कण and अच् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कणीका|कंकणीका
कङ्कणीका f. (-का) See कङ्कणी.
 E. कण् to sound in the reiterative form, and
ईकन् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत|कंकत|कंकतं|कङ्कतं|कंकतः|कङ्कतः
कङ्कत mfn. (-तः-तिका or -ती-तं) A comb, an instrument for cleaning the
hair.
	 m. (-तः) A tree.
 E. ककि to go, अतच् affix, fem. ङीष् or कन्
added in the fem. form.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोट|कङ्कत्रोटः
कङ्कत्रोट m. (-टः) A kind of fish commonly Kanila (Esox Cancila,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">Page147-a+ 60</a>]
HAM.)
 E. कङ्क a heron, and त्रोटि the throat; whose long snout re-
sembles the beak of a heron: also कङ्कत्रोटि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोटि|कङ्कत्रोटिः
कङ्कत्रोटि m. (-टिः) A kind of a fish: see the preceding; also जलसूचि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्र|कंकपत्र|कङ्कपत्रः
कङ्कपत्र m. (-त्रः) An arrow.
 E. कङ्क and पत्र leaf, (feather.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमाला
कङ्कमाला f. (-ला) Beating time by clapping the hands: see करताली.
