कञ्जर|कंजर|कंजरः|कञ्जरः
कञ्जर m. (-रः)
	 1. A name of BRAHMA.
	 2. The sun.
	 3. The belly.
	 4. An
elephant.
 E. कञ्ज a lotus, &c. ऋ to hate or injure, अच् or घञ् affix
कञ्जार, the pen. made short; also derived by some from कजि, a
Sautra root, to produce or grow, and अर Uṇādi aff.
