कठ|कठः
कठ m. (-ठः)
	 1. The name of a Muni or saint.
	 2. A note or simple
sound.
	 3. A portion of the Yajur Veda.
	 4. A Mantra or mystical
prayer.
	 5. A Brahman.
	 6. A Brahman versed in the Vedas, especi-
ally in the Rig Veda.
	 7. A student of the same.
	 8. Trouble, dis-
tress.
	 f. (-ठी) The wife of a Brahman.
 E. कठ् to be confused, and
अप् aff.
