कन्दर्प|कंदर्प|कंदर्पः|कन्दर्पः
कन्दर्प m. (-र्पः) A name of the deity KĀMA^1, the CUPID of the Hiudu
mythology.
 E. कं BRAHMĀ, दर्प to inflame, अच् affix; the inflamer
even of the first of the gods; corresponding in this respect with
his Grecian prototype.
	 f. (-र्पा) One of the presiding female deities
of the Jainas.
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.
