<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम
कम(उ)कमु r. 1st cl. (कामयति) To desire: this root is irregular.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम् ind.
	 1. Water.
	 2. The head.
	 3. Happiness or happily.
	 4. An exple-
tive.
 E. कम् to desire, विच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमठ|कमठं|कमठः
कमठ mn. (-ठः-ठं)
	 1. A water jar, especially one made of a hollow
gourd or cocoanut, and used by ascetics.
	 m. (-ठः)
	 1. A turtle,
a tortoise.
	 2. A bamboo.
	 3. The name of a Daitya or de-
mon.
	 4. A porcupine.
	 f. (-ठी) A female tortoise, a small one. E.
कम् to desire, &c. अठ Uṇādi affix, fem. affix. ङीष्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमण्डलु|कमंडलु|कमंडलुः|कमण्डलुः
कमण्डलु mn. (-लुः-लु) An earthen or wooden water pot, used by the
ascetic and religious student.
	 2. The waved-leaf fig tree: see प्लक्ष.
E. क BRAHMĀ or water, and मण्ड ornament or essence, ल from ला
to get or give, and डु aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन|कमनं|कमनः
कमन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)
	 1. Libidinous, desirous.
	 2. Beautiful, desirable.
m. (-नः)
	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.
	 2. KĀMA^1 or love.
	 3. A tree, (Jone-
sia asoca.)
 E. कम् to desire, affix युच् or ल्युट्.
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.
