<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करीका
कर्करीका f. (-का) A small water jar.
 E. कॄ to scatter, in the reiterative
form, and ईक Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेट|कर्करेटं
कर्करेट n. (-टं) The hand curved as a claw or half moon, for the pur-
pose of grasping anything.
 E. कर्कर hard, firm, इट् to go, to be,
affix अप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेटु|कर्करेटुः
कर्करेटु mf. (-टुः-टुः) The numidian crane: see करेटु.
 E. कर्कश hard, &c.
रेट् to sound, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कश|कर्कशः
कर्कश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)
	 1. Violent.
	 2. Hard.
	 3. Intangible.
	 4. Cruel.
	 5.
Unfeeling, unmerciful.
	 6. Harsh, unkind.
	 7. Miserly.
	 m. (-शः)
	 1. A
plant, commonly Sunda rochani, (Crinum?)
	 2. A kind of cassia,
(Cassia esculenta.)
	 3. Sugar-cane.
	 4. A sword, a scymitar.
	 f. (-शी)
Wild jujube; also कर्कशिका.
 E. कॄ to injure, विच् affix, कश with the
same meaning, and अच्, highly injurious: or कर्क a Sautra root,
and श aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

