कर्चूर|कर्चूरः|कर्च्चूरं|कर्च्चूरः
कर्चूर m. (-रः) A plant, (Curcuma reclinata, Rox.)
	 n. (-रं) Gold: see कर्बूर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूरक|कर्चूरकः|कर्च्चूरकः
कर्चूरक m. (-कः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet:) see कर्बूरक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ज|कर्ज्ज
कर्ज r. 1st cl. (कर्जति) To pain or make uneasy.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण r. 10th cl. (कर्णयति) To pierce or bore: with the prefix आङ्, समा,
(सम् and आङ्) or उप, to hear or listen.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण m. (-र्णः)
	 1. The ear.
	 2. KARṆA a prince, sovereign of Angadesha,
and elder brother, by the mother's side, to the Pandu princes,
being the son of SŪRYA by KUNTI, before the marriage with
PĀṆḌU.
	 3. The helm or rudder of a vessel.
	 4. (In prosody,) A
spondee, a foot of two long syllables.
	 5. (In geometry,) The hypo-
thenuse of a triangle, or the diagonal of a tetragon.
	 6. A plant,
(Cassia fistula.)
	 7. A kind of swallow wort, (Colotropis gigantea.)
E. कर्ण to hear, घञ् affix; or कृ to do, &c. न Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकण्डु|कर्णकण्डुः
कर्णकण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) Itching of the ear.
 E. कर्ण, and कण्डु itching.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकीटी
कर्णकीटी f. (-टो)
	 1. An insect or worm with many feet, and of a reddish
colour, (Julus cornifex.)
	 2. A small centipede.
 E. कर्ण the ear, and
कीट an insect, being supposed to attack the ear especially.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णक्ष्वेड|कर्णक्ष्वेडः|कर्ण्णक्ष्वेड
कर्णक्ष्वेड m. (-डः) An affection of the ear, a roaring or constant noise
in it.
 E. कर्ण, and क्ष्वेड a buzzing in the ear.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग
कर्णग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)
	 1. Hanging on the ear, next to the ear.
	 2. Ex-
tending to the ear.
 E. कर्ण, and ग what goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णगूथ|कर्णगूथं|कर्णगूथः
कर्णगूथ m. (-थः) The wax of the ear.
 E. कर्ण, and गूथ fœces, excrement.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णगोचर
कर्णगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Capable of being heard, perceptible to the ear.
E. कर्ण, and गोचर perceptible.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग्राह|कर्णग्राहः
कर्णग्राह m. (-हः) A helmsman.
 E. कर्ण, the helm, and ग्राह who holds.
