कर्त्तुकाम|कर्तुकाम
कर्त्तुकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Desirous or intending to do.
 E. कर्त्तुम् to do, काम
desire, the final of the first rejected.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृ|कर्तृ
कर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)
	 1. An agent, a doer, a maker, one who makes or
does.
	 2. One who practises what he knows.
	 m. (-र्त्ता)
	 1. A name of
BRAHMĀ.
	 2. (In grammar,) The active noun, the nominative case.
E. कृ to do, and तृच् affix: it may also be read कर्तृ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृक|कर्तृक
कर्त्तृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) An agent, one who does anything.
 E. कन् added
to the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृकत्व|कर्तृकत्व
कर्त्तृकत्व n. (-त्वं) Agency, action.
 E. कर्त्तृक, and त्व aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृका|कर्तृका
कर्त्तृका f. (-का) A small sword.
 E. कृत् to cut, कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृत्व|कर्तृत्व|कर्तृत्वं
कर्त्तृत्व n. (-त्वं) Agency, the act or property of an agent.
 E. कर्त्तृ, and त्व
affix; also with तल् affix कर्त्तृता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृवाच्य|कर्तृवाच्य|कर्तृवाच्यः
कर्त्तृवाच्य m. (-च्यः) (In grammar,) The active voice.
 E. कर्त्तृ agent, and
वाच्य to be said.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्र|कर्त्रं
कर्त्र r. 10th cl. (कर्त्रयति) To unloose, to remove: see कर्त्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्री
कर्त्री f. (-र्त्री) A scissors.
 E. कृत् to cut, तृच् and ङीष् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द r. 1st cl. (कर्दति) To grumble, as the bowels; to caw as a crow; or
to make any such noise.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द m. (-र्दः) Mud, clay.
 E. कर्द् to sound ill, अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दट|कर्दटः|कर्द्दट|कर्द्दटः
कर्दट m. (-टः)
	 1. The fibrous root of the lotus.
	 2. Mud, dirt.
	 3. Any
aquatic weed, as Vallisneria, &c.
 E. कर्द mud, and अट what goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दन|कर्दनं|कर्द्दन|कर्द्दनं
कर्दन n. (-नं) Grumbling of the bowels, borborygmi.
 E. कर्द् to make
such noise, and ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दम|कर्दमः|कर्द्दम|कर्द्दमं|कर्द्दमः
कर्दम m. (-मः)
	 1. Mud, mire, clay.
	 2. Sin.
	 3. A Prajāpati, the son of
BRAHMĀ by CHĀYĀ, and the father of Kapila: (this personage
appears to be an innovation in Hindu mythology.)
	 f. (-मी) A plant.
n. (-मं) Flesh.
 E. कर्द् to sound badly, and अम Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमाटक|कर्दमाटकः|कर्द्दमाटक|कर्द्दमाटकः
कर्दमाटक m. (-कः) A receptacle for filth, a sewer, a necessary.
 E. कर्दम
filth, अट to go, and वुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पट|कर्पटं|कर्पटः
कर्पट m. (-टः) Old and patched or ragged garments.
 E. कृप् to be able,
and अटन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटधारिन्
कर्पटधारिन् m. (-री) A religious mendicant, a Fakir, a beggar in patched
or ragged clothes, or sometimes with merely a cloth to cover the
privities.
 E. कर्पट as above, धृ to have, and णिनि affix; also कर्पटिक
and कर्पटिन्.
