कर्म्मकर|कर्मकर|कर्मकरः|कर्म्मकरः
कर्म्मकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)
	 1. A hired laborer.
	 2. A servant of any kind,
(as a pupil, &c.) not a slave.
	 3. An agent, any one who does work or
business.
	 m. (-रः) A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.
	 f. (-री)
	 1.
A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides.) See मूर्ब्बा.
	 2. Bryonia grandis: see
निम्बिका.
	 3. A female servant or slave.
 E. कर्म्म work, act, and कर who
does or performs; also कर्म्मकार.
