कर्म्मकार|कर्मकार|कर्मकारः|कर्म्मकारः
कर्म्मकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)
	 1. A worker, one who does any business, an
artisan, a mechanic.
	 2. One who performs any act.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=162-b" target="_blank">Page162-b+ 60</a>]
blacksmith, one of the progeny of the divine artist VISWAKARMA.
2. A bull.
 E. कर्म्म an act, कृञ् to perform, affix अण्.
