<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्व|कर्व|कर्वः|कर्व्वः
कर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः)
	 1. Love, desire.
	 2. A rat.
 E. कृ to injure, and व Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्वट|कर्वट|कर्वटः|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्व्वट mn. (-टः-टं)
	 1. The capital of a district, (of two or four hundred
villages,) in a pleasant site and of handsome construction, a
market town, &c.
	 n. (-टं) A city.
 E. कर्व्व to be proud, and अटच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्वर|कर्वर|कर्वरः
कर्व्वर m. (-रः)
	 1. A demon or imp.
	 2. A tiger.
	 f. (-री)
	 1. A name of
DURGĀ.
	 2. The leaf of the asafœtida plant: see हिङ्गुपत्री.
 E. कृ to in-
jure, क्वरच् Uṇādi affix; if derived from कर्ब्ब to go, &c. this word is
read कर्ब्बर, but such a reading is probably inaccurate: see कर्ब्बर,
also कर्ब्बुर; it is sometimes considered as a various reading of this
last, meaning, variegated.
