<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ष|कर्षः
कर्ष mn. (-र्षः-र्षं) A weight of gold or silver, a Karṣa equal to sixteen
Mashas; this, according to the ancient division of five Rettis to
the Masha, would make the Karṣa equal to about 176 grains troy;
in common use, eight Rettis are given to the Masha and the Karṣa
is therefore about 280 grains troy: see मास and रक्तिक.
	 m. (-षः)
	 1.
Drawing, dragging, pulling.
	 2. Ploughing.
	 3. Attracting.
	 4. Beleric
myrobalan: see विभीतक.
 E. कृष् to plough, अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. A cultivator of the soil, one who lives by til-
lage.
	 2. What draws or drags.
	 3. Attractive, what attracts.
 E. कृष् to
plough, बुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण n. (-णं)
	 1. Ploughing, cultivating the ground.
	 2. Pulling, drag-
ging.
	 3. Attracting.
 E. कृष् to plough, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणि|कर्षणिः
कर्षणि f. (-णिः) A dishonest woman.
 E. कृष्, and अनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणीय
कर्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)
	 1. To be drawn or pulled.
	 2. To be attracted, to
be conciliated or won.
 E. कृष् to plough, with अनीयर् aff.
