कलायखञ्ज
कलायखञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) One who trembles and totters as he walks.
 E. कलाय,
and खञ्ज a wagtail.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलायन|कलायनः
कलायन m. (-नः) A tumbler, a dancer, but especially one who dances
or walks on a sharp edge, as the edge of a sword. &c.
 E. कला a
part, and अयन going.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलालाप|कलालापः
कलालाप m. (-पः) A bee, &c.
 E. कल buzz, and आलाप speech.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलावत्|कलावन्त्
कलावत् m. (-वान्) A name of Chandra or the moon.
	 f. (-ती)
	 1. A celes-
tial lute or Vina.
	 2. The mother of RĀDHĀ^1.
	 3. An Apsara.
	 4. A
mystical ceremony, initiation of the Tantrika student, in which
the goddess DURGĀ is supposed to be transferred from the water-
jar to the body of the novice.
 E. कला a digit, or कल a sweet tone,
and मतुप् aff.
[1] Correction submitted by 2026-05-15 on Scott Rhodes. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/222.
