कल्किन्
कल्किन् mfn. (-ल्की-ल्किनी-ल्कि)
	 1. Foul, turbid, having sediment.
	 2.
Dirty.
	 3. Wicked.
	 m. (-ल्की) The last descent of VIṢṆU: see the
preceding.
 E. कल्क, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
