कल्पवृक्ष|कल्पवृक्षः
कल्पवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) One of the fabulous trees of INDRA'S heaven; a tree
which yields whatever may be desired.
 E. कल्प purpose, and वृक्ष a
tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पादि|कल्पादिः
कल्पादि m. (-दिः) The beginning of a Kalpa, the renovation of all
things.
 E. कल्प, and आदि beginning.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्त|कल्पांत|कल्पान्तः
कल्पान्त m. (-न्तः) The destruction of the world, the end of the Kalpa,
or four ages of its existence.
 E. कल्प the period, and अन्त the end.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्तस्थायिन्|कल्पांतस्थायिन्
कल्पान्तस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Lasting, permanent.
 E. कल्पान्त, and
स्थायिन् what stays.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पित|कल्पितः
कल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Made, fabricated, artificial.
	 2. Composed, in-
vented.
	 3. Arranged, put in order.
	 4. Prepared at once, put
together extempore.
	 5. Brought, conducted.
	 6. Inferred.
	 m.
(-तः) An elephant armed or caparisoned for war.
 E. कृप् to be able,
&c. क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पितार्घ
कल्पितार्घ mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं) One for whom or what a respectful offering is
prepared.
 E. कल्पित made, and अर्घ an offering.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प्य
कल्प्य mfn. (-ल्प्यः-ल्प्या-ल्प्यं)
	 1. To be made or contrived.
	 2. To be substi-
tuted.
 E. कृप् to be able, यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मष|कल्मषं|कल्मषः
कल्मष mfn. (-षः-षा-शं) Dirty, foul.
	 m. (-षः) A kind of hell, a division of
the infernal regions.
	 n. (-षं)
	 1. Sin.
	 2. The hand bellow the wrist.
E. कर्म्म virtuous or pious action, षो to destroy, and क affix; the
form is irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माष|कल्माषः
कल्माष mfn. (-षः-षा or -षी-षं) Of a mixed or variegated colour.
	 m. (-षः)
1. A variegated colour.
	 2. A mixture of black and white.
	 3. Black.
4. A demon or goblin.
	 f. (-षी) The spotted cow of Jamadagni, the
giver of all desires.
 E. कल् to go, &c. क्विप् affix, कल्, मष् to injure,
अण् affix माष; what injures or triumphs over other colours.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माषकण्ठ|कल्माषकंठ|कल्माषकण्ठः
कल्माषकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A name of ŚIVA.
 E. कल्माष black, and कण्ठ throat;
form irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माषपाद|कल्माषपादः
कल्माषपाद m. (-दः) The name of a king, also SAUDĀSA; transformed
to a Rākṣasa by VASIṢṬHA.
 E. कल्माष, and पाद a foot.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्य|कल्यं|कल्यः
कल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)
	 1. Ready, prepared, armed.
	 2. Healthy, free from
sickness.
	 3. Clever, dexterous.
	 4. Deaf and dumb.
	 5. Auspicious,
(speech or discourse.)
	 6. Counselling, monitory.
	 7. Sound, perfect,
free from mental or bodily imperfections.
	 n. (-ल्यं)
	 1. The dawn or
break of day.
	 2. Yesterday.
	 3. Tomorrow.
	 nf. (-ल्यं-ल्या)
	 1. Spirituous
liquor.
	 2. Congratulation, good wishes, annunciation of good
tidings.
	 f. (-ल्या) Emblic myrobalan: see हरीतकी.
 E. कल् to count,
&c. यक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यजग्धि|कल्यजग्धिः
कल्यजग्धि f. (-ग्धिः) The morning meal, breakfast.
 E. कल्य dawn, and
जग्धि eating.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यत्व|कल्यत्वं
कल्यत्व n. (-त्वं)
	 1. Health.
	 2. Recovery, convalescence.
 E. कल्य being
well, and त्व affix of the abstract; also कल्यता with तल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यपाल|कल्यपालः
कल्यपाल m. (-लः) A distiller.
 E. कल्य vinous liquor, and पाल who
nourishes; also with कन् added, कल्यपालक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यवर्त्त|कल्यवर्त|कल्यवर्तः|कल्यवर्त्तः
कल्यवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Breakfast.
 E. कल्य, and वर्त्त, from वृत् to be or abide,
affix घञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याण|कल्याणं|कल्याणः
कल्याण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Happy, well, right, prosperous, lucky.
	 f. (-णी)
1. A cow.
	 2. A leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)
	 n. (-णं)
	 1.
Good fortune, happiness, prosperity.
	 2. Gold.
 E. कल्य healthy, &c.
अ to be, to sound, अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणकर
कल्याणकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Propitious, auspicious, conferring good
fortune, &c.
 E. कल्याण, and कर what makes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणकृत्
कल्याणकृत् mfn. (-कृत्)
	 1. Virtuous, good.
	 2. Propitious, lucky.
 E. कल्याण,
and कृत् who does.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणचार
कल्याणचार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)
	 1. Following virtuous courses.
	 2. Lucky,
fortunate.
 E. कल्याण, चर् to go, अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणधर्मन्|कल्याणधर्म्मन्
कल्याणधर्मन् mfn. (-र्मा-र्मा-र्म) Good, virtuous.
 E. कल्याण, धर्म duty,
अनिच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणपञ्चमीक
कल्याणपञ्चमीक m. (-कः) A fortnight which has the fifth lunation lucky.
E. कल्याण, पञ्चमी the fifth, and कन् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणवचन
कल्याणवचन n. (-नं) Friendly speech, good wishes.
 E. कल्याण, and वचन
speech.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणवीज|कल्याणवीजः
कल्याणवीज m. (-जः) A sort of pulse, (Ervum hirsutum.)
 E. कल्याण, and
वीज seed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणाचार
कल्याणाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Virtuous, following good practices.
 E. कल्याण,
and आचार rule.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिका
कल्याणिका f. (-का) Red arsenic.
 E. कल्याणी, and कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिन्
कल्याणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)
	 1. Happy, lucky, prosperous.
	 2. Auspici-
ous, propitious.
 E. कल्याण, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यापाल|कल्यापालः
कल्यापाल m. (-लः) A distiller.
 E. कल्या spirituous liquor, and पाल who
preserves.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्युष
कल्युष n. (-षं) The wrist.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल r. 1st cl. (कल्लते)
	 1. To sound ill or indistinctly.
	 2. To sound.
	 3. To
be mute.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Deaf.
 E. कल्ल to sound indistinctly, affix अच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लत्व|कल्लत्वं
कल्लत्व n. (-त्वं)
	 1. Indistinct articulation, hoarseness.
	 2. Deafness.
 E. कल्ल
to sound indistinctly, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix कल्लता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लि
कल्लि ind. To-morrow.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोल|कल्लोलः
कल्लोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) An enemy, hostile, inimical.
	 m. (-लः)
	 1. A surge,
a billow.
	 2. Joy, happiness, pleasure.
 E. कल्ल to sound, ओलच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव
कव(ऋ)ववृ r. 1st cl. (कवते)
	 1. To describe, (as a poet.)
	 2. To paint, to
picture; also कब.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवक|कवकं|कवकः
कवक m. (-कः)
	 1. A mouthful.
	 2. A fungus, a mushroom, &c.
 E. कु to
sound, अक aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवच|कवचं|कवचः
कवच mn. (-चः-चं)
	 1. Armour, mail.
	 2. A drum used in battle, a kettle
drum.
	 3. An amulet, a charm.
	 4. A tree, (Hibiscus populneoides.)
see गर्द्दभाण्ड.
	 3. The mystical syllable Hum, forming part of a
Mantra, and considered as a preservative like armour; it is also
inscribed on a Birch leaf, &c. and worn as an amulet; being car-
ried about the person as a charm: see the next.
 E. कु to sound, अच्
Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचपत्र|कवचपत्रं|कवचपत्रः
कवचपत्र n. (-त्रं) The Birch tree, commonly Bhojpatra: see भूर्जपत्र. E.
कवच an amulet, and पत्र a leaf: see the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचहर|कवचहरः
कवचहर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Wearing armour or amulets.
	 m. (-रः) A boy,
a child.
 E. कवच, and हृ to take, अच् or ट aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवटी
कवटी f. (-टी) A door: see कवाट.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवयी
कवयी f. (-यी) A kind of flat fish, commonly Kavay or Kay; remark-
able for going by land from one spot to another, (Coiuscoboius,
Ham.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवर|कवरं|कवरः
कवर sub.
	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A braid or fillet of hair, adj. (-रः-री-रं)
	 1.
Mixed, intermingled, blended.
	 2. Set, inlaid.
	 mn. (-रः-रं)
	 1. Salt.
	 2.
Sourness or acidity.
	 f. (-रा or -री) A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)
	 f.
(-री) The leaf of the asafœtida plant, Hingupatri.
 E. क the head,
&c. वृ to screen, अच् affix, fem. do. टाप् or ङीष्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरकी
कवरकी f. (-की) A captive, a prisoner: see वन्दी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभार|कवरीभारः
कवरीभार m. (-रः) A fine head of hair.
 E. कवरी, and भार a load; also
कवरीभर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभृत्
कवरीभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Wearing a fillet of hair.
 E. कवरी, and भृत् who has.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवल|कवलं|कवलः
कवल m. (-लः)
	 1. A mouthful.
	 2. A kind of fish, commonly Baliya.
	 3.
An astringent wash for cleaning the mouth, a gargle.
 E. क the
head, water, &c. and वल to be strong, अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिका
कवलिका f. (-का) A piece of cloth over a sore, a bandage.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten
 E. कवल nominal verb, to eat, and क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवस|कवसः
कवस m. (-सः) Armour, mail.
 E. कु to sound, and अस Uṇādi affix; also
कवच.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट sub.
	 mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) A door, the leaf or pannel of the door.
 E. क
wind, air, वट् to exclude, and अण् affix; also कपाट.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटवक्र|कवाटवक्रं
कवाटवक्र n. (-क्रं) A plant, commonly Kapata ventu.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवार|कवारं
कवार m. (-रः)
	 1. A lotus.
	 2. A bird, (Tantalus falcinellus, BUCH.) E.
क water, वर to prefer, अण् aff.
