कस्तूरी
कस्तूरी f. (-री)
	 1. Musk, the animal perfume so called, as brought from
Kashmir, Napal, and western Asam or Bhutan, the latter is said
to be the best.
	 2. A plant, (Hibiscus abelmoschus.)
	 3. Another
plant, (Amaryllis zeylanica.)
 E. कस् to go, and तूरच् affix; its
scent going or spreading; the deriv. is irr.; also कन् being added
कस्तूरिका and कस्तुरिका as above.
