काकमुद्गा
काकमुद्गा f. (-द्गा) A plant, commonly Mugani, according to some, a wild
kind of beam.
 E. काक, and मुद्ग Moong.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकयव|काकयवः
काकयव m. (-वः) Barren corn, the ear of which has no grain.
 E. काक, and
यव barley.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Naked.
	 2. Timid, fearful.
	 3. Poor, indigent.
m. (-कः)
	 1. Fraud, deceit.
	 2. An owl.
	 3. A henpecked husband.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुहा
काकरुहा f. (-हा) A parasite plant, (Epidendrum tesseloides, &c.) see
वन्दा.
 E. काक, and रुह what mounts; on which crows rest.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकल|काकलं|काकलः
काकल n. (-लं) A jewel worn upon neck.
	 f. (-लिः or -ली) A low and
sweet tone, the song of a bird, &c.
 E. का instead of कु diminutive,
कल् to sound, इन् or ङीप् aff.
