काकोल|काकोलं|काकोलः
काकोल mn. (-लः-लं) A poisonous substances of a black colour, or
the colour of a raven, whence its name; possibly the berry of the
Cocculus Indicus.
	 n. (-ल) A division of the infernal regions or
hell.
	 m. (-लः)
	 1. A raven.
	 2. A potter.
	 3. A snake.
	 4. A boar.
5. A drug; as follows.
	 f. (-ली) The name of a vegetable substance
used in medicine, described as sweet and cooling, allaying fever,
removing phlegm, &c.: it it said to be a root brought from Nepal
or Morung.
 E. काक to be unsteady, &c. and ओलच् affix, deriv. irr.
