काचित|काचितं
काचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suspended by a swing or in a loop.
 E. काच a
nominal root, to hang by a loop or in a swing, and क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिम|काचिमः
काचिम m. (-मः) A tree considered as sacred, one growing near a
temple, and an object of religious veneration or worship, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चन|कांचन|काञ्चनं|काञ्चनः
काञ्चन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Golden, of gold.
	 n. (-नं)
	 1. Gold.
	 2. Wealth.
	 3.
A filament of the lotus.
	 m. (-नः)
	 1. Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia
variegata, &c.)
	 2. A tree bearing a yellow fragrant flower,
(Michelia champaca.)
	 3. Another plant, (Mesua ferrea:) see
नागकेसर.
	 4. Glomerous fig-tree: see उडुम्बर.
	 5. Common thorn
apple, (Datura metel.)
	 f. (-नी)
	 1. Turmeric.
	 2. A yellow pigment.
E. कचि to shine, &c. ल्युट् affix, the radical vowel lengthened; this
etymology gives the meaning gold, the others refer to their colour,
&c. in which they resemble the metal.
