कादम्ब|कादंब|कादंबः|कादम्बः
कादम्ब n. (-म्बं)
	 1. A tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)
	 2. A drake, or, accord-
ing to some, a teal.
	 3. An arrow.
	 f. (-म्बा) A plant, commonly
Mundiri: see कदम्बपुष्प.
 E. अण् added to कदम्ब.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बक|कादंबकः|कादम्बकः
कादम्बक m. (-कः) An arrow.
 E. कन् added to the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर|कादंबर|कादंबरं|कादम्बरं|कादम्बरः
कादम्बर n. (-रं) The surface or skim of coagulated milk.
	 m. (-रः) A
spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the Kadamba.
	 f.
(-री)
	 1. Wine, spirituous liquor in general.
	 2. A name of SARAS-
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">Page172-a+ 60</a>]
WATI.
	 3. The female Koil or Indian cuckoo.
	 4. The female of an-
other bird, (Turdus salica, BUCH.)
 E. कदम्ब the Kadamba flower, र
what gains or gets, from रा, affix ड.
