काननारि|काननारिः
काननारि m. (-रिः) The Śami or Śain tree, (Mimosa albida:) see समी.
E. कानन, and अरि enemy; injurious to a wood; being a thorny tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीन|कानीनः
कानीन mf. (-नः-नी) The son or daughter of a young and unmarried
woman.
	 m. (-नः)
	 1. A name of VYASA.
	 2. Also of KARṆA, (being
both born of mothers who were unmarried.)
 E. कन्या a virgin or
young girl, changed to कनीन् and अण् aff.
