कान्त|कांत|कान्तं|कान्तः
कान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)
	 1. Pleasing, agreeable.
	 2. Lovely, beautiful.
3. Dear, beloved.
	 m. (-न्तः)
	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.
	 2. The moon.
3. A husband.
	 4. Spring.
	 5. A precious stone; in which case it is
compounded with सूर्य्य, चन्द्र or अयस्, as सूर्य्यकान्त a crystal lens, &c.
f. (-न्ता)
	 1. A wife, a mistress, any beloved or lovely woman.
2. A plant, commonly Priyangu: see प्रियङ्गु.
	 3. A grass, (Cyperus
pertenuis.)
	 n. (-न्तं)
	 1. Iron.
	 2. Saffron.
 E. कम् to desire, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तता
कान्तता f. (-ता) Loveliness, beauty, splendor.
 E. कान्त pleasing, &c. तल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपक्षिन्|कांतपक्षिन्
कान्तपक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) A peacock.
 E. कान्त beautiful, पक्षिन् a bird.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपुष्प|कान्तपुष्पः
कान्तपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Mountain ebony, &c. (Bauhinia variegata.)
 E. कान्त
and पुष्प flower.
