कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहद m. (-दः) A tree, commonly Asoka, (Jonesia asoca.)
E. कान्ता a woman, अङ्घ्रि a foot, and दोहद desire; the tree being
supposed to blossom upon coming in contact with the foot of a
handsome female.
