कान्दिशीक|कांदिशीक|कान्दिशीकः
कान्दिशीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Flying, running away, put to flight.
 E. कदि
to fear, घञ् and इन् affixed, कन्दि; शीक् to go, to ooze. घञ् affix,
कन्दिशीक; and again, अण् affix, कान्दिशीक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यकुब्ज|कान्यकुब्जं|कान्यकुब्जः
कान्यकुब्ज m. (-ब्जः) A country, the modern Konouj; also कन्याकुब्ज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यजा
कान्यजा f. (-जा) A kind of perfume, commonly Nali.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटिक|कापटिकः
कापटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)
	 1. Wicked, bad, perverse.
	 2. Fraudulent, dis-
honest.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. A student, a scholar.
	 2. A flatterer, a para-
site.
 E. कपट fraud, &c. ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापट्य|कापट्यं
कापट्य n. (-ट्यं) Wickedness, fraud, dishonesty.
 E. कपट, and ष्यञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथ|कापथः
कापथ m. (-थः) A bad road.
 E. का for कु bad, vile, and पथिन् a road.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाल|कापालं|कापालः
कापाल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Cranial, relating to the skull.
	 m. (-लः) A kind
of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)
	 n. (-लं) A sort of leprosy.
E. कपाल, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिक|कापालिकः
कापालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to the skull.
	 m. (-कः)
A worshipper of ŚIVA of the left-hand order, characterised by
carrying a half of the skull as a cup, drinking spirituous liquors,
&c.
 E. कपाल, and ठञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Of a tawny colour.
	 m. (-लः)
	 1. A follower of
the Sankhya system of philosophy.
 E. कपिल the founder of the
school, and अण् affix.
	 2. Tawny, (the colour.)
 E. अण् pleonastic
added to कपिल, q. v.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिश|कापिशं
कापिश n. (-शं) A spirituous liquor, wine.
	 f. (-शी) A country.
 E. कपिश
brown, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशायन|कापिशायनं
कापिशायन m. (-नः)
	 1. A deity.
	 2. A kind of vinous liquor.
	 n. (-नं)
Honey.
	 f. (-नी) A grape.
 E. कपिश brown, or कापिशी a country, and
ष्फक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशेय|कापिशेयः
कापिशेय m. (-यः) A Pisacha, an imp or goblin.
 E. कपिश, and ढक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष|कापुरुषः
कापुरुष m. (-षः) A mean contemptible man, a coward, a wretch.
 E. का
for कु bad, vile, पुरुष a man.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुषत्व
कापुरुषत्व n. (-त्वं) Meanness, cowardliness.
 E. त्व added to the preced-
ing: also with तल्, कापुरुषता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेय|कापेयं|कापेयः
कापेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Belonging to or relating to a monkey.
 E. कपि a
monkey, and ढक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोत|कापोतं|कापोतः
कापोत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Of a dirty white colour.
	 m. (-तः)
	 1. Natron,
fossile alkali.
	 2. Antimony, considered as a collyrium or applica-
tion to the eyes.
	 3. A pale or dirty white colour.
	 n. (-तं) A flock
of pigeons,
 E. कपोत a pigeon, &c. अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोताञ्जन|कापोतांजन|कापोताञ्जनं
कापोताञ्जन n. (-नं) Antimony, especially considered as a collyrium. E.
कापोत a pigeon, and अञ्जन a collyrium.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकर|काप्यकरः
काप्यकर m. (-रः) A penitent, one who acknowledges his faults.
E. का for कु bad, आप्य having obtained, and कर who does; from कृ.
and अच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकार|काप्यकारः
काप्यकार m. (-रः)
	 1. Avowal or confession of sin.
	 2. A penitent, one
who confesses a crime. E. As before, affix अण्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काफल|काफलः
काफल m. (-लः) A bitter seed; see कट्फल.
 E. का bad, and फल fruit.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम|कामं|कामः
काम m. (-मः)
	 1. KĀMA^1 the Hindu Cupid or deity of love.
	 2. Wish,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">Page173-a+ 60</a>]
desire.
	 3. BALARĀMA the brother of KṚṢṆA.
	 4. The mango tree.
f. (-मा) Love, desire.
	 n. (-मं)
	 1. Semen virile.
	 2. An object of desire.
3. Willingly, voluntarily.
	 4. A particle of assent or agreement: see
कामम्. ind. (in composition.) Following one's own desire, as कामवाद
speaking what one lists; कामभक्ष eating whatever one likes; कामचार
doing whatever one chuses; in law, a child previous to the imposi-
tion of the characteristic cord is all these.
 E. कम् to desire, घञ् aff.
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकला
कामकला f. (-ला) RATI the wife of KĀMA^1.
 E. काम, and कला a part.
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
