काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य m. (-व्यः) A name of SUKRACHARYA, the preceptor of the demons.
f. (-व्या)
	 1. Understanding, intelligence.
	 2. A female fiend: see
पूतना.
	 3. A Pitṛ of a particular order, the son of KAVI or SUKRA.
n. (-व्यं) A poem, poetical composition.
 E. कवि a poet, &c. ञ्यत्
derivative or pleonastic aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यचौर|काव्यचौरः
काव्यचौर m. (-रः) A plagiarist.
 E. काव्य a poem, and चौर a thief.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश(ऋ)काशृ r. 1st cl. (काशते) also (उ ऋ) (उकाशृ) r. 4th cl. (काश्यते)
1. To shine. With निर् prefixed. To expel.
	 2. To hide or obscure;
with प्र, To make or become manifest.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश m. (-शः)
	 1. Cough, catarrh: see कास.
	 2. Sneezing.
	 n. (-शं)
	 1. A
species of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)
	 2. Irritation in the
throat.
	 f. (-शी) Kasi or Benares, the holy city so called. (-शी or -शा)
Saccharum spontaneum, as above.
 E. कश् to sound, in the causal
form, अच् affix; or काश् to shine, अच् and ङीष् fem. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
