काशिन्
काशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)
	 1. Having a cold or cough.
	 2. Shining bri-
lliant.
 E. काश cough, and इनि affix, or काश् to shine, णिनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिराज|काशिराजः
काशिराज m. (-जः) A name of DHANWANTARI or DIVODASA, a king of
Benares, and an author of medical works; he is often confound-
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-b" target="_blank">Page180-b+ 60</a>]
ed with his celestial namesake, the physician of the gods.
 E. काशि
the city, and राज a king or ruler; also काशीराज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिल
काशिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Made of kas grass, abounding with it, &c. E.
काश and इल aff.
