काष्ठ|काष्ठं
काष्ठ n. (-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Wood f.
	 1. A quarter or region of the world space.
tract.
	 2. Place, site.
	 3. Limit, boundary.
	 4. A measure of,
time the thirteenth part of a Kala, or eighteen twinkling.
of the eye.
	 5. Excellence, superiority.
	 6. A plant, (Curcum zan-
thorhiza, Rox.)
 E. काश् to shine, Uṇādi affix क्थन् changed to ष, and
थ after ष becomes ठ.
