कुट|कुटं|कुटः
कुट mn. (-टः-टं)
	 1. A water pot.
	 mf. (-टः-टी) A house; also कुटि.
	 m. (-टः)
1. A fort, a strong hold.
	 2. A tree: see कुठ.
	 3. A hammer, a mallet
for breaking small stones.
	 4. A mountain.
	 f. (-टी)
	 1. A kind of
perfume, commonly Mura.
	 2. A bawd, a procuress or go-between.
3. A nosegay, a bundle or tuft of flowers or vegetables.
 E. कुट् to
go crookedly, &c. क aff.
