कुणप|कुणपः
कुणप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Foul smelling, stinking.
	 mn. (-पः-पं)
	 1. A dead
body, a corpse.
	 m. (-पः)
	 1. A stink, a foul smell.
	 2. A spear.
	 f. (-पी)
A small bird, a kind of Maina or Salik: see विट्सारिका.
 E. कृण् to
sound, कपन affix, व is changed to its congener उ; sound proceeding
from the corpse, &c. by the escape of the vital air, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
