कुण्ड|कुंड|कुंडं|कुण्डं|कुंडः|कुण्डः
कुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A son born in adultery, the son of a woman by another
man than her husband, while the husband is alive.
	 n. (-ण्डं)
	 1. A
hole in the ground for receiving and preserving consecrated fire.
2. A pool, a well, a spring of basin of water, especially consecrated
to some holy purpose or person.
	 3. A measure.
	 mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी) A
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">Page187-b+ 60</a>]
pitcher.
	 f. (-ण्डी) A student's water-pot, made of a hollow cocoanut,
&c.
 E. कुडि to preserve, ड aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डकीट|कुंडकीट|कुण्डकीटः
कुण्डकीट m. (-टः)
	 1. A follower of the Charvaka doctrine, or the tenets
of those sects who deny the authority of the Vedas.
	 2. The son of
a woman of the Brahminical tribe born in adultery, particularly
with a man of an inferior caste.
	 3. A keeper of concubines, a man
who has female slaves.
 E. कुण्ड a pool, &c. and कीट a worm, a reptile.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
