<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतश्चित्
कुतश्चित् ind. Somewhere or other.
 E. चित् added to कुतस्
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्
कुतस् ind. Implying interrogation, 1. How, what.
	 2. How, in what
way, how should it be thus, &c. implying denial or concealment
of knowledge.
	 3. Whence, for what place.
 E. कु for किम् what,
and तसिल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्त्य
कुतस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं) Whence come, how happened.
 E. त्यप् added to
the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुक|कुतुकं
कुतुक n. (-कं)
	 1. Eagerness, vehemence.
	 2. Desire, inclination.
	 3.
Curiosity.
 E. कुत a particular sound, कै to emit sound, ड affix; also
कौतुक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुप|कुतुपं|कुतुपः
कुतुप m. (-पः) A small leathern oil bottle.
	 mn. (-पः-पं) The eighth hour of
of the day: see कुतप
 E. कुतु as below, and उपच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतू
कुतू f. (-तूः) A leathern oil bottle.
 E. कु bad, and तन् to spread, डु affix,
and the final lengthened.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूणक|कुतूणकः
कुतूणक m. (-कः) Weakness of the eyes in infants; also read कुकूणक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)
	 1. Excellent, best, praised, celebrated.
	 2. Sur-
prising, wonderful.
	 n. (-लं)
	 1. Eagerness, vehemence, impetuosity.
	 2.
Desire, inclination.
	 3. Curiosity.
 E. कु bad तूल् to send forth, क affix,
and ह inserted; or कुतू an oil bottle, and हल् to make limes or
furrows; or कु the earth, and तुद् to vex or tease; the etymologies
however are all fanciful; the word is also written कौतूहल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहलिन्
कुतूहलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)
	 1. Curious, inquisitive.
	 2. Eager, impatient.
E. कुतूहल, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतृण|कुतृणं
कुतृण n. (-णं) An aquatic plant, water-house leek, (Pistia stratiotes.) E.
bad, तृण grass.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्र
कुत्र ind. Where, wherein, in what place.
 E. कु substituted for किं what,
and त्रल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रचित्
कुत्रचित् ind. Somewhere.
 E. चित् added to कुत्र.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रापि
कुत्रापि ind. Wherever, somewhere.
 E. कुत्र, and अपि certainly.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स
कुत्स r. 10th cl. (कुत्सयते-ति) To despise, to abuse, to revile.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सन|कुत्सनं
कुत्सन n. (-नं) Abuse, contempt, reproach, reviling.
 E. कुत्स to revile, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सला
कुत्सला f. (-ला) The indigo plant: see नीली.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सा
कुत्सा f. (-त्सा) Reproach, contempt, censure.
 E. कुत्स् to despise, अङ् and
टाप् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सावादीन्
कुत्सावादीन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Censorious, abusive.
 E. कुत्सा and वादिन्
who speaks.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सित|कुत्सितं|कुत्सितः
कुत्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Low, vile, contemptible, contemned, reviled, &c.
n. (-तं) A grass. (Cyperus.)
 E. कुत्स् to reproach. &c., and क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ r. 4th cl. (कुथ्यति) To stink. r. 9th cl. (कुथ्नाति)
	 1. To be distressed;
see कुन्थ(इ)कुथि r. 1st cl. (कुन्थति)
	 1. To hurt or kill.
	 2. To afflict,
to give pain.
	 3. To be afflicted, to suffer pain.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
