<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपङ्क
कुपङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A slough, a heap of filth and mud.
 E. कु vile, पङ्क mud.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपत
कुपत ind. Excellently.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ|कुपथः
कुपथ n. (-थं)
	 1. A bad road.
	 2. Immorality, profligacy.
	 3. Heterodox
doctrine.
 E. कु bad, and पथिन् a road; also कापथ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथगामिन्
कुपथगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Wicked, going in a bad or wrong read. E.
कुपथ, and गामिन् who goes; also कुपथग, कृपथचर, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ्य
कुपथ्य mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)
	 1. Relating to a bad road, literally or figurative-
ly.
	 2. Counterindicated, improper, unwholesome, (as regimen, &c.)
E. कु and पथ्य proper, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपाणि|कुपाणिः
कुपाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Crooked-handed, having a deformed or maimed
hand.
 E. कु bad and पाणि, the hand.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपित
कुपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Incensed, angry, offended.
 E. कुप् to be angry,
क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितवायु|कुपितवायुः
कुपितवायु m. (-युः) Flatulence or hypochondria.
 E. कुपित, and वायु wind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितान्तक
कुपितान्तक m. (-कः) Imminent or threatening death.
 E. कुपित, and अन्तक
destroyer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनिन्
कुपिनिन् m. (-नी) A fisherman
 E. कुपिनी a net, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनी
कुपिनी f. (-नी) A kind of net or snare, for catching small fish, made of
bamboos or rushes,
 E. गुप् to cover or conceal, इनि and ङीष् affixes;
ग is changed to क.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिन्द|कुपिंद|कुपिंदः|कुपिन्दः
कुपिन्द m. (-न्दः) A weaver.
 E. कुप् or कुय् to spread out, किन्दच् Uṇādi
affix; also कुविन्द.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपीलु|कुपीलुः
कुपीलु m. (-लुः) A sort of ebony tree
 E. कु bad, पीलु a tree, so called.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुत्र|कुपुत्रः
कुपुत्र m. (-त्रः)
	 1. A son of an inferior degree, as one adopted, &c.
	 2. A
disobedient or wicked son.
 E. कु, and पुत्र a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुरुष|कुपुरुषः
कुपुरुष m. (-षः)
	 1. A low or vile man.
	 2. A poltroon.
 E. कु bad, and पुरुष
a man.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपूय|कुपूयः
कुपूय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Inferior, low, vile.
 E. कु bad, and पूय् to divide, अच्
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्य|कुप्यं
कुप्य n. (-प्यं) Base metal, copper, brass, &c. or any metal except gold
and silver.
 E. गुप् to conceal or preserve, क्यप् affix; ग is changed
irregularly to क.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यशाला
कुप्यशाला f. (-ला) A braziery, a foundery, a place where metallic vessels,
&c. are made or sold.
 E. कुप्य base metal, शाला a dwelling, a shop,
&c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्रिय|कुप्रियः
कुप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Low, vile, last, worst.
 E. कु reverse, and प्रिय be-
loved; disagreeable.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्लव|कुप्लवः
कुप्लव m. (-वः) A weak or frail raft or float.
 E. कु, and प्लव a raft.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब
कुब r. 1st and 10th cls. (इ) कुबि (कुम्बति कुम्बयति) To cover, to hide, to
clothe, to screen, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेर|कुबेरः
कुबेर m. (-रः) The deity KUVERA: see कुवेर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं) Humpbacked, crooked.
	 m. (-ब्जः)
	 1. A tree,
(Achyranthes aspera:) see अपामार्ग.
	 2. A scymitar.
	 3. A sort of fish.
(Bola cuja, HAM.)
 E. कु the earth, or कु ill badly, and उब्ज् to be
straight, affix अच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जक|कुब्जकः
कुब्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Humpbacked.
	 m. (-कः) An aquatic plant, (Trapa
bispinosa:) see वारिकण्टक.
 E. क water, and उब्ज् to be straight, affix
अच्, and कन् added, or कुब्ज and कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जकण्टक|कुब्जकण्टकः
कुब्जकण्टक m. (-कः) A white mimosa.
 E. कुब्ज, and कण्टक a thorn.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव्र
कुव्र n. (-व्रं)
	 1. A forest.
	 2. A hole for sacrificial fire.
	 3. An ear-ring.
	 4.
A thread.
	 5. A cart.
 E. कुवि to hide, रक् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्रह्म|कुब्रह्मः
कुब्रह्म m. (-ह्मः) A degraded or contemptible Brahman, one who officiates
for Śūdras.
 E. कु bad, ब्रह्मन् a Brahman, टच् affix; also retaining the
final, कुव्रह्मन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभ
कुभ r. 10th cl. (इ) कुभि (कुम्भयति) To cover, to clothe, to veil or hide:
see कुब.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार r. 10th cl. (कुमारयति) To play, especially as a child also कुमाल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार m. (-रः)
	 1. A boy, one under five years of age.
	 2. A name of
KARTIKEYA.
	 3. A prince, the heir apparent, and who is associated
to the empire, (in theatrical language.)
	 4. A horse-man, a caval-
ier.
	 5. A parrot.
	 6. One of the attendants on the twenty-four Jinas,
and also a sanctified character amongst the Jaina sect.
	 7. A tree,
(Tapia cratæva) see वरुण 8. A name of Sindhu river or Indus.
	 n.
(-रं) Pure gold.
	 f. (-री)
	 1. A young girl, one from ten to twelve
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">Page189-b+ 60</a>]
years old, a virgin: or in the Tantras any virgin to the age of
sixteen, or as long as menstruation has not commenced.
	 2. A
name of DURGĀ.
	 3. The central part of the universe according to
Hindu geography, Jambu Dwipa or India.
	 4. The most southerly
of the nine portions of the known continent, or of Jambu Dwipa,
the southern extremity of the peninsula, whence Cape Comorin
or Kumari.
	 5. The name of a river flowing from the mountain
Sactiman.
	 6. A plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see अपराजिता.
	 7. Double
jasmine.
	 8. The aloe tree, (Aloes perfoliata:) see घृतकुमारी.
	 9. The
Syama, a bird so named.
 E. कुमार to play as a child, affix अच् fem.
affix ङीष्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारक|कुमारकः
कुमारक m. (-कः)
	 1. A boy, a lad.
	 2. A tree: see वरुण.
 E. कन् added to
the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारघातिन्
कुमारघातिन् m. (-ती) The slayer of a child.
 E. कुप्तार, हन् to kill, णिनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारपाल|कुमारपालः
कुमारपाल m. (-लः)
	 1. A name of Raja SALIVAHANA.
	 2. Name of a king
of Guzerat.
 E. कुमार a child, and पाल a cherisher.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारभृत्या
कुमारभृत्या f. (-त्या) Care of a pregnant or lying-in woman, midwifery. E.
कुमार a child, and भृत्या cherishing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारयु|कुमारयुः
कुमारयु m. (-युः) A prince.
 E. कुमार prince, या to go or be, and उ Uṇādi
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारवाहिन्
कुमारवाहिन् m. (-ही) A peacock.
 E. कुमार KARTIKEYA, and वाहिन् what
bears; this god being usually represented riding on a peacock.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारसू
कुमारसू f. (-सूः) A name of GANGA, the river goddess.
 E. कुमार the god
KARTIKEYA, and मू a mother.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिका
कुमारिका f. (-का)
	 1. A girl from ten to twelve years old, or generally a
virgin.
	 2. Double jasmine.
	 3. A division of the known continent.
4. Large cardamoms.
	 5. An insect, (Spex Asiatica:) see कुमारी,
कन् being added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमाल
कुमाल r. 10th cl. (कुमालयति) To play as a child, &c. see कुमार.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमालक|कुमालकः
कुमालक m. (-कः) The name of a district, part of Malwa: also termed
Sauvira.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्
कुमुद् mfn. (-त् or -द्)
	 1. Niggardly, avaricious.
	 2. Unkind, unfriendly.
n. (-त् or -द्)
	 1. The esculent white water lily.
	 2. The red lotus. E.
कु the earth, or bad, vile, मुद् to be pleased, and क्विप् affix; also
कुमुद.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद|कुमुदं|कुमुदः
कुमुद n. (-दं)
	 1. The white esculent water lily, (Mymphæa escu-
lenta.)
	 2. The red lotus, (Nrubra.)
	 3. silver.
	 m. (-दः)
	 1. The ele-
phant of the south-west quarter.
	 2. One of the monkey heroes of
the Rāmāyaṇa.
	 3. One of the Naga or serpent race.
	 4. A Danava
or infernal deity.
	 5. Camphor.
	 f. (-दा)
	 1. An aquatic plant, (Pistia
stratiotes.)
	 2. A tree, (Gmelina arborea:) see गम्भारी. (-दी) A medi-
cinal and aromatic shrub, commonly Kayaphal.
 E. कु the earth
&c. मुद् to be pleased, and क aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदबान्धव|कुमुदबांधव|कुमुदबान्धवः
कुमुदबान्धव m. (-वः) The moon.
 E. कुमुद a lotus, and बान्धव the friend;
the white esculent lotus expanding its petals during the night,
and closing them in the day time; hence other similar appella-
tions of the moon, as कुमुदबन्धु, कुमुदप्रिय, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदवती
कुमुदवती f. (-ती) A place abounding in water lilies, &c. see कुमुद्वती.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदाकर|कुमुदाकरः
कुमुदाकर m. (-रः) A number of water lilies or place abounding with
them.
 E. कुमुद, and आकर a mine; also कुमुदवनं, कुमुदिनी, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदावास|कुमुदावासः
कुमुदावास m. (-सः) A pool abounding in lotuses.
 E. कुमुद, and आवास a
residence.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिक
कुमुदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Abounding with water lilies.
 E. कुमुद, and
ठच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिका
कुमुदिका f. (-का) A small tree, the seeds of which are aromatic, com-
monly Kayaphal: see कुमुदी, and कट्फल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनी
कुमुदिनी f. (-नी) A place abounding in lotuses, &c. see कुमुद्वती.
 E. कुमुद,
इनि and ङीष् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनीपति|कुमुदिनीपतिः
कुमुदिनीपति m. (-तिः) The moon.
 E. कुमुदिनी, and पति lord: see कुमुदबान्धव.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदेश|कुमुदेशः
कुमुदेश m. (-शः) The moon: see कुमुदबान्धब.
 E. कुमुद, and ईश a master.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्वत्|कुमुद्वन्त्
कुमुद्वत् mfn. (-द्वान्-द्वती-द्वत्) A place abounding in the flowers of the
Nymphæa esculenta.
	 f. (-ती)
	 1. The same.
	 2. A multitude of lotus
flowers.
	 3. The flexible stalk of a water lily.
	 4. A sort of water
lily, (Menyanthes Indica or cristata.)
 E. कुमुद the water lily, and
मतुप् poss. affix, or वति affix of comparison, fem. ङीष्.
