कुल्माष|कुल्माषं|कुल्माषः
कुल्माष mn. (-षः-षं) Sour gruel prepared by the spontaneous fermenta-
tion of the water of boiled rice.
	 n. (-षं)
	 1. Half ripe barley.
	 2.
Forced rice.
	 3. A sort of Phaseolus: see राजमाष.
	 4. A species of
Dolichos, (D. beflorus.) See यावक.
	 5. A disease.
	 m. (-षः) A dish
consisting of half boiled rice, with pulse, &c. commonly Khichri. E.
कुल a class or race, मष् or मस् to hurt or kill, अण् affix; hence the
word is also written कुल्मास.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

