कुशाङ्गुरीय|कुशांगुरीय
कुशाङ्गुरीय n. (-यं) A ring of Kusa grass, worn at religious ceremonies. E.
कुश, and अङ्गुरीय a ring; also कुशाङ्गुरीयकं.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाल्मलि|कुशाल्मलिः
कुशाल्मलि m. (-लिः) A tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)
 E. कु and शाल्मलि silk-cotton tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशारणि|कुशारणिः
कुशारणि m. (-णिः) The name of a sage celebrated for his irascibility:
see दुर्व्वासा.
 E. कुश the grass, and अरणि wood whose attrition pro-
duces fire; using Kusa for this purpose.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशासन
कुशासन n. (-नं) A seat of Kusa grass.
 E. कुश, and आसन a seat.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिंशपा
कुशिंशपा f. (-पा) A kind of Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)
 E. कु inferior, and
शिंशपा the Sisu tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिक|कुशिकः
कुशिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Squint-eyed.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. A Muni or divine sage
so named, the father of JAMADAGNI.
	 2. A ploughshare.
	 3. The Sal
tree, (Shorea robusta.)
	 4. Beleric myrobalan: see विभीतक.
	 5. The
sediment of oil.
 E. कुश the grass, &c. इकन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशित|कुशितं
कुशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Mixed, combined with water, &c.
 E. कुश् or कुष to
embrace, to mix, and इतच् Uṇādi affix; hence also कुषित.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिन्
कुशिन् m. (-शी) A name of VALMIKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa.
 E. कुश
the son of RAMA, affix इनि; the poem is supposed to be recited by
KUSA, and LAVA, the sons of the hero.
