कूप|कूपः
कूप m. (-पः)
	 1. A well.
	 2. A hole, a hollow.
	 3. A mast.
	 4. A tree or rock
in the midst of a river.
	 f. (-पी)
	 1. A small well.
	 2. The navel.
	 3. A
flask, a bottle.
 E. कु to sound, (frogs croaking in a well, &c.) and
प Uṇādi affix: the vowel is made long; also कूपक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपक|कूपकः
कूपक m. (-कः)
	 1. The mast of a vessel.
	 2. A stake, &c. to which a boat
is moored.
	 3. A leather oil vessel.
	 4. The hollow below the loins.
5. A funeral pile.
	 6. A well.
	 7. A temporary well, a hole dug for
water in the dry bed of a rivulet.
	 8. A tree or rock in the middle
of a stream.
 E. कन् added the preceding.
