कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र mfn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रा-च्छ्रं)
	 1. Attended with pain, painful.
	 2. Wicked,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=198-a" target="_blank">Page198-a+ 60</a>]
sinful.
	 mn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रं) Bodily pain. Penance, expiation.
	 3. Sin.
	 4.
difficulty, labour, trouble.
	 5. A kind of religious penance, accord-
ing to some, the same as the Prajapatya: see प्राजापत्य; (according
to others, as the Santapana: (see सान्तपन.)
 E. कृत् to cut, रक् Uṇādi
affix, and छ substituted for the final.
