कृत्ति|कृत्तिः
कृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)
	 1. The hide upon which the religious student sits, sleeps,
&c. usually the skin of an antelope.
	 2. The skin.
	 3. The bark of
the Bhūrjpatra, used for writing upon, for making hooka snakes,
&c.
	 4. One of the lunar mansions: see the next.
 E. कृत् to cut, क्तिन्
aff.
