<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यविधि|कृत्यविधिः
कृत्यविधि f. (-धिः) The way to do anything, a rule or precept.
 E. कृत्य, and
विधि rule.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Made, factitious, artificial, the reverse of what is
naturally or spontaneously produced.
	 m. (-मः)
	 1. Incense, olibanum.
2. An adopted son, used for कृत्रिमपुत्र.
	 n. (-मं) A kind of salt, the
common Bit Noban or Bit Lavan.
 E. कृ to make, क्त्रि Uṇādi affix,
and मम् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमधूप|कृत्रिमधूपः
कृत्रिमधूप m. (-पः) A compound perfume, containing ten or eighteen in-
gredients.
 E. कृत्रिम artificial, and धूप resin; also with कन् added
कृत्रिमधूपक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्र|कृत्रिमपुत्त्रः|कृत्रिमपुत्रः
कृत्रिमपुत्र m. (-त्रः) An adopted son; one of the twelve kinds recognized
in law, the son made.
 E. कृत्रिम, and पुत्र a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिममित्र|कृत्रिममित्रः
कृत्रिममित्र m. (-त्रः) An acquired friend; one on whom benefits have
been conferred, or from whom they have been received.
 E. कृत्रिम
made, and मित्र a friend; also similar compounds in this or other
senses, कृत्रिमशत्रु an acquired enemy, कृत्रिमौदासीन one who is indiffer-
ent to benefits or injuries, neither an acquired friend nor foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वा
कृत्वा ind. Having done, made, &c.
 E. कृ to do, क्त्वाच् aff.
