कृश|कृशः
कृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)
	 1. Small, thin, tittle, minute.
	 2. Thin, spare,
emaciated.
	 3. Weak, feeble.
 E. कृश् to pare or make thin, क्त affix,
deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशता
कृशता f. (-ता) Leanness, thinness.
 E. तल् added to the last; also with
त्व, कृशत्वं.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशर|कृशरः
कृशर mf. (-रः-रा)
	 1. A dish composed of milk, sesamum, and rise.
	 2.
Rice and pease boiled together with a few spices, commonly
Khichree: also कृसर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशला
कृशला f. (-ला) The hair of the head.
 E. कृश minute, ल what receives.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाकु
कृशाकु m. (-कुः)
	 1. Heating.
	 2. Grieving.
 E. कृश् to make small, and काकु
aff.
