<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशाकेशि
केशाकेशि n. (-शि) Pulling the hair mutually, hair to hair.
 E. केश hair,
repeated, affix इञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्त|केशांत|केशान्तः
केशान्त m. (-न्तः)
	 1. Cutting off the hair finally as a religious ceremony,
performed upon Brahmans at sixteen years of age; Kṣatriyas at
twenty-two; and Vaiśyas at twenty-four.
	 2. The tip or end of hair.
E. केश and अन्त end.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्तिक
केशान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)
	 1. Extending to the hair.
	 2. Relating to the
ceremony of final tonsure.
 E. केशान्त, and ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशारि|केशारिः
केशारि m. (-रिः) A tree, (Mesua ferrea.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशावमर्षण
केशावमर्षण n. (-णं) Pulling the hair, especially amorously, playing with
it, rubbing it, &c.
 E. केश the hair, अव implying improperly, and
मर्षण rubbing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिक|केशिकः
केशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)
	 1. Having fine or luxuriant hair.
	 2. Relating to
the hair.
 E. केश hair. ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिन्
केशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Having fine hair.
	 m. (-शी)
	 1. A name of
VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.
	 2. The name of a Daitya or demon killed by
KṚṢṆA.
	 3. A lion.
	 f. (-शिनी)
	 1. A kind of grass, (Andropogon
aculeatum.)
	 2. Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)
 E. केश hair,
इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिसूदन|केशिसूदनः
केशिसूदन m. (-नः) A name of KṚṢṆA.
 E. केशि a demon, सूदन destroyer
also similar compounds, as केशिहन्, केशिनिसूदन, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिहन्
केशिहन् m. (-हा) See the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशोच्चय|केशोच्चयः
केशोच्चय m. (-यः) Much or handsome hair.
 E. केश hair, उच्चय heap, abundance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसर|केसरं|केसरः
केसर mn. (-रः-रं) A filament.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A lion.
	 2. A horse.
	 3. The name
of a horse or lion, &c., see केशर.
	 4. A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)
	 5.
A tree used in dying, (Rottleria Tinctoria.)
	 nf. (-रं-री) Asafœtida.
n. (-रं)
	 1. Gold.
	 2. Sulphate of iron.
	 3. The flower of the Nageswar.
E. के on the head, सृ to go, ट aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरवर|केसरवरं
केसरवर n. (-रं) Saffron.
 E. केसर and वर best.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसराम्ल|केसराम्लः
केसराम्ल m. (-म्लः) A citron.
 E. केसर, and अम्ल sour.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिन्
केसरिन् m. (-री)
	 1. A lion.
	 2. A horse.
	 3. A plant used in dying: see
पुन्नाग.
	 4. Nageswar, (Mesua ferrea.)
	 5. A monkey the father of
HANUMAN.
 E. केसर a filament, a mane, इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिसुत|केसरिसुतः
केसरिसुत m. (-तः) The monkey HANUMAN.
 E. केसरि, and सुत son कै r.
1st cl. (कायति) To sound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैकेयी
कैकेयी f. (-यी) One of the wives of DAŚARATHA, and the mother of
BHARATA.
 E. केकय a king, father of this lady, and ढक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैङ्कर्य्य|कैङ्कर्य|कैंकर्यं|कैङ्कर्य्यं
कैङ्कर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Service, servitude.
 E. किङ्कर a servant, and ष्यञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभ|कैटभः
कैटभ m. (-भः) A demon slain by VIṢṆU.
	 f. (-भा) A name of DURGĀ.
E. कैटभ a demon in whose death the goddess was instrumental,
by having at the prayers of BRAHMĀ roused VIṢṆU from his
slumbers, during which two demons, Kaitabha and Madhu, were
about to demolish BRAHMĀ; also कैटभी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभजित्
कैटभजित् m. (-जित्) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. कैटभ the name of an Asur
killed by the deity, and जित् who conquers; also similar com-
pounds, as कैटभहन्, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभारि|कैटभारिः
कैटभारि m. (-रिः) A name of VIṢṆU: see कैटभजित्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटर्य्य|कैटर्य|कैटर्यः|कैटर्य्यः
कैटर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A plant used in medicine, commonly Kayaphal.
	 2.
The Nimb tree.
	 3. Mayana, (Vangueria spinosa.)
 E. कैटर from किट्
to fear, and रा to cause, alarming by its pungency; pleonastic
affix ष्यञ्; also कैडर्य्य.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतव|कैतवं|कैतवः
कैतव n. (-वं)
	 1. Deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery.
	 2. Gambling 3. The
lapis lazuli.
 E. कितव a cheat, &c. अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतवप्रयोग|कैतवप्रयोगः
कैतवप्रयोग m. (-गः) A trick, a device.
 E. कैतव and प्रयोग application.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतववाद|कैतववादः
कैतववाद m. (-दः) Evasion, falsehood.
 E. कैतव and वाद speech.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार|कैदारं|कैदारः
कैदार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Belonging to a field, a meadow, &c.
	 m. (-रः) Rice,
corn.
	 n. (-रं) A multitude of fields.
 E. केदार a field, and अण् affix;
also कैदारक, and कैदारिक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदारक|कैदारकं
कैदारक n. (-कं) A multitude of fields.
 E. केदार, and वुञ् affix; also with
ठञ् affix कैदारिक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार्य्य|कैदार्य|कैदार्य्यं
कैदार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्यी-र्य्यं) Belonging to a field, &c.
	 n. (-र्य्यं) A number
of fields.
 E. केदार and ष्यञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरव|कैरवं|कैरवः
कैरव m. (-वः)
	 1. A rogue, a cheat.
	 2. An enemy.
	 f. (-वी) Moonlight.
	 n.
(वं)
	 1. The white esculent water lily.
	 2. Fraud, trick.
 E. केरव here
said to mean, a goose, from के in water, and रु to sound, with अप्
affix; again, अण् affix, liked by the geese; or किरव a cheat, &c. or
कैरव a lotus, and अण् affix, implying identity or resemblance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविणी
कैरविणी f. (-णी) A place abounding in lotus flowers, or an assemblage
of lotuses.
 E. कैरव a white lotus, इनि and ङीष् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविन्
कैरविन् m. (-वी) The moon.
 E. कैरवी moonlight, इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैराटक|कैराटकः
कैराटक m. (-कः) A species ef poison, one of the fixed kinds.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरात|कैरातं|कैरातः
कैरात n. (-तं)
	 1. A sort of gentian, commonly Cherayta, (Gentiana
cherayta, Rox)
	 2. A kind of Sandal.
	 m. (-तः) A strong man. E.
किरात gentian, &c. अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैल|कैलं
कैल n. (-लं) Sport, pleasure.
 E. केलि, and अञ् pleonasm.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलास|कैलासः
कैलास m. (-सः) The mountain Kailasa, the fabulous residence of KUVERA,
and favourite haunt of ŚIVA; it is placed by the Hindus amongst
the Himālaya mountains, and the name is given to one of the lof-
tiest peaks lying on the north of the Manasa lake.
 E. कैलास crys-
tal, and the affix अण् implying nature or consistence; or कैल plea-
sure, आस् to abide, affix यञ्; the place where beings reside in
bliss.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलासनिकेतन|कैलासनिकेतनः
कैलासनिकेतन m. (-नः)
	 1. ŚIVA.
	 2. KUVERA.
 E. कैलास, and निकेतन dwell-
ing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलासौकस्
कैलासौकस् m. (-काः) A name of KUVERA.
 E. कैलास the mountain, औकस्
abode; whose abode is mount Kailasa.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्त|कैवर्त|कैवर्तः|कैवर्त्तः
कैवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A fisherman born of a prostitute by a Kṣatriya, or of
an Ayogava female by a Nisada father.
	 f. (-र्त्ती) The wife of a
fisherman.
 E. क water, the seventh case, के and वर्त्त who abides,
केवर्त्त a fish, अण् affix, implying enmity.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तक|कैवर्तक|कैवर्तकः
कैवर्त्तक m. (-कः) See the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तमुस्त|कैवर्तमुस्त|कैवर्त्तमुस्तं
