क्रुड
क्रुड r. 6th cl. (क्रुडति)
	 1. To sink.
	 2. To be childish.
	 3. To eat.
	 4. To
be thick.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुद्ध|क्रुद्धः
क्रुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)
	 1. Angry, wrathful.
	 2. Fierce, cruel.
	 n. (-द्धं) Anger.
E. क्रुध् to be angry, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध
क्रुध (औ, ऌ) औक्रुधॢ r. 4th cl. (क्रुध्यति) To be wrathful, to be flushed
with anger.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध
क्रुध f. (-क्रुत् or -क्रुद्) Anger, passion.
 E. क्रुध् to be angry, affix क्विप्; also
with अङ and टाप् affixes, क्रुधा.
