<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशित|क्लिशितः
क्लिशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distrest, afflicted, wearied,
 E. क्लिश to be distressed,
&c. affix क्त with इट inserted; also without इट्, क्लिष्ट.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशितवत्
क्लिशितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Suffering pain or distress.
 E. क्लिश, and क्तवतु aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्ट|क्लिष्टः
क्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Distressed, afflicted, &c.
	 2. Inconsistent, contra-
dictory.
 E. क्लिश् to be distressed, &c. affix क्त, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्टि|क्लिष्टिः
क्लिष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)
	 1. Calamity, distress.
	 2. Service.
 E. क्लिश् to afflict, क्तिन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतक
क्लीतक n. (-कं) Liquorice, (Glycirrbiza glabra)
 E. क्लीव् to be weak, affix
क्त, व being dropped; क्लीत weakness, कल् to remove, and ल drop-
ped by affixing ड.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतकिक
क्लीतकिक f. (-का) The indigo plant, (Indigofera Indica.)
 E. क्रीतक traffic,
कन् pleonastic, the fem. form; र is changed to ल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव (ऋ) क्लीवृ r. 1st. cl. (क्लीवते)
	 1. To be impotent.
	 2. To be timorous,
to be modest or unassuming.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव (ऋ) क्लीवृ r. 1st cl. (क्लीवते)
	 1. To be impotent.
	 2. To be timid or
modest.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)
	 1. Weak, impotent.
	 2. Idle, slothful.
	 mn. (-वः-वं)
1. The neuter gender.
	 2. A eunuch.
 E. क्लीव् to be weak or timid,
affix क; also read क्लीवक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेद|क्लेदः
क्लेद n. (-दं)
	 1. Wetness, dampness, moisture, &c.
	 2. Running, discharge
from a sore.
 E. क्लिद् to be wet, affix घञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदक|क्लेदकः
क्लेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Wetting, moistening, making wet or moist.
	 m.
(-कः) Phlegm in the stomach, excess of saliva.
 E. क्लिद् to be wet,
causal form, वुन् aff.
