क्वाथ m. (-थः)
	 1. A decoction, any solution or infusion prepared with a
continued and gentle heat.
	 2. Pain, sorrow.
	 3. Calamity, distress.
4. The mixture of the materials for a decoction.
 E. क्वथ to decoct,
घञ् aff.
