क्षुद्र|क्षुद्रः
क्षुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)
	 1. Small, little.
	 2. Mean, low.
	 3. Mean, niggardly,
avaricious.
	 4. Cruel.
	 5. Poor, indigent.
	 f. (-द्रा)
	 1. A woman maim-
ed or crippled, wanting a limb, &c.
	 2. A dancing girl.
	 3. A whore,
a harlot.
	 4. A fly.
	 5. A bee or wasp.
	 6. A gnat, &c.
	 7. A prickly
nightshade: see कण्टकारी.
	 8. The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)
9. Sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)
 E. क्षुद् to bruise or pound, Uṇādi
affix रक्.
