खल|खलं|खलः
खल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)
	 1. Low, vile. base.
	 2. Low, inferior.
	 3. Cruel.
mischief-making.
	 4. Bad, wicked.
	 mn. (-लः-लं)
	 1. Earth, mould or
soil.
	 2. Place, site.
	 3. Sediment, deposit of oil, &c.
	 4. A granary,
a threshing floor.
	 5. A mill.
	 m. (-लः)
	 1. The sun.
	 2. A tree with
black blossoms: see तमाल.
	 3. The Dhatura plant.
 E. खल् to gather,
(misfortune, &c.) affix अच्.
