	 2. An ascetic, a penitent, 3. A pauper, E.
खिद् to suffer pain, किरच् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद्यमान|खिद्यमानः
खिद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Suffering pain or distress.
 E. खिद्, with शानच्
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद्र|खिद्रः
खिद्र m. (-द्रः)
	 1. Disease, sickness.
	 2. A pauper, a poor man
 E. खिद् to be
in pain, रक् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिन्न|खिन्नः
खिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)
	 1. Distrest, suffering pain or uneasiness.
	 2. Weari-
ed, exhausted.
 E. खिद् to be pain, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिल|खिलं|खिलः
खिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)
	 1. Waste or unploughed land.
	 2. Empty, vacant.
m. (-लः)
	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.
	 2. VIṢṆU.
	 mn. (-लः-लं) A com-
pendium, a compilation, especially of hymns and prayers.
 E. ख
vacuity, &c. ल what gets or possesses, affix ड, and इ substituted
for the penultimate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खु
खु (ङ) खुङ् r. 1st cl. (खुवते) To sound.
