<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन|गलनं
गलन n. (-नं)
	 1. Melting, fusing.
	 2. Trickling, dropping, oozing.
	 3. Fall-
ing. down or off.
	 4. Leaking.
 E. गल् to drop, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलनीय
गलनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fusible, liquefiable, to be melted, &c.
 E. गल् to
melt, अनीयर् affix; also गलितव्य and गल्य.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन्तिका|गलंतिका
गलन्तिका f. (-का)
	 1. A small pitcher.
	 2. A small water jar with small
holes in the bottom, from which the water drops upon a Linga
or Tulasi plant, placed beneath.
 E. गड् to drop, affix झच्, गडन्ति कन्
in the fem. form added, and ड changed to ल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलमेखला
गलमेखला f. (-ला) A thread worn round the neck, a necklace.
 E. गल the
throat, and मेखला a girdle.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलव्रत|गलव्रतः
गलव्रत m. (-तः) A peacock.
 E. गल the throat, व्रत holy observance.
also the same as गरव्रत q. v. ल being substituted for र.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलशुण्डिका|गलशुंडिका
गलशुण्डिका f. (-का) The uvula or soft palate.
 E. गल the throat, and
शुण्डिका the elephant's trunk, resembling it in being a pendulous,
roundish, and fleshy substance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलस्तनी
गलस्तनी f. (-नी) A she-goat.
 E. गल the throat, and स्तन the breast; some
species of the Bengal goat have small fleshy processes, resembling
nipples depending from the throat; also गलस्तनी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलहस्त|गलहस्तः
गलहस्त m. (-स्तः) Throttling.
 E. गल, and हस्त the hand.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाङ्कुर|गलांकुर|गलाङ्कुरः
गलाङ्कुर m. (-रः) A disease of the throat, inflammation of the fauces,
and enlargement of the tonsils.
 E. गल the throat, and अङ्कुर a new
sprout.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाविल
गलाविल m. (-लः) A prawn or shrimp: see गङ्गाटेय. Some books read this
गलानिल, and others गलानिक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलि|गलिः
गलि m. (-लिः) A strong and lazy ox.
 E. गल् to eat, and इन् affix; who
is good for nothing but eating.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलित|गलितः
गलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Fallen, dropped.
	 2. Liquefied, melted.
	 3. Dis-
tilled, oozing, flowing.
	 4. Decayed, impaired.
	 5. Lost, deprived.
6. Untied, loosed.
 E. गल् to drop, to ooze, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितकुष्ठ
गलितकुष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) Advanced and incurable leprosy, when the fingers and
toes fall off.
 E. गलित, and कुष्ठ leprosy.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितदन्त
गलितदन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Toothless.
 E. गलित, and दन्त tooth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनख
गलितनख mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं) Having no nails.
 E. गलित, and नख the nail.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनयन
गलितनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Blind.
 E. गलित, and नयन the eye.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेगण्ड|गलेगंड|गलेगंडः|गलेगण्डः
गलेगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A kind of bird, (the Adjutant or Ardea argala.)
 E. गल
the throat, in the seventh case, and गण्ड a boil; alluding to a pen-
dulous fleshy purse hanging from the throat.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेस्तनी
गलेस्तनी f. (-नी) A she-goat; see गलस्तनी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलू
गलू m. (-लूः) A sort of gem.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ r. 1st cl. (गल्भते) To be bold or confident.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ mfn. (-ल्भः-ल्भा-ल्भं)
	 1. Proud, haughty.
	 2. Confident, bold, auda-
cious.
 E. गल्भ् to be proud, &c. अच् affix, more commonly प्रगलभ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्या
गल्या f. (-ल्या)
	 1. A multitude of throats.
	 2. A quantity of a kind of
grass, or ropes made of it.
 E. गल a throat, &c. य aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ल|गल्लः
गल्ल m. (-ल्लः) The cheek.
 E. गल् to eat, and ल affix; from ला to get or
receive.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लचातुरी
गल्लचातुरी f. (-री) A small round pillow to put underneath the cheek. E.
गल्ल the cheek, and चातुर a pillow.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्वर्क|गल्वर्कः
गल्वर्क m. (-र्कः)
	 1. A goblet, a vessel for drinking spirituous liquor.
	 2.
Lapis lazuli.
 E. गल् to drop, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ह
गल्ह r. 1st cl. (गल्हते) To blame, to censure or despise: see गर्ह.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवय|गवयः
गवय m. (-यः)
	 1. A species of ox, the Gayal, erroneously classed by
Hindu writers amongst the kinds of deer, (Bos gavæus.)
	 2. A
monkey chief: the son of VAIVASWATA.
	 f. (-यी) The female Gayal.
E. गु to sound, and अय affix, form irregular; or गो a cow, and य
from या to obtain. affix ड, resembling a cow.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवराज|गवराजः
गवराज m. (-जः) A bull.
 E. गो a cow, affix अण् गव relating to a cow, and
राजन् king, chief; the more direct compound makes गोराज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवल|गवलं|गवलः
गवल m. (-लः) A wild buffalo.
	 n. (-लं) Buffalo's horn.
 E. गु to sound,
अलच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्ष|गवाक्षः
गवाक्ष m. (-क्षः)
	 1. An air hole, a loop hole, a round window, a bull's
eye, &c.
	 2. A monkey chief; one of the sons of VAIVASWATA. E.
गो a ray of light, अक्ष् to spread, affix घञ्, or गो an ox, and अक्ष an
eye; ox eyed.
	 f. (क्षी) A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspata-
nus.)
	 2. A plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see अपराजिता.
 E. गो the earth,
अक्ष् to spread, affix अण् or ङीप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्षजाल
गवाक्षजाल n. (-लं) A lattice, a jalousie, trellice work.
 E. गवाक्ष, and जाल
a net.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाची
गवाची f. (-ची) A fish, (Macrognathus pancalus.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवादन|गवादनं
गवादन n. (-नं) Pasture or meadow grass.
	 f. (-नी)
	 1. A hay rack, a trough
for holding grass out of which cattle feed.
	 2. A species of cucum-
ber, (Cucumis madraspatanus, or, according to some, C. coloquin-
tida.)
	 3. A plant, (Clitoria ternatea:) see the preceding.
 E. गो a
cow, अदन food, fem. affix ङीप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवालूक|गवालूकः
गवालूक m. (-कः) The Gayal, (Bos gavæus:) see गवय.
 E. गो a cow, लोक
to see, with आङ् prefixed, deriv. irr.; in appearance a cow.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाशन|गवाशनः
गवाशन m. (-नः) An outcaste.
 E. गव, and अशन who eats, eating beef.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाषिका
गवाषिका f. (-का) Lac, the dye.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाह्निक
गवाह्निक n. (-कं) A day's feed for a cow.
 E. गो and आह्निक daily.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवीश्वर|गवीश्वरः
गवीश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Owner of kine.
 E. गो a cow, ईश्वर a lord or master.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेडु|गवेडुः
गवेडु m. (-डुः) A cloud.
	 f. (-डुः) A kind of grain, (Coix barbata.)
 E. गो a
cow or the earth, एड् to preserve, उ affix, or with कन् added गवेडुका
also गवेधु, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेधु|गवेधुः
गवेधु f. (-धुः) Coix barbata: see the preceding; also with कन् added
गवेधुका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेरुक|गवेरुकं
गवेरुक n. (-कं) Red chalk.
 E. गो light or colour, ईर् to send, affix वुन्,
and the penultimate changed to उ irregularly; also read गवेधुक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेशका
गवेशका f. (-का) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेष|गवेषः
गवेष r. 10th cl. (गवेषयति)
	 1. To seek, to hunt for, to search or inquire.
2. To make an effort.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेषण|गवेषणं
गवेषण nf. (-णं-णा) Research, inquiry after any thing, (physical or phi-
losophical, &c.)
 E. गवेष to inquire, affix युच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेषित|गवेषितं
गवेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sought, inquired for.
 E. गवेष to search or hunt, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवोद्व
गवोद्व m. (-द्वः) An excellent cow.
 E. गो a cow, and उद्व implying excel-
lence; the compound remains masculine.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्य|गव्यं
गव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)
	 1. Of or belonging to a cow, (as milk, curds, &c.)
2. Proper or fit for cattle.
	 nf. (-व्यं-व्या) A bowstring.
	 f. (-व्या)
	 1. A
multitude of cows.
	 2. A measure of two Kos: see गव्यूति.
	 n. (-व्यं) A
colouring substance, a yellow pigment or dye.
 E. गो a cow, &c.
and यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्यूत|गव्यूतं
गव्यूत n. (-तं)
	 1. A Kos, a measure of length equal 4000 cubits.
	 2. A
measure of two Kos: see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्यूति|गव्यूतिः
गव्यूति mf. (-तिः) A measure of two Kos, a league measured by 2000
Dands or fathoms.
 E. गो the earth, यु to join, क्तिन् affix, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह r. 10th cl. (-गहयति) To be thick or impervious as a forest, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह m. (-ह) A cave.
	 2. A forest.
 E. गह् to be impervious अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=235-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहन|गहनं|गहनः
गहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Impervious, inaccessible.
	 n. (-नं)
	 1. A wood, a
thicket.
	 2. A cave.
	 3. Pain, distress.
 E. गाह् to tremble, &c. affix
युच्, and the radical vowel made short; or गह् to be thick, affix as
before.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहीय
गहीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to a cave or a thicket, which is deep
and difficult of access, impervious.
 E. गह a thicket, छ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्वर|गह्वरं|गह्वरः
गह्वर nf. (-रं-री) A cave, a cavern, a grotto, a recess in a rock or moun-
tain, &c.
	 n. (-रं)
	 1. A thicket, a wood.
	 2. Hypocrisy.
	 3. Weeping,
crying, but not violently.
	 m. (-रः) An arbour, a bower.
 E. गाह to
be agitated, and ष्वरच् Uṇādi affix, the radical vowel made short.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा r. 1st cl. (ङ) गाङ् (गाते) To go, to go to or towards. r. 3rd. cl. but
restricted to the Vedas. (जगाति) To praise.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा f. (-गा) A verse or metrical composition.
 E. गै to sing, क and टाप्
affixes: see ग.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=236-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
