गुञ्ज|गुंज|गुंजः|गुञ्जः
गुञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.
	 f. (-ञ्जा)
	 1. A small
shrub, (Abrus precatorius,) bearing a red and black berry, which
forms the smallest of the jeweller's weights.
	 2. The berry which
averages about 15-16 grains troy, or the artificial weight called by
this name, weighing about 23. 16 grains: see रक्तिका &c.
	 3. A kettle
drum.
	 4. A low murmuring sound.
	 5. A tavern.
	 6. Reflection,
meditation.
 E. गुजि to sound, affix क where the bees buz.
