गुर
गुर r. 1st cl. (गोरति) r. 6th cl. (-ई) गुरी (गुरते) To make an effort or exertion.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरण|गुरणं
गुरण n. (-णं) Effort, perseverance, great or continued exertion.
 E. गुर्
to make an effort, affix ल्युट्; also गोरण.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरु|गुरुः
गुरु mfn. (-गुरुः-गुर्व्वी-गुरु)
	 1. Heavy, weighty.
	 2. Great, (large or eminent)
3. Difficult, arduous.
	 4. Important.
	 5. Much, excessive.
	 6. Best,
excellent.
	 7. Venerable, respectable.
	 8. Dear, valuable, highly
prized.
	 9. Accented long, (as a foot or vowel.)
	 mn. (-रुः-रु) The
long vowel, a sound equal to two Matras or simple sounds.
	 m.
(-रुः)
	 1. A spiritual parent, from whom the youth receives the in-
itiatory Mantra or prayer, and who conducts the ceremonies
necessary at various seasons of infancy and youth, up to the period
of investiture with the characteristic thread or string; this per-
son may be the natural parent or the religious preceptor.
	 2. A
religious teacher, one who explains the law and religion to his
pupil, instructs him in Śāstras, &c.
	 3. A name of VṚHASPATI,
who is considered as the Guru or preceptor of the gods.
	 4. A
father or any venerable male relation.
 E. गृ to sound or speak, &c.
Uṇādi affix कु and उ substituted for ऋ; declaring the mode of
performing the rites, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=241-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

