<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्म|गुल्मं|गुल्मः
गुल्म m. (-ल्मः)
	 1. The division of an army, a body of troops, consisting
of nine platoons, or nine elephants, nine chariots, twenty-seven
horse, and forty-five foot.
	 2. The spleen.
	 3. A shrub, a bush.
	 4.
A clump of grass, &c.
	 5. A fort, an intrenchment.
	 6. Disciplining
an army, keeping it in a posture of defence.
	 7. A wharf or stairs,
a Ghat.
	 8. A disease; according to some, a chronic enlargement of
the spleen, but as variously situated, it is any glandular enlarge-
ment in the abdomen, as that of the mesenteric gland, &c. so as
to be perceived externally.
	 f. (-ल्मी)
	 1. A tent.
	 2. Emblic myrobalan
also आमलकी.
	 3. Small cardamoms: see एला.
	 4. A cluster or clump
of trees, a multitude of thickets.
	 5. A kind of plant, commonly
Kurkavali.
 E. गुड to surround, मक् affix, ड changed to ल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=242-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मकेतु|गुल्मकेतुः
गुल्मकेतु m. (-तुः) A small sort of cane or reed.
 E. गुल्म and केतु banner.
