<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यसूत्र
गृह्यसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A precept of the Grihya or ritual of the Vedas.
 E. गृह्य,
and सूत्र a rule.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गॄ
गॄ r. 6th cl. (गिरति or गिलति) To swallow, to eat. r. 9th cl. (गृणाति) To
sound, to sound intelligibly or articulately, to speak. r. 10th cl.
(गीरयते)
	 1. To know.
	 2. To make known, to teach. With निर् or उत्
prefixed, To reject, to vomit. With सम् and उत्, 1. To throw up.
	 2.
To cry aloud.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेण्डु|गेण्डुः
गेण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) A ball for playing with.
 E. गा to go, affix इण्डु, or
with कन् added गेण्डुक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेण्डुक|गेंडुक|गेंडुकः|गेण्डुकः
गेण्डुक m. (-कः) A ball; also गेण्डूक, the penultimate being made long.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेप
गेप r. 1st cl. (ऋ)गेवृ (गेपते) 1. To shake or tremble.
	 2. To move.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेय|गेयं|गेयः
गेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)
	 1. A singer.
	 2. A song or chant, what is to be sung
or chanted.
	 n. (-यं) Song, singing.
 E. गै to sing, affix यत्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेव
गेव r. 1st cl. (ऋ) गेवृ(गेवते) To serve, to gratify by service.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष
गेष r. 1st cl. (ऋ)गेषृ(गेषते) To seek, to search, to investigate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष्ण|गेष्णः
गेष्ण m. (-ष्णः)
	 1. A professional singer, an actor, a mime, &c.
	 2. A chanter
of the Sama Veda.
 E. गै to sing, and इष्णच् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष्णु|गेष्णुः
गेष्णु m. (-ष्णुः)
	 1. A singer.
	 2. An actor.
	 3. A chanter of the Sama
Veda: see गेष्ण
 E. गै to sing, and इष्णुच् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेह|गेहं
गेह n. (-हं) A house, a dwelling.
 E. ग a name of GANESHA इह् to desire,
affix घञ्; that deity being usually invoked upon laying the found-
ations of a house.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहनर्द्दिन्
गेहनर्द्दिन् m. (-र्द्दी) A lazy or effeminate man, a cotquean.
 E. गेह a house,
and नर्द्दिन् who makes a noise: see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहशूर
गेहशूर m. (-रः) A slothful and trifling man, one who is unfit for con-
cerns beyond those of the house, a cotquean, a house-hero.
 E. गेह a
house, and शूर a hero.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहिन्
गेहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Having a house, householder, &c.
 E. गेह, and
इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गै
गै r. 1st cl. (गायति) To sound, to sing. With उद् or प्र prefixed; (उद्गायति
प्रगायति) To sing, to chant, to sing out or aloud. (उद्गीयते प्रगीयते) To
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">Page245-a+ 60</a>]
be sung or chanted. With वि (विगायति) To assert repeatedly.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैर
गैर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Mountain, mountaineer, mountain-born.
 E. गिरि, and
अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरिक|गैरिकं|गैरिकः
गैरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mountain, mountain-born or produced n. (-कं)
	 1.
Red chalk, or as sometimes applied, red orpiment.
	 2. Gold.
 E. गिरि
a mountain, affix ठक्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरेय|गैरेयं
गैरेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Mountain, mountaineer, mountain-born.
	 n. (-यं)
	 1.
Bitumen.
	 2. Red chalk.
 E. गिरि a mountain, affix ढक्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गो
गो m. (-गौः)
	 1. Heaven, Svarga or paradise.
	 2. A bull.
	 3. A ray of light.
4. The thunderbolt.
	 5. The moon.
	 6. The sun.
	 7. A kind of sacri-
fice, the sacrifice of a cow.
	 8. The moment of the sun's entering
Taurus. mn (-गौः-गु)
	 1. The hair of the body.
	 2. Water: (in the last
sense some confine it to the mas. plu. गावः and according to others,
it is neuter in several other senses.)
	 f. (-गौः)
	 1. A cow.
	 2. The eye.
3. An arrow.
	 4. quarter, as the east, west, &c.
	 5. Speech; also identi-
fied with the goddess of speech. SARASWATI.
	 6. The earth.
	 7. A
mother.
 E. गम् to go, and करणे डो Uṇādi aff. गच्छति अनेन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकण्टक|गोकंटक|गोकण्टकः
गोकण्टक m. (-कः)
	 1. The name of a plant: see गोखुर.
	 2. The print of a
cow's hoof or spot so marked.
 E. गो the earth or a cow, &c. and
कण्टक a thorn. गोः पृथिव्याः कण्टक इव ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकर्ण|गोकर्णः
गोकर्ण m. (-र्णः)
	 1. A span from the tip of the thumb to that of the little
finger.
	 2. A kind of deer, (the Nilgau)
	 3. A mule.
	 4. A class of
demigods.
	 5. A kind of snake.
	 6. A snake in general.
	 7. A place of
pilgrimage on the Malabar coast.
	 f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Aletris hyacin-
thoides:) see मूर्व्वा.
 E. गो a cow, and कर्ण an ear, having ears like a
cow, &c. गौः नेत्रं कर्णौ यस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकिराटिका
गोकिराटिका f. (-का) A bird, considered as one kind of the common
Maina, (Turdus salica.)
 E. गो the earth, and किर a hog, अट who
goes, with कन् added in the fem. form; resembling a hog, feeding
on ordure, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकिल|गोकिलः
गोकिल m. (-लः)
	 1. A plough.
	 2. A pestle.
 E. गो the earth, and किल् to
go. affix क; also गोकील.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकील|गोकीलः
गोकील m. (-लः)
	 1. A pestle.
	 2. A plough.
 E. गो the earth, and कील a pin
or bolt. गोः पृथिव्याः कील इव ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकुल|गोकुलं
गोकुल n. (-लं)
	 1. A herd of kine, a multitude of cattle.
	 2. A cow-house
or station.
	 3. A village or tract on the Jumna, the residence of
NANDA and of KṚṢṆA during his youth.
	 n. गो a cow, and कुल an
assemblage.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकुलिक|गोकुलिकः
गोकुलिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Squint-eyed.
	 2. One who does not give help
to a cow in the mud.
 E. गो the eye, &c. and कुल् to accumulate, affix ठक्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकृत|गोकृतं
गोकृत n. (-तं) Cowdung.
 E. गो a cow, and कृत made.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोक्षुर|गोक्षुरः
गोक्षुर m. (-रः) The name of a plant; also Gokhura, (Ruellia longifolia,
Rox, it is also applied in Bengal to Tribulus lanuginosus.)
	 n. (-रं)
A cow's hoof.
 E. गो a cow, and क्षुर a hoof, the thorns getting be-
tween the hoofs of cattle; also with कन् added गोक्षुरक, and with खुर
a hoof, गोखुर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोक्षुरक|गोक्षुरकः
गोक्षुरक m. (-कः) See the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोखुर|गोखुरः
गोखुर m. (-रः) See गोक्षुर; also गोखुरि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगोयुग|गोगोयुगं
गोगोयुग n. (-गं) A pair of oxen.
 E. गो, and गोयुग a pair. गवोर्द्वित्वम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगोष्ठ|गोगोष्ठं
गोगोष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A cattle shed.
 E. गो, and गोष्ठ a shed. गोः स्थानम् गा + स्थाने गोष्ठच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगृष्टि|गोगृष्टिः
गोगृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A cow that has had one calf.
 E. गो a cow, and गृष्टि q. v.
the same as the compound. सकृत् प्रमूतायां गवि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रन्थि|गोग्रंथि|गोग्रन्थिः
गोग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः)
	 1. Dried cow-dung.
	 2. A station for cows, a cow-yard
or house, &c.
 E. गो a cow, ग्रन्थ् to arrange, and इन् aff. गोर्जातो ग्रन्थिः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रह|गोग्रहः
गोग्रह m. (-हः) Spoil, booty, capture of cattle.
 E. गो, and ग्रह seizing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रास|गोग्रासः
गोग्रास m. (-सः) The ceremony of presenting grass to the cow when
making atonement.
 E. गो, and ग्रास a mouthful.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोघ्न|गोघ्नः
गोघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Who or what kills kine.
	 m. (-घ्नः) A guest.
 E. गो a
cow, and घ्न what kills, from हन् with क affix; a cow being killed
on the arrival of the latter, or being presented to him.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोघृत|गोघृतं
गोघृत n. (-तं)
	 1. Rain.
	 3. Ghee made from cow's milk.
 E. गो the earth,
घृत what sprinkles, from घृ to sprinkle or wet, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचर|गोचरः
गोचर m. (-रः)
	 1. An object of sense, as sound, shape, colour, &c.
	 2. A.
country, a district.
	 3. The house or mansion of a planet, or its
presence in any sign which is that of a person's nativity.
	 4. Pas-
turage.
 E. गो an organ of sense, &c. and चर what goes, from चर् to
go, निपातने अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचर्म्मन्|गोचर्मन्
गोचर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)
	 1. A cow's hide.
	 2. A hide of land, 300 feet long, by
10 broad: it is also defined as that extent of land, the crop of
which will support a man for a year.
 E. गो and चर्म्मन् skin.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचारक|गोचारकः
गोचारक m. (-कः) A cowhered.
 E. गो, चर to go, causal form णिच् ण्वुल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोछाल|गोच्छाल|गोच्छालः
गोछाल m. (-लः) The palm of the hand with the fingers extended, &c.
see अलम्बुष. गां भूमिम् आच्छादयति छद-णिच् अण् पृषोदरादित्वात् । भूकदम्बे ।
चाकुलिया ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजल|गोजलं
गोजल n. (-लं) Cow's urine.
 E. गो, and जल water. गवि जातं जलम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजागरिक|गोजागरिकं|गोजागरिकः
गोजागरिक m. (-कः) A prickly nightshade.
	 n. (-कं) Happy, fortunate,
auspicious.
 E. गो the earth, जागृ to wake or to be awake, affix ठक्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजिह्वा
गोजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A potherb growing wild. (Elephantophus scaber.)
 E. गो
a cow, and जिह्वा a tongue: the leaves being so compared; also with
कन् added गोजिह्वका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोडु
गोडु m. (-डुः) A lump of flesh on the navel.
 E. गुड् to be sound, affix घञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोडुम्ब|गोडुंब|गोडुंबः|गोडुम्बः
गोडुम्ब mf. (-म्बः-म्बा) The water melon.
	 f. (-म्बा) A kind of cucumber,
(Cucumis madras patanus.)
 E. गो the earth, तुवि to hurt, affix क
and त changed to ड. गां भूमिं तुम्बति अर्दति । तुवि-क पृषोदराः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोणी
गोणी f. (-णी)
	 1. Torn or ragged clothes.
	 2. A sack.
	 3. The measure of
a Drona.
 E. गुण् to reckon, affixes घञ् नि-गुणः and ङीष् the deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोण्ड|गोंड|गोंडः|गोण्डः
गोऽण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) A person with a prominent navel.
	 m. (-ण्डः) A
man of a low tribe, a mountaineer, especially inhabiting the eastern
portion of the Vindhya range, between the Nerbudda and Krishna
giving name to the province of Gondwana.
	 2. A prominent navel,
or a lump of flesh on the navel, &c.
 E. गुडि to enclose, &c. अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतम|गोतमः
गोतम m. (-मः) The name of a sage belonging to the family of ANGIRAS
father of SATANANDA; also गौतम. गोभिस्तमो ध्वस्तं यस्य पृषोदरादित्वात् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतमान्वय|गोतमान्वयः
गोतमान्वय m. (-यः) A name of SAKYA or SAKYA MUNI, a Bauddha sage.
E. गोतम a sage, and अन्वय lineage; the descendant of GOTAMA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतल्लज|गोतल्लजः
गोतल्लज m. (-जः) An excellent cow.
 E. गो a cow, तल्लज implying excellence.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्र|गोत्रं|गोत्रः
गोत्र n. (-त्रं)
	 1. Family, race, lineage, kin.
	 2. A name, an appellation.
	 3. A
forest.
	 4. A field.
	 5. A Chattra, an umbrella or parasol.
	 6. A road.
7. Knowledge of futurity, inspiration.
	 8. A genus, a class or species
9. A caste, a tribe or subdivision of it into families, as in that of
the Brahman; twenty-four Gotras are reckoned, supposed to be
sprung from and named after celebrated teachers, as SANDILYA,
KAŚYAPA, GAUTAMA, BHARADWAJA, &c.
	 10. Increase.
	 11. Wealth.
f. (-त्रा)
	 1. The earth.
	 2. A herd of kine.
	 m. (-त्रः) A mountain.
 E. गु
to sound, and त्र Uṇādi affix, or गो the earth, &c. and त्र what pre-
serves, from त्रै with क aff. गां भूमिं त्रायते त्रैङ् पालने क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्रज|गोत्रजः
गोत्रज mf. (-जः-जा) A relation: in law, the term is nearly equivalent to
the Gentile of Roman law, and is applied to kindred of the same
general family, who are connected by offerings of food and water,
and stands opposed to the Bandhu or cognate kin, who do not
partake in the offerings to the common ancestors: see बन्धु.
 E. गोत्र
as above, ज born. गोत्रे समाने वंशे जायते जन-ड ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्रभिद्
गोत्रभिद् m. (-भिद्- or भित्) A name of INDRA.
 E. गोत्र a mountain, and
भिद् who splits, (with his thunderbolt.) गोत्रं पर्वतं मेघं वा भिनत्ति ।
भिद्-क्विप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्ररिवथ
गोत्ररिवथ n. (-क्थं) Patrimony, inheritance.
 E. गोत्र, and रिवथ wealth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोद|गोदः
गोद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what gives a cow.
	 m. (-दः) The brain.
 E. गो
light or a cow, and द what gives. गां नेत्रं दायति शोधयति दै-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदन्त|गोदंत|गोदन्तं
गोदन्त m. (-न्तः)
	 1. Yellow orpiment.
	 2. A cow's tooth.
	 3. A fossile subs-
tance of a white colour, apparently an earthy salt.
 E. गो a cow,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=246-a" target="_blank">Page246-a+ 60</a>]
and दन्त a tooth, a cow's tooth, from its similar hardness,
&c.
