<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमीन|गोमीनः
गोमीन m. (-नः) A sort of fish, the bull-fish.
 E. गो, and मीन a fish.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमुख|गोमुखं|गोमुखः
गोमुख n. (-खं)
	 1. A house build unevenly or crookedly, viz. with
angles, projections, &c.
	 2. A kind of musical instrument, (a sort
of horn or trumpet)
	 3. Spreading unguents, plastering, smear-
ing.
	 4. A hole in a wall made by thieves, &c. a breach.
	 m. (-खः)
1. A shark.
	 2. A kind of Yakṣa; according to the Jainas, a
demigod subservient to their deified saints.
	 nf. (-खं-खी) A cloth-
bag, containing a rosary into which the hand is thrust to count
the beads.
	 f. (-खी) The chasm in the Himālaya mountains through
which the Ganges flows, erroneously conceived by the Hindus to
be of the shape of a cow's mouth.
	 2. A river in Bengal.
 E. गो a
cow, and मुख face, having the face of a cow, &c. गोमुखमिव मुखमस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूढ
गोमूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Stupid as an ox.
 E. गो, and मूढ foolish.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूत्र|गोमूत्रं
गोमूत्र n. (-त्रं) Cow's urine.
 E. गो, and मूत्र urine. षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूत्रिका
गोमूत्रिका f. (-का)
	 1. A kind of grass, described as growing in corn
fields, of a reddish colour, and eaten by cattle, commonly Tam-
bada (ताम्बड)
	 2. A verse the second half of which repeats nearly
all the syllables of the first.
	 3. A form of calculation.
 E. गो, मूत्र
urine, ठन् affix; operating on cows as a diuretic. गोर्मूत्रस्येव गतिरस्ति
अत्र ।
