<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवशा
गोवशा f. (-शा) A barren cow.
 E. गो a cow, and वशा barren.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविन्द|गोविंद|गोविन्दः
गोविन्द m. (-न्दः)
	 1. One of the most usual appellations of KṚṢṆA or
VIṢṆU in that form.
	 2. A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of
JUPITER.
	 3. A cow-keeper, one who protects, cherishes or owns
cattle.
 E. गो language, here the language of the Vedas especially,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-b" target="_blank">Page248-b+ 60</a>]
and विन्द who knows, from विद् to know, with श affix; also गो
heaven, a cow, विद् to obtain, by whom heaven is obtained, or who
obtains felicity by protecting kine. गां वेदमयीं वाणीं, भुवं धेनुं स्वर्गं वा
विन्दति ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविष्
गोविष् f. (-विट्) Cow-dung.
 E. गो a cow, and विष् ordure; also गोविष्ठा.
