गौड|गौडः
गौड m. (-डः) The district of Gaur, the central part of Bengal, extend-
ing from Banga to Bhubaneshwar in Orrissa: the ruins of its capital,
called by the same name, are still in existance.
	 m. plu. (-डाः) The
inhabitants of Gaur.
	 f. (-डी)
	 1. Rum or spirit distilled from Gur or
molasses.
	 2. One of the Rāgiṇīs.
	 3. A style of poetry, the bold
and spirited style,
 E. गुड to surround, or गुड raw sugar, and अण्
affix, fem. affix ङीष्.
