चक्रधर|चक्रधरः
चक्रधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having a wheel, &c.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A village or
common tumbler or juggler.
	 2. One who holds a wheel, discus, &c.
3. The manager or owner of many villages.
	 4. A name of VIṢṆU
or KṚṢṆA, who is represented as holding a discus in one hand.
5. A snake.
 E. चक्र a wheel, &c. and धर who holds. धृ अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रनामन्
चक्रनामन् m. (-मा) A pyritic ore or iron: see माक्षिक.
 E. चक्र a wheel, &c.
and नामन् appellation. चव्रवाके माक्षिकधातौ च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपद्माट|चक्रपद्माटः
चक्रपद्माट m. (-टः) Cassia tora: see चक्रमर्द्दक.
 E. चक्र a wheel, पद्म a lotus,
and अट what goes or is अच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपर्णी|चक्रपर्ण्णी
चक्रपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant commonly Chakuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia,
Rox.)
 E. चक्र a wheel, and पर्ण a leaf, the leaves being nearly round.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाणि|चक्रपाणिः
चक्रपाणि m. (-णिः) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. चक्र and पाणि the hand, being
always represented with a discus in one hand.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाद|चक्रपादः
चक्रपाद m. (-दः)
	 1. A carriage, 2. An elephant.
 E. चक्र a wheel, and पाद
a foot; also चक्रपादक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाल|चक्रपालः
चक्रपाल m. (-लः)
	 1. Superintendent of a province.
	 2. One who carries a
discus.
	 3. A circle.
	 4. The horizon.
 E. चक्र and पाल who or what
protects.
 E. पालि + अण् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रफल|चक्रफलं
चक्रफल n. (-लं) A missile weapon, a kind of discus.
 E. चक्र and फल
fruit, bearing a discus as it were for fruit.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रबान्धव|चक्रबांधव|चक्रबान्धवः
चक्रबान्धव m. (-वः) The sun.
 E. चक्र the ruddy goose, and बान्धव a friend;
these birds being supposed to couple only in the day time.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रभृत्
चक्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. चक्र a discus, and भृत् who cher-
ishes: see चक्रपाणि, &c. चक्रं विभर्त्ति भृ-क्विप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रभेदिनी
चक्रभेदिनी f. (-नी) Night.
 E. चक्र the ruddy goose, and भेदिनी what di-
vides, (male and female;) these birds being condemned, according
to the Hindus, to be separated at night. भिद-णिनि ङीप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमण्डलिन्|चक्रमंडलिन्
चक्रमण्डलिन् m. (-ली) A large snake, (Boa constrictor.)
 E. चक्र a wheel,
and मण्डल a circumference, implying either that the body of the
snake, or the spots on the body may be compared to a wheel.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमर्द्द|चक्रमर्द|चक्रमर्द्दः
चक्रमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) Cassia tora.
 E. चक्र a wheel, here meaning figuratively
a large leprous spot, and मर्द्द what cleanses or removes, from मृद्
with अण् added; or with ण्वुल् affix चक्रमर्द्दक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमर्द्दक|चक्रमर्दक|चक्रमर्द्दकः
चक्रमर्द्दक m. (-कः) See the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमुख|चक्रमुखः
चक्रमुख m. (-खः) A hog.
 E. चक्र a discus, and मुख face; cutting the
ground as it were with a sharp weapon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रयान|चक्रयानं
चक्रयान n. (-नं) Any wheel carriage.
 E. चक्र a wheel, and यान a carriage.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ररद|चक्ररदः
चक्ररद m. (-दः) A hog, a boar.
 E. चक्र and रद a tooth or tusk: see चक्रमुख.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रलक्षणा
चक्रलक्षणा f. (-णा) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum:) see गुडूची.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रला
चक्रला f. (-ला) A plant, (Kyllinga monocephala.)
 E. चक्र a wheel, and
ल what gets. लाति ला-क । उच्चटायाम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवत्|चक्रवन्त्
चक्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)
	 1. Circular, being in a ring or circle.
	 2.
Armed with a discus.
	 3. Wheeled, &c.
	 m. (-वान)
	 1. The proprietor
of an oil mill, or any one in which seeds are bruised.
	 2. VIṢṆU.
3. An emperor.
 E. चक्र a wheel. &c. मतुप् poss. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवत्|चक्रवन्त्
चक्रवत् ind. In rotation, going round or revolving like a wheel.
 E. चक्र,
and मतुप् aff. मस्य वः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्त्तिन्|चक्रवर्तिन्
चक्रवर्त्तिन् m. (-त्तीं) An emperor, a sovereign of the world, the ruler of
a Chakra or country described as extending from sea to sea;
twelve princes beginning with Bharata are especially considered
as Chakravartis.
 E. चक्र a reign, and वृत् to abide, affix णिच्
वा णिन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्त्तिनी|चक्रवर्तिनी
चक्रवर्त्तिनी f. (-नी) A fragrant plant, commonly Chakawat.
 E. चक्र a heap,
and वर्त्तिन् what abides or grows, fem. affix ङीप्,
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाक|चक्रवाकः
चक्रवाक m. (-कः) The ruddy goose. commonly called in India, the Brah-
many duck or goose, (Anas casarca.)
 E. चक्र an imitative sound,
and वाक speech. वच परिभाषणे कर्मणि घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाट|चक्रवाटः
चक्रवाट m. (-टः)
	 1. Limit, boundary.
	 2. A lamp stand.
	 3. Engaging in
any action.
 E. चक्र and वट् वेष्टने to surround, affix घञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाड|चक्रवाडं
चक्रवाड m. (-डः) See चक्रवाल. चक्रमिव वाडते वेष्टयति वाड-अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवात|चक्रवातः
चक्रवात m. (-तः) A whirlwind, a hurricane.
 E. चक्र a circle, and वात wind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाल|चक्रवालं|चक्रवालः
चक्रवाल m. (-लः) A range of mountains supposed to encircle the earth,
and to be the limit of light and darkness.
	 n. (-लं) The sensible
horizon.
 E. चक्र a region, वल् to encompass, and अण् affix; girding
the world; or वाड to emerge, &c. affix अच् what emerges (from
darkness), in the shape of a wheel; ड changed to ल also चक्रवाड.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रव्यूह|चक्रव्यूहः
चक्रव्यूह m. (-हः) The circular array of troops.
 E. चक्र and व्यूह array.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवृद्धि|चक्रवृद्धिः
चक्रवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Compound interest.
 E. चक्र a wheel, वृद्धि increase.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रश्रेणी
चक्रश्रेणी f. (-णी) A plant bearing a crooked fruit: see अजशृङ्गी
 E. चक्र a
wheel, and श्रेणी a line or row.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रसंज्ञ
चक्रसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Tin.
 E. चक्र and संज्ञा a name.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रसंवर|चक्रसंवरः
चक्रसंवर m. (-रः) The name of a Bauddha deity; also हेरम्ब.
 E. चक्र a
discus, and संवर who holds.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रहस्त|चक्रहस्तः
चक्रहस्त m. (-स्तः) VIṢṆU.
 E. चक्र and हस्त hand: holding a discus.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्की|चक्रांकी
चक्राङ्की f. (-ङ्की) A wild goose.
 E. चक्र a number, and अकि to go, affixes
अच् and ङीष् flying in large flocks.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्ग|चक्रांग|चक्राङ्गः
चक्राङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)
	 1. A gander.
	 2. A carriage.
	 f. (-ङ्गी)
	 1. A goose.
	 2. A
drug: see कटुकि.
	 3. A potherb, (Hilancha repens:) see हिलमोचिका.
E. चक्र a wheel, &c. and अङ्ग a limb or the body.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राट|चक्राटः
चक्राट m. (-टः)
	 1. A juggler, a snake-catcher, one who exhibits snakes
and pretends to cure their bites.
	 2. A knave, a cheat, a rogue.
	 3.
A gold coin or certain weight of gold, a Dinar.
 E. चक्र a number
of villages, and अट who goes, i. e. a vagabond, &c. चक्राकारमटति अट-
अण् उप-सः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राण|चक्राणः
चक्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)
	 1. Doing.
	 2. Done.
 E. कृ to do, काणच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राधिवासिन्
चक्राधिवासिन् m. (-सी) The orange tree.
 E. चक्र a heap, and अधिवस् to
abide, णिनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रावर्त्त|चक्रावर्त|चक्रावर्तः|चक्रावर्त्तः
चक्रावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Turning round, whirling or rotatory motion.
 E. चक्र
a wheel, and आवर्त्त revolving.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रि|चक्रिः
चक्रि m. (-क्रिः) An agent, a maker, a doer.
 E. कृ to do, कि affix the
root reduplicate and the deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिका
चक्रिका f. (-का) The knee. चक्रं तदाकारोऽस्ति अस्य ठन् । जानुनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिन्
चक्रिन् mfn. (-क्री-क्रिणी-क्रि)
	 1. Having or holding a discus, &c.
	 2. Wheeled,
having a wheel.
	 3. Circular.
	 m. (-क्री)
	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.
	 2. A
potter.
	 3. The ruddy goose.
	 4. A snake.
	 5. An informer.
	 6. A tumb-
ler, one who exhibits tricks with a discus or a wheel.
	 7. An oil
grinder.
	 8. An emperor, a Chakravarti: see चक्रवर्त्तिन् 9. One who
rides in a carriage.
	 10. A crow.
	 11. An ass.
	 12. Cassia, (the tree.)
E. चक्र a wheel, &c. and इनि poss. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रीवत्|चक्रीवन्त्
चक्रीवत् m. (-वान्)
	 1. An ass.
	 2. The name of a king.
 E. चक्र a wheel, वतु
affix, and deriv. irr. rolling over like a wheel.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रु|चक्रुः
चक्रु m. (-क्रुः) An agent, a maker, a doer.
 E. कृ to make or do, with the
reduplicate initial, and कु Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रेश्वरी
चक्रेश्वरी f. (-री) A female deity peculiar to the Jainas, one of their
Vidya Devis or goddesses of wisdom.
 E. चक्र the universe and ईश्वरी
mistress.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ष
चक्ष (इङ्) चक्षिङ् r. 2nd cl. (चष्टे)
	 1. To speak, to tell.
	 2. To see; (in this
sense आङ् is usually prefixed.)
	 3. To eat. ख्या or कश are substitu-
ted for the radical letters in several tenses of this verb. कथने त्यागे
च अदा-आ-सक-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षण|चक्षणं
चक्षण n. (-णं)
	 1. Eating a relish to promote drinking.
	 2. Speaking,
saying.
 E. चक्ष् to speak, to eat, affix ल्युट्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षस्
चक्षस् m. (-क्षाः)
	 1. A name of VṚHASPATI the preceptor of the gods.
	 2.
A spiritual teacher, an instructor in sacred science.
 E. चक्ष् to
speak affix असि न ख्यादेशः ।
