चात्वाल|चात्वालं|चात्वालः
चात्वाल m. (-लः)
	 1. A hollow made in the ground to receive, a burnt off-
ering or sacrificial fire.
	 2. Any hole in the ground.
 E. चत् to ask,
(to solicit the gods) and वालञ् Uṇādi affix; also चत्वाल q. v.
