<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्ल|चिल्लः
चिल्ल r. 1st cl. (-चिल्लति)
	 1. To be loose, to be slack or flaccid.
	 2. To in-
dicate one's meaning.
	 3. To act wantonly. भ्वा-प-अक-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्ल|चिल्लः
चिल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ली-ल्लं) Blear-eyed.
	 m. (-ल्लः)
	 1. The Bengal kite, (Falco
cheela, Lath.)
	 2. A bleared or sore eye.
	 f. (-ल्ली)
	 1. A potherb, said
to be a small kind of Chenopodium: see वास्तुक.
	 2. A cricket.
 E. चिल्ल्
to be flaccid or loose, affix अच्ः see चुल्ल, or नि preposition, लच् in
the second sense, and चिल् substituted for नि. or चिल्ल् अच् । पक्षिभेदे ।
(चिल्) क्लिन्ने त्रि० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लका
चिल्लका f. (-का) A cricket: see चीलिका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लभक्ष्या
चिल्लभक्ष्या f. (-क्ष्या) A vegetable perfume: see हट्टविलासिनी.
 E. चिल्ल a kite,
and भक्ष्य eatable.
