चुलुक m. (-कः)
	 1. Mud, mire.
	 2. A small vessel or pot, a gallipot, &c.
3. The hand hollowed to hold water.
	 n. (-कं) Water in which pulse
has been steeped.
 E. चुल् to dip into, aff. उकक्ः see चलुक.
