छत्रभङ्ग|छत्त्रभङ्गः|छत्रभंग|छत्रभङ्गः
छत्रभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)
	 1. Widowhood.
	 2. Wilfulness, independence.
	 3. Sub-
version of dominion, loss of empire, deposition, &c.
 E. छत्र a
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">Page276-a+ 60</a>]
parasol, and भङ्ग a breaking; in the first two senses छत्र is
used metaphorically, for any cover or defence, as a husband, &c.
in the last it is used by synecdoche, a parasol being one of the
ensigns of royalty.
 E. छत्रस्य भङ्गः यत्र । नृपनाशे, वैधव्ये, स्वातन्त्र्ये च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्राक|छत्त्राकं|छत्त्राकः|छत्राकः
छत्राक n. (-कं) A mushroom.
	 f. (-की) A plant, commonly Rasna: see
रास्ला.
 E. छत्र a parasol, and अक् to go, to resemble; affixes अण् and
ङीष् । छत्रा अतिछत्रा इव कायति कै-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
