	 1. A plant, and vermifuge: see विडङ्गः 2. Asafœtida.
m. (-घ्नः) A citron.
 E. जन्तु an animal, (a worm) and घ्न what destroys.
जन्तून् कृमीन् हन्ति हन-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुनाशन|जन्तुनाशनं
जन्तुनाशन n. (-नं) Asafætida.
 E. जन्तु, and नाशन destroying. जन्तून् नाशयति
नश-णिच्-ल्यु । हिङ्गुनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुफल|जंतुफल|जन्तुफलः
जन्तुफल m. (-लः) Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)
 E. जन्तु an ani-
mal, and फल a leaf; its leaves swarm with insects. जन्तवः फले अस्य ।
उडम्बरे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुला
जन्तुला f. (-ला) A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)
 E. जन्तु an
animal or insect, and ला what gets. जन्तून् कीटान् लाति ला-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्म|जन्मं
जन्म mn. (-न्मः-न्मं) Birth: see जन्मन्.
 E. जन-वा-मन् । जन्मनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मकील|जन्मकीलः
जन्मकील m. (-लः) VIṢṆU.
 E. जन्म birth, and कील the stay. जन्मनः कीलः इव
रोधकत्वात् । विष्णौ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मद|जन्मदः
जन्मद m. (-दः) A father.
 E. जन्म birth, and द who gives.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मन्
जन्मन् n. (-न्म) Birth, production.
 E. जन् to be born, and मनिन् Uṇādi
affix, or with a final vowel जन्म.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मनक्षत्र
जन्मनक्षत्र n. (-त्रं) The planet or constellation under which a person is
born, the natal star.
 E. जन्म, and नक्षत्र asterism.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभूमि|जन्मभूमिः
जन्मभूमि f. (-मिः) Native country, birth place.
 E. जन्म, and भूमि land.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवत्|जन्मवन्त्
जन्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Mortal, living.
 E. जन्म, and मतुप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवर्त्मन्
जन्मवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्मः) The vulva. जन्म birth, and वर्त्मन् path or way.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवैलक्षण्य
जन्मवैलक्षण्य n. (-ण्यं) Acting contrary to one's origin, unbecoming one's
birth, &c.
 E. जन्म, and वैलक्षण्य inconsistency.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मशोधन
जन्मशोधन n. (-नं) Acquitting the obligations derived from birth.
 E. जन्म,
and शोधन wiping away.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मसाफल्य
जन्मसाफल्य n. (-ल्यं) Attainment of the object or end of existence. E.
जन्म, and साफल्य fruitfulness.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तर|जन्मांतर|जन्मान्तरं
जन्मान्तर n. (-रं)
	 1. The other world.
	 2. Regeneration, another birth. E.
जन्म, and अन्तर difference.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्ध|जन्मांध|जन्मान्धः
जन्मान्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Blind from birth.
 E. जन्म, and अन्ध blind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्माष्टमी
जन्माष्टमी f. (-मी) The eighth lunation or dark half of Bhadra, the birth
day of KṚṢṆA.
 E. जन्म, and अष्टमी eighth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मिन्
जन्मिन् m. (-न्मी) An animal, an existent being.
 E. जन्म birth, and इनि
aff. जन्म अस्ति अस्य व्रीह्यादि इनि । प्राणिनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मेजय|जन्मेजयः
जन्मेजय m. (-यः) The name of a prince: see जनमेजय.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)
	 1. To be born or produced.
	 2. Fit for or favourable
to men.
	 m. (-न्यः)
	 1. A father.
	 2. The friend, attendant, or companion
of a bridegroom.
	 f. (-न्या) The friend of a mother.
	 2. The relation or
companion of a bride, a bride's maid, &c.
	 3. Pleasure, happiness.
	 4.
Affection.
	 5. A mother.
	 n. (-न्यं)
	 1. War, combat.
	 2. Rumour, report.
3. A market, a fair.
	 4. A portent, one occurring at birth.
 E. जन to
be born, &c. affix णिच् कर्त्तरि यत् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्यु|जन्युः
जन्यु m. (-न्युः)
	 1. An animal, an existent. and sentient being.
	 2. A name
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">Page281-b+ 60</a>]
of BRAMHA.
	 3. Fire or Agni.
 E. जन् to be born, &c. Uṇādi affix युच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप r. 1st cl. (जपति)
	 1. To speak, to say or tell.
	 2. To meditate, to
speak internally, to say to one's self. With उप prefixed, to divide.
भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप m. (-पः) Muttering prayers, repeating inaudibly passages from the
scriptures, charms, names of a deity, counting silently the beads of
a rosary, &c.
	 f. (-पा) The China rose, the flower or plant; also जवा.
E. जप् to repeat inaudibly, affix कर्त्तरि अच्; the flower is a sacred
object.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्त्वा
जप्त्वा ind. Having repeated inaudibly.
 E. जप्, and क्त्वा affix: see जपित्वा;
the omission of इट् is unusual.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपन|जपनं
जपन n. (-नं) Inaudible repetition of prayers, &c.: see the last.
 E. जप्
as before, affix भावे ल्युट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपनीय
जपनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be meditated on, to be repeated inaudibly. E.
जप्, and अनीयर् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपपरायण|जपपरायणः
जपपरायण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Devoted to religious meditation, engaged
in muttering prayers, &c.
 E. जप् as above, and परायण adhering or
attached to.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपमाला
जपमाला f. (-ला) A rosary.
 E. जप, and माला a string of beads, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपयज्ञ|जपयज्ञः
जपयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Muttering prayers as a religious rite, or sacrifice.
 E. जप,
and यज्ञ sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित्वा
जपित्वा ind. Having repeated inaudibly.
 E. जप्, and क्त्वा affix, इट् inserted.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित
जपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Repeated inaudibly.
 E. जप् to mutter prayers, and
क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्य|जप्यः
जप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be repeated inaudibly, to be said over repeat-
edly, (a prayer, &c.)
 E. जप्, and कर्मणि यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ् r. 1st. cl. (जभति-ते) also (इ) जभि r. 1st cl. (जम्भति)
	 1. To gape or
yawn.
	 2. To copulate. r. 10th cl. (जम्भयति-ते) To destroy, to efface.
भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । चु० उभ० सक० इदित् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम
जम (उ) जमु r. 1st cl. (जमति) To eat; also चम । भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम
जम ind. A wife. It is used in composition: see जम्पती.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमदग्नि|जमदग्निः
जमदग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Muni, the father of PARASURAMA.
 E. जमन् प्रज्वलितः
अग्निः इव ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमन|जमनं
जमन n. (-नं)
	 1. Eating.
	 2. Food, victuals.
 E. जम् to eat, affix भावेल्युट्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्पति
जम्पति m. du. (-ती) Husband and wife.
 E. जं for जाया a wife, and पति
a husband: see दम्पती &c. जाया च पतिश्च द्व० जायायाः जम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बाल|जंबाल|जंबालः|जम्बालः
जम्बाल mn. (-लः-लं)
	 1. Mud, clay.
	 2. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)
&c.
	 m. (-लः) A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)
 E. जल
water, बल् to move, affix अण्, and the deriv. irr. or जम्ब-घञ् जम्बम्
आलाति आदत्ते आ-ला-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बालिनी|जंबालिनी
जम्बालिनी f. (-नी) A river.
 E. जम्बाल mud, इनि and ङीष् affs. नद्याम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बिर|जम्बिरः
जम्बिर m. (-रः) A lime: see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बीर|जंबीर|जंबीरः|जम्बीरः
जम्बीर m. (-रः)
	 1. Common lime, (Citrus acida;) the name seems to be
applied to more than one species.
	 2. A plant, called by some a
sort of basil, with small leaves; also जम्भीर, and जम्बिर.
 E. जम् to eat,
ईरन् affix, and वुक् augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बु|जंबु|जम्बुः
जम्बु mn. (-म्बुः-म्बु)
	 1. Jambu Dwipa, said to be so named from the
Jambu tree abounding in it, and implying, according to the
Puranas the central division of the world, or the known world:
according to the Bauddhas, it is confined to India.
	 2. A fabulous
river, said to flow from the mountain Meru.
	 f. (-म्बुः) A fruit tree
the rose apple, (Eugenia jambolana;) also applied to every species
of Eugenia.
	 fn. (-म्बुः-म्बु) The fruit.
 E. जम् to eat, वुक् augment, and
कु or कू Uṇādi affix; hence it is also written जम्बू.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुक|जंबुक|जंबुकः|जम्बुकः
जम्बुक m. (-कः)
	 1. A jackal.
	 2. The deity of water, VARUṆA.
	 3. A low
man.
	 4. The rose apple. जम् to eat, affix उकच् and वुक् augment,
eating flesh, &c. or जम्बु as above, and क added the affix also being
ऊकच्, जम्बूक । जम्बः इव कायति कै-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुद्वीप|जंबुद्वीप|जम्बुद्वीपः
जम्बुद्वीप m. (-पः) One of the divisions of the world.
 E. द्वीप a continent,
added to जम्बु । जम्बुवृक्षयुक्तः द्वीपः । भूमेः सप्तद्वीपान्तर्गते द्वीपभेदे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुमत्|जम्बुमन्त्
जम्बुमत् m. (-मान्)
	 1. A monkey.
	 2. A mountain.
	 f. (-मती) An Apsara or
heavenly nymph.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बू|जंबू
जम्बू f. (-म्बूः) See जम्बु.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूक|जंबूक|जंबूकः|जम्बूकः
जम्बूक m. (-कः) See जम्बुक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूल|जंबूल|जम्बूलः
जम्बूल m. (-लः)
	 1. A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)
2. The rose apple.
	 n. (-लं) Jokes addressed to the bridegroom by
his female relatives and friends.
 E. जम्बू as above, and ल what
gets or is.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूलमालिका
जम्बूलमालिका f. (-का) Compliments or jokes addressed to the bride and
bridegroom.
 E. जम्बूल, and मालिका a string.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ|जंभ|जंभः|जम्भः
जम्भ m. (-म्भः)
	 1. A tooth.
	 2. The lime.
	 3. Food, victuals.
	 4. The chin.
	 5.
A quiver.
	 6. A part, a portion.
	 7. The name of a demon.
 E. जभि to
destroy, affix अच् and नुम् । दैत्यभेदे । करणे घञ् दन्ते । कर्मणि घञ् जम्बीरे ।
भावे घञ् भक्षणे । कर्मणि घञ् अंशे । करणे घञ् तूणे हनौ च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भक|जंभक|जम्भकः
जम्भक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Who or what yawns, opens, expands, &c.
	 2.
Who or what kills or destroys.
	 m. (-कः) A lime or citron.
	 f. (-का)
Yawning.
 E. जभि to yawn, &c. ण्वुल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भद्विष्|जंभद्विष्
जम्भद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A name of INDRA.
 E. जम्भ a demon, and द्बिष् a foe;
also similar compounds. जम्भम् असुरं द्वेष्टि द्विष-क्विप् । इन्द्रे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भभेदिन्|जंभभेदिन्
जम्भभेदिन् m. (-दी) INDRA.
 E. जम्भ as above, and भेदिन् destroying: see
the last. जम्भम् असुरं भिनत्ति भिद-णिनि । इन्द्रे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भर|जंभर|जंभरः|जम्भरः
जम्भर m. (-रः) A lime or citron. E. See the next, ल being changed to र ।
जम्भं भक्षणरुचिं राति ददाति रा-क । जम्बीरे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भल|जंभलः|जम्भलः
जम्भल m. (-लः)
	 1. A lime or citron.
	 2. A Jina or deified Jaina saint.
	 f.
(-ला) A female Rakshasi, the worship of whom is supposed to
procure for women procreation.
 E. जभि to destroy, (sickness, sin,
&c.) कलच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भरि
जम्भरि m. (-रिः)
	 1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.
	 2. Fire or its deity.
	 3. INDRA.
E. जम्भ the demon, and अरि a foe. जम्भस्य भक्ष्यस्य असुरभेदस्य वा अरिः ।
वह्नौ वज्रे च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भिन्|जंभिन्
जम्भिन् m. (-म्भी) A lime or citron.
 E. जभि to destroy, (disease,) affix णिनि
and नुम् । जम्बीरे । जृम्मायुक्ते त्रि० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भीर|जंभीर|जंभीरः|जम्भीरः
जम्भीर m. (-रः)
	 1. The lime or citron, apparently of more than one
species.
	 2. A plant, considered to be a kind of basil with small
leaves.
 E. जभि to destroy, (sickness,) ईरन् affix, and नुम् augment;
also जम्बीर, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय|जयः
जय m. (-यः)
	 1. Conquest, victory, triumph.
	 2. A name of YuDHISH-
ṬHIRA.
	 3. A proper name, the son of INDRA.
	 4. One of VIṢṆU'S
door keepers.
	 5. The name of a king; also विजयनन्दन.
	 6. A kind of
Mung or bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)
	 f. (-या)
	 1. A name of the goddess
PARVATI.
	 2. One of her female companions.
	 3. The 3rd, 8th, or
13th lunar day of either half month.
	 4. Yellow myrobalan, (Ter-
minalia chebula.)
	 5. A plant: see जयन्ती.
	 6. A tree, commonly
Ganiyari, (Premna spinosa.)
	 7. Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)
	 8. A
banner, a flag.
 E. जि to conquer or excel, affixes भावे अच् and टाप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयकोलाहल|जयकोलाहलः
जयकोलाहल m. (-लः)
	 1. A kind of dice.
	 2. Shouts of victory.
 E. जय vic-
tory, कोलाहल a noise. जयस्य कोलाहलः यस्मिन् । पाशकक्रीडाभेदे, जयध्वनौ च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयगर्व्व|जयगर्व
जयगर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः) Pride of conquest, exultation.
 E. जय, and गर्व्व pride.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयत्|जयन्त्
जयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Conquering, excelling.
 E. जि to conquer, शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयढक्का
जयढक्का f. (-क्का) A large kettle drum, beaten as a sign of victory. E.
जय, and ढक्का a drum. जयसूचिका ढक्का । वाद्यभेदे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदत्त|जयदत्तः
जयदत्त m. (-त्तः) The son of INDRA.
 E. जय victory, दत्त given, to whom
victory is given by his enemies.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयद्रथ|जयद्रथः
जयद्रथ m. (-थः) A chief in the army of DURYODHANA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन|जयनं
जयन n. (-नं)
	 1. Armour for cavalry, elephants, &c.
	 2. Conquering, sub-
duing.
	 f. (-नी) INDRA'S daughter.
 E. जि to conquer or excel, affixes
करणे ल्युट् and ङीष् । हयादिसन्नाहे । भावे ल्युट् जये ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयनयुज्
जयनयुज् mfn. (-युक्)
	 1. Caparisoned, (as a war horse.)
	 2. Victorious. E.
जयन, and युज् having.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन्त|जयंत|जयंतः|जयन्तः
जयन्त m. (-न्तः)
	 1. A hero and demigod, the son of INDRA.
	 2. A name of
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">Page282-b+ 60</a>]
ŚIVA.
	 3. The moon.
	 4. A name of BHIMA.
	 f. (-न्ती)
	 1. A tree,
(Æschynomene sesban.)
	 2. A name of the goddess DURGĀ.
	 3. The
daughter of INDRA.
	 4. A flag, a banner, 5. A particular combina-
tion in astronomy, or the rising of the asterism ROHINI at midnight,
on the 8th of the dark half of Sravan, or in fact on the birth day
of KṚṢṆA, which is then particularly sacred.
	 6. Blades of barley
planted at the commencement of the Dasahara, and plucked at its
close.
 E. जि to conquer or excel, Uṇādi affix झच् fem. affix ङीष्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपत्र|जयपत्रं
जयपत्र n. (-त्रं) Record of victory or triumph; in law, the sealed and
written award of the judge in favour of either party; in historical
tradition, the label on the brow of a horse turned loose for the
Aswamedha sacrifice.
 E. जय conquest, and पत्र a leaf; also with कन्
added जयपत्रक । जयसूचकं पत्रम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपाल|जयपालः
जयपाल m. (-लः)
	 1. A name of BRAMHA.
	 2. VIṢṆU.
	 3. A king, a sover-
eign; (it is also the appellation of several celebrated Hindu princes.)
4. A tree, (Croton tiglium.)
 E. जय victory, पाल who nourishes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयध्वनि
जयध्वनि m. (-निः) Shout of victory.
 E. जय, and ध्वनि sound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपुत्रक|जयपुत्रकः
जयपुत्रक m. (-कः) A kind of dice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयमङ्गल|जयमंगल|जयमङ्गलः
जयमङ्गल m. (-लः) The royal elephant.
 E. जय victory, and मङ्गल good
fortune.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जययज्ञ|जययज्ञः
जययज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The Aswamedha or sacrifice of a horse, as a mark of
dominion.
 E. जय, and यज्ञ sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवह
जयवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)
	 1. Conferring victory.
	 2. Victorious.
 E. जय and
वह what bears.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवाहिनी
जयवाहिनी f. (-नी) The wife of INDRA.
 E. जय conquest, and वाहिनी who
bears.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशब्द|जयशब्दः
जयशब्द m. (-ब्दः) A shout or song of victory, or the exclamation Jaya
Jaya repeated like the Io of the Greeks, as जयदेवहरे, &c.
 E. जय
and शब्द sound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशील
जयशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Victorious, triumphant.
 E. जय and शील possessed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयश्री
जयश्री f. (-श्रीः) Victory, glory.
 E. जय, and श्री splendor.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयान्तराय
जयान्तराय m. (-यः) An impediment or hindrance to victory.
 E. जय and
अन्तराय obstacle.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयारव
जयारव m. (-वः) The Io or song of victory: see जयशब्द.
 E. जय and आरव sound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयावह
जयावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)
	 1. Victorious.
	 2. Conferring victory.
 E. जय and,
आवह what gives.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Victorious.
 E. जय victory, शीलार्थे इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयोद्धुर
जयोद्धुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Victorious, conquering.
 E. जय and उद्धुर firm.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्य|जय्यः
जय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Able to conquer, victorious.
 E. जि to subdue, affix
यत्, deriv. irr. जेतुं शक्यः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्यता
जय्यता f. (-ता) Victory, success, ability to conquer.
 E. जय्य and तल् affix;
with त्व जय्यत्वम्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठ|जरठः
जरठ mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)
	 1. Hard, solid.
	 2. Herd-hearted, harsh, cruel.
	 3.
Pale, yellowish-white.
	 4. Old, decayed, infirm.
	 5. Bent, bowed
down, drooping.
	 m. (-ठः)
	 1. A name of Pandu, father of the five
Pandavas.
	 2. Decrepitude.
 E. जॄ to become old or decayed, Uṇādi
affix अठ्, and the deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण|जरणं|जरणः
जरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Old, infirm, decayed.
	 m. (-णः)
	 1. Cuminseed.
	 2.
A plant yielding a pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)
	 3. A sort of
salt, (Bit-laban.)
	 4. Old age, becoming old and infirm.
	 n. (-णं)
Asafœtida.
 E. जॄ to become old, affix ल्यु ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्ड|जरंड|जरण्डः
जरण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Old, decayed.
 E. जॄ to be old, अण्डच् Uṇādi
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्|जरन्त्
जरत् mfn. (-रन्-रती-रत्)
	 1. Old, ancient, advanced in years.
	 2. Infirm,
decayed.
	 m. (-रन्) An old man.
	 f. (-ती) An old woman.
 E. जॄ to be
or become old, participial affix शतृ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारु|जरत्कारुः
जरत्कारु m. (-रुः) A celebrated Muni or sage so named.
	 f. (-रुः) The
wife of JARATKARU, the snake goddess MANASA.
 E. जरत् being old,
and कारु a maker; a practiser of austerities in old age.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारुप्रिया
जरत्कारुप्रिया f. (-या) The goddess MANASA, exercising a peculiar power
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">Page283-a+ 60</a>]
over serpents, as the sister of VĀSUKI, the Naga.
 E. जरत्कारु as
above, and प्रिया the beloved.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरद्गव|जरद्गवः
जरद्गव m. (-वः) An old ox.
	 f. (-वी) An old cow.
 E. जरत् old, गो a cow,
affix टच् fem. affix ङीष्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरन्त|जरंत|जरन्तः
जरन्त m. (-न्तः)
	 1. A buffalo.
	 2. An old man.
 E. जॄ to be or become old,
Uṇādi affix झच्.
