जरसान|जरसानः
जरसान m. (-नः) A man.
 E. जॄ to grow old, असानच् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरा
जरा f. (-रा)
	 1. Decrepitude, the general relaxation and debility conse-
quent upon old age, or old age itself.
	 2. A tree, (Mimusops kauki,
Rox.)
	 3. A female demon or Rakshasi.
 E. जॄ to grow old, affixes
अङ् and टाप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरातुर|जरातुरः
जरातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Infirm, decrepid, debilitated, old.
 E. जरा infirmi-
ty and आतुर diseased, affected.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापरिणत
जरापरिणत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stooping, bent down with age or infirmity.
E. जरा, and परिणत bent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापुष्ट|जरापुष्टः
जरापुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A proper name: see जरासन्ध.
 E. जर a female Rakshasi,
and पुष्ट fostered; assisted at his birth by a demon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जराभीरु|जराभीरुः
जराभीरु m. (-रुः) Love or the deity KĀMA^1.
 E. जरा decrepitude, and भीरु formidable.
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.
