<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायमान
जायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being born, coming into life.
 E. जन् to be born,
शानच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया f. (-या) A wife, one wedded according to the perfect ritual. E.
जन् to be born, affix यक्; in whom a man is again born, that is to
say, he is re-born in his children. जायते अस्याम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाघ्न|जायाघ्नः
जायाघ्न m. (-घ्नः)
	 1. A murderer of his wife.
	 2. A mole or mark on the
body, indicative of the death of a wife.
 E. जाया and घ्न what destroys.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाजीव|जायाजीवः
जायाजीव m. (-वः) An actor, a dancer.
 E. जाया a wife, and जीव who gets
a livelihood. जायया तन्नर्त्तनवृत्त्या जीवति अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायात्व
जायात्व n. (-त्वं) The character or attributes of a wife.
 E. जाया, and त्व aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायानुजीविन्
जायानुजीविन् m. (-वी)
	 1. An actor, a dancer, a mime, &c.
	 2. A kind of
crane, the Vaka (Ardea nivea.)
	 3. A needy man, a pauper.
	 4. The
husband of a harlot.
 E. जाया a wife, अनु like or with, and जीविन्
who gets a livelihood; who is supported by his wife. जायया अनुजी-
वति अनु + जीव-णिनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायापती
जायापती m. du. (-ती) Husband and wife.
 E. जाया a wife, and पति hus-
band.
