<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितक्रोध|जितक्रोधः
जितक्रोध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of subdued passion, not to be provoked or
made angry.
 E. जित, and क्रोध wrath. जितः क्रोधः येन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितनेमि|जितनेमिः
जितनेमि m. (-मिः) A staff made of the wood of religious fig tree. E.
जित excelled, (by which,) and नेमि circumference of a wheel, (of
any other wood.) जिता नेमिः अत्र ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितशत्रु|जितशत्रुः
जितशत्रु mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु) Victorious, triumphant.
	 m. (-त्रुः) The father
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">Page290-a+ 60</a>]
Ajita, the 2nd Jaina saint.
 E. जित, and शत्रु a foe: see other simi-
lar compounds, जितामित्र, जितारि, &c. जितः शत्रुः येन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितश्रम
जितश्रम m. (-मः) One who is free from worldly cares, a stoic.
 E. जित,
and श्रम fatigue, exertion.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताक्षर|जिताक्षरः
जिताक्षर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Reading well or readily.
 E. जित mastered, and
अक्षर a letter. जितानि आयत्तीकृतानि अक्षराणि येन.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितात्मन्
जितात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-subdued, void of passion.
 E. जित, and
आत्मन् spirit. जितः वशीकृतः आत्मा इन्द्रियं मनः वा येन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितामित्र|जितामित्रः
जितामित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Triumphing, victorious over an enemy.
	 m.
(-त्रः) VIṢṆU.
 E. जित subdued, by whom, and अमित्र a foe. जितः
अमित्रः येन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितारि|जितारिः
जितारि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि) Victorious, triumphant.
	 m. (-रिः)
	 1. A Jina or
Jaina deified saint.
	 2. The father of SAMBHAVA, the third of the
Jaina pontiffs of this age.
	 3. A conqueror.
 E. जित conquered, (by
whom,) and अरि an enemy.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताहव|जिताहवः
जिताहव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Victorious, triumphant.
 E. जित conquered, and
and आहव war, battle. जितः शत्रुः आहवे येन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रिय|जितेंद्रिय|जितेन्द्रियः
जितेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Having subdued the senses, calm, unmoved.
m. (-यः) An ascetic, a sage, one who has completely subdued his
passions.
 E. जित subdued, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense. जितानि वशीकृतानि
इन्द्रियाणि येन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रियत्व
जितेन्द्रियत्व n. (-त्वं) Continece, subjugation of the senses or passions.
 E. त्व added to the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्तम|जित्तमः
जित्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Most victorious, first of the victors.
	 m. (-मः) The
constellation, Gemini.
 E. जित, and तमप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्य|जित्यः
जित्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Conquerable, vincible.
	 m. (-त्वः) A harrow.
	 f. (-त्या)
A ploughshare.
 E. जि to excel, क्यप् affix, तुक् augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वर|जित्वरः
जित्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Victorious, triumphant.
	 f. (-री) The city of
Benares.
 E. जि to conquer or excel, क्वरप् affix, तुक् inserted, fem.
affix ङीप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वा
जित्वा ind. Having conquered or excelled.
 E. जि to conquer, क्त्वाच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन|जिनः
जिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Victorious, triumphant.
	 m. (-नः)
	 1. A Jina,
the generic name of the personage peculiar to the Jaina sect,
who is ranked by them as superior to the gods of the other
sects: a saint and teacher: twenty-four Jinas are supposed to
flourish in an Avasarpiṇī or Jaina age, and their writers enumer-
ate those of the ages past, present, and to come.
	 2. A Buddha; a
generic term applied to the chief saints of the Buddha sect, in
the same manner as to those of the Jainas.
	 3. A name of VIṢṆU.
4. A very old man.
	 5. A sage, one who is omniscient.
 E. जि to
conquer or excel, नक् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनयोनि|जिनयोनिः
जिनयोनि m. (-निः) A deer.
 E. अजिन the skin of a deer, and योनि a place
of production; the initial of the first word rejected; also
अजिनयोनि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनसद्मन्
जिनसद्मन् n. (-द्म) A Jaina temple, or monastery.
 E. जिन a Jina, and सद्मन् abode.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनेन्द्र|जिनेंद्र|जिनेन्द्रः
जिनेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A Jaina or Jina saint.
 E. जिन a Jaina teacher, and
इन्द्र a lord or master.
