टुण्टुक|टुंटुक|टुण्टुकः
टुण्टुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Low, little, vile.
	 2. Cruel, harsh.
	 m. (-कः)
1. A plant, (Bigonia Indica.)
	 2. A black species of catechu.
	 3. A
small bird, (Silvia sutoria.)
	 f. (-का) A plant, commonly Akanadhi:
see टङ्गिनी.
 E. टुण्टु imitative sound, and क what utters.
