<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्द्रन
तान्द्रन m. (-नः) Wind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप m. (-पः)
	 1. Heat, burning, (moral or physical.)
	 2. Pain, sorrow,
distress.
 E. तप् to burn or inflame, affix घञ्.
	 f. (-पी) A name of
the Tapti or Surat river.
	 2. A name of the Yamuna or Jamna
river.
 E. तप the sun, affix of descent अच्, ङीष् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापक|तापकः
तापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Burning, inflaming, heating.
	 m. (-कः) Fever,
morbid heat.
 E. तप् to burn, ण्वुल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्य|तापत्यः
तापत्य m. (-त्यः) ARJUNA.
 E. तपती, and ण्य affix of descent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) What heats or inflames.
	 m. (-नः)
	 1. The sun.
2. Of KĀMA^1'S arrows, the inflamer.
	 3. Sun-shine.
	 4. Heating, in-
flaming.
 E. तप् to heat, in the causal form, and णिच् and भावे
ल्युट् affs. or तापि-कर्त्तरि ल्यु । सूर्य्ये ।
[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/264.
