ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|तांबूलिकः|ताम्बूलिकः
ताम्बूलिक mf. (-कः-की) A seller of betel.
 E. ताम्बूल, and ठक् aff. ताम्बूलं
तद्रचनं शिल्पमस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिन्|तांबूलिन्
ताम्बूलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Relating or belonging to a Pan having one,
giving one, &c.
	 m. (-ली) The Pan-bearer, a servant who prepares
and furnishes the Pan.
 E. ताम्बूल as above, इनि aff. ताम्बूलं पण्यतया
अस्ति अस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्यत्
ताम्यत् mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-म्यत्) Distressing, afflicting, annoying.
 E. तम् to
distress, शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्री-म्रं) Of a coppery red colour.
	 n. (-म्रं)
	 1. Copper.
	 2. A
kind of sandal, represented as of a dark red colour, and smelling
like a lotus.
	 3. A dark or coppery red.
	 m. (-म्रः) A leprosy with
large red spots.
	 f. (-म्री) A copper or metallic cup of prescribed
capacity, and perforated by a small hole at the bottom, answering
the purpose of an hour glass: it is put into a vessel of water;
the water gradually filling it, and the cup sinking, marks the
time that has elapsed.
 E. तम् to desire, Uṇādi affix रक्, and the
vowel made long; or ताम्र copper, अण् and ङीष् affixes, implying
analogy or derivation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रक|ताम्रकं
ताम्रक n. (-कं) Copper.
 E. ताम्र as above, and कन् pleonastic aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकर्णी
ताम्रकर्णी f. (-र्णी) A name of the female elephant of the west.
 E. ताम्र
coppery, and कर्ण ear.
