तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं|तीक्ष्णः
तीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)
	 1. Hot, warm.
	 2. Hot, pungent.
	 3. Self-devoted,
self-abandoning, committing suicide, &c.
	 4. Zealous, active, warm.
5. Keen, intelligent.
	 6. Devout, ascetic, a devotee, a zealot.
	 7.
Sharp, (as a sword.)
	 n. (-क्ष्णं)
	 1. Heat, warmth.
	 2. Poison.
	 3. Iron.
4. War, battle.
	 5. Plague, pestilence, epidemic, destruction.
	 6.
Death, dying.
	 7. Any weapon.
	 8. Haste, hurry.
	 9. Sea salt.
	 10.
The scrotum or testicles.
	 11. Any metal.
	 12. Pungency, the heat
of pepper, &c.
	 m. (-क्ष्णः) Nitre.
	 f. (-क्ष्णा)
	 1. Orris root.
	 2. The cast
skin of a snake.
 E. तिज् to sharpen or be sharp, Uṇādi affix
क्स्न ।
