<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिल|तुंदिल|तुन्दिलः
तुन्दिल See तुण्डिल, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्न|तुन्नः
तुन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)
	 1. Tormented, vexed, injured.
	 2. Cut, broken,
cut down, &c.
	 m. (-न्नः) Toon or Tuna, a tree of which the wood
bears some resemblance to mahogany, and is used for furniture,
&c. (Cedrela tunna.)
 E. तुद् to vex, affix क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नवाय|तुन्नवायः
तुन्नवाय m. (-यः) A taylor.
 E. तुन्न cut, (cloth, &c.) and वे to sew, affix अण्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नसेवनी
तुन्नसेवनी f. (-नी) A suture of the skull.
 E. तुन्न cut, and सेवनी a suture. तुन्नं
छिन्नं सीव्यते अनया सिव-करणे ल्युट् ङीष् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुप
तुप r. 1st, 6th and 10th cls. (तोपति तुपति, तोपयति) (इ) तुपि r. 1st and
10th cls. (तुम्पति, तुम्पयति-ते) To injure, to hurt or kill; also तुफ, तुम्ब,
तुम्प, &c.
 E. भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् । तुदा० बधे० सक० क्लेशे-मुचादि-पर-सेट् ।
अदने चुरा० उभ-सक-सेट् इदित् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुफ
तुफ r. 1st, 6th and 10th cls. (तोफति, तुम्फति, तोफयति-ते) To hurt or kill.
E. भ्वा-सक-सेट् । बधे सक-क्लेशे अक-तुदा-मुचा-पर-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुब
तुब(इ)तुबि r. 1st and 10th cls. (तुम्बति तुम्बयति-ते) To kill or hurt. r. 10th
cl. (तुम्बयति-ते) To disappear.
 E. भ्वा-पर-सेट् इदित् । पक्षे चुरा-उभ-सक ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुभ
तुभ r. 1st cl. (तोभते) 4th cl. (तुभ्यति) 9th cl. (तुभ्नाति) To kill, to hurt, to
injure in any manner.
 E. भ्वा-आत्म-लुङि उभ-सक-सेट् । दिवा-क्य्रा च पर-सक
सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुर|तुमुरः
तुमुर mn. (-रः-रं) Mingled combat: see तुमुल.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुल|तुमुलं|तुमुलः
तुमुल mn. (-लः-लं)
	 1. Mingled or tumultuous combat.
	 2. Uproar,
clangour, tumult, tumultuous sound or noise.
	 m. (-लः) Beleric
myrobalan.
 E. तु a Sautra root, to kill, to injure, &c. मुलक् affix;
or with the vowel long तुमूल.
	 mn. (-लः-लं) and ल being changed to
र, तुमुर as above.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्प
तुम्प r. 1st and 6th cls. (तुफति, तुम्पति)
	 1. To hurt or kill.
	 2. To be
distressed.
 E. भ्वा-सक-पर-सेट् । बधे सक-क्लेशे अक-तुदा-पर-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्फ
तुम्फ r. 1st. cl. (तुफति, तुम्फति) To hurt or kill.
 E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । बधे सक-
क्लेशे अक-तुदा-पर-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब|तुंब|तुंबः|तुम्बः
तुम्ब mf. (-म्बः-म्बा or -म्बी) A long gourd, &c. See तुम्बि.
	 f. (-म्बा) a cow
disposed to be milked.
 E. तुबि to destroy, (bile, &c.) affix अच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बक|तुम्बकः
तुम्बक m. (-कः) A long gourd.
	 n. (-कं) The gourd. कन् added to the
preceding: see तुम्बि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बि|तुंबि|तुंबिः|तुम्बिः
तुम्बि f. (-म्बिः or -तुम्बी) A long gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaris.)
 E. तुबि to
destroy, (bile, sickness, &c.) अच् affix; fem. affix इन् or ङीष् also
with कन् added तुम्बिका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बीपुष्प|तुम्बीपुष्पं
तुम्बीपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) The flower of the Cucurbita lagenaris.
 E. तुम्बी, and
पुष्प a flower.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरी
तुम्बुरी f. (-री)
	 1. Coriander.
	 2. A bitch: see तुम्बुरु.
 E. शम्यां धन्याके च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरु|तुंबुरु|तुंबुरुः|तुम्बुरुः
तुम्बुरु m. (-रुः)
	 1. One of the Gandharbas or singers of heaven.
	 2. A
celestial inhabitant and attendant upon the sanctified Jaina teach-
ers.
	 n. (-रु) Coriander.
 E. तुबि to hurt, &c. उरन् affix; also with
the pen. long तुम्बूरु.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर r. 3rd cl. (तुतोर्त्ति) To go quick, to hurry, to make haste; this root
is restricted to the Vedas: see त्वर जुहो० पर० अक० सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Quick, swift.
 E. तुर् to make haste, क aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरग|तुरगः
तुरग m. (-गः)
	 1. A horse.
	 2. The mind.
 E. त्वर speed, velocity, and ग
what goes, व changed to उ.
	 f. (-गी)
	 1. A plant, (Physalis flexuosa:)
see अश्वगन्ध.
	 2. A mare.
 E. ङीष् added to तुरग तुरेण वेगेन गच्छति गम-ड ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगगन्धा
तुरगगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant: see the preceding.
 E. तुरग a horse, and गन्ध
smell, smelling like a horse; also अश्वगन्ध, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यक|तुरगब्रह्मचर्यक|तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यकं
तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यक n. (-कं) Necessary celibacy, leading a life of continence, in
consequence merely of being without female society.
 E. तुरग a horse,
and ब्रह्मचर्य्यक the practice of a religious student, one of whose
duties is continence.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगिन्
तुरगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Equestrian, riding, mounted or carried in
a horse.
	 m. (-गी) A horse-man, cavalier, &c.
 E. तुरग a horse, and
इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्ग|तुरंग|तुरंगः|तुरङ्गः
तुरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)
	 1. A horse.
	 2. The mind, considerd as the seat of feeling
as well as intellect, the heart.
 E. त्वर speedily, and ग what goes.
	 f.
(-ङ्गी)
	 1. A plant: see तुरगी and तुरगगन्धा.
	 2. A mare.
 E. ङीष् added
to the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गक|तुरंगक|तुरंगकः|तुरङ्गकः
तुरङ्गक m. (-कः) A plant, a kind of Ghosha, commonly हस्तिधोष.
 E. तुरङ्ग
a horse, and कन् affix analogy; coursing through the body.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गद्विषणी|तुरंगद्विषणी
तुरङ्गद्विषणी f. (-णी) A she buffalo.
 E. तुरङ्ग, and द्विषणी disliking.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गप्रिय|तुरंगप्रिय|तुरङ्गप्रियः
तुरङ्गप्रिय m. (-यः) Barley.
 E. तुरङ्ग, and प्रिय fond of.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गम|तुरंगम|तुरंगमः|तुरङ्गमः
तुरङ्गम m. (-मः) A horse.
 E. तुर speed, and गम् to go, with खच् and मुम्
affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
