तुरङ्गारि|तुरंगारि|तुरङ्गारिः
तुरङ्गारि m. (-रिः)
	 1. A buffalo.
	 2. Oleander.
 E. तुरङ्ग, and अरि foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गिन्|तुरंगिन्
तुरङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी)
	 1. A horse-man, a rider.
	 2. A groom.
 E. तुरङ्ग, and
इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरायण|तुरायणं|तुरायणः
तुरायण subst.
	 mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Attachment to any object or pur-
suit. adj Attached to any object or pursuit.
	 m. (-णः) A particular
sacrifice.
 E. तुर speed, haste, अय् to go, affix ल्यु; speeding towards
a given end or in a certain cause: see परायण.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
