<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरी
तुरी f. (-री)
	 1. A brush or a fibrous stick used by weavers to clean and
separate the threads of the woof.
	 2. A painter's brush, &c. see तुली.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीय|तुरीयं|तुरीयः
तुरीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fourth, a fourth.
	 m. (-यः) A fourth part, a quarter.
n. (-यं) The divine being, or universal spirit. E. irr. derived from
चतुर् four, with छ affix; also तूर्य्य and तुर्य्य । तुरीय-अच् । चतुर्णां पूरणः
चतुर् + छ आद्यलोपश्च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयभाग
तुरीयभाग m. (-गः) A fourth part or share.
 E. तुरीय, and भाग share.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयभाज्
तुरीयभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) A sharer of a fourth.
 E. तुरीय, and भाज् who
divides.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयवर्ण|तुरीयवर्णः
तुरीयवर्ण m. (-र्णः) The Śūdra or fourth tribe of the Hindus.
 E. तुरीय
fourth, and वर्ण tribe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयांश
तुरीयांश m. (-शः) A fourth part, a quarter share.
 E. तरीय, and अंश a share.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरुष्क|तुरुष्कः
तुरुष्क m. (-ष्कः)
	 1. Incense.
	 2. A country, or m. plu. (-ष्काः) 1ts inhabit-
ants; Turan or Turkestan, the original country of the Turks. E.
तुर् to haste, (into smoke, &c.) affix उसिक्, and कन् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्य्य|तुर्य|तुर्य्यः
तुर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Fourth. E. irr. derived from चतुर् four, with यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व|तुर्व्व
तुर्व(ई)तुर्वी r. 1st cl. (तुर्वति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.
 E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व्वसु|तुर्वसु|तुर्व्वसुः
तुर्व्वसु m. (-सुः) One of the sons of YAYATI, king of the south and
eastern portion of India, reigning over the Mleccha tribes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल
तुल r. 1st and 10th cls. (तोलति तुलति तोलयति-ते or irr. तुलयति) To weigh
or measure.
 E. भ्वा-पर-सक-सेट् । पक्षे-चुरा-उभ० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलयित्वा
तुलयित्वा ind. Having weighed, having counterpoised, mode equal or like,
&c.
 E. तुल् to weigh, क्त्वा. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसारिणी
तुलसारिणी f. (-णी) A quiver.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसी
तुलसी f. (-सी) A small shrub held in veneration by the Hindus, Tulasi
or holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)
 E. तुला resemblance, and षो to
destroy, affixes ङ and ङीप्; being unparalleled: this plant is said
to be a female metamorphosed. तुलां सादृश्यं स्यति सो-क गौरा० ङीष् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुला
तुला f. (-ला)
	 1. Measure by weight.
	 2. A measure or weight of gold and
silver, 100 Palas, or about 145 ounces troy.
	 3. Any balance, es-
pecially a fine balance, goldsmith's or assay scales.
	 4. The sign of
the zodiac, Libra.
	 5. Resemblance, likeness, equality, similarity.
6. A vessel.
	 7. Sloping beams or timbers in the roof of a house.
E. तुल् to weigh or to resemble, affix अङ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाकोटि|तुलाकोटिः
तुलाकोटि f. (-टिः-टी)
	 1. An ornament of the feet or toes.
	 2. A certain
weight.
	 3. A hundred millions.
 E. तुला a balance, कुट् to measure,
affixes अङ् and इन् or ङीप्; what is valued by weight, &c. or तुला
a measure, &c. and कोटि Crore, or million. तुलया तुलां वा कोटयति कुट
परितापे इन् वा ङीप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाकोश|तुलाकोशः
तुलाकोश m. (-शः) A sort of ordeal, in which the accused is tried by
being weighed repeatedly in a scale: if he is lighter the second
time he is pronounced innocent; if equipoised still, or heavier, he
is guilty.
 E. तुला a scale, and कोश ordeal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधट|तुलाधटः
तुलाधट m. (-टः)
	 1. An oar, a paddle.
	 2. The scale or cup of a balance. E.
तुला, and धट a scale. तुलायै तोलनाय धटः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधर|तुलाधरः
तुलाधर m. (-रः) The sun.
 E. तुला the sign, and धर who has or possesses.
तुलाया मानदण्डस्य धरः धृ-अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधार|तुलाधारः
तुलाधार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A trader, a dealer, trafficking, trading.
	 m. (-रः)
1. The sign Libra.
	 2. The string of a balance.
	 3. The beam.
 E. तुला
the scales, &c. आधार what or who supports.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापरीक्षा
तुलापरीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Ordeal by the balance, the weight of the accused
being first taken, certain prayers and ceremonies are performed,
after which he is weighed again: if lighter, he is innocent, if heavy,
or as at first, guilty.
 E. तुला, and परीक्षा test.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुष|तुलापुरुषः
तुलापुरुष m. (-षः) A person weighed in a balance, or an effigy of him
used as a weight.
 E. तुला, and पुरुष a man.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुषदान|तुलापुरुषदानं
तुलापुरुषदान n. (-नं) Gift of gold or valuables of the weight of the donor.
E. तुलापुरुष, and दान gift.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाप्रग्रह|तुलाप्रग्रहः
तुलाप्रग्रह m. (-हः) The string of a balance.
 E. तुला, and प्रग्रह holding; also तुलाप्रग्राह ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलामान
तुलामान n. (-नं) Measure by weight.
 E. तुला, and मान measure.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलावीज|तुलावीजं
तुलावीज n. (-जं) The Gunja or berry of the Abrus precatorius, from
which the goldsmith's or jeweller's weight in India is taken; the
berry weighs about 1(5/16) grain troy, the factitious weight about
2(3/16).
 E. तुला weight, and वीज seed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलासूत्र
तुलासूत्र n. (-त्रं) The string of a balance.
 E. तुला, and सूत्र thread.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलि|तुलिः
तुलि f. (-लिः or -ली)
	 1. A fibrous stick or brush used by weavers for
cleaning the threads of the woof.
	 2. A painter's brush, or fibrous
stick used for that purpose: see तूलिका,
 E. तुल् to resemble, &c. affix
क, fem. affix इन् or ङीष्; also with ल changed to र, तुरि, तुरी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिका
तुलिका f. (-का) A small bird said to resemble the wagtail.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलित
तुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Made equal or like, equalled, compared.
	 2.
Weighed, counterpoised.
 E. तुल् to weigh, णिच् and कर्मणि क्त affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिफला
तुलिफला f. (-ला) The Simul or silk-cotton tree.
 E. तुलि for तूलि cotton,
and फल fruit. तुलि तुलयुक्तं फलमस्याः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्य|तुल्यः
तुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Like, resembling, equal or analogous to.
 E. तुला
resemblance, and यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यता
तुल्यता f. (-ता) Likeness, sameness, equality.
 E. तल् added to the last;
also with त्व, तुल्यत्वं.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यपान|तुल्यपानं
तुल्यपान n. (-नं) Drinking together.
 E. तुल्य alike, and पान drinking.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यबल
तुल्यबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of equal strength.
 E. तुल्य, and बल strength.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यभावन
तुल्यभावन n. (-नं) Combination of like series, (in calculation.)
 E. तुल्य, and
भावन computing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यरूप
तुल्यरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)
	 1. Like, similar, analogous.
	 2. Of like or equal
form.
 E. तुल्य, and रूप nature, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यवृत्ति
तुल्यवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Following the same or similar occupation.
E. तुल्य, and वृत्ति business.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यशुद्धि
तुल्यशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Equal substraction, transposition, (in Arithmetic.) E.
तुल्य, शुद्धि substraction.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्याकृति
तुल्याकृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Alike, of the same form.
 E. तुल्य, and आकृति
form.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवर|तुवरः
तुवर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)
	 1. Astringent.
	 2. Beardless.
	 mn. (-रः-रं) An astringent
taste.
	 f. (-री)
	 1. A fragrant earth.
	 2. A kind of lentil, (Cytisus
cajan:) see आढकी.
 E. तु a Sautra root, to remove, (disease, &c.)
ष्वरच् and affix ङीष्; also कन् being added, in the fem. form तुवरिका
f. (-का.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
