त्रिगत
त्रिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Tripled.
	 2. Gone or done in three ways.
	 n.
(-तं) The expression of different senses by the same word.
 E. त्रि,
and गत gone.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त्त|त्रिगर्त|त्रिगर्त्तः
त्रिगर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)
	 1. A country in the north-west division of India, or m.
plu. (-र्त्ताः) Its inhabitants: apparently part of Lahore, said, by
Mr. WILFORD, to be the modern Tahora, but differently described
in the Koshas: see जालन्धर and वालहीक.
	 2. A form of calculation,
(गणितान्तरे.)
	 f. (-र्त्ता)
	 1. A small worm.
	 2. A lascivious woman, a
wanton.
	 3. A woman in general.
	 4. A pearl.
 E. त्रि three, and गर्त्त
a hole, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त्तक|त्रिगर्तक|त्रिगर्त्तकः
त्रिगर्त्तक m. (-कः) A country, the same as Valhika: see वाल्हीक.
 E. कन्
added to the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुण|त्रिगुणं
त्रिगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं)
	 1. Thrice, three times, triple.
	 2. Possessing
the three Gunas or properties.
	 n. (-णं) The aggregate of the three
qualities incident to human nature.
 E. त्रि three, गुण a time or
property.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणाकृत|त्रिगुणाकृतं
त्रिगुणाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)
 E. त्रिगुण three
times, and आकृत made, wrought.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगूढ
त्रिगूढ n. (-ढं) The dancing or acting of a man in female attire.
 E. त्रि,
and गूढ concealed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचतुर
त्रिचतुर mfn. plur. (-राः-राः-राणि) Three or four.
 E. त्रि, and चतुर् four,
अच added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजातक|त्रिजातकं
त्रिजातक n. (-कं) Three spices collectively, mace, cardamoms, and
cassia leaf.
 E. त्रि, and जातक species.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिज्या
त्रिज्या f. (-ज्या) A radius, a sine of three signs or ninety degrees.
 E. त्रि,
and ज्या a sine.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिण|त्रिणं
त्रिण n. (-णं) Grass, meadow grass. E. See तृण, ऋ being changed to रि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणता
त्रिणता f. (-ता)
	 1. A bow.
	 2. The state or abstract property of grass.
E. त्रिण for तृण grass. and तल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणाचिकेत|त्रिणाचिकेतः
त्रिणाचिकेत n. (-तं) A portion of the Yajur Veda.
	 m. (-तः) A follower of
that branch of the Vedas. It is also sometimes read तृणाचिकेत ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितक्ष|त्रितक्षं
त्रितक्ष nf. (-क्षं-क्षी) An assemblage of three carpenters.
 E. त्रि three, तक्ष
a carpenter, affix अच् समा० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितय|त्रितयं
त्रितय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Third.
 E. त्रि three, तयप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्ड|त्रिदंड|त्रिदण्डः
त्रिदण्ड n. (-ण्डं)
	 1. Three staves collectively.
	 2. Triple subjection of
words, thoughts, and acts; the state of a religious ascetic.
 E. त्रि
three, दण्ड a staff, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डधारण
त्रिदण्डधारण n. (-णं) Carrying three staves tied together, (as done by
some mendicants.)
 E. त्रिदण्ड, and धारण holding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डिन्|त्रिदंडिन्
त्रिदण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी)
	 1. A wandering devotee, one who carries three long
bamboo staves in his right hand.
	 2. The religious man who has ob-
tained a command over his words, thoughts, and actions, or mind,
body, and speech.
 E. त्रि three, and दण्ड a punishment, a staff, &c.
इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदला
त्रिदला f. (-ला) A creeping plant, (Cissus pedata.)
 E. त्रि three, and दल
a leaf.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रिदश m. (-शः) A god, a deity, an immortal.
 E. त्रि the third, and दशा
state, being, (youth;) enjoying perpetual youth, or त्रि three, and
दश state, subject as well as mortals to the three conditions, of
birth, being, and destruction.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रिदश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Thirteenth.
	 f. (-शी) The thirteenth day of the
fortnight; also त्रयोदश ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशदीर्घिका
त्रिदशदीर्घिका f. (-का) The heavenly Ganges.
 E. त्रिदश a deity, and दीर्घिका
a long pool.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशन्
त्रिदशन् mfn. plu. (-श) Thirteen.
 E. त्रि three, and दशन् ten.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशनदी
त्रिदशनदी f. (-दी) The heavenly Ganges.
 E. त्रिदश, and नदी a river.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशपति
त्रिदशपति m. (-तिः) INDRA.
 E. त्रिदश, and पति chief.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशबधू
त्रिदशबधू f. (-धूः) A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.
 E. त्रिशद, and बधू wife.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशवनिता
त्रिदशवनिता f. (-ता) A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.
 E. त्रिदश, and वनिता
a wife.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाङ्कुश|त्रिदशांकुश
त्रिदशाङ्कुश n. (-शं) The thunderbolt.
 E. त्रिदश a deity, and अङ्कुश a goad.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाचार्य्य|त्रिदशाचार्य
त्रिदशाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The preceptor of the gods, VṚHASPATI.
 E. त्रिदश a
deity, and आचार्य्य a teacher.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशायुध|त्रिदशायुधं
त्रिदशायुध n. (-धं) The thunderbolt of INDRA.
 E. त्रिदश a deity, and आयुध
a weapon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशारि|त्रिदशारिः
त्रिदशारि m. (-रिः) An Asura or infernal being hostile to the gods, a
Titan, a Giant.
 E. त्रिदश a deity, and अरि a foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशालय|त्रिदशालयः
त्रिदशालय m. (-यः)
	 1. Svarga, INDRA'S heaven or paradise.
	 2. The moun-
tain Sumeru.
 E. त्रिदश a deity, and आलय an abode.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशावास|त्रिदशावासः
त्रिदशावास m. (-सः) Svarga, the heaven of INDRA.
 E. त्रिदश a god, and
आवास abode.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाहार|त्रिदशाहारः
त्रिदशाहार m. (-रः) Amrita or ambrosia.
 E. त्रिदश a deity, and आहार food.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदालिका
त्रिदालिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Charmaghasa.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिन
त्रिदिन n. (-नं) Three days collectively.
 E. त्रि, and दिन a day.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिनस्पृश्
त्रिदिनस्पृश् m. (-स्पृक्) Conjunction or concurrence of three lunations with
one solar day.
 E. त्रिदिन, and स्पृश् contact.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिव|त्रिदिवः
त्रिदिव mn. (-वः-वं)
	 1. Svarga or paradise.
	 2. Sky, atmosphere, heaven.
f. (-वा) The name of a river.
 E. त्रि the three, BRAMHA, VIṢṆU,
and ŚIVA, दिव् to sport, affix क; the place where these three gods
take divine pleasure.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवेश|त्रिदिवेशः
त्रिदिवेश m. (-शः) A god, a deity.
 E. त्रिदिव heaven, and ईश master or
lord.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवौकस्
त्रिदिवौकस् m. (-काः) A god, a celestial.
 E. त्रिदिव heaven, and ओकस्
asylum.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदृश्
त्रिदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Tri-ocular, three-eyed.
	 m. (-दृक्) A name of ŚIVA. E.
त्रि three, and दृश् an eye.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोष|त्रिदोषं
त्रिदोष n. (-षं) Disorder of the three humours of the body, vitiation of
the bile, blood, and phlegm.
 E. त्रि three, and दीष a fault.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषघ्न
त्रिदोषघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Correcting the vitiated state of the three hu-
mours.
 E. त्रिदोष, and घ्न what destroys.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषज|त्रिदोषजः
त्रिदोषज m. (-जः) Disease, &c. proceeding from disorder of the three hu-
mours of the body.
 E. त्रिदोष, and ज produced.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधा
त्रिधा ind. In three ways.
 E. त्रि, and धाच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधातु|त्रिधातुः
त्रिधातु m. (-तुः) A name of GANESA.
	 n. (-त) Three minerals, &c.
 E. त्रि
three, and धातु mineral, &c. त्रीन् धर्मार्थकामान् दधाति पुष्णाति धा-तुन् ।
