त्रिपुण्ड्र n. (-ण्ड्रं) Three curved horizontal marks, made across the fore-
head with cowdung, &c.; they are worn especially by the fol-
lowers of ŚIVA, or SAKTI, and are indispensable in proceeding to
worship the former.
 E. त्रि three, triple, and पुण्ड्र a line; also with
