त्रिपुर|त्रिपुरं|त्रिपुरः
त्रिपुर nf. (-रं-री)
	 1. The three cities gold, silver and iron erected by the
demon Maya and burnt down by ŚIVA.
	 2. A district, the modern
Tipperah, &c.
	 m. (-रः) The name of an Asura, and king of
Tripura.
 E. त्रि three, and पुर a city, the district and dominion of
that Asura, consisting of three strong and famous cities.
