त्रिवर्ग|त्रिवर्गः
त्रिवर्ग m. (-र्गः)
	 1. Three human objects or pursuits as love, duty, and
wealth.
	 2. Three conditions of a king or state; prosperity, even-
ness, and decay; or loss, gain, equality, &c.
	 3. The three qualities
of nature, purity, blindness, and depravity.
	 4. The three myroba-
lans.
	 5. The three spices: see त्रिकटु.
	 6. propriety, good behavior.
