<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्गपारीण
त्रिवर्गपारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having passed through the three condi-
tions, or attained the three objects of life.
 E. त्रिवर्ग, and पारीण
gone to the opposite shore.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्णक|त्रिवर्णकं
त्रिवर्णक n. (-कं)
	 1. The three myrobalans.
	 2. The three spices.
	 3. A
plant, (Ruellia longifolia:) see गीक्षुरक.
 E. त्रि three, वर्ण a class, and
कन् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्षिका
त्रिवर्षिका f. (-का) A three years old heifer.
 E. त्रि, and वर्ष a year, affix ठन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवली
त्रिवली f. (-ली) Three folds of skin on the abdomen, from obesity.
 E. त्रि,
and वली a wrinkle.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविक्रम|त्रिविक्रमः
त्रिविक्रम m. (-मः) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. त्रि, and विक्रम going; crossing
over the three worlds in three steps, to the discomfiture of BALI.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविद्या
त्रिविद्या f. (-द्या) Three branches of knowledge, especially that of the
three Vedas.
 E. त्रि, and विद्या knowledge.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविध
त्रिविध mfn. (धः-धा-धं) In three ways, of three kinds.
 E. त्रि, and विध sort.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टप|त्रिविष्टपं
त्रिविष्टप n. (-पं)
	 1. Heaven or paradise.
	 2. The three worlds, or heaven,
earth, and hell: see त्रिपिष्टप ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टपसद्
त्रिविष्टपसद् m. (-सद्) A deity; also त्रिपिष्टपसद् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्
त्रिवृत् mfn. (-वृत्) Triple, triform, threefold.
	 m. (-वृत्)
	 1. A plant of
valuable purgative properties, commonly called Teori, and distin-
guished into two species, white and black, (Convolvulus turpe-
thum.)
	 2. Combining any thing by three.
	 3. A triple cord, a girdle,
&c. of three strings.
	 4. A kind of sacrifice.
 E. त्रि three, (three seed
vessels,) वृ to cherish, affix क्विप्, and तुक् added: also with टाप्
added त्रिवृता f. (-ता.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्करण|त्रिवृत्करणं
त्रिवृत्करण n. (-णं) Combining earth, water, and fire, in the proportion of
half of one with a quarter of each of the others.
 E. त्रिवृत्, and करण
making.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्पर्णी
त्रिवृत्पर्णी f. (-र्णी) A potherb, (Hilancha repens.)
 E. त्रिवृत् Teori, and पर्ण
a leaf; having similar leaves.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणी
त्रिवेणी f. (-णी) A name of the Ganges.
 E. त्रि three, वेणी a braid of hair:
the name is especially applied to the river at Allahabad, where it
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">Page326-a+ 60</a>]
receives the Jumuna, and is supposed to receive under ground the
Sarasvatī; it is also that of a village in Bengal, above Hugli.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेद|त्रिवेदः
त्रिवेद n. (-दं) The three Vedas collectively.
 E. त्रि, and वेद a Veda.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेदिन्
त्रिवेदिन् m. (-दी) A Bramhan acquainted with three Vedas.
 E. त्रिवेद, and
इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कु|त्रिशंकु|त्रिशङ्कुः
त्रिशङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)
	 1. The name of a king of the solar race, famous for
attempting to go to heaven in his mortal frame, by the aid of
VISWAMITRA.
	 2. A cat.
	 3. A grasshopper.
	 4. A bird, the Chataka,
(Cuculus melanoleucos.)
	 5. A fire-fly.
 E. त्रि three, शङ्कु a dart, ट aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुज|त्रिशंकुज|त्रिशङ्कुजः
त्रिशङ्कुज m. (-जः) A name of HARISCHANDRA, a prince.
 E. त्रिशङ्कु, and ज
born, descended from TRISANKU.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुयाजिन्|त्रिशंकुयाजिन्
त्रिशङ्कुयाजिन् m. (-जी) VISWAMITRA, a celebrated sage and saint.
 E. त्रिशङ्कु
the king so named, and याजिन् causing to worship; being the
family priest of the monarch.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशरण|त्रिशरणः
त्रिशरण m. (-णः) A Jina, a sanctified teacher of the Jaina sect.
 E. त्रि
three, (the three worlds,) and शरण protection.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशला
त्रिशला f. (-ला) The mother of VARDDHAMANA, the last of the Jaina
pontiffs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिख|त्रिशिखं|त्रिशिखः
त्रिशिख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Three-crested, three-headed.
	 n. (-खं)
	 1. A crest,
a tiara with three points.
	 2. A trident, a three pronged spear.
	 m.
(-खः) The son of RAVANA, a demon with three heads.
 E. त्रि three,
and शिखा a crest.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिरस्
त्रिशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Three-headed.
	 m. (-राः) A name of KUVERA.
2. Fever personified as a demon with three heads: see त्रिपाद.
	 3. A
son of RAVANA.
 E. त्र three, and शिरस् a head.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशीर्षक|त्रिशीर्षकं
त्रिशीर्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Three-headed.
	 m. (-कः) A trident, tri-pointed
spear.
 E. त्रि three, and शीर्ष a head, affix कन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूल|त्रिशूलं
त्रिशूल n. (-लं) A trident, a three-pointed pike or spear, especially the
weapon of ŚIVA.
 E. त्रि three or Tri, and शूल a dar.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूलिन्
त्रिशूलिन् m. (-ली) A name of ŚIVA.
 E. त्रिशूल, and इनि affix, armed with
a trident.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशृङ्ग|त्रिशृंग|त्रिशृङ्गः
त्रिशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)
	 1. A hill with three peaks.
	 2. A triangle.
 E. त्रि three,
and शृङ्ग a horn.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशृङ्गिन्
त्रिशृङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A sort of fish, commonly Rohi, (Cyprinus rohita,
HAM.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषवण
त्रिषवण n. (-णं) The three ablutions to be performed in the day or at
dawn, noon, and sunset.
 E. त्रि three, षवन bathing; also read
त्रिसवन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषवणस्नायिन्
त्रिषवणस्नायिन् m. (-यी) A man performing regularly the prescribed ablu-
tions, at morning, noon, and night.
 E. त्रि three, सवन time or period
of ablution, and स्नायिन् who bathes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिष्टुभ्
त्रिष्टुभ् f. (-ष्टुप्) A form of metre, the stanza consisting of four lines of
eleven syllables each, or of five lines, one of eleven and four of
eight each, forming altogether forty-four syllables; there are other
varieties.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिष्ठ
त्रिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Situated in three places.
 E. त्रि, and स्था to be, क
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसन्ध्य|त्रिसंध्य|त्रिसन्ध्यं
त्रिसन्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या or न्ध्यी-न्ध्यं) The three periods of the day, or dawn,
noon, and eve.
 E. त्रि three, and सन्ध्य either of the periods.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसम|त्रिसमं
त्रिसम n. (-मं) An aggregate of three like or equal things.
 E. त्रि, and सम
same.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसर|त्रिसरः
त्रिसर subst.
	 mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A dish of sesamum, rice, &c.
 E. त्रि three,
threefold, and सर what is, from सृ to go or get, affix अप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसवन|त्रिसवनं
त्रिसवन n. (-नं) Bathing thrice: see त्रिषवण ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसीत्य|त्रिसीत्यं
त्रिसीत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)
 E. त्रि thrice, and
सीत्य ploughed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्ण|त्रिसुपर्णः
त्रिसुपर्ण m. (-र्णः)
	 1. A portion of the Rig and Yajur Vedas.
	 2. A ob-
servance enjoined by it.
	 3. A Brahman following it.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्णिक
त्रिसुपर्णिक m. (-कः) A Tri Suparna Brahman: see the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्रोतस्
त्रिस्रोतस् f. (-ताः)
	 1. The Ganges.
	 2. Another river.
 E. त्रि three, and
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">Page326-b+ 60</a>]
स्रोतस् a river, the river of the three worlds, or one with three
channels.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहल्य|त्रिहल्यं
त्रिहल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)
 E. त्रि thrice, हल्य
ploughed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहायण
त्रिहायण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Three years, (old, &c.)
	 f. (-णी) A three-years-
old heifer.
 E. त्रि, and हायन a year; also read त्रिहायन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुट
त्रुट r. 4th cl. (त्रुट्यति) r. 6th cl. (त्रुटति) and 10th cl. (त्रोटयते) To cut,
literally or metaphorically; to cut, (wood, &c.) to cut or solve,
(difficulties, doubts, &c.) दिवा० तुदा० प० अक० सेट् । चुरा० आत्म० सक०
सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिटि
त्रिटि f. (-टिः-टी)
	 1. Cutting, breaking.
	 2. Loss, destruction.
	 3. Breaking
a promise, &c.
	 4. Small cardamoms, (Alpinia cardamomum).
5. A short time, a moment.
	 6. Doubt, uncertainty.
	 7. (Always
feminine, though used attributively.) Little, small.
	 8. An
atom, or a visible atom composed of three subtler elementary par-
ticles.
 E. त्रुट् to cut or divide, affix इन् and ङीप् optionally added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटित
त्रुटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Cut, broken, divided.
	 2. Hurt, wounded.
 E. त्रुट,
and क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटितवत्
त्रुटितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Chapped, chafed, cut.
 E. त्रुट, and क्तवतु
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटिवीज|त्रुटिवीजः
त्रुटिवीज m. (-जः) An esculent root: see कचु.
 E. त्रुटि small, and वीज
a seed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुप
त्रुप r. 1st cl. (त्रोपति) To hurt, to injure or kill.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुफ
त्रुफ r. 1st cl. (त्रोफति) To hurt, to kill or injure; also तुफ, तुम्फ, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्प
त्रुम्प r. 1st cl. (त्रुम्पति) To hurt or injure: see तुप, तुम्प, &c. भ्वा० पर० सक०
सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्फ
त्रुम्फ r. 1st cl. (त्रुम्फति) To kill or injure; also त्रुफ, &c. भ्वा० पर० सक०
सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेता
त्रेता f. (-ता)
	 1. The second Yuga or age of the Hindus, consisting of
1,296,000 years.
	 2. The three sacred fires collectively, or the
southern, household, and sacrificial fires.
 E. त्र preservation, &c.
derived from त्रै to preserve, इत obtained, got.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेताग्नि
त्रेताग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A man who has preserved the three sacred fires.
 E. त्रेता
as above, and अग्नि fire.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेतायुग|त्रेतायुगं
त्रेतायुग n. (-गं) The second or Treta age.
 E. त्रेता, and युग age.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेधा
त्रेधा ind. Triple, threefold, in three ways.
 E. त्रि three, धा affix, and ए
substituted for the vowel.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रै
त्रै (ङ) त्रैङ् r. 1st cl. (त्रायते) To preserve, to protect, to cherish, to de-
fend, &c.
 E. भ्वा० आ० सक० अनिट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुणिक
त्रैगुणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Giving three times, relating to thrice, three
qualities, &c.
 E. त्रिगुण, and ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुण्य|त्रैगुण्यं
त्रैगुण्य n. (-ण्यं)
	 1. The quality of three Gunas or properties collectively.
2. A trine, a multiplication by three.
 E. त्रिगुण, and ष्यञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैदशिक
त्रैदशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sacred to the gods, belonging or relating to
them. त्रिदश, and ठञ् aff. त्रिदशा देवता अस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधम्
त्रैधम् ind. In three ways, threefold.
 E. त्रि three, धमञ् affix; also ड
being added, the word becomes an attributive, and may be in-
flected in the three genders, also त्रैध, mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुर|त्रैपुरः
त्रैपुर m. (-रः) Tripura or Tipperah: see त्रिपुर.
 E. स्वार्थे अण् added to त्रिपुर ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=326-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैराशिक|त्रैराशिकं
त्रैराशिक mf. (-कः-का) (In Arithmetic,) The rule of three: it is of two
kinds क्रमत्रैराशिकः Rule of three direct, व्यस्त or विलोमत्रैराशिकः Rule
of three inverse.
 E. त्रि three, राशि quantity, ठञ् aff.
