थुर्व|थुर्व्व
थुर्व (ई) थुर्वी r. 1st cl. (थुर्वति) To kill, to injure or hurt. भ्वा-पर-सक-
सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थोडन|थोडनं
थोडन n. (-नं) Covering, clothing, wrapping up.
 E. थुड्, and ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द The third letter of the dental class, and eighteenth consonant in
the Deva Nagari alphabet, corresponding to the letter D.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द n. (-दं) A wife.
	 nf. (दंदा)
	 1. Gift, donation.
	 2. Dividing, cutting,
breaking, &c.
	 f. (दा)
	 1. Purifying, cleansing.
	 2. Preserving, cherish-
ing.
	 3. Repentance.
	 m. (दः)
	 1. A donor, a giver.
	 2. A mountain.
3. A gift, a thing given.
 E. दा to give, or दो to cut, &c. affix ड.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश r. 1st cl. (दंशति) To bite, to sting.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश m. (-शः)
	 1. A gadfly.
	 2. A tooth.
	 3. Biting, stinging.
	 4. Armour,
mail.
	 5. Cutting, dividing, tearing.
	 6. Fault, defect.
	 7. A joint, a
limb.
	 8. The sting of a snake.
	 9. Pungency.
	 f. (-शी) A small gadfly.
E. दंश् to bite or sting, affix अच्, diminutive affix ङीष् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशक|दंशकः
दंशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What bites or stings.
	 m. (-कः) A gadfly.
 E. दंश-
ण्वुल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन n. (-नं)
	 1. Biting, stinging.
	 2. Armour, mail.
 E. दंश् to bite, &c.
भावे ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशभीरु|दंशभीरुः
दंशभीरु m. (-रुः) A buffalo.
 E. दंश a gadfly, and भीरु afraid of; also with
कन् added, दंशभीरुक m. (-कः) दंशात् भीरुः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशमूल|दंशमूलः
दंशमूल m. (-लः) A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga.)
 E. दंश biting, and
मूल a root; the root of this plant is substituted in Bengal for
horseradish.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Armed, mailed.
	 2. Bitten, stung.
 E. दंश armour,
and इतच् affix, or दंश to bite, affix इतच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशेर
दंशेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Mischievous, noxious.
 E. दंश् to bite or sting,
Uṇādi affix एरच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रा
दंष्ट्रा f. (-ष्ट्रा) A large tooth, a tusk.
 E. दंश् to bite, affix ष्ट्रन्, and टाप् fem.
aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिका
दंष्ट्रिका f. (-का) The beard.
 E. दंष्ट्रा a tooth, इकन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन् mfn. (-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रिणी-ष्ट्रि)
	 1. Biting or wounding with the teeth, (any
animal, &c.)
	 2. Tusked, having tusks or sharp teeth.
	 3. Carnivo-
rous.
	 m. (-ष्ट्री)
	 1. A hog.
	 2. A snake.
 E. दंष्ट्रा a tooth, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसन|दंसनं
दंसन n. (-नं) Armour, mail: see दंशन ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक|दकं
दक n. (-कं) Water. E. See उदक, the initial vowel being dropped.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष r. 1st cl. (दक्षते)
	 1. To grow or increase.
	 2. To dispatch, to expedite,
to do quickly.
	 3. To go, to move.
	 4. To hurt or kill. भ्वा-आ-अक-सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Clever, able, dexterous.
	 m. (-क्षः)
	 1. A Bramhadika;
according to one legend, son of BRAMHA, born from the thumb of
his right hand, for the purpose of peopling the world: according
to another, he is the son of the Munis, called Prachetasas. DAKṢA,
had sixty daughters, of whom twenty-seven are the nymphs who
form the lunar asterisms, and wives of the Moon; one of his
daughters also SATI or DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA; and seventeen
were married to KAŚYAPA, and were the mothers of all created
beings. DAKṢA was on one occasion decapitated by ŚIVA: see
दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्; he is sometimes regarded as an Avatara of Bramha
himself.
	 2. A Muni and legislator, who flourished in the beginning
of the Treta Yuga.
	 3. A kind of tree.
	 4. The bull of ŚIVA.
	 5. A
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">Page329-a+ 60</a>]
cock.
	 6. A scholar, a Pandit.
	 7. A dexterous or clever man.
	 8. ŚIVA.
9. A name of Agni or fire.
	 10. A general lover, one attached to
many mistresses.
	 f. (-क्षा) The earth.
 E. दक्ष् to grow or increase,
affix कर्त्तरि अच ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=328-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षकन्या
दक्षकन्या f. (-न्या)
	 1. A name of DURGĀ.
	 2. Any lunar mansion.
 E. दक्ष,
and कन्या the maiden, the daughter of DAKṢA, who in this case
seems to be identified with Himālaya, the snowy mountain.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजा
दक्षजा f. (-जा)
	 1. The goddes DURGĀ.
	 2. A lunar asterism.
 E. दक्ष, and
जा born: see the preceding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजापति|दक्षजापतिः
दक्षजापति m. (-तिः)
	 1. The moon.
	 2. The deity ŚIVA.
 E. दक्षजा a lunar
asterism or DURGĀ, and पति husband.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षता
दक्षता f. (-ता) Dexterity, cleverness.
 E. तल् added to दक्ष; also with
त्व, दक्षत्वम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षयज्ञ
दक्षयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The sacrifice made by DAKṢA.
 E. दक्ष, and यज्ञ sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी
दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.
 E. दक्षयज्ञ, and विनाशिनी destructress.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षसावर्णि|दक्षसावर्णिः
दक्षसावर्णि m. (-र्णिः) The ninth Manu.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्
दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत् m. (-कृत्) A name of ŚIVA.
 E. दक्ष the Bramhadika, as
DAKṢA, अध्वर a sacrifice, ध्वंसकृत् subduer or disturber: DAKṢA
having on one occasion made a sacrifice, to which he invited all
the gods, except his son-in-law ŚIVA, and his wife SATI, the latter
went unbid, and being received coolly, threw herself into the fire;
This being informed siva, tore off a lock of his hair and cast it vio-
lently on the ground. It started up into being a demon named
Birbhadra who being ordered by siva proceeded against DAKṢA,
and an affray ensued, in which the gods and Ṛṣis were maltreated
and dispersed, and DAKṢA decapitated; he was restored to life,
and the head of a ram substituted for the one he had lost.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाय्य|दक्षाय्यः
दक्षाय्य m. (-य्यः)
	 1. The bird of VIṢṆU, Garuḍa.
	 2. A vulture.
 E. दक्ष् to
hurt, आय्य Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)
	 1. Candid, sincere, honest, upright.
	 2. Right,
(not left.)
	 3. South, southern.
	 4. Dependent, subject.
	 5. Clever,
able, dexterous.
	 f. (-णा)
	 1. A present to Brahmans, upon solemn
or sacrificial occasions.
	 2. The south.
	 3. Completion of any rite,
fixing or establishing any act or place.
	 4. A form or figure of
DURGĀ, in which the right side is said to be advanced.
	 5. Dona-
tion to Brahmans, personified as a goddess, said to be born from
KṚṢṆA'S right side.
 E. दक्ष् to prosper, &c. Uṇādi affix इनन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणकालिका
दक्षिणकालिका f. (-का) A form of DURGĀ worshiped by the Tantrikas.
E. दक्षिण, and कालिका a form of the same.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतस्
दक्षिणतस् ind. Southward, southerly.
 E. तसि added to दक्षिण ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथ|दक्षिणापथः
दक्षिणापथ n. (-थं)
	 1. The south.
	 2. Southern road or course.
	 3. Deccan. E.
दक्षिण, and पथ for पथिन् path.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्वा|दक्षिणपूर्व्वा
दक्षिणपूर्वा f. (-र्वा) The south-east quarter.
 E. दक्षिण south and पूर्व east.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=329-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणस्थ|दक्षिणस्थः
दक्षिणस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Upon the right side, to the south, &c.
	 m.
(-स्थः) A charioteer.
 E. दक्षिण as above, and स्थ who stays or abides.
