दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)
	 1. Burnt, scorched, consumed by fire.
	 2. Tasteless.
3. A term of abuse usually prefixed to the word it vilifies.
	 f. (-ग्धा)
1. The quarter where the sun is observable.
	 2. An epithet of certain
lunations, on which it is unlucky to do any thing, and religious
rites are prohibited.
	 n. (-ग्धं) A fragrant grass.
 E. दह् to burn,
affix क्त ।
