दण्डिन् mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि) Having a staff or stick.
	 m. (-ण्डी)
	 1. A door-
keeper, a warder, a porter, a staff or mace-bearer.
	 2. A name of
YAMA.
	 3. A man of the fourth order or beggar.
	 4. A mendicant
carrying a staff.
	 5. A mendicant of a particular order, derived from
SANKARACHARYA.
	 6. A Jina or Jaina saint.
 E. दण्ड a staff, &c. and
इनि aff.
