दत्|दन्त्
दत् m. (-दन्तः-दन्तौ-दन्तः) 2nd case plu. (दतः) A tooth: see दन्त; the nasal
is dropped after the 2nd case.
 E. दम् to subdue, affix डत्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)
	 1. Given, presented, made over, assigned.
	 2.
Preserved, guarded, protected.
	 m. (-त्तः)
	 1. The name of a king.
	 2.
A saint; also दत्तात्रेय.
	 3. A common surname or title of a man of
the Vaiśya or third tribe, at present common to the Kayeth
class.
	 n. (-त्तं) A gift, a donation.
 E. दा to give, affix कर्मणि क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक|दत्तकः
दत्तक m. (-कः) A son given: see the next.
 E. कन् added to the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=330-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तकपुत्त्र
दत्तकपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A son given away by his natural parents, to persons
engaging to adopt him; one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by
the old Hindu law.
 E. दत्तक, and पुत्त्र a son; also simply दत्तक, and
sometimes दत्त्रिम.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तवत्|दत्तवन्त्
दत्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Gave, was giving.
 E. दा to give, क्तवतु aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तशुल्का
दत्तशुल्का f. (-ल्का) A bride for whom a sum of money has been paid to
her father.
 E. दत्त, and शुल्क dower.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्मन्
दत्तात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-given.
	 m. (-त्मा) A youth or orphan, who
gives himself to persons disposed to take the place of parents. E.
दत्त given, and आत्मन् self.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्रेय|दत्तात्रेयः
दत्तात्रेय m. (-यः) A sage, the son of ATRI given to him by three deities
BRAMHA, VIṢṆU and ŚIVA.
 E. दत्त, and आत्रेय son of ATRI: also
दत्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादत्त
दत्तादत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given and received.
 E. दत्त, and आदत्त taken.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादर
दत्तादर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Treated with respect.
 E. दत्त, and आदर respect.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=331-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तानपकर्म्मन्|दत्तानपकर्मन्
दत्तानपकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Nonresumption of gifts.
 E. दत्त a gift, अन for अ neg.
before अपकर्म्मन् resuming.
