दशपारमिताधर|दशपारमिताधरः
दशपारमिताधर m. (-रः) A Buddha or Bauddha saint.
 E. दश, पारमिता a
particular work or scripture of this sect, धर who has.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपुर|दशपुरं
दशपुर n. (-रं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus:) see दाशपुर.
	 2. A
district, part of Malwa or Bundelkhand.
	 3. A town or city.
 E. दश
for दाश a fisherman, and पुर or पूर to nourish, affix दश; also दश
ten, and पुर a city: district of ten cities.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपूर
दशपूर n. (-रं) A fragrant grass: see the preceding; also दाशपूर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबल|दशबलः
दशबल m. (-लः) A Buddha of Bauddha teacher.
 E. दश ten, (the ten
worlds,) बल powerful.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशभूमिग|दशभूमिगः
दशभूमिग m. (-गः) BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect, or a
Buddha, the generic name of the sanctified teachers of that sect.
E. दश ten, भूमि earth, and ग who goes; traversing the ten worlds;
also दशभूमीश m. (-शः) Lord of the same.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशम|दशमः
दशम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Tenth.
	 f. (-मी)
	 1. The tenth day of the half
month.
	 2. The tenth or last stage of human life, the last ten
years of a century.
 E. दशन् ten, and मट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमहाविद्या
दशमहाविद्या f. (-द्या) DURGĀ.
 E. दश ten, (forms, or names,) महा great,
and विद्या a name of DURGĀ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमाल
दशमाल nf. (-लं-ली) A collection of ten garlands.
 E. दश ten, माला a
garland, टच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमिन्
दशमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Very old or aged.
 E. दशमी the tenth, (stage
of life,) and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीङ्गत|दशमींगत
दशमीङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very old, above ninety.
 E. दशमी, and गत arrived at.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीस्थ|दशमीस्थः
दशमीस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)
	 1. Impotent.
	 2. Very old, turned of ninety.
	 3.
Dying, on the point of death.
 E. दशमी the last stage of life, and
स्थ who is.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुख|दशमुखः
दशमुख m. (-खः) A name of RAVANA.
 E. दश ten, and मुख a face.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुखान्तक|दशमुखान्तकः
दशमुखान्तक m. (-कः) A name of RAMA.
 E. दशमुख RAVANA, and अन्तक
destroyer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमूल|दशमूलं
दशमूल n. (-लं) A tonic medicament prepared from the roots of ten
plants.
 E. दश ten, and मूल a root.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरथ|दशरथः
दशरथ m. (-थः) A proper name, sovereign of Ayodhya or Oude,
and father of RAMA.
 E. दश ten, and रथ a car; whose car bore
him to the ten quarters of the universe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरात्र|दशरात्रः
दशरात्र n. (-त्रं) A period of ten days and nights.
 E. दश, and रात्र for
रात्रि night.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरूपभृत्
दशरूपभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) A name of VIṢṆU.
 E. दश ten, रूप forms, (Ava-
taras,) and भृत् who assumes.
