E. दाह heat, and हरण removing; this root being woven into
screens, and kept wet, for the purpose of excluding or tempering
the hot winds. दाहो ह्रियते अनेन हृ-ल्युट् and णिच् कर्त्तरि ल्यु वा ।
वीरणमूले ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह्य
दाह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be burnt, inflammable.
 E. दह् to burn,
ण्यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्क|दिक्कः
दिक्क m. (-क्कः) A young elephant.
 E. दिक् an imitative sound, and क who
utters, some books have धिक्क, and others विक्क in place of this
word. दिक्षु कायति कै-क । विंशतिवर्षवयस्के करिशावके ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्कर|दिक्करः
दिक्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Young, juvenile.
	 f. (-री) A young woman.
 E. दिक्
inflection of दिश् place, कर who makes; who is restlessly active,
changing place continually.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पति|दिक्पतिः
दिक्पति m. (-तिः) A regent of a quarter of the universe, as the sun of
the east; Saturn of the west; Mars of the south; Mircury of
the north; Venus of the south-east; Rahu of the south-west;
Chandra of the north-west; and Jupiter of the north-east.
 E. दिश्,
and पति master: see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पाल|दिक्पालः
दिक्पाल m. (-लः) A regent of a quarter of the universe, INDRA of the
east; AGNI of the south-east; Yama of the south; NAIRRIT of
the south-west; VARUṆA of the west; MARUTA of the north-west;
KUVERA of the north; ISANA of the south-east.
 E. दिश्, and पाल
who protects: this word applicable to the Dikpatis, (see the last,)
as that term is to these also.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्शूल|दिक्शूलं
दिक्शूल n. (-लं) An inauspicious planetary conjunction, as for the Sun
and Venus to be in the west, &c.
 E. दिश्, and शूल a spear or stake.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्त|दिगंत|दिगन्तः
दिगन्त m. (-न्तः) The horizon.
 E. दिक्, and अन्त end.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तर|दिगंतर
दिगन्तर n. (-रं) Space, the atmosphere.
 E. दिक्, and अन्तर interval.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तराल
दिगन्तराल n. (-लं) The sky, the atmosphere, space.
 E. दिक्, and अन्तराल
interval.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बर|दिगंबर|दिगम्बरः
दिगम्बर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)
	 1. Naked, unclad, unclothed.
	 2. Dressed in,
or enveloped by the atmosphere, clouds, &c.
	 m. (-रं)
	 1. A Bauddha
mendicant, wearing coloured clothes, or going naked.
	 2. Any
mendicant not wearing clothes.
	 3. Darkness.
	 4. A name of ŚIVA,
(from his being naked.)
	 5. A Jain of one great division, which
represents the images of their saints, either naked or plainly
attired.
	 f. (-री) A name of DURGĀ.
 E. दिक् inflection of दिश् space,
अम्बर vestment; whose only garment is the atmosphere. दिक् शून्य-
मम्बरं यस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्गज|दिग्गजः
दिग्गज m. (-जः) An elephant of a quarter or point of the compass, one
of eight attached to the north, north-east, &c. supporting the
globe.
 E. दिश् a quarter, and गज an elephant.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दाह|दिग्दाहः
दिग्दाह m. (-हः) Preternatural redness of the horizon, as if on fire. E.
दिश्, and दाह burning.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्ध|दिग्धः
दिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Smeared, anointed.
	 m. (-ग्धः)
	 1. A poison-
ed arrow.
	 2. A name of fire.
	 3. Oil, unguent, oily substance.
4. A tale, true or false.
 E. दिह् to smear or anoint, affix क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वासस्
दिग्वासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Naked.
	 m. (-साः) A name of ŚIVA.
 E. दिक्
for दिश् space, and वासस् vesture: see दिगम्बर ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजय|दिग्विजयः
दिग्विजय m. (-यः) Subjugation of an extensive country, either in arms or
controversy.
 E. दिश्, and विजय triumph.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजयक्रम
दिग्विजयक्रम m. (-मः) Invasion, going forth to conquer the world. E.
दिग्विजय, and क्रम march.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभाग
दिग्विभाग m. (-गः) A quarter or point of the compass.
 E. दिक्, and विभाग
division.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभावित
दिग्विभावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Famous, celebrated, known in all quarters.
E. दिक्, and विभावित made known.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्व्यापिन्
दिग्व्यापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Spreading through all space.
 E. दिक्, and
व्यापिन् what pervades.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्क|दिङ्कः
दिङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A nit.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मण्डल|दिङ्मंडल
दिङ्मण्डल n. (-लं) The circle of the heaven, or any point of the compass.
E. दिश्, and मण्डल sphere.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मुख
दिङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Looking to, or facing any point or quarter.
	 n.
(-खं) Any part of the heavens.
 E. दिश्, and मुख face.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्नाग|दिङ्नागः
दिङ्नाग m. (-गः) An elephant of the quarter: see दिग्गज.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित|दितं
दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut, torn, divided.
 E. दी to cut, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिति|दितिः
दिति f. (-तिः)
	 1. One of the wives of KAŚYAPA, and mother of the Dai-
tyas or infernal race, opposer of the gods.
	 2. Cutting, splitting,
dividing.
	 m. (-तिः) A king, a prince.
 E. दो to cut, affix क्तिच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दितिज|दितिजः
दितिज m. (-जः) An Asura, a sort of Titan or giant.
 E. दिति as above,
and ज born.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दितिसूत
दितिसूत m. (-तः)
	 1. Titan or giant.
 E. दिति as above, and सुत a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्य|दित्यः
दित्य m. (-त्यः)
	 1. Titan, a demon or giant.
 E. दिति as above, affix
यत्, and the vowel unchanged: see दैत्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सा
दित्सा f. (त्सा) Desire or purpose to give.
 E. दा to give, desid. form,
अ and टाप् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सु
दित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing to give.
 E. दा to give, desid. form,
affs. सन् and उ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षमाण
दिदृक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wishing to see.
 E. दृश् to see, desid. form,
शानच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षा
दिदृक्षा f. (-क्षा) Desire or wish to see.
 E. दृश् to see, desid. form, सन् भावे
अ and टाप् affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षु
दिदृक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Desirous of seeing.
 E. दृश् to see, desid. form,
सन् and उ affs.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षावत्
दिदृक्षावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wishing to see.
 E. दिदृक्षा, and मतुप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदेविषत्
दिदेविषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Wishing to play or sport.
 E. दिव् to play,
desid. form, शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्युत्
दिद्युत् mfn. (-द्युत्) Shining, blazing, bright.
 E. द्यु to shine, शतृ affix,
intens. form.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्योतिषु
दिद्योतिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to shine.
 E. द्यू to shine, desid. form,
उ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षमाण
दिधक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wishing to burn.
 E. दह to burn, desid. v.
शानच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षयत्
दिधक्षयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Desiring to burn.
 E. दह् to burn, desid. v. शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधि|दिधिः
दिधि f. (-धिः) Firmness, stability, fixed state of mind or being.
 E. धा
to have, affix कि, and the root reiterated.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषाय्य|दिधिषाय्यः
दिधिषाय्य m. (-य्यः) A pretended friend, an intimate.
 E. धा to have, Uṇādi
affix आय्य, the root reduplicated, इट् and षुक् augments.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषु|दिधिषुः
दिधिषु m. (-षुः) The second husband of a woman twice married.
	 f. (-षुः)
A virgin widow remarried.
 E. धा to have (sin), or धिष् to be re-
proached, root reduplicate, affix कु or कू; in the first case, इट् and
षुक् augments; also दिधिषू.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषू
दिधिषू f. (-षूः)
	 1. A virgin widow remarried: see the preceding; also
दिधीषू.
	 2. An elder sister unmarried, whose junior is a bride.
	 m.
(-षूः)
	 1. The husband of a woman married a second time: see दिधिषु.
2. Instability, want of firmness.
 E. दिधि firmness, षो to abandon, कू
Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषुपति
दिधिषुपति m. (-तिः) The husband of a woman remarried.
 E. दिधिषू as
above, and पति a husband.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन|दिनं|दिनः
दिन mn. (-नः-नं) A day.
 E. दी to waste, नक् affix, and the vowel made
short; or दो to destroy, (darkness,) किनन् Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकर|दिनकरः
दिनकर m. (-रः) The sun.
 E. दिन day, and कर who makes, कृ-ट ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकरात्मजा
दिनकरात्मजा f. (-जा) The Yamuna or Jumna river.
 E. दिनकर the sun,
and आत्मजा daughter.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकृत्
दिनकृत् m. (-कृत्) The sun.
 E. दिन, and कृत् who makes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकेशव|दिनकेशवः
दिनकेशव m. (-वः) Darkness.
 E. दिन day, and केशव hair.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनज्योतिस्
दिनज्योतिस् n. (-तिः) Sunshine, day-light.
 E. दिन day, and ज्योतिस् night.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनदुःखित|दिनदुःखितः
दिनदुःखित m. (-तः) The ruddy goose.
 E. दिन day, and दुःखित pained;
regretting throughout the day, the approaching nocturnal separa-
tion from its female.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनप्रणी
दिनप्रणी m. (-णीः) The sun.
 E. दिन day, and प्रणी leading, bringing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनबल|दिनबलः
दिनबल m. (-लः) A name of certain signs of the zodiac, the fifth to the
eighth; also the eleventh and twelfth.
 E. दिन, and बल strong.
