दीक्ष
दीक्ष r. 1st cl. (दीक्षते)
	 1. To be shaved.
	 2. To perform a sacrifice.
	 3.
To initiate.
	 4. To teach religious observances.
	 5. To be selfres-
trained भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।
