दीक्षा
दीक्षा f. (-क्षा)
	 1. Sacrificing, offering oblations.
	 2. Worshipping in
general.
	 3. Engaging in a course of austerities.
	 4. Certain cere-
monies preliminary to a cacrifice.
	 5. Receiving the initiatory Man-
tra or incantation.
 E. दा to give, (knowledge,) and क्षि to destroy,
(sin;) deriv. irr. or दीक्ष् to initiate, &c. affixes अ and टाप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
