दुर्दर्श|दुर्द्दर्श
दुर्दर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) Dazzling painful to the sight.
	 2. Difficult to be
seen or met with.
 E. दुर्, and दृश seeing. दुःखेन दृश्यते असौ दुर् + दृश्-
कर्मणि खल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दान्त|दुर्दांत|दुर्दान्तः|दुर्द्दान्त
दुर्दान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Untameable, intractable, difficult to be res-
trained or disciplined.
	 m. (-न्तः)
	 1. Strife, tumult.
	 2. A caff.
 E. दुर्,
and दान्त daunted. दुःखेन दान्तः दमितः दमि + क्त वा नि० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दिन|दुर्द्दिनं
दुर्दिन n. (-नं)
	 1. A dark or cloudy day.
	 2. Rain, or cloudy and rainy
weather.
 E. दुर् bad, vile, दिन a day. दुष्टं दिनम् प्रा० स० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दुरुट
दुर्दुरुट m. (-टः) An atheist.
 E. दुर् vile, repeated, अट् to go or be, affix
घञ्, and उ substituted for the penultimate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दृष्ट
दुर्दृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Ill seen, (literally or figuratively) ill-examined,
imperfectly investigated.
	 2. Looked at with an evil eye.
 E. दुर्
bad, दृष्ट seen.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दैव|दुर्द्दैव
दुर्दैव n. (-वं) Bad luck, misfortune.
 E. दुर्, and दैव fate.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्धरुट
दुर्द्धरुट m. (-टः) A pupil who obeys his teacher only after judging of the
propriety or obedience.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रिता
दुर्द्रिता f. (-ता) A creeping plant.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रुम|दुर्द्रुमः
दुर्द्रुम m. (-मः) A green onion.
 E. दुर् bad, and द्रुम a tree: see दुद्रुम.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्धर्ष
दुर्द्धर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)
	 1. Difficult of attainment or approach.
	 2. Haughty,
distant.
 E. दुर्, pride. दुःखेन धृष्यते असौ दुः + धृष-कर्मणि खल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=346-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर|दुर्द्धरः|दुर्धरः
दुर्धर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)
	 1. Difficult to be sustained or borne, troublesome,
unbearable.
	 2. Irresistible, difficult to be restrained.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A
division of hell.
	 2. A kind of drug, commonly Rishabha.
	 3. The
name of an Asura or Titan.
 E. दुर् bad, ill, धर having, possessing;
it is also written दुर्द्धर । दुःखेन धार्य्यते दुर् + धृ-कर्मणि खल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामक|दुर्नामकं|दुर्नामकः
दुर्नामक n. (-कं) Hæmorrhoids.
 E. दुर्, bad नामन् a name, and कप् added;
see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामन्
दुर्नामन् mf. (-मा-म्नी) A cockle.
	 n. (-म) Piles or hæmorrhoids.
E. दुर्, bad and नामन् a name, fem. affix, टाप् or ङीष्; also in the
first sense, with a final vowel दुर्नामा.
	 f. (-मा) ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निग्रह
दुर्निग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Ungovernable, difficult of restraint.
 E. दुर्, and
निग्रह restraint.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निवार
दुर्निवार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)
	 1. Difficult to be stopped, hindered, condradict-
ed, &c. Invincible, unconquerable.
 E. दुर्, and निवार resistance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=347-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

