दू
दू (ओ, ङ) ओदूङ r. 4th cl. (दूयते)
	 1. To suffer or be consumed with
pain.
	 2. To inflict pain or anxiety. दिवा० आ० अक० सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दू f. (-दूः) Pain, distress.
 E. दू, and क्विप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूडभ|दूडभः
दूडभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Unfortunate, distressed.
 E. दूर् difficult, दन्भ to
deceive, deriv. irr. दुःखेन दभ्यते असौ दन्भ-कर्मणि खल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूडाश|दूडाशः
दूडाश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Pained, afflicted.
 E. दुर bad, painful, दशि to hurt,
deriv. irr. दुःखेन दाश्यते दुर् + दाश्-कर्मणि खल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूढ्य|दूढ्यः
दूढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं) Bad, vile.
 E. दुर्, and ध्यै to meditate, क aff.
दुष्टं ध्यायति दुर् + ध्यै-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=348-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
