इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर्षि|देवर्षिः
देवर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A Ṛṣi, a saint of the celestial class, as NĀRADA, ATRI,
MARĪCHĪ, BHARADWĀJA, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, BHRIGU,
VASIṢṬHA, PRACHETAS; also BHARATA, TUMBURU, KANĀDA, and
others.
 E. देव divine, and ऋषि a saint: see ऋषि, and राजर्षि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवल|देवलः
देवल m. (-लः)
	 1. An attendant upon an idol; a Brahman of an inferior
order, who subsists upon the offerings made to the images which
he attends, and who conducts the ceremonies of all sorts of people
for hire.
	 2. A Muni; according to some authorities, a name of NĀ-
RADA; to others, of a different saint, who is also a legislator, the
son of ASITA and also named ASHTĀVAKRA.
	 3. A husband's bro-
ther: see देवर.
	 4. A holy or virtuous man.
 E. देव a deity, ला to bring,
and क aff. or देव-कलच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=352-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलक|देवलकः
देवलक m. (-कः) The attendant on an idol: see the preceding.
 E. कन्
added to देवल ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलता
देवलता f. (-ता) Double jasmine.
 E. देव divine, and लता a creeper.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलोक|देवलोकः
देवलोक m. (-कः)
	 1. Heaven or paradise.
	 2. Any one of the seven
superior worlds, from earth to the highest or Satya loka, in op-
position to those below the earth.
	 3. The particular sphere or
heaven of any divinity.
 E. देव, and लोक a world.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववक्त्र|देववक्त्रं
देववक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) Fire or its deity AGNI.
 E. देव a deity, and वक्त्र a face,
here implying, mouth; the mouth of the gods, eating or con-
suming the oblations made to them.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववल्लभ|देववल्लभः
देववल्लभ m. (-भः) A tree: see पुन्नाग ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर
देववर m. (-रः) A superior or supreme deity.
	 n. (-रं) A divine boon or
blessing.
 E. देव, and वर best.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर्द्धकि
देववर्द्धकि m. (-किः) A name of VIŚWAKARMĀ, the divine architect. E.
देव a deity, वर्द्धकि a carpenter.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववृक्ष|देववृक्षः
देववृक्ष m. (-क्षः)
	 1. A tree, (Echites scholaris.)
	 2. A tree of heaven or
paradise.
	 3. A plant yielding a fragrant resin, (Bdellium.)
 E. देव
a god, वृक्ष a tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रत|देवव्रतः
देवव्रत m. (-तः)
	 1. A worshipper of the gods.
	 2. A name of BHĪṢMA.
n. (-तं) Any obligation or vow of a deity.
 E. देव a deity, and व्रत
religious obligation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवश्रुत|देवश्रुतः
देवश्रुत m. (-तः) A god.
	 2. A sacred treatise or branch of scripture.
	 3. A
name of NĀRADA.
 E. देव divine, and श्रुत heard.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभा
देवसभा f. (-भा) An assembly of the gods.
 E. देव a deity, and सभा
assembly.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभ्य|देवसभ्यः
देवसभ्य m. (-भ्यः)
	 1. A player, a gambler, a frequenter of clubs or assem-
blies.
	 2. An attendant on a deity.
 E. देव sport in general, or gam-
bling, सभा an assembly, and यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसन्ध|देवसंध
देवसन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Divine, relating to a deity.
 E. देव, and सन्ध con-
nected.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसहा
देवसहा f. (-हा) A small shrub: see सहदेवा.
 E. देव a deity, सह् to bear,
affixes टाप् and अञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसात्
देवसात् ind. In or on a deity, becoming as a deity, appropriate or offer-
ed to one.
 E. देव, and साति aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसायुज्य|देवसायुज्यं
देवसायुज्य n. (-ज्यं)
	 1. Inferior deification, the state or being of the infe-
rior gods.
	 2. Absorption into or identification with a deity.
 E. देव a
god, स with युज् to join or be joined, affix क्विप्, देवसयुज् junc-
tion with a deity, ष्यञ् added, implying the state or condition.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसृष्टा
देवसृष्टा f. (-ष्टा) Spirituous liquor.
 E. देव, and सृष्ट created, made by
the gods.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेना
देवसेना f. (-ना)
	 1. The daughter of INDRA.
	 2. An army or host of celes-
tials.
 E. देव Indra or any deity, and सेना an army.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेनापति|देवसेनापतिः
देवसेनापति m. (-तिः) A name of SKANDA.
 E. देवसेना as above, and पति
ruler; commander of the hosts of heaven.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवस्व|देवस्वं
देवस्व n. (-स्वं) The property applicable to religious purpose, endowment,
&c.
 E. देव divine, and स्व wealth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=353-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाजीव|देवाजीवः
देवाजीव m. (-वः) An attendant upon an idol, a low Brahman, subsist-
ing by attendance upon an image, and upon the offerings made to
it.
 E. देव a deity, and आजीव who gets a livelihood; also इनि added
देवाजीविन् m. (-वी.)
