	 1. What is proper to be proved or ordered.
	 2.
Local.
	 3. Present at any transaction, on the spot.
	 n. (-श्यं)
	 1. The
postulate, the statement or exhibition of a question or argu-
ment.
	 2. The fact or charge to be proved or substantiated.
	 m.
(-श्यं) An eyewitness of any thing, one who was on the spot.
E. दिश् to show or command, affix ण्यत्; or देश, and यत् aff.
