<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युपति|द्युपतिः
द्युपति m. (-तिः)
	 1. The sun.
	 2. A name of INDRA.
 E. द्यु, a day or
paradise, and पति ruler.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युमणि|द्युमणिः
द्युमणि m. (-णिः) The sun.
 E. द्यु a day, and मणि a gem.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युमयी
द्युमयी f. (-यी) The daughter of VISWAKARMĀ, and wife of the sun. E.
द्यु a day, and मयट् affix of identity.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युम्र
द्युम्र n. (-म्रं)
	 1. Wealth, property, substance.
	 2. Strength, power. E.
द्यु day, म्रा to remember or regard, affix क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युवन्
द्युवन् m. (-वा)
	 1. The sun.
	 2. Heaven.
 E. द्यु to go (through the
heavens,) Unādi affix कनिन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=356-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
