द्रुहिण|द्रुहिणः
द्रुहिण m. (-णः) A name of BRAMHĀ.
 E. द्रुह् to injure or hurt, (the
wicked,) and इनन् affix, or द्रु a tree, (figuratively the universe,) हन्
to destroy, इनि affix, destroyer of the world; न changed to ण;
also द्रुहण ।
