द्वन्द|द्वंद|द्वन्दं|द्वंदः|द्वन्दः
द्वन्द m. (-न्दः) A clock or plate on which hours are struck.
	 n. (-न्दं) A
pair, a couple, (male and female especially:) see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्व|द्वंद्व|द्वंद्वं|द्वन्द्वं|द्वन्द्वः
द्वन्द्व n. (-न्द्वं)
	 1. A pair, a brace.
	 2. A couple of animals, or male and
female.
	 3. Union of the sexes or coupling.
	 4. Strife, dispute.
	 5. A
secret.
	 m. (-न्द्वः)
	 1. A form of grammatical combination uniting two
or more words in the same case, properly separated by a conjunc-
tion, as रामलक्ष्मणौ RĀMA and LAKSHMANA; पाणिपादं hand and foot.
2. A sign of the zodiac (Gemini.)
	 3. A species of disease, a
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=359-b" target="_blank">Page359-b+ 60</a>]
complication of two disorders, or compound affection of two
humours.
 E. द्वि two, reduplicate, deriv. irr.
