धन्व|धन्वं|धन्वः
धन्व n. (-न्वं) A bow: see धन्वन्. धन्व गतौ सौ० भ्वा० प० सक० सेट् । r. 1st cl.
(धन्वति) To go.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वदुर्ग|धन्वदुर्गं
धन्वदुर्ग n. (-र्गं) A desert.
 E. धन्व the same, and दुर्ग strong-hold.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन् mn. (-न्वा-न्वं) A bow.
	 m. (-न्वा) A country scantily supplied with
water, a desert, a waste.
	 n. (-न्वं) A firm spot, land, ground.
 E. धन्वि
Sautra root, to go or move, (by or on which,) and कनिन् Unādi
affix; also with अच् affix धन्व.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन् m. (-न्वः) A medicinal plant, commonly called Dhāminiya or
Dhamin.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरि|धन्वंतरि|धन्वंतरिः|धन्वन्तरिः
धन्वन्तरि m. (-रिः)
	 1. The physician of the gods, who was produced at
the churning of the ocean.
	 2. A celebrated physician; also
काशिराज, being the same as the preceding in another existence:
he appears to have been the founder of the Hindu medical school.
3. The sun.
	 4. A name of ŚIVA.
	 5. One of the nine gems of the
court of VIKRAMĀDITYA. धनोः तन्निमित्त शल्यस्य अन्तं पारं ऋच्छति ऋ गतौइन्
किच्च । समुद्रोत्थिते देववैद्यभेदे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरिग्रस्ता
धन्वन्तरिग्रस्ता f. (-स्ता) A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.
 E. धन्वन्तरि, and ग्रस्त
eaten.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वयवास|धन्वयवासः
धन्वयवास m. (-सः) A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji.)
 E. धन्व dry soil, यु to
unite, आसच् affix; also with कन् added धन्वयवासक. मरुभवे यवास भेदे,
दुरालभाभेदे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वयास|धन्वयासः
धन्वयास m. (-सः) A plant: see the last, alse simply यास, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन्
धन्विन् m. (-न्वी)
	 1. An archer, a bow-man.
	 2. A name of ARJUNA.
	 3. A
tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)
	 4. A wag, a wit, a sharp or shrewd
man.
 E. धन्व a bow, इनि aff. धन्वं चापोऽस्ति अस्य धम ध्माने सौ० पर० सक०
सेट् । धमति । To blow.
