धर्म्मचिन्तन n. (-नं) Virtuous reflection.
 E. धर्म्म, and चिन्ता reflection. चिन्ति
भावे ल्युट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिंता
धर्म्मचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Virtuous reflection.
 E. धर्म्म, and चिन्ता reflection: see
the last. चिन्ति भावे अ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मजीवन|धर्मजीवन|धर्मजीवनः
धर्म्मजीवन m. (-नः) Brahman who lives according to rule: one who
practises the outward acts of the law.
 E. धर्म्म, and जीवन living.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मज्ञ|धर्मज्ञ|धर्म्मज्ञः
धर्म्मज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Knowing one's duty, conversant with virtue.
E. धर्म्म, and ज्ञ who knows. धर्मं जानाति ज्ञा-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मज्ञान|धर्मज्ञान
धर्म्मज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of moral, legal, and religious duty.
 E. धर्म्म
and ज्ञान knowledge.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मण|धर्मण|धर्म्मणः
धर्म्मण m. (-णः)
	 1. A sort of tree, commonly Dhāminiya.
	 2. A kind of
large snake, not poisonous, commonly Dhamna. धर्माय नम्यते
नम-वा-कर्मणि-ड । धामनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
