धावित|धावितः
धावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Purified, Clean, cleansed.
	 2. Gone, gone or run
away.
	 3. Run to, advanced to or against.
 E. धाव् to clean, affix क्त,
with इट् augment, or without the augment धौत.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासस्
धासस् m. (-साः) A mountain.
 E. धा to uphold, Unādi affix असुन् and षुट्
augment; the word is considerd as peculiar to the Vedas.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि r. 6th cl. (धियति) To have hold, to keep, to possess. तुदा० प० सक०
अनिट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् ind. An interjection of reproach or menace, (fie, shame, shame,
&c.)
 E. धक्क् to annihilate, डिकन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कार|धिक्कारः
धिक्कार m. (-रः) Disrespect, reproach, censure, contempt.
 E. धिक fie,
and कार making.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृत|धिक्कृतः
धिक्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Cursed.
	 2. Reproached, reviled, censured,
condemned.
 E. धिक् fie, and कृत made.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्किया
धिक्किया f. (-या) Reproach.
 E. धिक् fie, and क्रिया making.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्पारुष्य
धिक्पारुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Excessive abuse.
 E. धिक्, and पारुष्य violence.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष
धिक्ष r. 1st cl. (धिक्षते)
	 1. To kindle.
	 2. To be weary, 3. To live. सन्दीपने
सक; क्लेशे जीवने अक० भ्वा० आ० सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वण|धिग्वणः
धिग्वण mf. (-णः-णा) A man of a low caste sprung from a Brāhman,
and a female of the tribe called Ayogava.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्दण्ड|धिग्दंड|धिग्दण्डः
धिग्दण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Reprimand, censure.
 E. धिक, and दण्ड punishment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Deceptive, wishing to trick or deceive.
 E. दम्भ
to cheat. desid. v. सन् उ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियाम्पति|धियांपति|धियाम्पतिः
धियाम्पति m. (-तिः)
	 1. A Jina or Jaina deified saint.
	 2. The soul.
 E. धी
the understanding, in the seventh case, and पति master.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिव
धिव (इ) धिवि r. 1st and 5th cls. (धिनोति)
	 1. To please, to satisfy.
	 2. To
be pleased or satisfied.
	 3. To go or approach: this verb takes उ,
and substitutes अ for the final, whence its unusual form for the
first class, in the instance given. प्रीणने अक० गतौ च सक० स्वा० पर०
सेट् इदित् । सार्वधातुके धिः आदेशः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष
धिष r. 3rd cl. (दिधेष्टि) To emit sound. जु० प० अक० सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
धिषण m. (-णः)
	 1. A name of VṚHASPATI.
	 2. Any Guru or spiritual
preceptor.
	 f. (-णा) The understanding, the intellect.
 E. धृष् to be
presumptuous, Unādi affix क्यु, and धिष substituted for the root.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ट्य|धिष्ट्यं|धिष्ट्यः
धिष्ट्य See धिष्ण्य.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठ्य
धिष्ठ्य See the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य n. (-ष्ण्यं)
	 1. A place, a spot, a country.
	 2. A house.
	 3. A star, an
asterism.
	 4. Fire.
	 5. Power. strength.
	 m. (-ष्ण्यः) A name of AGNI,
the deity of fire.
	 2. A name of SUKRA, regent of VENUS.
 E. धृष् to
be proud or overbearing, deriv. irr.; or more correctly. धृष-ण्य-नि०
the word is also written धिष्ट्य or धिष्ठ्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी (ओ ङ) ओधीङ् r. 4th cl. (धीयते)
	 1. To contain, to hold.
	 2. To light,
to disregard or despise.
	 3. To accomplish. With अन्तर, To dis-
appear, to become invisible. दिवा० आ० सक० अनिट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी f. (-धीः) Understanding, intellect.
 E. ध्यै to meditate, affix क्विप्, the
final diphthong rejected, and the semi-vowel changed to its congen-
er इ, which becomes long. धै-सम्प-भावे-क्किप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drank, sucked.
 E. धे to drink, participal affix, क्त
and the form irr. अनादृते आराधिते च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीति|धीतिः
धीति f. (-तिः) Thirst.
 E. धे to drink, affix क्तिन्, and the radical vowel
changed to ई.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
धीदा f. (-दा)
	 1. A virgin, a maiden.
	 2. Understanding, intellect धियं
ददाति दा-क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीन्द्रिय|धींद्रिय|धीन्द्रियं
धीन्द्रिय n. (-यं) An intellectual organ, as the mind, the eye, the ear,
the nose, the tongue, and skin.
 E. धी the intellect, इन्द्रिय an organ
of sense in general.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धीमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Sensible, wise, learned.
	 m. (-मान्) A name of
VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.
 E. धी wisdom, understand-
ing मतुप् possess. aff. धी अस्ति अस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)
	 1. Wise, sensible, learned.
	 2. Firm, steady, con-
sistent, determined.
	 3. Cool, collected.
	 4. Head-strong, self-willed,
uncontrollable.
	 5. Lazy, dull, slow.
	 6. Strong, powerful.
	 7. Well-
behaved, decorous, decent.
	 8. Gentle, steady, (as a breeze.)
	 9.
Deep, (as a sound)
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A name of BALI, a celebrated prince.
2. The ocean.
	 mn. (-रः-रं) Saffron.
	 f. (-रा)
	 1. A drug;
also काकोली.
	 2. A woman who, although jealous of a husband or
lover, suppresses all expression of resentment in his presence. E.
धी understanding, रा to possess, क affix; or धी with ईर to go to,
affix अण्; or धी to possess, क्तन् Unādi aff. धियं राति रा-क । धियमीरयति
ईरअण् वा । उप० स ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरत्व|धीरत्वं
धीरत्व n. (-त्वं)
	 1. Firmness, fortitude.
	 2. The feminine property of sup-
pressing violent expression of jealousy.
 E. धीर firm, steady, affix
त्व; also with तल् affix धीरता.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरप्रशान्त|धीरप्रशांत|धीरप्रशान्तः
धीरप्रशान्त n. (-न्तं) The hero of a poem or play who unites all good
qualities.
 E. धीर, and प्रशान्त calm.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरललित|धीरललितः
धीरललित m. (-तः) The hero of a poem or play, who is firm and brave,
but reckless and inconsiderate.
 E. धीर and ललित sportive.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरस्कन्द
धीरस्कन्द m. (-न्दः) A buffalo.
 E. धीर strong, स्कन्द a shoulder.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीराधीरा
धीराधीरा f. (-रा) A mistress or wife, who having cause for jealousy,
pursues a middle conduct between the suppression and expression
of resentment.
 E. धीरा and अधीरा joined.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोदात्त|धीरोदात्तः
धीरोदात्त m. (-त्तः) The hero of a poem or play whose characteristics
are benevolence and fortitude.
 E. धीर, and उदात्त liberal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोद्धत|धीरोद्धतः
धीरोद्धत m. (-तः) The hero of a poem or play who is deficient in magn-
animity.
 E. धीर and उद्धत haughty.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटि|धीलटिः
धीलटि f. (-टि) A daughter. लट-बाल्योक्तौ इन्-धिया कर्मणा लटिः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवन्
धीवन् m. (-वा)
	 1. A brazier.
	 2. A fisherman.
 E. धृ to hold, Uṇādi affix
कनिन् and ऋ changed to ई.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर m. (-रः) A fisherman.
	 f. (-री)
	 1. A fisherman's wife.
	 2. A sort of
harpoon for catching fish with.
 E. धी to hold or gain, (fish,)
Unādi affix ष्वरच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=370-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीशक्ति|धीशक्तिः
धीशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) An intellectual faculty or power of the understanding,
as attention, comprehension. &c.
 E. धी the intellect, and शक्ति
power.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसख|धीसखः
धीसख m. (-खः)
	 1. A counsellor, an adviser, a minister.
	 2. A tutor or
friend.
 E. धी the understanding, and सखि a friend.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसचिव|धीसचिवः
धीसचिव m. (-वः)
	 1. A counsellor, a minister.
	 2. A friendly or prudent
adviser.
 E. धी the intellect, and सचिव a friend.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु (ञ) धुञ् r. 7th cl. (धुनोति-धुनुते) To shake, to agitate: see धू कम्पने अक०
चालने सक० स्वादि० उभ० अनिट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु f. (-धुः) Shaking, trembling.
 E. धु to shake भावे डु aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष
धुक्ष r. 1st cl. (धुक्षते)
	 1. To kindle.
	 2. To be weary.
	 3. To live. भ्वा० आ०
अक० अनिट्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, deserted, left.
	 2. Shaken, agitated,
(as leaves by wind, &c.)
 E. धु to shake, affix क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुतपाप
धुतपाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Purified from sin.
 E. धुत shaken, पाप sin.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनन
धुनन n. (-नं) Shaking, agitation.
 E. धु to shake, affix ल्यु also धूनन &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनान
धुनान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shaking, agitating.
 E. धु to shake, शानच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनि f. (-निः) A river; see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनी
धुनी f. (-नी) A river.
 E. धु to go, affix इन् fem. affix ङीप्; the affix is
sometimes considered as निक् leaving नि, which makes धुनि ut sup.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनीनाथ|धुनीनाथः
धुनीनाथ m. (-थः) The ocean.
 E. धुनी and नाथ lord.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुमार|धुंधुमारः|धुन्धुमारः
धुन्धुमार m. (-रः)
	 1. The name of a sovereign; also named Kuvalayāswa.
2. An insect, (Coccinella.)
	 3. The smoke of a house.
	 4. A house.
A house lizard
 E. धूम smoke reiterated, ऋ to go, affix अण्, deriv.
irr. or धुन्धुं मारयति-मारि-अण्-उप-स० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वत्|धुन्वन्त्
धुन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Shaking, agitating.
 E. धु to shake, शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वान
धुन्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shaking, agitating.
 E. धु to shake, शानच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् f. (-धूः)
	 1. The forepart of a carriage, the pole or the path where
the yoke is fixed.
	 2. Agitation, trembling.
	 3. Reflection, recollec-
tion.
	 4. A spark of fire.
	 5. A burthen, a load.
	 6. A part, a portion.
7. Wealth.
	 8. A name of the Gānges.
 E. धुर्ब्ब hurt, affix क्विप्, and
व rejected; also with टाप् added, धुरा ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरन्धर|धुरंधर|धुरन्धरः
धुरन्धर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)
	 1. Bearing a burthen.
	 2. Bearing, (figuratively,)
laden with good qualities, heavy duties, &c.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A beast
of burthen.
	 2. A man of business.
	 3. A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)
E. धुर् a burthen, and धृ to have, affix खच् । खचिह्रस्वः ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा f. (-रा) A burthen, a load.
 E. धुर्व to hurt, affixes क and टाप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Bearing, (as a burthen.)
	 2. Charged with,
abounding with, (qualities, duties, &c.)
	 m. (-ण)
	 1. A beast of bur-
then.
	 2. A man of business.
 E. धुर a burthen, ख aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीय|धुरीयः
धुरीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)
	 1. Fit for a load, suited to a burthen 2. Charged
with important duties.
	 m. (-यः)
	 1. A beast of burthen.
	 2. A man
of business.
 E. धुर्, and छ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=371-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य्य|धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) Fit for a burthen, adopted to it, &c.
	 m. (-र्य्यः)
1. A beast of burthen.
	 2. minister, a charged affairs.
	 3. A house.
E. धुर् a burthen, यत् aff.
