नकुल|नकुलः
नकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Disgraced, rejected from a family or race.
	 m.
(-लः)
	 1. The Bengal mungoose, (Viverra ichneumon)
	 2. A proper
name, NAKULA, the fourth of the five Pāṇḍu princes.
	 3. A son.
4. A name of ŚIVA.
	 f. (-ली)
	 1. Silk cotton tree, 2. Indian spikenard.
3. A sort of perfume: see शङ्क्षिनी. Saffron.
	 4. The letter ह as used
in the Tantras.
 E. न not, कुल race or heap, fem. affix ङीष्.
