नक्रराज्
नक्रराज् m. (-राट्) or नक्रराज m. (-जः) A shark, but applied also differ-
ently: see ग्राह.
 E. नक्र a crocodile, and राज् or राज king.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्र|नक्षत्रं
नक्षत्र n. (-त्र)
	 1. A star in general.
	 2. An asterism in the moon's path
or lunar mansion, of which twenty-eight, distinct in name, figure,
and number of stars, are enumerated; the Pourānic and popular
enumeration of those constellations is twenty-seven; Abhijit, the
twenty-eighth, being considered as formed of portions of the two
contiguous asterisms, and not distinct from them 2. A pearl. E.
नक्ष् to go, Unādi, affix अत्रन् or क्षद Sautra root, to injure, or क्षर् to
drop, or क्षी to waste or decay, with the negative prefix, and ष्ट्रन्
affix; deriv. irr. न क्षीयते क्षरते वा ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=375-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रचक्र|नक्षत्रचक्रं
नक्षत्रचक्र n. (-र्क्र)
	 1. A particular diagram for astrological calculations
2. The lunar asterisms collectively.
 E. नक्षत्र and चक्र a circle.
