नख|नखं|नखः
नख mf. (-खः-खी) A fingernail.
	 m. (-खः) A part, a portion.
	 nf. (-खं-खी)
A perfume, a dried substance, of a brown colour, and of the
shape of a nail; apparently, a dried shell-fish, used as a perfume.
f. (-खी) A vegetable perfume, different from the one above,
though known by the same name, NAKHI.
 E. न privative, ख
sense; or नह् to bind ख Unādi affix, the radical ह rejected. नखम्
छिद्रम् अत्र ।
