नद्ध|नद्धः
नद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)
	 1. Bound, tied.
	 2. Drawn up, raised.
 E. नह् to tye,
affix कर्मणि क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध्री
नद्ध्री f. (-द्ध्री) A leather cord, a thong
 E. नह् to bind, करणे ष्ट्रन्-ङीप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननन्दृ|ननंदृ
ननन्दृ f. (-न्दा) A husband's sister.
 E. न negative, नन्द to please, ऋत्
Unādi affix; also the penultimate being made long, ननान्दृ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु ind.
	 1. A particle of interrogation, (how, what.)
	 2. Of affirmation,
(certainly.)
	 3. Of assent.
	 4. A consolatory and kind expression.
	 5.
A vocative particle, (ho, hola.) or one implying kindness, concilia-
tion, (pray, good friend, &c.)
	 6. An inceptive particle, implying
doubt or dissent, (may be, but, on the other hand.)
	 7. A responsive
particle.
	 8. A particle of reproach.
 E. न negative, नुद् to send or
command, affix डु ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननुच
ननुच ind. An inceptive particle, implying doubt, dissent, or contra-
diction.
 E. ननु as above, and च particle. अष्यय० ननु + च + स्रमा-द्व० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्तव्य
नन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be saluted, to be revered or honoured.
 E. नम्
to salute, तव्य aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द|नंद|नंदः|नन्दः
नन्द mf. (-न्दः-न्दी) Happiness, pleasure, felicity.
	 m. (-न्दः)
	 1. One of
KUVERA'S nine inestimable gems or treasure.
	 2. The cow-
herd NANDA, the foster father of KṚṢṆA.
	 3. A name of
VIṢṆU.
	 4. A prince, the son of MAHĀNANDI.
	 5. A flute, one
eleven inches long.
	 f. (-न्दा)
	 1. An earthen water jar.
	 2. The first,
sixth, or eleventh day of the fortnight.
	 3. Prosperity, increase.
	 4.
A husband's sister.
	 f. (-न्दी) INDRA'S garden.
	 f. (-न्दा or -न्दी) A name
of DURGĀ.
 E. नदि to be prosperous or happy, affixes अच् and टाप्
or भावे घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दक|नंदक|नन्दकः
नन्दक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Rejoicing, making happy or delighted.
	 2.
Cherishing or rearing a family.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. Happiness, pleasure.
	 2.
The sword of KṚṢṆA.
	 3. The foster father of KṚṢṆA.
	 4. A
frog.
 E. नदि to make happy, affix ण्वुल् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकि|नंदकिः|नन्दकिः
नन्दकि f. (-किः) Long pepper.
 E. नन्द to delight, affix इन् वा कुक् ।
