नन्दिकेश्वर m. (-रः)
	 1. One of ŚIVA'S chief attendants.
	 2. An inferior
Purāna.
 E. नन्दिक INDRA'S garden, and ईश्वर master.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिघोष|नंदिघोष|नन्दिघोषः
नन्दिघोष m. (-षः)
	 1. The car of ARJUNA.
	 2. The acclaim or proclam-
ation of a panegyrist or herald.
 E. नन्दि happy, and धोष sound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिन्|नंदिन्
नन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि) Happy, rejoiced, delighted.
	 m. (-न्दी)
	 1. The
name of one of ŚIVA'S chamberlains, and chief attendants.
	 2. The
Indian fig tree.
	 3. Parspipal, (Hibiscus populneoides.)
	 4. The
speaker of the prelude or prologue to a drama.
	 f. (-न्दिनी)
	 1. A name
of the goddess PĀRVATĪ.
	 2. GANGĀ, the river goddess.
	 3. A hus-
band's sister.
	 4. A fabulous cow, related to the cow of plenty, and
the property of the sage VAŚISHṬHA.
	 5. The Alakānanda river.
6. The mother of the writer VYĀḌI.
 E. नन्द happiness, णिनि aff.
