नर्म्मद|नर्मद|नर्मदः|नर्म्मदः
नर्म्मद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Delighting, making happy, giving pleasure.
	 m.
(-दः) The associate or companion of a person's sports or amuse-
ments.
	 f. (-दा)
	 1. The Narmadā river, which rising in the Vindhya
mountains, runs westward to the gulf of Cambay.
	 2. A plant: see
पृक्का.
 E. नर्म्म pleasure, and द what gives. नर्म ददाति दा-क ६ त० स० ।
