नवद्वार
नवद्वार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having nine doors; an epithet applied to the
body, which has nine inlets or outlets, as the nostrils, ears, mouth,
&c.
 E. नव, and द्वार a door.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवधा
नवधा ind. Nine-fold, in nine ways.
 E. नव nine, and धा aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवन्
नवन् mfn. always plu. (-व) Nine.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनी
नवनी f. (-नी) Fresh butter.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीत|नवनीतं
नवनीत n. (-तं) Fresh butter.
 E. नव new, and नीत procured from milk,
&c.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतक|नवनीतकं
नवनीतक n. (-कं) Clarified butter.
 E. कन् added to the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतधेनु|नवनीतधेनुः
नवनीतधेनु f. (-नुः) A quantity of butter as a present to Brāhmans. E.
नवनीत, and धेनु a milch cow.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवपल्लव
नवपल्लव n. (-वं) A new shoot or sprout.
 E. नव, and पल्लव a shoot.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवफलिका
नवफलिका f. (-का)
	 1. A bride, a newly married woman.
	 2. A girl in
whom menstruation has recently begun.
 E. नव new, फल fruit, and
ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवब
नवब(व)धू f. (-धूः) A bride, a newly married woman.
 E. नव, and बधू a
wife.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवम|नवमः
नवम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Ninth.
	 f. (-मी) The ninth day of a lunar half
month.
 E. नव nine, and डढि-मट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमल्लिका
नवमल्लिका f. (-का) Double jasmine: see the next.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमालिका
नवमालिका f. (-का) Double jasmine, (J. Zambac.)
 E. नव excellent,
praised, and मालिका or मल्लिका jasmine: see the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवयौवना
नवयौवना f. (-ना) A young woman.
 E. नव new, and यौवन young.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरक्तक
नवरक्तक n. (-कं) A newly dyed garment.
 E. नव, रक्त red, and कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरङ्ग|नवरङ्गं
नवरङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Gift to five and acceptance by fours persons of the best
Kayastha families.
 E. नव, and रङ्ग colour.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरत्र
नवरत्र n. (-त्रं)
	 1. Nine precious gems, or a pearl, ruby, topaz, diamond,
emerald, lapis lazuli, coral, sapphire, and one called Gomedā.
	 2.
The nine men of letters at the court of VIKRAMĀDITYA, or DHAN-
WANTARI, KSHAPANAKA, AMARASINHA, SANKU, VETĀLABHATTA,
GHATAKARPARA, KĀLIDĀSA, VARĀHAMIHIRA, and VARARŪCHI.
E. नव and रत्र a jewel.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरात्र|नवरात्रं
नवरात्र n. (-त्रं) The period of nine days, from the first of the light half
of Aswin to the ninth; part of the time devoted to the worship of
DURGĀ.
 E. नव, and रात्रि a night.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववरिका
नववरिका f. (-का) A newly married woman.
 E. नव new, वर a blessing,
affix कन् added, fem. affix टाप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववस्त्र|नववस्त्रं
नववस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) New cloth.
 E. नव, new, and वस्त्र cloth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्
नवशस् ind. Nine by nine.
 E. नव, and शस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्य
नवशस्य n. (-स्य) Grain of the year's harvest.
 E. नव, and शस्य grain.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्येष्टि
नवशस्येष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A sacrifice performed on eating the new rice or
grain of the year, नवशस्य, and इष्टि sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशायक|नवशायकः
नवशायक m. (-कः) A name given to any of nine inferior classes, the
cowherd, gardener, oilman, weaver, confectioner, betel seller,
potter, blacksmith, and barber.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवश्राद्ध
नवश्राद्ध n. (-द्धं) The first series of Shrāddhas collectively, or funeral offer-
ings on the first, third, fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh days
after a person's demise.
 E. नव, and श्राद्ध obsequial rite.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नधसूतिका
नधसूतिका f. (-का)
	 1. A milch cow.
	 2. A woman recently delivered. E.
नव new, and सूत offspring, and कन् affix, fem. form.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवांश|नवांशः
नवांश m. (-शः) A ninth, a ninth part.
 E. नव, and अंश share,
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवान्न|नवान्नं
नवान्न n. (-न्नं)
	 1. New rice or grain.
	 2. A ceremony observed on first
eating the rice, &c. of the last harvest.
 E. नव, and अन्न food.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाम्बर|नवाम्बरं
नवाम्बर n. (-रं) New and unbleached cloth.
 E. नव new, and अम्बर cloth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवार्च्चिस्|नवार्चिस्
नवार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) The planet Mars or its deified personification.
 E. नव
nine, and अर्च्चिस् light.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाह|नवाहः
नवाह m. (-हः)
	 1. A new day.
	 2. The first day of the fortnight.
 E. नव
new, and अह a day.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकरण
नवीकरण n. (-णं) Renewing, doing or making anew,
 E. नव, करण making,
च्वि augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकृत
नवीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Renewed, revived, done or made anew,
 E. नव,
and कृत made, च्वि augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीन|नवीनं
नवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) New.
 E. नव new, ख pleonasm, and the semi-vowel
changed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीभूत
नवीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Renewed, revived.
 E. नव, and, भूत become, च्वि
augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवै
नवै ind. Not so perhaps, a particle implying doubt.
 E. न not, वै
expletive.
