<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोढा
नवोढा f. (-ढा) A newly married woman, a bride.
 E. नव new, and ऊढा
a wife.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोद्धृत|नवोद्धृतं
नवोद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Newly extracted or drawn up.
	 n. (-तं)
	 2. Fresh
butter.
 E. नव new, उद्धृत made or drawn up.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
नव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) New, recent, young, modern. &c.
	 m. (-व्यः) Praise,
panegyric.
 E. नव new, and स्वार्थे यत् aff. रक्तपुनर्नवायाम् च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशाक|नशाकः
नशाक mf. (-कः-का) A bird, said to be a sort of crow.
 E. नश् to destroy,
affix आक ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशितृ
नशितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Destroying.
 E. णश to destroy, affix तृच् with इट्
augment, else with a nasal augment नष्टृ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्
नश्यत् mfn. (श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्) Perishing, decaying, wasting, being destroy-
ed.
 E. नश् to perish, and शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्प्रसूतिका
नश्यत्प्रसूतिका f. (-का) A female bearing a dead child.
 E. नश्यत्, प्रसूतिका a
mother.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)
	 1. Mischievous.
	 2. Destructive, perishable.
 E. णशि
to destroy, affix छरप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Lost, destroyed, removed, annihilated.
 E. णश to
perish, affix क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचन्द्र|नष्टचन्द्रः
नष्टचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The moon on the fourth lunation of either half of
Bhādra.
 E. नष्ट, and चन्द्र the moon: it is is very unlucky to see the
moon on these days.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेतन
नष्टचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fainted, insensible.
 E. नष्ट, and चेतन conscious.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेष्ट
नष्टचेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Insensible, inert.
 E. नष्ट, and चेष्टा effort.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेष्टता
नष्टचेष्टता f. (-ता) Fainting, swooning, insensibility, proceeding either
from joy or sorrow, &c.
 E. नष्ट lost, चेष्टता effort. हर्षशोकादिभिः सर्व-
चेष्टाराहित्ये ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टसंस्मृति
नष्टसंस्मृति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Unmindful, forgetful.
 E. नष्ट, and संस्मृति
recollection.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाग्नि|नष्टाग्निः
नष्टाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A Brāhman or householder who has lost his conse-
crated fire.
 E. नष्ट lost, and अग्नि fire.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाप्तिसूत्र|नष्टाप्तिसूत्रं
नष्टाप्तिसूत्र n. (-त्रं) Booty, plunder.
 E. नष्ट lost, आप्ति gain, and सूत्र thread
or chain.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टार्थ
नष्टार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Reduced, become poor.
 E. नष्ट, and अर्थ wealth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टेन्दुकला|नष्टेंदुकला
नष्टेन्दुकला f. (-ला) The day of new moon when it rises invisible.
 E. नष्ट,
and इन्दुकला a digit.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् f. (-नाः) The nose.
 E. नस् to sound, affix क्विप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसा
नसा f. (-सा) The nose: see नासा and नासिका ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्त|नस्तः
नस्त m. (-स्तः) The nose.
	 n. (-स्तं) A sternutatory, snuff, &c.
	 f. (-स्ता) A
hole bored in the septum of the nose.
 E. णस् to make crooked,
affix संज्ञायां त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तित|नस्तितः
नस्तित m. (-तः) An ox or any other draft animal, with a string through
his nose, the sort of rein usually employed in India.
	 f. (-ता)
Nozzled.
 E. नस्त as above, the nose, formed into a nominal verb,
and क्त added, nozzled or nose-led. णस्-तार-इतच् । (नाकफोडा) ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तोत|नस्तोतः
नस्तोत mf. (-तः) An ox led by a string through his nose: see the last;
also नस्योत. नसि नासिकायां सम्यक् ऊतः आ + वे-क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्य|नस्यं
नस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Nasal, relating or belonging to the nose.
	 n.
(-स्यं) A sternutatory, snuff.
	 f. (-स्या) The nose.
 E. नसा the nose,
यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्योत|नस्योतः
नस्योत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) An ox or other animal led by a string through
the septum of the nose.
 E. नसा the nose, यत् affix of relation or
fitness, and ऊत woven: see नस्तित । आ + वे + क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह
नह (-औ) औनह r. 4th cl. (नह्यति-ते) To bind: see णह ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहि
नहि ind. No, not.
 E. णह् to bind or tie, affix इन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष|नहुषः
नहुष m. (-षः)
	 1. The name of a Nāga or serpent.
	 2. The name of a
king, one of the lunar race, son of AYUS and grandson of PURŪ-
RAVAS.
 E. णह् to bind, Unādi affix उषन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुषात्मज|नहुषात्मजः
नहुषात्मज m. (-जः) A king, also YAYĀTI.
 E. नहुष as above, आत्मज son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ना
ना ind. No, not (another form of न ।)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक|नाकः
नाक m. (-कः) Heaven, paradise, æther. sky, atmosphere.
 E. न not
with अक derived from क happiness, and the privative अ prefixed
misery; in which there is no unhappiness. न कम् अकम् दुःखम् तत्
नास्ति यत्र ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकनाथ|नाकनाथः
नाकनाथ m. (-थः) A name of INDRA.
 E. नाक paradise, and नाथ lord;
also with कन् added नाकनाथक ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकनायक|नाकनायकः
नाकनायक m. (-कः) INDRA.
 E. नाक, and नायक a chief.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकवनिता
नाकवनिता f. (-ता) A nymph of heaven.
 E. नाक, and वनिता a wife.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकषेधक
नाकषेधक m. (-कः) INDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकसद्
नाकसद् m. (-सत्) A deity.
 E. नाक, and सद् who dwells in.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिन्
नाकिन् m. (-की) A deity, a god.
 E. नाक heaven, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकु|नाकुः
नाकु m. (-कुः)
	 1. An ant or mole hill, a burrow.
	 2. A mountain.
	 3. A
name of a Muni or saint.
 E. न privative, अक् to go, affix उ, or नम्
to be crooked or bowed, Unādi affix उ, and नाक substituted for
the radical letters.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुल|नाकुलः
नाकुल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Relating or belonging to an ichneumon.
	 f. (-ली)
1. A plant; the ichneumon plant, a vegetable supposed to furnish
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">Page382-b+ 60</a>]
the mungoose with an antidote, when bitten in a conflict with a
snake, (Serpent ophioxylon)
	 2. The root of the Simul tree,
(कुक्कुटोकन्द) A sort of pepper, (Piper chavya)
 E. नकुल the ichneu-
mon, affixes अण् and ङीष् । चविके, (चै) राम्नायां, यवतिक्तायां, श्वेत-
कण्टकार्य्यां च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुलान्ध्य
नाकुलान्ध्य n. (-न्धं) Weakness of sight
 E. नाकुल, and अन्ध्य blindness.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुसद्मन्
नाकुसद्मन् m. (-द्मा) A snake.
 E. नाकु a mound of earth, सद्मन् a dwelling.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्र|नाक्षत्रं|नाक्षत्रः
नाक्षत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) Relating or belonging to the luner asterisms.
	 n.
(-त्रं) A month, one computed by the moon's passage through the
twenty-seven mansions, or of thirty days of sixty Gharis each. E.
नक्षत्र, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्रिक|नाक्षत्रिकः
नाक्षत्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to the lunar asterisms.
m. (-कः) A month of twenty-seven days, each day being the period
of the moon's passage through a luner asterism, f. (-की) The
state or condition to which a person is subjected agreeably to the
asterism presiding over his nativity.
 E. नक्षत्र as above, and ठञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग|नागं|नागः
नाग m. (-गः) Nāga or demi-god so called, having a human face, with
the tail of a serpent, and the expanded neck of the Koluber Nāga;
the race of these beings is said to have sprung from KADRU, the
the wife of KĀSYAPA, in order to people Pātāla or the regions
below the earth.
	 2. A serpent in general or especially the specta-
cle snake, or cobra capella, (Coluber Nāga.)
	 3. An elephant.
	 4. A
cruel or tyrannical person.
	 5. A cloud.
	 6. (In composition,) Pre-
eminent.
	 7. A pin or nail projecting from a wall to hang any
thing upon.
	 8. A small tree, (Mesua ferrea.)
	 9. A sort of grass,
(Cyperus pertenuis.)
	 10. A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria.)
11. One of the airs of the body, that which is expelled by belching.
12. Betel or Pān.
	 13. The name of a country.
	 14. A shark.
	 n. (-गं)
	 1.
Tin.
	 2. Lead.
	 3. One of the astronomical periods called Karaṇas;
it is one of those termed invariable, and always corresponds to
the last half of Āmavasya or new moon.
	 4. The effects of that
period on any thing done or happening during it.
 E. नग a moun-
tain, and अण् affix; living or produced in mountainous regions,
&c. नगे पर्वते भवः अण् न गच्छति अगः न अगो वा ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागकेशर|नागकेशरः
नागकेशर m. (-रः) A small tree, commonly Nageshwar, (Mesua ferrea).
E. नाग, and केशर synonymes of the same plant compounded; the
word is also written नागकेसर.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागगर्भ|नागगर्भं
नागगर्भ n. (-भं) Red lead.
 E. नाग lead. and गर्भ origin. सिन्दुरे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागज|नागजं
नागज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by or of a Nāga. &c.
	 n. (-जं)
	 1. Red
lead.
	 2. Tin.
 E. नाग lead, &c. and ज produced.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजिह्वा
नागजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa:) see शारिवा
 E. नाग
a snake, and जिह्वा a tongue.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजिह्विका
नागजिह्विका f. (-का) Red arsenic.
 E. नाग a snake, जिह्वा a tongue, कन्
affix of comparison. मनःशिलायाम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजीवन|नागजीवनं|नागजीवनः
नागजीवन m. (-नः) Tin.
 E. नाग lead, जीवन proceeding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्त|नागदंत|नागदन्तः
नागदन्त m. (-न्तः)
	 1. Elephant's tooth or ivory; also the tooth of the ele-
phant.
	 2. A shelf, a pin or bracket projecting from a wall, and
used to hang things upon.
	 f. (-न्ती)
	 1. A sort of sun-flower, (Helio-
tropium Indicum.)
	 2. A whore.
 E. नाग an elephant, and दन्त a tooth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तिक
नागदन्तिक m. (-कः) A wooden pin or bracket, projecting from a wall, a
shelf.
 E. नागदन्त an elephant's tooth, and कन् affix of resemblance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तिका
नागदन्तिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly called Rāmadūtī, see विशल्या ।
E. नागदन्ती a plant, and कन् affix of resemblance. (विछाति ।)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदलोपम|नागदलोपमं
नागदलोपम m. (-मः) A sort of tree commonly Parusha.
 E. नाग one of
the plants so called, दल a leaf, and उपमा resemblance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागद्रु|नागद्रुः
नागद्रु m. (-द्रुः) Euphorbia
 E. नाग a snake, and द्रु a tree; being used in
offerings to the snake goddess MANASĀ. सि वृक्षे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागनिर्य्यूह|नागनिर्यूह|नागनिर्यूहः|नागनिर्य्यूहः
नागनिर्य्यूह m. (-हः) A large pin or bracket, projecting from a wall like
a shelf.
 E. नाग an elephant, and निर्य्यूह projection.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपाश|नागपाशः
नागपाश m. (-शः)
	 1. A weapon of VARUṆA the regent of water.
	 2. A
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">Page383-a+ 60</a>]
sort of magical noose or knot, used in battle to entangle an
enemy.
 E. नाग an elephant, and पाश a binding.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=382-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपुष्प|नागपुष्पः
नागपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)
	 1. A tree in used in dyeing, (Rottleria tinctoria.)
	 2.
Nāgeshwar, (Mesua ferrea.)
	 3. The Champaka, (Michelia champa-
ca)
 E. नाग an elephant, and पुष्प flower.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबन्धु|नागबंधु|नागबन्धुः
नागबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)
 E. नाग an elephant
and बन्धु friendly, liked.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबल|नागबलः
नागबल m. (-लः) A name of BHĪMA.
	 f. (-ला) A creeping plant, (Hedy-
sarum lagopodioides.)
 E. नाग an elephant, and बल strong. (गोरक्ष
चाकुलिया ।)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागभिद्
नागभिद् m. (-भिद्) A sort of snake, (Amphisbæna.)
 E. नाग an elephant,
and भिद् destroying; the word is sometimes written नागभृत्, from
भृत् cherishing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमल्ल|नागमल्लः
नागमल्ल m. (-ल्लः) The elephant of INDRA.
 E. नाग an elephant, and मल्ल a boxer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमातृ
नागमातृ f. (-ता)
	 1. A name of MANASĀ, a goddess supposed to preside
over snakes.
	 2. Red arsenic.
 E. नाग a snake, and मातृ a mother.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाममार
नाममार m. (-रः) A sort of potherb; also केशराज
 E. नाग a snake, and
मार destroying; considered as an antidote.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागयष्टि|नागयष्टिः
नागयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A piece of wood erected in a newly dug pond for
showing the depth of water.
 E. नाग a snake, and यष्टि a staff; also
नागयष्टिका ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)
	 1. Clever, sharp, knowing, (as a buck, a blood,
a wag. &c.)
	 2. Town-born or bred, citizen.
	 3. Nameless.
	 4. Rela-
ting to a city.
	 5. Polite, civil 6. Bad, vile.
	 n. (-रं)
	 1. Dry ginger.
2. A short of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis).
	 3. A form of writing,
the “Devanāgari alphabet.” m. (-रः)
	 1. A husband's brother.
	 2. An
orange.
	 3. A lecturer.
	 4. Denial of knowledge.
	 5. Fatigue.
	 6.
Desire of final beatitude.
	 f. (-री)
	 1. A sort of Euphorbia.
	 2. A
clever or intriguing woman.
 E. नगर a city अण् aff. नगरे भवः अण् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक m. (-कः)
	 1. The orange; see नागरङ्ग 2. A thief.
	 3. An artist. E.
नागर, and वुञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक्त|नागरक्तं
नागरक्त m. (-क्तः) Red lead.
 E. नाग mountain, and रक्त red. सिन्दुरे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरङ्ग|नागरंग|नागरङ्गः
नागरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The orange; in India usually applied to the Sylhet
orange, (Citrus aurantium.)
 E. नाग an elephant, रङ्ग to be sick,
affix घञ्; on which elephants feed till they become ill; or नाग
red lead, and रङ्ग colour, of the colour of red lead. (नाराङ्गी नेवु ।)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरमुस्ता
