नागाधिप m. (-पः) The great serpent ANANTA.
 E. नाग a serpent, and
अधिप a king.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागान्तक|नागांतक|नागान्तकः
नागान्तक m. (-कः) Garuda, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.
 E. नाग a
snake, and अन्तक a destroyer; this and similar compounds are
also applied to the “Ardea Argala,” the peacock, and other birds
who are natural enemies of the serpent genus.
