नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य mfn. adj. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)
	 1. Eternal, everlasting, continual, perpe-
tual, past, present, and future.
	 2. Regular, fixed, invariable.
3. Ordinary.
	 4. Necessary.
	 n. adv. (-त्यं) Always, eternally, conti-
nually. sub. Indispensable rite or act.
	 m. (-त्यः) The ocean.
	 f. (-त्या)
1. A name of PĀRVATĪ.
	 2. The goddess MANASĀ.
	 3. A Saktī,
a form of DURGĀ, or personified energy of ŚIVA.
 E. नि particle
implying perpetually, and त्यप aff.
