नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)
	 1. Relating to state or condition.
	 2. Belonging
to the character or office of a perpetual student.
	 3. Firm, fixed.
4. Final.
	 5. Highest, perfect.
	 6. Completely versed in.
	 7. Vowing
perpetual abstinence and chastity.
	 m. (-कः) The Brāhman who
continues with his spiritual preceptor, and always remains in the
condition of the religious student.
 E. निष्ठा certainty, ठक् aff.
