पञ्चाग्नि|पंचाग्नि|पञ्चाग्निः
पञ्चाग्नि n. (-ग्नि)
	 1. A collection of five fires, amidst which a devotee
performs penance during the summer season; or four fires light-
ed severally to the north, south, east and west, and the sun over
head.
	 2. Five mystic fires, supposed to be present in the body.
m. (-ग्निः)
	 1. A householder who maintains five fires, or the do-
mestic one, and one for warming visitors in addition to the
other three.
	 2. One who is acquainted with the doctrine of the
five mystic fires. viz:--अन्वाहार्य्य, पचन, गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय, सभ्य and
आवसथ्य ।
 E. पञ्च five, and अग्नि fire.
