पतञ्ज
पतञ्ज(ञ्च)लि m. (-लिः)
	 1. The name of a saint or Muni and teacher of the
Yoga philosophy, thence called after him PĀTANJALA; also the
author of Mahābhāshya or commentary on PĀṆINI.
	 2. A name of
the poet VARARUCHI.
 E. पत् falling, अञ्जलि the hands joined as a
mark of respect; having fallen from heaven, it is said, in the
shape of small snake, into the hands of the saint PĀṆINI as he
was performing this act of reverence.
