<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्न्याट|पत्न्याटः
पत्न्याट m. (-टः) The Harem, the private or women's apartments. E.
पत्री a wife, आट who goes, from अट, with घञ् affix, and आङ्
prefix.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्र|पत्त्रं|पत्रं
पत्र(त्त्र) n. (-त्रं)
	 1. A leaf.
	 2. A vehicle in general; as a car, a horse, a
camel, &c.
	 3. The wing of a bird.
	 4. The feather of an arrow.
5. The leaf of the Laurus cassia.
	 6. The leaf of a book.
	 7. Gold
leaf, &c. any thin sheet or plate of metal.
	 8. A letter.
	 9. The
blade of a weapon.
	 10. Painting the person as a decoration.
11. A knife, a dagger.
	 12. The leaf of a flower.
	 nf. (-त्रं-त्री) A letter,
any written document or address.
 E. पत् to go, ष्ट्रन् aff. and one
त rejected; also sometimes पत्त्र ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रक|पत्रकं
पत्रक n. (-कं)
	 1. A leaf.
	 2. The leaf of the Laurus cassia.
	 3. Staining
the person with Sandal, &c. by way of decoration.
 E. पत्र with
स्वार्थे-क added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकाहला
पत्रकाहला f. (-ला) The noise made either by the flapping of wings, or
by the rustling of leaves.
 E. पत्र a leaf, a wing, &c. and काहल noise.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकृच्छ्र|पत्रकृच्छ्रः
पत्रकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) A sort of penance, drinking infusion of any leaves
for a given time.
 E. पत्र a leaf, and कृच्छ्र a penance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रगुप्त|पत्रगुप्तः
पत्रगुप्त m. (-प्तः) A species of Euphorbia, commonly Teykānta Sij.
E. पत्र a leaf, and गुप्त hidden.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रङ्गं|पत्रङ्ग
पत्रङ्गं n. (-ङ्गः) Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santalinus.) also पत्राङ्ग.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रझङ्कार|पत्त्रझङ्कार|पत्रझङ्कारः
पत्रझङ्कार m. (-रः) The current of a river: other authorities have in
place of this word, पुरसंस्कार, and पत्रसस्कार, of which the last
appears to be most accurate. रायभटीवृक्षे च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रणा
पत्रणा f. (-णा)
	 1. Trimming the feathered butt of an arrow.
	 2. Pain-
ting figures on the body as a decoration.
 E. पत्र the feather of an
arrow, णी to get, aff. ड.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रगण्डुला
पत्रगण्डुला f. (-ला)
	 1. A woman.
	 2. A kind of barley.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रतरु|पत्रतरुः
पत्रतरु m. (-रुः) The fœtid Mimosa. दुष्खदिरे ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रदारक|पत्रदारकः
पत्रदारक m. (-कः) A saw.
 E. पत्र a leaf, &c. and दृ to tear, ण्वुल् aff. (करात) ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रनाडिका
पत्रनाडिका f. (-का) The fibre or vein of a leaf.
 E. पत्र a leaf, नाडी a
vessel, aff. कन्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=417-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपरशु|पत्रपरशुः
पत्रपरशु m. (-शुः) A small file used by silversmiths, &c.
 E. पत्र a sheet
of metal, परशु an axe; also with पर्शु the same, पत्रपर्शु m. (-र्शुः) (छेनी) ।
