पद्मासन|पद्मासनं|पद्मासनः
पद्मासन n. (-नं) A posture in religious meditation, sitting with the
thighs crossed, one hand resting on the left thigh, the other held
up with the thumb upon the heart; the eyes directed to the
tip of the nose.
	 2. A seat or throne made in the shape of a
lotus, one especially on which idols are placed.
	 m. (-नः)
	 1. A
name of BRAMHĀ.
	 2. The sun.
 E. पद्म a lotus, and आसन sitting.
