पद्मिन्
पद्मिन् m. (द्मी-) An elephant.
	 f. (-नी)
	 1. A multitude of lotuses, or
place abounding in them.
	 2. A woman of one of the four classes
into which the sex is distinguished; the first and the most
excellent. She is thus described in Vāchaspatya:--
भवति कमलनेत्रा नासिकाक्षुद्ररन्ध्रा ।
अविरलकुचयुग्मा दीर्घकेशी कृशाङ्गी ॥
मृदुचरणसुशीला गीतनृत्यानुरक्ता ।
सकलतनुसुवेशा पद्मिनी पद्मगन्धा ॥
3. A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)
	 4. A pool or pond, espe-
cially one deep enough for the growth of the lotus.
	 5. The
fibrous stalk of a lotus.
	 6. A female elephant.
 E. पद्म coloured
marks. &c. or a lotus, इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=420-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

