 E. परभूमि, and स्थ who stays.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूषण
परभूषण n. (-णं) Another's ornament.
	 m. (-णः) Peace purchased by
ceding the produce of lands.
 E. पर, and भूषण ornament.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत्
परभृत् m. (-भृत्) A crow.
 E. पर another, (the cuckoo,) and भृत् who
nourishes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=422-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत|परभृतः
परभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished or nourished by a stranger, fostered,
adopted.
	 m. (-तः) The Indian cuckoo, which is supposed to leave
its eggs in the nest of the crow to be hatched.
 E. पर another,
and भृत nourished.
