पाण्डु mfn. (-ण्डुः-ण्डुः-ण्डु) Pale of yellowish white.
	 m. (-ण्डुः)
	 1. Pale
or yellowish white, (the colour.)
	 2. the name of a sovereign of
ancient Delhi, and nominal father of YUDHIṢṬHIRA and he
other four Pāṇḍava princes; he was a son of Vyāsa by the
wife of Bichitrabirya.
	 3. The jaundice.
	 4. A white elephant.
f. (-ण्डुः) A plant, commonly Māshaparni, (Glycine debilis.) E.
पडि to go, aff. कु, and the penultimate vowel made long.
