पारवत|पारवतः
पारवत m. (-तः) A pigeon. See पारावत.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव|पारशवः
पारशव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)
	 1. Made or derived from an axe.
	 2. Made of
iron.
	 m. (वः)
	 1. The son of a Śūdra woman by a Brāhman.
2. A son by another's wife, an adulterine, a bastard.
	 3. An iron
weapon.
 E. पर another, शव् to go, अच् aff. and अण् implying
descent, added; or पार crossing, शव a corpse, a living corpse;
or परशु an axe, aff. अञ्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=444-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशीक|पारशीकः
पारशीक m. (-कः)
	 1. Persia.
	 2. A native of Persia.
	 3. A Persian horse.
also पारसीक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वध|पारश्वधः
पारश्वध m. (-धः) One armed with an axe, a hatchet-man, a pioneer,
&c.
 E. परश्वध an axe, aff. अण्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वधिक|पारश्वधिकः
पारश्वधिक m. (-कः) A soldier, or any other man armed with an axe. E.
परश्वध an axe, ठञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वय
पारश्वय m. (-यः) Gold.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसिक|पारसिकः
पारसिक m. (-कः) Persia; plu. The Persians also पारसीक.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीक|पारसीकः
पारसीक m. (-कः)
	 1. The kingdom of Persia.
	 2. A Persian, an inhabi-
tant of Persia.
	 3. A Persian horse.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्त्रैणेय|पारस्त्रैणेयः
पारस्त्रैणेय m. (-यः) An adulterine, the son of another's wife.
 E. पर
another, स्त्री woman, ढञ् aff. of descent, and इणङ् augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारा
पारा f. (-रा) Name of a river.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापत|पारापतः
पारापत m. (-तः) A pigeon; also पारावत.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापा
पारापा(वा)र m. (-रः) The ocean.
	 n. (-रं) The two banks of a river. E.
पार the further bank, and अपार near bank.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायण|पारायणं
पारायण n. (-णं)
	 1. Totality, entireness, completeness.
	 2. Going over,
reading or doing any thing completely.
	 3. Going across.
	 4. Reading
a Purāna, or causing it to be read.
	 f. (-णी)
	 1. The goddess SARA-
SWATĪ.
	 2. Action, act.
	 3. Considering, meditating.
	 4. Light.
 E. पार
the boundary or limit, and अयन going to, extending: when used
attributively it remains always neuter.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायणिक|पारायणिकः
पारायणिक m. (-कः)
	 1. A pupil, a scholar.
	 2. A lecturer, a reader of
the Purānas.
 E. पारायण reading through, ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारारुक|पारारुकः
पारारुक m. (-कः) A rock.
 E. पार the further bank, ऋ to go to, aff.
डकञ्. Also पारारुप ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावत|पारावतः
पारावत m. (-तः)
	 1. A dove, a pigeon.
	 2. A monkey.
	 3. A sort of ebony,
(Diospyros glutinosa.)
	 4. A mountain.
	 f. (-ती)
	 1. The name of a
river in the peninsula.
	 2. The fruit of the Annona reticulata.
	 3.
A form of song, peculiar to the cowherds.
 E. पर another, (life,
&c.) अव् to go, to preserve, शतृ participial aff., and अण् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावतपदी
पारावतपदी f. (-दी) Heart-pea: see पारावताङ्घ्रि । काकजङ्घायाम्च ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावताङ्घ्रि|पारावतांघ्रि|पारावताङ्घ्रिः
पारावताङ्घ्रि f. (-ङ्घ्रि) Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.) E.
पारावत a pigeon, अङ्घ्रि a foot, the root being compared to a
pigeon's foot; also similar compounds, as पारावतपदी.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
