पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छ m. (-च्छः) A pigeon.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावार|पारावारं|पारावारः
पारावार m. (-रः) The ocean.
	 n. (-रं) The near and opposite banks of
a stream.
 E. पार the further bank, वृ to surround, with आङ् pre-
fix, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावारीण|पारावारीणः
पारावारीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)
	 1. On both sides of a river, &c.
	 2. One who
goes to both sides.
 E. पार the opposite side, अवार this side,
aff. खञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर|पाराशरं|पाराशरः
पाराशर m. (-रः) A name of the poet VYĀSA.
	 n. (-रं) The rules of
PARĀSARA, or VYĀSA, the conduct of the mendicant orders. E.
पराशर, and अण् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरकल्पिक|पाराशरकल्पिकः
पाराशरकल्पिक m. (-कः) A follower of PARĀSARA, the institutor of
rules for the mendicant order.
 E. पराशर the sage, कल्प aff., and
ठक् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरि|पाराशरिः
पाराशरि m. (-रिः)
	 1. VYĀSA.
	 2. An epithet of Sūkra.
 E. पराशर, and इञ् patronymic aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरिन्
पाराशरिन् m. (-री)
	 1. A recluse. Plu. The religious mendicant or
Brāhman, who having passed through the three stages of
student, house-holder, and ascetic leads a vagrant life, and
subsists upon alms; or the class of ascetics who study the Shā-
riraka Sutra of Vyāsa.
 E. पाराशर्य्य VYĀSA, the author of the rules
of this order, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर्य्य|पाराशर्य|पाराशर्यः|पाराशर्य्यः
पाराशर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The poet VYĀSA.
 E. पाराशर the father of the poet,
and यञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिकाङ्क्षिन्|पारिकांक्षिन्
पारिकाङ्क्षिन् m. (-ङ्क्षी)
	 1. An ascetic, one who devotes his days to
devout contemplation.
	 2. The religious mendicant.
 E. परि imply-
ing secession, (abandoning worldly wishes,) काङ्क्षि to desire,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">Page445-b+ 60</a>]
and णिनि aff.; or पारि derived from पर, supreme felicity, and
काङ्क्षिन् who desires.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिखेय
पारिखेय f. (-यीः) Surrounded by a ditch.
 E. परिखा, affix, ढक् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजात|पारिजातः
पारिजात m. (-तः)
	 1. Name of one of the five trees of paradise sup-
posed to have been produced at the churning of the ocean.
	 2.
The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)
 E. पारि said to mean, above,
and जात produced.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजातक|पारिजातकः
पारिजातक m. (-कः)
	 1. A tree of paradise.
	 2. The coral tree.
 E. कन्
added to the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=445-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाय्य|पारिणाय्यं
पारिणाय्य mfn. (य्यः-य्यी-य्यं) Belonging to specifically or peculiarly.
	 n.
(-य्यं) Property received at the time of marriage by a woman.
	 f.
(य्यी)
	 1. Relating to marriage.
 E. परि about, around, णी to get,
aff. ष्यञ् ।
