पिङ्ग|पिंग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Of a tawny colour.
	 m. (-ङ्गः)
	 1. Tawny, (the
colour.
	 2. A rat.
	 3. A buffalo.
	 n. (-ङ्गं) A young animal.
	 f. (-ङ्गा)
	 1.
A yellow dye: see गोरोचना.
	 2. Asafœtida.
	 3. A tubular vessel of
the body, which according to the Yoga system, is the channel of
respiration and circulation for one side.
	 4. A name of DURGĀ.
5. Turmeric.
	 6. Bamboo manna.
	 f. (-ङ्गी) A sort of Mimosa, (M.
suma, Rox.)
 E. पिजि to colour, aff. अच्; or पिङ्ग tawny, aff. टाप्, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गकपिशा|पिंगकपिशा
पिङ्गकपिशा f. (-शा) A cockroach.
 E. पिङ्ग tawny, and कपिश brown.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=448-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

