	 1. The
pomegranate.
	 2. Cuttle-fish-bone considered to be the foam of
the sea.
 E. पिण्ड a ball, &c. ईर to go, to resemble, aff. अण्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीशूर|पिंडीशूर|पिण्डीशूरः
पिण्डीशूर m. (रः) A cot queen, an effeminate braggart.
 E. पिण्ड a
house, and शूर a hero.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोद्धरण|पिंडोद्धरण
पिण्डोद्धरण n. (-णं) Participating in obsequial offerings, presenting
them to common ancestors.
 E. पिण्ड, and डद्धरण sharing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोलि|पिंडोलि|पिंडोलिः|पिण्डोलिः
पिण्डोलि f. (-लिः) Orts, leaving of a meal, or fragments dropped
from the mouth.
 E. पिडि to heap, aff. ओलि.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्या
पिण्या f. (ण्या) Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.)
 E. पण्
to praise, ण्यत् aff., and इ substituted for the radical vowel: see
पण्या.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्याक|पिण्याकं|पिण्याकः
पिण्याक m. (-कः)
	 1. The sediments of seeds, &c. ground for oil; oil-
cake, or the seeds after expression.
	 2. Saffron.
	 3. Asafœtida.
4. Incense.
 E. पिषु to pound or bruise, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=450-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितामह|पितामहः
पितामह m. (हः)
	 1. A paternal grandfather.
	 2. A name of BRAHMĀ.
the great father of all.
	 f. (-ही) A paternal grandmother.
 E. पितृ
a father, and डामह aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृ
पितृ m. (-ता) A father, dual, (-रौ) Mother and father, parents.
plu. always, (-रः)
	 1. Paternal ancestors.
	 2. The manes, or the
deceased and deified progenitors of mankind, inhabiting a
peculiar region or heaven, or according to some, the orbit of the
moon.
 E. पा to nourish, Unādi aff. तृच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक|पितृकं
पितृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)
	 1. Paternal, ancestral, parental, obsequial,
relating or belonging to parents or progenitors.
 E. पितृ a sire,
and कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितॄक्थ
पितॄक्थ n. (-क्थं) Paternal property.
 E. पितृ, and ऋक्थ wealth.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकर्म्मन्|पितृकर्मन्
पितृकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Obsequial rites.
 E. पितृ, and कर्म्मन् act.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकार्य्य|पितृकार्य
पितृकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Obsequial rites.
 E. पितृ, and कार्य्य to be done.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकानन|पितृकाननं
पितृकानन n. (-नं) A cemetery.
 E. पितृ an ancestor, and कानन a
wood.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक्रिया
पितृक्रिया f. (-या) Obsequial rites.
 E. पितृ, and क्रिया ceremony.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगण|पितृगणः
पितृगण m. (-णः) A class of progenitors, the sons of the Ṛṣis or
Prajāpatis: the principal classes are the Somasads descended
from VIRĀT, the Agnishwattās from MARĪCI, Bārhishads from
ATRI, Somapās from BHRIGU, Havishmats from ANGIRAS,
Ājyapas from PULASTYA, Sukālins from VASHISTHA; there are
also the Agnidaghas and Anagnidagdhas, Kavyas and Saumyas.
E. पितृ father, (of mankind,) गण a troop.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगामिन्
पितृगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Belonging to, or pertaining to a
father.
 E. पितृ, and गामिन् what goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगृह|पितृगृहं
पितृगृह n. (-हं)
	 1. A paternal mansion.
	 2. A burying ground, a
cemetery.
 E. पितृ a deceased ancestor, and गृह a house.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृघातक|पितृघातकः
पितृघातक m. (-कः) A parricide.
 E. पितृ and घातक a slayer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतर्पण|पितृतर्पणं
पितृतर्पण n. (णं)
	 1. The part of the hand between the middle
finger and thumb, sacred to the manes.
	 2. Gifts in honour of
deceased relations, distributed at the Śrāddhas or funeral
ceremonies.
	 3. The act of throwing water out of the right hand
at seasons of ablution, by way of offering to the manes or
deceased ancestors in general.
 E. पितृ a father, a progenitor, and
तर्पण satisfying.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतस्
पितृतस् ind. From or by the father.
 E. पितृ, and तसि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतिथि|पितृतिथिः
पितृतिथि m. (-थिः) Day of new moon, on which she rises invisible. E.
पितृ a progenitor, and तिथि a lunar day, sacred to the manes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतीर्थ|पितृतीर्थं
पितृतीर्थ n. (-र्थं)
	 1. Gaya, the city so called, where the performance
of funeral sacrifices is peculiarly efficacious and meritorious.
	 2.
The part between the forefinger and thumb, sacred to the
manes.
 E. पितृ a progenitor, and तीर्थ a place of pilgrimage.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृत्व
पितृत्व n. (-त्वं)
	 1. Paternity.
	 2. The state or condition of a Pitṛ, or
deified progenitor.
 E. त्व added to पितृ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृदान|पितृदानं
पितृदान n. (-नं) Gift in honour of deceased ancestors.
 E. पितृ a pro-
genitor, and दान giving or gift; also with कन् added, पितृदानक
n. (-कं).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृदाय|पितृदायः
पितृदाय m. (-यः) Patrimony.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितदैवत
पितदैवत n. (-तं) The tenth lunar asterism or Maghā.
 E. पितृ, and
दैवत divinity, presiding over the asterism.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपक्ष|पितृपक्षः
पितृपक्ष m. (-क्षः)
	 1. The paternal side.
	 2. The second half of the
month of Bhādrapada peculiarly appointed for the celebration of
obsequial rites to the manes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपति|पितृपतिः
पितृपति m. (-तिः) YAMA, regent of the dead.
 E. पितृ a deceased pro-
genitor, and पति lord.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपद
पितृपद n. (-दं) The world or state of the manes.
 E. पितृ, and पद
degree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपात्र
पितृपात्र n. (-त्रं) A cup or vessel used at obsequial rites.
 E. पितृ, and
पात्र a cup.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपितृ
पितृपितृ m. (-ता) A paternal grandfather.
 E. पितृ a father, and पितृ the
same, father's father.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृप्रसू
पितृप्रसू f. (-सूः)
	 1. Twilight.
	 2. A father's mother.
 E. पितृ a deceased
progenitor, and प्रसू the parent; the first is the time when
manes are abroad.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृप्राप्त
पितृप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)
	 1. Received from a father.
	 2. Inherited
patrimonially.
 E. पितृ, and प्राप्त obtained.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृबन्धु|पितृबंधु|पितृबन्धुः
पितृबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A remote or cognate kinsman by the father's side,
as the son of the paternal grandfather's sister, of the paternal
grandmother's sister, and of the father's maternal uncle. E.
पितृ, and बन्धु a kinsman.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृबान्धव|पितृबान्धवः
पितृबान्धव m. (-वः) A remote kinsman of the paternal line: see the
last.
 E. पितृ, and बान्धव a kinsman.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभक्ति
पितृभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Filial duty to a father.
 E. पितृ, and भक्ति devotion.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभोजन|पितृभोजनः
पितृभोजन n. (-नं)
	 1. Food offered to the manes.
	 2. A father's food.
3. A kind of pulse: see Māsha.
 E. पितृ, and भोजन food.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभ्रातृ
पितृभ्रातृ m. (-ता) A father's brother.
 E. पितृ, and भ्रातृ a brother.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमन्दिर|पितृमंदिर
पितृमन्दिर n. (-रं)
	 1. The paternal mansion.
	 2. A cemetery.
 E. पितृ,
and मन्दिर a dwelling.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमेध|पितृमेधः
पितृमेध n. (-धं) Obsequial rites.
 E. पितृ, and मेध sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयज्ञ|पितृयज्ञः
पितृयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)
	 1. Obsequial rites.
	 2. Oblations of water daily
offered to the manes.
 E. पितृ a progenitor, and यज्ञ sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयाण
पितृयाण n. (णं) The carriage of the manes, a car to convey holy
persons after their decease to heaven.
 E. पितृ a progenitor, and
यान a vehicle. पितरो यान्ति अनेन या-करणे ल्युट् संज्ञात्वात् णत्वम् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृराज
पितृराज m. (-जः) An epithet of Yama.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृरुप
पितृरुप m. (-पः) An epithet of SĪVA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृलोक|पितृलोकः
पितृलोक m. (-कः) The world or sphere of the manes: it is variously
situated, but principally in Bhuva region or midheaven.
 E. पितृ,
and लोक world.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवत्
पितृवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a father living, &c.
 E. पितृ, and
मतुप् poss. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवन|पितृवनं
पितृवन n. (-नं) A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or
buried.
 E. पितृ a deceased progenitor, वन a wood.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवनेचर|पितृवनेचरः
पितृवनेचर m. (-रः)
	 1. SĪVA.
	 2. A goblin.
 E. पितृवन a cemetery, in the
seventh case, and चर who goes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवसति|पितृवसतिः
पितृवसति f. (-तिः) A cemetery.
 E. पितृ a deceased progenitor, and
वसति an abode.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=451-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवाक्पर
पितृवाक्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Obedient to parents.
 E. पितृ, वाच् speech,
पर attentive to.
