पिशाच|पिशाचः
पिशाच m. (-चः) A goblin, a fiend, a malevolent being something
between an infernal imp and a ghost, but always described as
fierce and malignant.
	 f. (-ची) A female imp, a she-demon.
 E. पिश
for पिशित flesh, and अश् to eat, aff. अण्, deriv. irr.; According to
Vāchaspatya:--पिशितमाचामति आ + चम-बा-ड० पृषो० । also with कन्
added, पिशाचक, पिशाचिका.
