पिष्ट|पिष्टं
पिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Ground, pounded, bruised.
	 2. Clasped, (as the
hands,) squeezed, rubbed together.
	 3. Kneaded.
	 n. (-ष्टं)
	 1. Lead.
2. The flour or meal of any thing that is ground.
 E. पिष् to
pound or bruise, aff. क्त.
