पुत्त्राचार्य्य
पुत्त्राचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A father instructed in sacred science by his son.
 E. पुत्त्र, and आचार्य्य a teacher.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रार्थिन्
पुत्त्रार्थिन् Adj. Wishing for a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रान्नाद
पुत्त्रान्नाद m. (-दः)
	 1. One who is maintained by his son.
	 2. A mendicant
of a particular order.
 E. पुत्त्र a son, अन्न food, and आद who takes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिका
पुत्त्रिका f. (-का)
	 1. A daughter.
	 2. A doll, a puppet.
	 3. The cotton or
pappus of the tamarisk.
 E. पुत्त्री a daughter, कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकापुत्त्र
पुत्त्रिकापुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)
	 1. The son of a daughter, appointed to raise issue
for her father; one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by the old
Hindu law.
	 2. A daughter's son, who by agreement becomes
the son of her father, (according to some interpretation.)
	 3. A
daughter who returns to her father's house being considered as
his son, (according to other interpretation.)
	 4. A grandson in
general.
 E. पुत्त्रिका a daughter, and पुत्त्र a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकाभर्त्तृ
पुत्त्रिकाभर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A daughter's husband.
 E. पुत्त्रिका, and भर्त्तृ husband.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकाप्रसू
पुत्त्रिकाप्रसू f. (-सूः) The mother of a daughter.
 E. पुत्त्रिका, and प्रसू a
mother.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकासुत
पुत्त्रिकासुत m. (-तः) A daughter's son, a grandson.
 E. पुत्त्रिका, and सुत a son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिन्
पुत्त्रिन् m. (-त्त्री) The father of a son.
	 f. (-णी)
	 1. The mother of a son, or
of children generally.
	 2. A parasite plant.
	 3. A plant, (Siphonan-
thus Indica.)
 E. पुत्त्र a son or offspring, इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रीय
पुत्त्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a son, or child.
	 2. Filial.
f. (-या) The desire of a son.
 E. पुत्त्र, and छ aff.; also पुत्त्र्य.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रीयत्
पुत्त्रीयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Wishing for a son.
 E. पुत्त्र, and क्यच् aff. or
nominal v., शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रेप्सु
पुत्त्रेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desiring a son.
 E. पुत्त्र, and इप्सु desirous.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रेष्टि
पुत्त्रेष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A sacrifice performed for the purpose of obtaining
children.
 E. पुत्त्र, offspring, and इष्टि sacrifice; also with कन् added
in the feminine form, पुत्त्रेष्टिका.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रैश्वर्य्य
पुत्त्रैश्वर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Resignation of property or power by a father to his
son.
 E. पुत्त्र, and ऐशर्य्य masterhood.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्र्य
पुत्त्र्य mfn. (-त्त्र्यः-त्त्र्या-त्त्र्यं) Belonging to a son, &c.
 E. पुत्त्र, and यत् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुथ
पुथ r. 4th cl. (पुथ्यति) To hurt or kill. r. 10th cl. (पोथयति-ते)
	 1. To shine.
2. To speak. (इ) पुथि r. 1st cl. (पुन्थति)
	 1. To hurt.
	 2. To suffer pain
or uneasiness. हिंसे दिवा० पर० सक० सेट् । वधे० सक० क्लेशे अक० भ्वा० पर० सेट०
इदित् । दीप्तौ चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुद्गल|पुद्गलः
पुद्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)
	 1. Beautiful, handsome, of a handsome form or
figure.
	 2. Having form or property.
	 m. (-लः)
	 1. The body.
	 2. The
soul.
	 3. An atom.
	 4. An epithet of Śiva.
 E. पूर what fills, and गल
what decays, deriv. irr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपाक
पुनःपाक m. (-कः) Repeated boiling or cooking.
 E. पुनर्, and पाक dressing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुनर्
पुनःपुनर् Ind. Repeatedly, again and again.
 E. पुनर् again, repeated.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुना
पुनःपुना f. (-ना) The Pumpā river in Bihar.
 E. पुनर् again, repeated,
irrly.; perhaps from the meandering course of the river; or cor-
rectly पुनः पुनाति पू-नक्-पृषो० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसन्धान
पुनःसन्धान n. (-नं) Reuniting.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसम्भव|पुनःसंभवः
पुनःसम्भव m. (-वः) Coming into existence again, metempsychosis.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंस्कार|पुनःसंस्कारः
पुनःसंस्कार m. (-रः) Repetition of any essential ceremony, as re-investi-
ture with the sacrificial string of a Brāhman, who has forfeited
it by unknowingly drinking spirits, &c.
 E. पुनर् again, संस्कार
ceremony.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्
पुनर् Ind.
	 1. Again, once more.
	 2. But, on the contrary, neverthe-
less, however.
	 3. Assuredly, certainly.
	 4. A particle indicating
division or change of subject.
 E. पण् to praise, अर् aff., and the
radical vowel changed to उ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=457-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरपि
पुनरपि Ind.
	 1. Even, again, also.
	 2. And, on the other hand.
