पृषदश्व|पृषदश्वः
पृषदश्व m. (-श्वः) The god of air, or wind divinely personified.
 E. पृषत्
the porcine deer, or a drop of rain, and अश्व a horse; whose steeds
are like deer, or may be considered as the drops of rain, accom-
panying a gale.
