<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामह|पैतामहं
पैतामह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)
	 1. Belonging or relating to the grand-father,
inherited from him, (property, &c.)
	 2. Relating to Brahmā.
	 m. (-हः)
plu. Ancestors, forefathers.
 E. पितामह, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृक|पैतृकं
पैतृक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)
	 1. Paternal, ancestral, belonging or relating to the
father or to progenitors.
	 2. Sacred to the manes.
	 n. (कं) A Śhrā-
ddha performed in honor of the manes.
 E. पितृ a father, ठञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृकभूमि|पैतृकभूमिः
पैतृकभूमि f. (-मिः)
	 1. Father-land, the country of one's ancestors.
	 2. A
paternal estate.
 E. पैतृक, भूमि land.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृकष्वसेय
पैतृकष्वसेय m. (-यः) A paternal aunt's son.
	 f. (-यी) The daughter of a
paternal aunt.
 E. पितृ a father, स्वसृ a sister, aff. ढक् whence the
vowel of स्वसृ is rejected.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृमत्य|पैतृमत्यः
पैतृमत्य m. (-त्यः) The son of an unmarried woman.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृस्वस्रीय
पैतृस्वस्रीय mf. (-यः-या) The son or daughter of a father's sister.
 E. पितृ
a father, स्वसृ a sister, छण् aff. whence the ऋ of स्वसृ is changed to
री ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्ति
पैत्ति mfn. (-त्तः-त्ती-त्तं) Biliary, bilious.
 E. पित्त, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तिक|पैत्तिकः
पैत्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bilious, biliary.
 E. पित्त, and ठञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र|पैत्रं
पैत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)
	 1. Paternal, ancestral, relating or belonging to a
parent or progenitor.
	 2. Sacred to the manes.
	 n. (-त्रं)
	 1. The part
of the hand between the thumb and forefinger, or according to
some the root of the forefinger.
	 2. A year, month, day, &c. of the
Pitṛs.
 E. पितृ a parent, aff. अण् । Also पैत्र्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्राहोरात्र|पैत्राहोरात्रः
पैत्राहोरात्र m. (-त्रः) A day and night of the Pitṛs, or progenitors, equal
to a month of mortals.
 E. पैत्र relating to the manes, अहन् a day,
and रात्रि night.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्रिक्
पैत्रिक् mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Paternal, ancestral.
 E. पितृ, and ठञ् aff. and the
vowel changed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैल|पैलः
पैल m. (-लः) A Sage, the promulgator of the Rig-Veda.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलव
पैलव Adj.
	 f. (-वी) Made of the wood of the pilu tree.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशल्य|पैशल्यं
पैशल्य n. (-ल्यं) Mildness, affability.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच|पैशाचः
पैशाच mfn. (-चः-ची-चं) Infernal, demoniacal, relating or belonging to a
Pīśacha or goblin.
	 m. (-चः)
	 1. A mode of marriage the ravishment
of a girl by her lover; it is the last of the eight forms of marriage
in Hindu law, in it the lover defiles a damsel without her consent
when she is sleeping or intoxicated or deranged in intellect.
	 2. A
kind of demon.
	 f. (-ची)
	 1. A present to a friend, or to secure friendly
regard made at a religious ceremony.
	 2. Night.
	 3. The lowest Prā-
krita dialect spoken on the stage by demons in Hindu dramatical
representations.
 E. पिशाच an imp, aff. अण् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाचिक
पैशाचिक Adj.
	 f. (-की) Infernal, demoniacal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन|पैशुनं
पैशुन n. (-नं)
	 1. Information, reporting evil of others.
	 2. Roguery.
3. Backbiting.
 E. पिशुन a spy, &c. अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन्ध
पैशुन्ध n. (-न्यं)
	 1. Information, espionage, &c.
	 2. Depravity, wickedness.
E. पिशुन a spy, a rogue, aff. यञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्ट|पैष्टः
पैष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टी-ष्टं) Ground or made up into a cake.
	 f. (-ष्टी) Spiritu-
ous liquor distilled from meal.
 E. पिष्ट ground, अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिक|पैष्टिकं
पैष्टिक n. (-कं)
	 1. A quantity of cakes.
	 2. Spirituous liquor distilled from
meal.
	 f. (की) Made of flour.
 E. पिष्ट, and ठक् aff.
