प्रकर|प्रकरं|प्रकरः
प्रकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what does much or well.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A
heap a, quantity.
	 2. A bundle of flowers, a nosegay.
	 3. Aid, assis-
tance, friendship.
	 4. Usage, custom, continuance of a similar
practice.
	 5. Respect.
	 6. Seduction, abduction.
	 n. (-रं) Aloe wood,
(Agallochum.)
	 f. (-री)
	 1. Theatrical dress or disguise, as wearing
a woman's garb, &c.
	 2. An episodical incident in a drama.
	 3. An
open piece of ground, the meeting of four roads, or the proper
scite of any magical operations.
 E. प्र before कृ to make, aff. अप् ।
