प्रयत|प्रयतः
प्रयत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Well-governed, restrained, self-subdued.
2. Careful, prudent.
	 m. (-तः) A holy or pious person, one purified
by austerity and mortification.
	 f. (-ता)
	 1. Pure.
	 2. Submissive.
	 3.
Keeping the organs of sense under restraint.
 E. प्र intensely, यत् to
to endeavour, aff. नङ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतात्मन्
प्रयतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Devout, pious of a holy spirit.
 E. प्रयत, and आत्मन् soul.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्न|प्रयत्नः
प्रयत्न n. (-त्नं)
	 1. Continued or presevering effort, exertion.
	 2. Act, action.
3. (In logic,) Active effort of three kinds, engaging in any act,
prosecuting it, and completing it.
	 4. Caution, care.
	 5. Articula-
tion of sounds.
 E. प्र intensitive, यत्न effort.
