प्राजापत्य|प्राजापत्यं|प्राजापत्यः
प्राजापत्य m. (-त्यः)
	 1. A form of marriage, the gift of a girl, respectfully
by her father to her lover.
	 2. A name of Allāhābād or Prayāga.
3. The first of the persons, called Vāsudevas, by the Jainas.
	 n.
(-त्यं)
	 1. A sort of penance, eating once a day for three days in
the morning, once in the night for three days subsisting, three
days on food given as alms, and fasting three days more.
	 2.
A particular sacrifice performed before appointing a daughter to
raise issue in default of male heirs.
	 3. The asterism Rohīnī.
	 f.
(त्या) Giving away the whole of one's property before entering up-
on the life of an ascetic or mendicant.
 E. प्रजापति BRAMHA,
and ण्यत् aff.
