प्रौ
प्रौ(प्रो)ढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)
	 1. Full-grown.
	 2. Confident, bold, arrogant.
	 3.
Impudent.
	 4. Full-grown, (as the moon.)
	 5. Thick, heavy, (darkness,
&c.)
	 6. Forward, (as the hand to seize any thing.)
	 7. Raised, lifted
up.
	 8. Controverted.
	 9. Old.
	 10. Married.
	 f. (-ढा)
	 1. A woman from
thirty years of age to fifty-five.
	 2. A description of the Nāyikā
or mistress, a woman whose feelings are violent or impetuous, or
one who is not in any awe of her lover or husband.
 E. प्र before,
वह to bear, aff. क्त ।
