प्लव|प्लवं|प्लवः
प्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Who or what goes by leaps or jumps, leaping, just-
ing, a tumbler.
	 m. (-वः)
	 1. Jumping, leaping, plunging, going by
leaps or plunges.
	 2. Swimming, floating, diving.
	 3. A raft, a float.
4. A frog.
	 5. A monkey.
	 6. A sheep.
	 7. A diver, or bird so called,
(Pelicanus fusicollis.)
	 8. A sort of duck.
	 9. A man of a low or de-
graded tribe.
	 10. Waved-leaf fig-tree, (Ficus infectoria.)
	 11. The
continuous protracted accent, the lengthened sound of vowels in
poetry or the Vedas.
	 12. Protracting a sentence through several
stanzas.
	 13. A declivity or shelving ground.
	 14. A piece of water.
15. A sort of basket or snare of basket-work for catching fish.
	 16.
An enemy.
	 17. Sending, directing.
	 n. (-वं)
	 1. A sort of grass, (Cy-
perus rotundus.)
	 2. Fragrant grass in general, or another sort E.
प्लु to go, aff. अच् ।
