फल्गु|फल्गुः
फल्गु mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु)
	 1. Pithless, sapless.
	 2. Vain, unprofitable,
unmeaning, useless.
	 3. Weak, feeble.
	 f. (-ल्गुः)
	 1. The opposite
leaved fig-tree, (F. oppositi-folia, Rox.)
	 2. The name of a river
which is said to run underneath Gya.
	 3. Falsehood, false or lying
speech.
	 4. A red powder, usually of the root of wild ginger, col-
oured with sappan wood, and thrown over one another by the
Hindus, at the Holi festival.
	 5. The spring season.
 E. फल् to bear
fruit, Unādi aff. गुक ।
