बन्धूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)
	 1. Wavy, undulating, uneven.
	 2. Bowing, bent.
3. Beautiful, handsome.
	 m. (-रः) A hole, a chasm.
 E. बन्ध् to bind,
Unādi aff. ऊरच्; also बन्धुर ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूलि|बंधूलि|बंधूलिः|बन्धूलिः
बन्धूलि m. (-लिः) A flower, (Pentapetes, &c.): see बन्धूक.
 E. बन्ध् and ऊलिच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्य|बंध्य|बन्ध्यः
बन्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं)
	 1. Barren, unfruitful, not bearing fruit in due
season.
	 2. Detained, confined, under arrest.
	 f. (-न्ध्या)
	 1. A child-
less woman.
	 2. A barren cow.
	 3. A perfume, commonly Bālā. E.
बन्ध् to bind, aff. यत् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभूवस्
बभूवस् mfn. (-वान्-भूषी-वः) Been, become.
 E. भू to be, बसु aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्र
बभ्र r. 1st cl. (बभ्रति) To go; also वभ्र ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रवी
बभ्रवी f. (-वी) A name of DURGĀ.
 E. बभ्रु ŚIVA, and ङीप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रि|बभ्रिः
बभ्रि mfn. (-भ्रिः-भ्रिः-भ्रि) Who or what has, holds, possesses, &c.
 E. भृ to
cherish, किन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रु|बभ्रुः
बभ्रु mfn. (-भ्रुः-भ्रुः or -भ्रूः-भ्रु)
	 1. Large, great.
	 2. Tawny, &c.
	 3. Bald-
headed through disease.
	 m. (-भ्रुः)
	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.
	 2. SĪVA.
3. AGNI or fire.
	 4. A large ichneumon.
	 5. The name of a
Muni or holy sage.
	 6. A rat.
	 n. (-भ्रु)
	 1. A tawny or brown
colour.
	 2. Any object of that colour.
 E. भृ to fill, aff. कु, and the
initial repeated; or बभ्र, उ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भर|बंभर|बंभरः|बम्भरः
बम्भर m. (-रः) A bee.
 E. बम्भ् imitative sound, रा to make, क aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भराली|बंभराली
बम्भराली f. (-ली) A fly.
 E. बम्भ् imitative sound, रा to make, लच् aff.: also
भम्भराली ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर
बर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Best, excellent.
	 m. (-रः)
	 1. A boon, a blessing, &c.
2. A Son-in-law.
	 3. Surrounding, encompassing.
	 4. A catamite.
	 n.
(-र) Saffron.
	 m. (-रः) Asparagus racemosus.
	 f. (-रा) The three my-
robalans.
	 n. or ind. (-रं) Slightly desired, preferable.
 E. बॄ, to
select, &c. अच् aff.; the root is more usually written वॄ, and the
derivative वर, q. v.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्ब|बर्ब
बर्ब्ब (र्ब) r. 1st cl. (बर्ब्बति) To go.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बट|बर्बट|बर्बटः|बर्ब्बटः
बर्ब्बट mf. (-टः-टी) A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.) “बरबटी” f. (-टी) A
whore.
 E. बर्ब्ब् to go, अट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बणा|बर्बणा
बर्ब्बणा f. (-णा) A blue fly.
 E. बर्ब्ब् to go, aff. युच् or ल्यु; or derived from
बर् imitative sound, and बण् or वण् to sound, aff. अच्, बर्ब्बण or
बर्ब्बण ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बर|बर्बर|बर्बरः
बर्ब्बर m. (-रः)
	 1. A blockhead, a fool.
	 2. A barbarian.
 E. बर्ब्ब् to go, अरच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्बुर|बर्बुरः
बर्बुर n. (-रं) Water.
 E. बर्ब-उरच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह r. 1st cl. (बर्हते)
	 1. To be pre-eminent or excellent; (also वर्ह, but less
usually.
	 2. To speak or tell.
	 3. To kill or hurt.
	 4. To cover.
	 5. To
remember.
	 6. To spread.
	 7. To give. (In these senses it is more
usually वर्ह.) r. 10th cl. (-बर्हयति) To hurt or kill; also वर्ह ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह mn. (-र्हः-र्हं)
	 1. A peacock's tail.
	 2. A leaf.
	 3. Dependents, retinue.
E. बर्ह to spread, &c. aff. अच्; this word and the corresponding
forms are more usually derived from वृह् to increase, &c. and are
written with the semi-vowel: see वर्ह, वर्हिस्, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल r. 1st and 10th cls. (बलति बलयति)
	 1. To live.
	 2. To hoard
grain.
	 3. To prevent or obstruct wealth. r. 1st cl. (बलते)
	 1. To kill
2. To go. r. 10th cl. (बालयते) To explain. (बालयति) To support,
nourish, rear, as a child.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, stout, robust, powerful.
	 m. (-लः)
	 1. BALA-
DEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA, and the third of the three
incarnations termed RAMĀS.
	 2. A crow.
	 3. A demon, slain by IN-
DRA.
	 4. The Varunā tree.
	 n. (-लं)
	 1. Strength, power.
	 2. Bulkiness.
3. Form, figure.
	 4. An army, forces.
	 5. Gum myrrh.
	 6. Semen
virile.
	 7. The body.
	 8. The leaf of a tree.
	 9. Blood.
	 10. Rigour,
severity.
	 f. (-ला) An aquatic plant, (Sida cordifolia.)
 E. बल् to live,
aff. अच्; in some of the senses it may be derived from वल् to go or
surround, and may then be written with the semi-vowel; see वल ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्ष|बलक्षः
बलक्ष m. (-क्षः) White, (the colour, &c.)
 E. बल strength, and क्षै to waste,
aff. क; this word is more properly written वलक्ष, q. v.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलज|बलजं
बलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by or from strength or power.
	 n. (-जं)
1. A field.
	 2. A city-gate.
	 3. Fruit.
	 4. War.
	 5. Pith, marrow.
	 f.
(-जा)
	 1. A pretty or handsome woman.
	 2. The earth.
	 3. Arabian
jasmine.
 E. बल strength, and ज born.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलद|बलदः
बलद m. (-दः) An ox.
 E. बल, द who gives.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलद्विष्
बलद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A name of INDRA.
 E. बल, and द्विष् a foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेव|बलदेवः
बलदेव m. (-वः) BALADEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.
	 2. Air, wind.
f. (-वा) A medicinal plant, commonly Trāyamāṇa.
 E. बल the same
and देव divine, or बल strength, and देव who sports.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलनिग्रह
बलनिग्रह m. (-हः) Weakening, reducing strength or power.
 E. बल, and
निग्रह restraint.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलप्रसू
बलप्रसू f. (-सूः) ROHINĪ, the mother of BALARĀMA.
 E. बल and प्रसू the
mother.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्र|बलभद्रः
बलभद्र m. (-द्रः)
	 1. BALADEVA.
	 2. ANANTA, the great serpent, consi-
dered as identified with the proceding, BALADEVA being re-
garded by some authorities as an incarnation of ANANTA.
	 3. A
strong or robust man.
	 4. A tree, commonly Lodh.
	 f. (-द्रा)
	 1. A
young girl, a maiden.
	 2. A drug, commonly Trāyamāṇa.
 E. बल
strength, and भद्र auspicious, excellent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्रिका
बलभद्रिका f. (-का) A medicinal plant, Trāyamāṇa.
 E. बलभद्र the
same, and कन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभिद्
बलभिद् mfn. (-भिद्) Breaking or routing an army.
	 m. (-भिद्) INDRA. E.
बल and भिद् who or what destroys.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलराम|बलरामः
बलराम m. (-मः) The demi-god named BALARĀMA, half brother to
KṚṢṆA, and the third of the RĀMAS; according to some, the
eighth Avatār of VIṢṆU.
 E. बल strength, रम् to sport, aff. घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलल|बललः
बलल m. (-लः) BALARĀMA: see the last.
 E. बल strength, aff. कलच्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्|बलवन्त्
बलवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Strong, stout, lusty, powerful.
 E. बल
strength, and मतुप् poss. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्ता
बलवत्ता f. (-त्ता) Strength, power.
 E. बलवत्, and तल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलबर्द्धन
बलबर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)
	 1. Strengthe ning.
	 2. Ennobling.
 E. बल, and
वर्द्धन augmenting.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्द्धिन्
बलवर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि) Strengthening.
	 f. (-र्द्धिनी) A plant: see
जीवक.
 E. बल, and वर्द्धिन् what augments.
