बुद्ध|बुद्धः
बुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Known, understood.
	 m. (-द्धः)
	 1. A generic name
for a deified teacher of the Bauddha sect, amongst whom numer-
ous Buddhas are reckoned; the name is especially applied to the
9th incarnation of VIṢṆU and the apparent founder of the reli-
gion of the Bauddhas; the term is often confounded but impro-
perly, with a Jina: see जिन.
	 2. A sage, a wise or learned man.
E. बुध् to know, aff. क्तः see बुध ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धद्रव्य|बुद्धद्रव्यं
बुद्धद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) Avarice, covetous accumulation.
 E. बुद्ध known, द्रव्य thing.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धि|बुद्धिः
