ब्रह्मपुत्त्र
ब्रह्मपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)
	 1. A sort of poison.
	 2. The Brahmaputra river, which
rises in the Himālaya and with the Ganges falls into the Bay of
Bengal.
	 2. A place of pilgrimage, probably the source of the
stream.
	 f. (-त्री)
	 1. The SARASWATĪ river.
	 2. The goddess SARAS-
WATĪ.
 E. ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ and पुत्त्र offspring.
