भर्त्तृताङ्गत|भर्तृताङ्गत
भर्त्तृताङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subject, married.
 E. भर्त्तृतां 2nd case, and गत gone.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृदारक|भर्तृदारक|भर्तृदारकः|भर्त्तृदारकः
भर्त्तृदारक m. (-कः) A young prince, designated as successor, and
associated to the empire, (in theatrical language.)
	 f. (-रिका) (in
theatrical language.) A princess.
 E. भर्त्तृ the master or monarch,
and दारक the son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृहरि|भर्तृहरि|भर्तृहरिः|भर्त्तृहरिः
भर्त्तृहरि m. (-रिः) The brother of VIKRAMĀDITYA, prince and poet.
E. भर्त्तृ a prince and हरि VIṢṆU, a deity amongst kings.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्रिम
भर्त्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Maintained, nourished, supported.
 E. भृ to
nourish, क्ति aff. and मप् added.
