भावन|भावनं|भावनः
भावन nf. (-नं-ना)
	 1. Mental perception, recollection, the present con-
sciousness of past ideas or perceptions.
	 2. Imagination.
	 3. Religi
ous and abstract meditation.
	 4. Looking about, (literally or figur-
atively.) observing, investigating.
	 5. Causing to be.
	 6. Decorating
any person or object with flowers, perfume, &c, scenting, anoint-
ing.
	 7. Steeping, infusion, especially repeatedly drying the article
by day and keeping it moist at night.
	 8. (In arithmetic,) Composi-
tion.
	 9. (In law,) Ascertainment, proof.
 E. भू to be, in the causal
form, to bring present or into being, aff. णिच्-ल्यु ।
