<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष्
मक्ष् r. 1st cl. (मक्षति)
	 1. To fill.
	 2. To be angry.
	 3. To mix, to combine.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष|मक्षः
मक्ष m. (-क्षः)
	 1. Hypocrisy, slyness, concealment of one's own defects.
2. Multitude.
 E. मक्ष् to fill. aff. अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षिका
मक्षिका f. (-का) A fly.
 E. मक्ष् to be angry, Unādi aff. सिकन्; or मक्ष् the same, क्कुन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षीका
मक्षीका f. (-का) A fly. E. See the last, the pen. vowel made long.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख r. 1st cl. (मखति) also (इ) मखि (मङ्क्षति) To go, to move.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख m. (-खः) Sacrifice, oblation.
 E. मख् to go, aff. घञ् or घ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखत्रातृ
मखत्रातृ m. (-ता) RĀMA, the son of DASARATHA, and second incarnation
of VIṢṆU so named.
 E. मख sacrifice, and त्रातृ who preserves; his
first exploit being the discomfiture of the Rākshasas, who dis-
turbed the sacrifices of VISWĀMITRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखवह्नि|मखवह्निः
मखवह्नि m. (-ह्निः) Sacrificial-fire.
 E. मख sacrifice, and वह्नि fire; also
similar compounds, as मखाग्नि &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखानल|मखानलः
मखानल m. (-लः) Sacrificial-fire.
 E. मख and अनल fire.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखासुहृद्
मखासुहृद् m. (-द) ŚIVA.
 E. मख् sacrifice, here meaning the sacrifice
offered by DAKṢA and असुहृद् unfriendly; having disturbed the
ceremony, and slain the sacrificer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्
मग् (इ) मगि r. 1st cl. (मङ्गति) To go, to move.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध|मगधः
मगध m. (-धः)
	 1. A country, South Behar.
	 2. An inhabitant of that
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">Page541-a+ 60</a>]
country.
	 3. A bard, whose peculiar province is to sing the praises
of a chief's ancestry in his presence, a family bard or minstrel.
	 f.
(-धा)
	 1. Long pepper.
	 2. The town of the Magadhas.
 E. मगध a
Kandwādi verb, to ask, aff. अच्; or मगध the country, अण् aff.,
with alteration of the vowel optional; hence also मागध ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगधेश्वर|मगधेश्वरः
मगधेश्वर m. (-रः) A name of JARA SANDHA.
 E. मगध South Bihar, ईश्वर king.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्न|मग्नः
मग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)
	 1. Plunged, dived, immersed.
	 2. Sunk, drowned.
	 3.
Absorbed.
 E. मस्ज् to plunge into water, aff. क्त.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ्
मघ् (इ) मघि r. 1st cl. (मङ्घते)
	 1. To go, to move.
	 2. To begin moving.
	 3.
To begin.
	 4. To move swiftly.
	 5. To blame.
	 6. To gamble.
	 7. To
cheat, to be addicted to dishonest practices. (मङ्घति) To decorate,
to adorn.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ|मघः
मघ m. (-घः)
	 1. One of the Dwīpas or divisions of the universe.
	 2. A
country, that of the modern Mugs, or Ārrākān.
	 3. A drug.
	 4.
Pleasure, happiness.
	 5. A kind of medicine.
	 n. (-घं) A kind of
flower.
	 f. (-घा) The tenth lunar asterism, containing five stars
figured by a house: it is sometimes considered to be confined to
the plural number. (मघाः)
	 f. (-घा-घी) A sort of grain.
 E. मह to wor-
ship, aff. कन् and ह changed to घ; or मघि-अच् पृषो० ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवत्|मघवन्त्
मघवत् m. (-वान्) A name of INDRA.
 E. मघ happiness, (of paradise
or Svarga,) मतुप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवन्
मघवन् m. (-वा)
	 1. INDRA.
	 2. One of the twelve Chakravartis, or uni-
versal monarchs of the Jainas.
	 3. An epithet of Vyāsa 4. An owl.
E. मह to sacrifice, कनिन् Unādi aff. and वुक् augment, form irr.;
before the vowel affs. of the second case plural, and the last five
cases, the व of this word is changed to उ, and thence becomes ओ
as usual, as मघोनः, मघोना, मघोने, &c.; also with ङीष् aff. the fem.
form is मघीनी f. (-नी) Sāchi, the wife of INDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभव|मघाभवः
मघाभव m. (-वः) The planet VENUS.
 E. मघा the asterism, and भव born.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभू
मघाभू m. (-भूः) SUKRA.
 E. मघा and भू born; see the last.
