मङ्क्षुण|मंक्षुण|मङ्क्षुणं
मङ्क्षुण n. (-णं) Cuisses or greaves, armour for the thighs or legs;
a sort of iron chain-work petticoat, coming down to the knees,
is still worn in some parts of India.
