	 2. Admitted, believed, held
or entertained, (as opinion, &c.)
	 3. Respected, reverenced, mind-
ed, regarded.
	 n. (-तं)
	 1. Purpose, intention, wish, mind, (as to
have a mind to any thing.)
	 2. Knowledge.
	 3. Doctrine, tenet,
belief, opinion.
	 4. Counsel, advice.
	 5. Design, aim.
	 6. Approba-
tion.
 E. मन् to mind, aff. क्त ।
