मत्स्यावतार|मत्स्यावतारः
मत्स्यावतार m. (-रः) VIṢṆU in his first Avatāra; when the seventh
Manu was reigning, the whole earth was destroyed by a flood and
all living beings perished except the reigning Manu and the
seven Ṛṣis who were saved by VIṢṆU in the form of a fish.
