मलिम्लुच m. (-चः)
	 1. A thief.
	 2. Burning, blazing.
	 3. Fire.
	 4. Air, wind.
5. The intercalary lunar month, introduced every third year, in
order to approximate the lunar, and solar modes of computation.
6. A gnat, a musquito.
	 7. Frost.
	 8. A thief, a robber.
	 9. A Brāh-
mana who neglects the five daily acts of piety.
	 10. A demon. E.
मलि possession, and म्लुच् to steal, aff. क ।
