महत्|महन्त्
महत् mfn. (-हान्-हती-हत्)
	 1. Great, large, bulky.
	 2. Much, many.
	 3.
Best, excellent, illustrious.
	 4. Loud.
	 5. Far advanced.
	 6. Long.
	 7.
Intense.
	 8. Important.
	 9. Eminent, high.
	 10. Dense, thick.
	 11.
Numerous.
	 n. (-त्)
	 1. Kingdom, dominion.
	 2. The intellectual
principle, the second principle in creation.
	 3. Sacred knowledge.
4. Infinity, greatness. Adv. Much, very, exceeding.
	 f. (-ती) The
Vinā or lute of NĀRADA, containing seven or one hundred
strings.
	 2. The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)
	 m. (-हान्)
	 1. The
second of the twenty five principles of creation according to
Sānkhya philosophy.
	 2. A camel.
	 3. An epithet of Rudra.
 E. मह् to
worship, अति Unādi aff. In composition महा is generally substi-
tuted, आ being inserted in place of the final.
