मही
मही f. (-ही)
	 1. The earth.
	 2. A river, the Mahī which rises in the pro-
vince of Mālwā, and after pursuing a westerly course of about
280 miles, falls into the upper part of the gulf of Cambay.
	 3. A
cow.
	 4. A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)
	 5. The base of a plain
figure, (in geometry.)
 E. मह् to worship or be worshipped, aff. इ,
and ङीष् added; also without the addition महि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीक्षित्
