माक्षि
माक्षि (क्षी) क n. (-कं)
	 1. A mineral substance, of which two kinds are des-
cribed; the स्वर्णमाक्षिक or gold Mākshika, of a bright yellow colour,
apparently the common pyritic iron ore: and the रूप्यमाक्षिक or
silver Mākshika, which answers in appearance to the Hepatic py-
rites of iron; other names of these ores occur; as विट्माक्षिक and
कांस्यमाक्षिक, or feculent Mākshika and mixed metal Mākshika
they are however, perhaps rather synonymes of the gold and
silver ore, respectively, than names of distinct species.
	 2. Honey.
E. मक्षिका a bee, अण् aff. of derivation; the name is applied to the
ore, from its honey-like colour.
