माहिष्य m. (-ष्यः) A man of a mixed class, sprung from a Kṣatriya
father and Vaiśya mother.
 E. महिष a buffalo, and यत् aff., with
अण् added; attendance on cattle forming with the practice of as-
tronomy and music, are the business of the Māhishya.
