<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्ष्
म्लक्ष् r. 10th cl. (म्लक्षयति-ते)
	 1. To mix, to unite.
	 2. To speak incorrectly.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लात
म्लात f. (-ता) Adj. Faded, withered.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लान|म्लानं
म्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)
	 1. Foul, dirty.
	 2. Languid, weary.
	 3. Faded,
withered.
	 4. Melancholy.
 E. म्लै to be languid, aff. क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानि|म्लानिः
म्लानि f. (-निः)
	 1. Weariness, languor.
	 2. Foulness, filth.
	 3. Fading,
decay.
	 4. Sadness.
 E. म्लै to be languid, &c., aff. क्तिन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लास्नु
म्लास्नु f. (-स्नु)
	 1. Growing languid.
	 2. Growing thin.
	 3. Growing withered.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्ट|म्लिष्टं|म्लिष्टः
म्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)
	 1. Indistinct, (as speech.)
	 2. Languid.
	 n. (-ष्टं)
Indistinct speech.
 E. म्लेच्छ् to speak indistinctly, aff. क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुक्त
म्लुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Mixed, intermixed, inlaid, set.
 E. म्लुच् to go, aff. क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुच्
म्लुच्(उ)म्लुचु r. 1st cl. (म्लोचति) To go, to move. With अभि and नि pre-
fixed.
	 1. To go down.
	 2. To set as the sun.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुञ्च्|म्लुंच्
म्लुञ्च् (उ) म्लुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (म्लुञ्चति) To go, to move; also read म्लुन्च् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ्|म्लेछ्
म्लेच्छ् r. 1st and 10th cls. (म्लेच्छति म्लेच्छयति-ते) To speak inarticulately
or incorrectly, to use a provincial or barbarous dialect.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेच्छः|म्लेछ
म्लेच्छ m. (-च्छः)
	 1. The generic term for a barbarian or foreigner; that
is, for one speaking any language but Sanskrit, and not subject
to the usual Hindu institutions.
	 2. A sinner, a criminal.
	 3. Indis-
tinct or barbarous speech.
 E. म्लेच्छ् to speak inarticulately, aff. घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छकन्द|म्लेच्छकंद|म्लेच्छकन्दः
म्लेच्छकन्द m. (-न्दः) Garlic.
 E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and कण्ड root. “लशुने ।”
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छजाति|म्लेच्छजातिः
म्लेच्छजाति m. (-तिः) A Mleccha or barbarian or a man of an outcast
race. The tribes enumerated under this head by MANU, but who
are by him said to be properly, degraded Kṣatriyas, appear to be
chiefly the inhabitants of the countries bordering immediately
upon India, both to the north and south: as far as modern re-
search and similarity of appellation may be trusted, the tribes of
Mlecchas are as follows: the Pauṇḍrakas, (the people of pro-
vinces bordering on Bengal and Bihar, and to the south of the
Ganges,) Oḍras, (Urīyās,) Drāviras, (people of the southern part
of the Coromandel coast,) Cāmbojas, (Arachosians,) Yavanas,
(Greeks or Bactrians,) Śakas, (the people of the Sacha region or
Sakai,) Pāravas, (Paropamisans,) Pahlavas, (the ancient Persians,)
Chīnas, (Chinese,) Kirātas, (generally mountaineers, here per-
haps especially the inhabitants of the Himālaya or Imaus,) Dera-
das, (Daradæ,) and Khasas, (Scuthi or Chasas.)
	 n. (-च्छं) Copper. E.
म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and जाति tribe, class.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छदेश|म्लेच्छदेशः
म्लेच्छदेश m. (-शः) The countries bordering on India, or those inhabi-
ted by people of a different faith and language; defined to be any,
where the black antelope is not found.
 E. म्लेच्छ् a barbarian, an
outcast, देश country.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभोजन|म्लेच्छभोजनं|म्लेच्छभोजनः
म्लेच्छभोजन m. (-नः) Wheat.
	 n. (-नं) Half-ripe barley.
 E. म्लेच्छ an outcast, भोजन food.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमण्डल|म्लेच्छमंडल|म्लेच्छमण्डलं
म्लेच्छमण्डल n. (-लं) The country of the Mlecchas or barbarians. E.
म्लेच्छ, मण्डल region.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमुख|म्लेच्छमुखं
म्लेच्छमुख n. (-खः) Copper.
 E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and मुख countenance.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छवाच्
म्लेच्छवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Speaking a barbarous dialect.
 E. म्लेच्छ, वाच् speech.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छाश|म्लेच्छाशः
म्लेच्छाश m. (-शः) Wheat.
 E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, अश् to eat, aff. अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छास्य|म्लेच्छास्यं
म्लेच्छास्य n. (-स्यं) Copper.
 E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and आस्व face, which
would seem to allude to the fair complexion of the Greek or Maha-
mmedan invaders of Hindusthan.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
