रजनीमुख|रजनीमुखं
रजनीमुख n. (-खं) Evening, beginning of the night.
 E. रजनी, मुख commencement.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीहासा
रजनीहासा f. (-सा) A flower, (Nyctanthes arbor tristis.) “शेफालिकायाम्”.
E. रजनी night, हास a smile; the flowers blossoming at night,
and diffusing a powerful scent after sunset.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्
रजस् n. (-जः)
	 1. The second of the three primary qualities of nature
the quality or property of passion: that which produces sensual
desire, worldly coveting, pride, and falsehood, and is the cause of
pain.
	 2. Dust.
	 3. The dust or pollen of a flower.
	 4. Any particle of
matter.
	 5. The menstrual evacuation.
	 6. Cultivated fields.
	 7. A
mole in a sun-beam.
 E. रञ्ज् to colour, to be attached to, Unādi
aff. असुन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजसानु|रजसानुः
रजसानु m. (-नुः)
	 1. A cloud.
	 2. The heart or mind.
 E. रञ्ज् to colour, to
feel affection for, सानु Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्तमस्क
