राजसूय|राजसूयः
राजसूय n. (-यं)
	 1. A sacrifice performed only by an universal monarch,
attended by his tributary princes; as in the case of YUDHIṢṬHIRA,
and others.
	 2. A lotus.
	 3. A mountain.
	 4. A sort of rice.
 E. राज a
king, (by him,) and षू to be produced, to be effected, aff. क्यप्; or
राज the moon, for the moon-plant of which the acid-juice is drank
at the ceremony, and सु to bring forth, the same aff., deriv. irr.
