राम|रामं|रामः
राम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)
	 1. Black.
	 2. White.
	 3. Beautiful, pleasing.
	 m. (-मः)
1. A name common to three incarnations of VIṢṆU, viz:-firstly,
PARAŚURĀMA, the son of the Muni JAMADAGNI, born at the com-
mencement of the second or TRETA YUGA, for the purpose of
punishing the tyrannical kings of the Kṣatriya race. Secondly,
RĀMACHANDRA, the son of DAŚARATHA, king of Oudh, born at
the close of the second age, to destroy the demons who infested
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">Page604-a+ 60</a>]
the earth, and especially RĀVAṆA the Daitya-sovereign of Ceylon.
Thirdly, BALARĀMA, (the elder and half-brother of KṚṢṆA,)
the son of BĀSUDEVA by ROHINI, born at the end of the DWĀPARA
or third age.
	 2. A name of VARUṆA, regent of the waters.
	 3. A
horse.
	 4. A sort of deer.
	 f. (-मा)
	 1. A woman, a female, a plea-
sing or beautiful female.
	 2. Asafœtida.
	 3. A river.
	 4. Vermilion.
n. (-मं)
	 1. A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)
	 2. A sort of Costus,
(C. speciosus.)
 E. रम् to sport, aff. घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकरी
रामकरी f. (-री) One of the Rāgīnis, or female personifications of the
musical modes.
 E. राम delighting, करी who makes; also रामकली ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकर्पूर
रामकर्पूर m. (-रः) A fragrant sort of grass.
 E. राम pleasant, and कर्पूर
(smelling like,) camphor.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासकली
रासकली f. (-ली) A Rāgīni.
 E. राम pleasant, कला sound or note, ङीप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामगिरि|रामगिरिः
रामगिरि m. (-रिः) The name of a mountain, variously applied, but espe-
cially assigned to a mountain called COMPTEH or CHITRAKŪṬA in
BUNDELKHUND, and to another near NĀGPORE, called now RĀMTEK.
E. राम the hero RĀMA, and गिरि a mountain; being one of his
halting places in his progress from Oudh to the Peninsula.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामचन्द्र|रामचंद्र|रामचन्द्रः
रामचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The hero RĀMACHANDRA, the son of DASARATHA. E.
राम and चन्द्र the moon, the moon-like RĀMA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामजननी
रामजननी m. (-नी) The mother of BALARĀMA.
 E. राम and जननी mother,
hence it is equally applicable to RENUKĀ, the mother of
PARAŚURĀMA, and to KAUŚALYA, the mother of RĀMACHANDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामठ|रामठं|रामठः
रामठ n. (-ठं) Asafœtida.
 E. रम् to please, अठ Unādi aff., and the radi-
cal vowel lengthened.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणीयक|रामणीयकं
रामणीयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Beautiful, pleasing.
 E. रमणीय the same, and वुञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामदूत|रामदूतः
रामदूत m. (-तः) The monkey HANUMĀNA, the friend and messenger of
RAMĀ.
	 f. (-तिः-ती) A shrub, apparently a variety of basil with
small leaves. “नाग्दोना”.
 E. राम RĀMA, and दूत a messenger.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामनवमी
रामनवमी f. (-मी) The ninth day in the light-half of Chaitra, the anni-
versary of the birth of RĀMACHANDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामपूग|रामपूगः
रामपूग m. (-गः) A small species of the areca or betel-nut tree, (Areca
triandra, Rox.)
 E. राम RĀMA, पूग areca.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामभद्र|रामभद्रः
रामभद्र m. (-द्रः) The hero RĀMACHANDRA.
 E. राम the same, and भद्र auspicious.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामवीणा
रामवीणा f. (-णा) A sort of Vina or lute.
 E. राम RĀMA and वीणा a lute;
it may be also ironically applicable to the horn blown by BALA-
RĀMA, and called still the RĀMASINHĀ.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामशर|रामशरः
रामशर m. (-रः) A variety of the Saccharum Sara, a sort of grass.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसख|रामसखः
रामसख m. (-खः) The monkey-king SUGRĪVA.
 E. राम RĀMA, and सख
friend; RĀMA having restored him to his throne, whence he had
been driven by his elder brother BĀLI.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसेतु|रामसेतुः
रामसेतु m. (-तुः) A bridge of sand, now a chain of islands, between the
Indian Peninsula and Ceylon, popularly known by “Adam's bridge”.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामायण|रामायणं
रामायण n. (-णं)
	 1. The first epic poem of the Hindus, written by the
poet VĀLMIKI, recording the adventures of RĀMA, the son of DAŚA
RATHA, sovereign of Oudh.
	 2. A name of several poems on the
life and adventures of RĀMA.
 E. राम the prince, and अयन abode.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामानुज|रामानुजः
रामानुज m. (-जः) Name of the founder of a Vedāntic sect.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामिल|रामिलः
रामिल m. (-लः)
	 1. KĀMA or CUPID.
	 2. A lover, a husband.
 E. राम
pleasing, agreeable, इलच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्भ|रांभ|रांभः|राम्भः
राम्भ m. (-म्भः) The bamboo staff of a religious student.
 E. रम्भा a bamboo, aff. अञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायण|रायणं
रायण n. (-णं)
	 1. Pain.
	 2. Sounding, crying.
 E. रै to sound, aff. ल्युट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायभाटी
रायभाटी f. (-टी) The current or flow of a river.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारस्यमान
रारस्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Crying aloud and repeatedly.
 E. रस to cry, reit. v., शानच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राल|रालः
राल m. (-लः) Resin, the resinous and fragrant exudation of the Shorea
robusta. “धुना”.
 E. रा to give or get, aff. अलच्; also अराल ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राव|रावः
राव m. (-वः) Sound, noise.
 E. रु to cry or sound, aff. घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावण|रावणः
रावण m. (-णः) The Daitya-sovereign of Lankā or Ceylon, killed by
RĀMACHANDRA.
	 n. (-णं) Noise, tumult.
 E. रु to cry, (in the causal
form,) aff. ल्युट; afflicting mankind.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणारि|रावणारिः
रावणारि m. (-रिः) The hero RĀMA.
 E. रावण, अरि the foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणि|रावणिः
रावणि m. (-णिः) The eldest son of RĀVAṆA.
 E. रावण, इञ् patronymic aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राश्
राश्(ऋ)राशृ r. 1st and 4th cl. (राशते राश्यते) To sound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशि|राशिः
राशि m. (-शिः)
	 1. A heap, a quantity.
	 2. A sign of the zodiac.
	 3. Arith-
metical or algebraic quantity.
	 4. A part and its divisor or nu-
merator and denominator.
	 5. A congeries of number or quantity.
E. अश् to pervade, इण् Unādi aff., and रुट् initial augment; or
रश् to sound, with the same aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिगत
राशिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Heaped, accumulated.
	 2. Computed, sum-
med either by arithmetic or algebra.
 E. राशि, and गत gone to.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिचक्र|राशिचक्रं
राशिचक्र n. (-क्रं) The zodiac.
 E. राशि, a sign, and चक्र a wheel or circle.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशित्रय
राशित्रय n. (-यं) The rule of three.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभाग|राशिभागः
राशिभाग m. (-गः) A fraction.
 E. राशि, भाग a part.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभोग|राशिभोगः
राशिभोग m. (-गः) Passage of a planet through a sign of the zodiac. E.
राशि, भोग enjoyment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकरण
राशीकरण n. (-णं) Heaping, piling, gathering.
 E. राशि, करण making, च्वि augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकृत
राशीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped, piled, &c.
 E. राशि, कृत made, च्वि aug.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीभूत
राशीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped, piled.
 E. राशि, and भूत become, च्वि aug.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं|राष्ट्रः
राष्ट्र mn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्रं)
	 1. An inhabited country or realm, a region.
	 2. Any
public calamity, as plague, famine, &c.
 E. राज् to shine or govern,
aff. ष्ट्रन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रनिवासिन्
राष्ट्रनिवासिन् m. (-सी) An inhabitant of any civilized country.
 E. राष्ट्र a
district, निवासिन् a dweller.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिक|राष्ट्रिकः
राष्ट्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bolonging to or inhabiting a country.
	 f. (-का)
A prickly sort of night-shade, (Solanum jacquini.) “कण्टकारी”.
 E. राष्ट्र
a country, and ठन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिय|राष्ट्रियः
राष्ट्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of or belonging to a kingdom, produced or born
in it, &c.
 E. राष्ट्र a region, घ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रीय|राष्ट्रीयः
राष्ट्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a region or realm.
	 m.
(-यः) A king's brother-in-law, (in theatrical language.)
 E. राष्ट्र a
region, छ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्
रास्(ऋ)रासृ r. 1st cl. (रासते) To sound, to cry.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास|रासः
रास m. (-सः)
	 1. Confused noise, uproar, hubbub.
	 2. Sound in general.
	 3.
Speech, discourse.
	 4. A chain.
	 5. A festival amongst the cowherds,
including songs and dances, especially the circular dance as per-
formed by KṚṢṆA and the Gopis or cowherdesses.
	 6. A game
played by children.
 E. रास् to sound, घञ् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासक|रासकं
रासक n. (-कं) A kind of minor drama in one act.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभ|रासभः
रासभ m. (-भः) An ass.
	 f. (-भी) The she-ass.
 E. रास् to sound, अभच Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभधूसर
रासभधूसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Grey or light-brown, ass-grey.
 E. रासभ,
धूसर grey.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभवन्दिनी
रासभवन्दिनी f. (-नी) Arabian jasmine.
 E. रासभ an ass, वदि to praise, aff. णिनि ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासयात्रा
रासयात्रा f. (-त्रा) A festival held in honour of KṚṢṆA on the full-
moon of Kārtika.
 E. रास, and यात्रा festival.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेरस|रासेरसः
रासेरस m. (-सः)
	 1. An assembly, a company, a party.
	 2. A game or
festival peculiar to the cowherds: see रास.
	 3. Love, desire, the
passion or sentiment.
	 4. Alchemy: see रससिद्धि.
	 5. The sixth night
after delivery, on which the family and friends sit up all night.
6. Sport, mirth, pastime.
	 7. Any festival or holiday.
 E. रास noise,
&c., and रस flavour, taste.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्ना
रास्ना f. (-स्ना)
	 1. A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)
	 2. Another plant, (the ser-
pent ophioxylon.)
	 3. A sort of perfume.
 E. रस् to sound, नक् Unādi
aff., and the vowel made long.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहित्य|राहित्यं
राहित्य n. (-त्यं) The being without anything, destitution.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहु|राहुः
राहु m. (-हुः) The ascending node; in mythology, the son of VIPRACHITTI
by SINHIKĀ, a Daitya, with the tail of a dragon, whose head was
severed from his body by VIṢṆU, on the information of the sun
and the moon who caught him in the act of drinking Amrita which
was being served to gods, but being immortal by tasting it, his
head and tail retained their separate existence, and being transferred
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">Page605-a+ 60</a>]
to the stellar sphere, became the authors of eclipses; the first
especially, by endeavouring at various times to swallow the sun
and the moon to wreak his vengeance.
 E. रह् to abandon, (the
planets which it has vainly attempted to devour,) aff. उण्, and the
vowel made long.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्रस्त
राहुग्रस्त m. (-स्तः) Eclipsed, (as the sun or moon.)
 E. राहु, and ग्रस्त seized.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्रास|राहुग्रासः
