रुक्मिन्
रुक्मिन् m. (-क्मी) The name of a prince slain by BALARĀMA.
	 f. (-क्मिणी)
1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.
	 2. A name of the daughter of king
BHĪMAKA. She was betrothed to Sīśupāla, but she had enter-
tained a passion for KṚṢṆA and sent to invite him to marry her
off. KṚṢṆA made her his own by the Rākshasa ritual. PRA-
DYUMNA was her son.
 E. रुक्म gold, and इनि poss. aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिभिद्
रुक्मिभिद् m. (-भित्) BALARĀMA.
 E. रुक्मि a prince, the elder brother of
RUKMINĪ, and भिद् breaker, conqueror.
