लाक्षा
लाक्षा f. (-क्षा) Lac, a red dye, or an insect which is analogous to the
cochineal insect, and like it forms when died and prepared, a dye
of a red colour; the nest is formed of a resinous substance
which is used as sealing wax, and as an article of decoration by
women, and is usually termed Shel lac.
 E. लक्ष् to mark or stain,
aff. अ, and अण् added, the vowel made long; or लक्ष a hundred
thousand, अण् aff.; made by a multitude of the insects.
