	 5. In-
ference, probable conclusion.
	 6. The premises leading to a con-
clusion.
	 7. Nature or Prakritī, according to the Sānkhya
philosophy, which considers this as the active power in creation.
8. Gender, (as पुंलिङ्गः the masculine gender, &c.)
	 9. The order of
the religious student.
	 10. Symptom or mark of disease.
	 11. The
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">Page618-a+ 60</a>]
predicate of a proposition.
	 12. Evidence.
 E. लिगि to go, &c., aff.
अच् ।
