लुप्
लुप् r. 4th cl. (लुप्यति)
	 1. To disturb, to bewilder, to perplex, and con-
found the understanding.
	 2. To vanish. (ॡ, औ, ऋ) औलुऌ r. 6th
cl. (लुम्पति-ते)
	 1. To cut, to divide, to cut off or down.
	 2. To rob.
3. To seize.
	 4. To suppress. With वि, 1. To break off.
	 2. To carry
away.
	 3. To destroy.
