वत्
वत् Ind. As, like, similar: this is more generally considered as an
affix to words, termed technically वति, as ब्राह्मणवत् like a Brāh
man, &c.
	 f. (-वती) An affix added to nouns to form possessive
adjectives, as लक्ष्मीवत्; also added to past passive participles to
form past active participles, as कृतवत् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत
वत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Uttered, sounded, spoken.
	 2. Asked, begged.
Ind.
	 1. A particle analogous to ah, oh, &c. expressing sorrow.
	 2.
Compassion.
	 3. Pleasure.
	 4. Oh, ho, a vocative particle.
 E. वन् to
ask or beg, &c. aff. क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

