वन्दिन्|वंदिन्
वन्दिन् m. (-न्दी)
	 1. A panegyrist, a bard, a herald, a servant whose
duty it is to proclaim the titles of a great man as he passes along;
or a poet, who sings the praises of a prince in his presence, or
accompanies an army, to chant martial songs: considered as
one of a distinct tribe, he is the son of a Kṣatriya by a Śūdra
female.
	 2. A flatterer.
	 3. A prisoner.
 E. वदि to praise, aff. णिनि ।
