वल्मीक|वल्मीकं|वल्मीकः
वल्मीक mn. (-कः-कं) A hillock, ground thrown up by moles, &c., but
especially the large accumulations of soil, sometimes made by the
white ant.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. The poet VĀLMĪKI.
	 2. Elephantiasis, or
swellings of the neck, chest, hands and feet, which break and
discharge ichor in many places.
 E. वल् to cover, or बल् to live,
ईक Unādi aff., and मुट् augment; in the latter case this word
and the corresponding ones are written बल्मीक, &c.; also वल्मिक ।
