वल्लुर|वल्लुरं
वल्लुर n. (-रं)
	 1. An arbour, a bower, a place over-grown with creeping
plants.
	 2. An uncultivated field or place overrun with wild grass.
3. A sand, a desert, a place destitute of water.
	 4. A field.
	 5. A
compound pedicle.
	 6. A solitude, a wild.
	 7. A thicket, a wood.
8. Dried flesh.
 E. वल्ल् to cover, उरन् aff.; also वल्लूर ।
