<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसि|वसिः
वसि m. (-सिः)
	 1. Dwelling, abode.
	 2. A dwelling.
	 3. Clothes.
 E. वस् to dwell, Unādi aff. इन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित
वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Stored, (as grain.)
	 2. Dwelling, inhabiting.
3. Put on, worn.
	 n. (-तं) Abiding, residence.
	 f. (-ता) The power of
subduing all things: see वशिता.
 E. वस् to dwell, &c., क्त aff.; or
वशिता as above, and श changed to स ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसितृ
वसितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what wears.
 E. वस् to put on, तृच् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित्वा
वसित्वा Ind. Having put on, (as clothes,) wearing.
 E. वस् to wear, क्त्वा aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिर|वसिरं
वसिर n. (-रं) Sea-salt.
	 m. (-रः) A pungent fruit, considered as a sort of
pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)
 E. वस् to abide, (in the sea,) इरन् aff.;
also, as derived from वश् to desire, वशिर &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिष्ठ|वसिष्ठः
वसिष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A celebrated Muni.
 E. वस् to abide, (in the practice of
religious austerities,) aff. णिनि, वसिन्, superlative aff. इष्टन् added;
pre-eminent amongst the ascetics; also वशिष्ठ &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)
	 1. Sweet, sweet-flavoured.
	 2. Dry, dried.
	 n. (-सु)
	 1.
Wealth, thing, substance.
	 2. A gem, a jewel.
	 3. A medicinal root,
commonly Vriddhi.
	 4. Water.
	 5. Gold.
	 6. A yellow kind of kidney-
bean.
	 7. A sort of salt.
	 8. The number eight, i. e. the eight
Vasus.
	 m. (-सुः)
	 1. A kind of demi-god, of whom eight are enumer-
ated, viz.:--DHARA, DHRUVA, SOMA or the moon, ĀPA, ANILA
or wind, ANALA or fire, PRABHĀSA and PRATYUSA.
	 2. A name
of ĀGNI or fire.
	 3. A ray of light.
	 4. The tie of a yoke.
	 5. A tree,
(Sesbana grandiflora.)
	 6. The name of a king.
	 7. A name of
KUVERA.
	 8. A tree in general.
	 9. A lake, a pool.
	 10. A rein, a
halter.
	 11. A plant, (Trophis aspera.)
	 12. ŚIVA.
	 13. The sun.
14. A kind of fish.
 E. वस् to abide or dwell, Unādi aff. उ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु(सू)क n. (-कं) A fossil-salt, brought from a district in Ajmere,
Sambhar-salt.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. A shrub, (Gigantic Asclepias.)
	 2. A tree,
(Sesbana grandiflora.)
 E. कन् added to the preceding; or वसु
wealth, कै to sound, aff. ड ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुकीट|वसुकीटः
वसुकीट m. (-टः) A supplicant, a beggar, a petitioner.
 E. वसु wealth, कीट a worm.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदा
वसुदा f. (-दा) The earth.
 E. वसु wealth, and दा who gives.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेव|वसुदेवः
वसुदेव m. (-वः) BASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.
 E. वसु a deity, the in-
carnation of one of the Vasus, or वसु wealth, दिव् to shine, aff. अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवता
वसुदेवता f. (-ता) The constellation Dhanisṭhā.
 E. वसु the Vasus, and
देवता divinity; presiding over the asterism.
