वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)
	 1. Left, not right.
	 2. Reverse, contrary, inverted.
3. Beautiful, pleasing.
	 4. Vile, base, wicked.
	 5. Short.
	 6. Crooked.
m. (-मः)
	 1. A name of ŚIVA.
	 2. KĀMA or CUPID.
	 3. An udder,
a breast.
	 4. A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)
	 5. An animal, a
sentient being.
	 6. A snake.
	 n. (-मं) Wealth, possessions.
	 f. (-मा)
1. A woman.
	 2. Gourī.
	 3. LAKṢMĪ.
	 4. SARASWATĪ.
	 f. (-मी)
	 1. A
mare.
	 2. A she-ass.
	 3. A young female elephant.
	 4. The female of
the jackal.
 E. वा to go, Unādi aff. मन् ।
