	 f.
(-रिः)
	 1. A name of SARASWATĪ; the goddess of speech.
	 2. The place
where an elephant is tied or fastened.
	 3. A captive, a prisoner.
	 f.
(-रिः or री)
	 1. A water-pot, whether large or small, pitcher, a jar.
	 2.
The rope that fastens an elephant.
