वाशिष्ठ|वाशिष्ठः
वाशिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Relating to the sage VASIṢṬHA.
	 f. (-ष्ठी) The
Goomti river, which rising in the Kumaun hills, pursues a
winding and south-easterly course, and passing Lucknow and
Jonpur falls into the Ganges, below Benares.
 E. वशिष्ठ the saint,
अण् aff., derived from him; also read वासिष्ठ ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशुरा
वाशुरा f. (-रा) Night.
 E. वाश् to sound, Unādi aff. उरच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्र|वाश्रं|वाश्रः
वाश्र m. (-श्रः) A day.
	 n. (-श्रं)
	 1. An edifice, a dwelling, a building.
	 2.
A place where four roads meet.
 E. वाश् to sound, Unādi aff. रक्;
also read वास्र ।
