<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसत्
विकसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)
	 1. Opening, expanding.
	 2. Budding, blow-
ing.
 E. वि before, कस् to go, शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसित|विकसितं
विकसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blown, as a flower, budded, opened, expanded.
E. वि apart, कस् to go, aff. क्त; also विकशित ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस्वर|विकस्वरः
विकस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opening, expanding.
 E. वि apart, कस् to go, aff.
वरच्; also derived from कश् or कष्, विकश्वर, and विकष्वर ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकार|विकारः
विकार m. (-रः)
	 1. Change of form or nature, alteration or deviation
from the natural state.
	 2. Sickness, disease, change from the state
of health.
	 3. Passion, feeling, emotion, transition from the natural
or quiescent condition of the soul.
	 4. Anything evolved from a
previous source, (in Sānkhya Philosophy.)
 E. वि implying
alteration, कृ to make, aff. घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारित
विकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Changed, converted, made to undergo a
changing.
	 2. Rendered unfavourable or unfriendly.
 E. वि before, कृ
to make, causal v., क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारिन्
विकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)
	 1. Producing a change.
	 2. Undergoing a
change.
 E. वि before, कृ to make, णिनि aff.; or विकार, इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाल|विकालः
विकाल m. (-लः) Twilight, the close of day.
 E. वि implying prohibition,
(of peculiar ceremonies,) and काल time.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकालक|विकालकः
विकालक m. (-कः) Evening, twilight.
	 f. (-लिका) A perforated copper-
vessel, which is placed in a pan of water, and being filled at the
expiration of a certain period, defines that period: a sort of Clep-
sydra, or water-clock. “तांँवी”.
 E. वि before, काल time, and कन्
added; or वि before, कल् to go, aff. क्कुन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश|विकाशः
विकाश m. (-शः)
	 1. Solitude, loneliness, privacy.
	 2. Display, manifes-
tation, open or splendid appearance.
	 3. Opening, expanding.
	 4.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">Page650-b+ 60</a>]
Budding, blowing, (as a flower.)
	 5. Pleasure, enjoyment.
	 6. Ether,
heaven.
	 7. An open course.
	 8. An oblique course.
	 9. Retreat.
	 10.
Eagerness.
 E. वि before, काश to shine, aff. घञ्; the vowel of the
prefix is more usually made long: see वीकाश ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशता
विकाशता f. (-ता)
	 1. Appearance, display.
	 2. Loneliness.
	 3. Expansion.
E. विकाश shining, aff. तल्; also with त्व, विकाशत्वं ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशन|विकाशनं
विकाशन n. (-नं)
	 1. Expansion, extent.
	 2. Manifestation.
	 3. Blowing,
(of a flower.)
 E. विकाश and ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशभृत्
विकाशभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)
	 1. Expanding, being full.
	 2. Blown, budded. E.
विकाश, भृत् who or what has.
