विड्
विड् f. (-विड्) A bit, a fragment.
 E. विड् to break, क्विप् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड|विडं|विडः
विड n. (-डं)
	 1. Factitious salt, or salt procured by boiling soil found
near the sea-shore, or any earth impregnated with saline particles.
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">Page655-b+ 60</a>]
2. A particular fetid kind of salt, used as a tonic aperient, com-
monly called black salt or Vit-lavaṇ, prepared by fusing fossile-
salt with a small portion of Emblic myrobalans; the produce is
muriate of soda with small quantities of muriate of lime, sulphur
and oxid of iron.
	 3. A part, a fracture, a bit.
 E. विड् to divide,
aff. क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडगन्ध
विडगन्ध n. (-न्धं) The medicinal salt called Vit-lavaṇ: see the last. E.
विड salt, गन्ध smell.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्ग|विडंग|विडङ्गं|विडङ्गः
विडङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Clever, able, skilful, conversant.
	 mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गं)
A vegetable and medicinal substance, considered of great efficacy
as a vermifuge.
 E. विड् to break, to curse, Unādi aff. अङ्गच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्ब|विडंब|विडंबः|विडम्बः
विडम्ब m. (-म्बः)
	 1. Imitation.
	 2. Distressing, afflicting.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बन|विडंबन|विडंबनं|विडम्बनं
विडम्बन nf. (-नं-ना)
	 1. Afflicting, distressing.
	 2. Vexation, mortification.
3. Frustrating, rendering vain.
	 4. Imitation, copying, especially
assuming a similar appearance or dress, disguise, masquerade.
5. Deception, fraud.
	 6. Ridiculousness.
	 7. The supernatural
assumption of a borrowed form, transformation.
 E. वि before, डवि
to heap, aff. ल्युट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बनीय
विडम्बनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)
	 1. To be distressed or annoyed.
	 2. To be
assumed as a disguise.
 E. वि before, डवि to heap, अनीयर् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

