	 1. A sort of lock or bolt with three divisions or wards.
2. An elephant.
	 f. (-ण्डा)
	 1. Controversy, argument, the subversion
of another's opinion or interpretation and establishment of one's
own.
	 2. Criticism.
	 3. An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)
	 4. Ben-
zoin or styrax.
	 5. The Oleander plant, (Nerium odorum.)
