वितर्दि|वितर्दिः|वितर्द्दिः
वितर्दि f. (र्दिः or र्दी)
	 1. A quadrangular building, or sort of covered
terrace of wood in the centre of the court-yard of a temple or
palace.
	 2. A quadrangular resting place made of wood, a seat, a
bench.
	 3. A place in a court-yard for sitting in or standing under.
4. A floor on four posts in the midst of a quadrangular house.
5. A temporary stage or shed in the middle of a court-yard, for
performing sacrifices, representing plays, &c.
	 6. A terrace furnished
with pillars, a vārāndāh, a balcony.
	 7. A covered temporary terrace
on which idols are sometimes placed and worshipped.
 E. वि pri-
vative, तर्द् to injure, aff. इन्; also ङीष् optionally added, and
with कन् added in the fem. form वितर्दिका ।
