विमार्ग m. (-र्गः)
	 1. A broom, a brush.
	 2. A bad road.
	 3. A wrong road,
literally or figuratively, evil conduct.
 E. वि before मृज् to clean,
aff. घञ्; or वि privative, and मार्ग a road.
