<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमत्
विरमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)
	 1. Resting, stopping.
	 2. Sporting.
 E. वि, रम् to sport, शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)
	 1. Fine, delicate, thin, (but with interstices.)
2. Loose, relaxed.
	 3. Apart, wide, separated by an interval.
	 4.
Remote, rare, occurring at distant or repeated intervals of time.
n. (-लं) Sour curds.
 E. वि apart, रा to go or be, aff. कलन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलम्
विरलम् Ind. It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “rarely,”
“unfrequently.”
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलजानुक
विरलजानुक m. (-कः) A man with bandy legs.
 E. विरल wide, जानु the knee, कन् added.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलद्रवा
विरलद्रवा f. (-वा) Gruel made of rice or other grain, with the addition
of Ghee, &c.
 E. विरल apart, द्रु to ooze, aff. अच् ।
