विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं) All, entire, whole, universal.
	 n. (-श्वं) The world,
the universe.
	 m. Plu. (-श्वः) A deity of a particular class in which
ten are enumerated; their names are VASU, SATYA, KRATU, DAKṢA,
KĀLA, KĀMA, DHRITI, KURU, PURURAVAS, MĀDRAVAS: they are
worshipped particularly at the funeral obsequies in honour of
deceased progenitors in general, and receive an oblation of clarified
butter at the daily and domestic Śrāddha.
	 nf. (-श्वं-श्वा) Dry ginger.
f. (-श्वा) A tree, the bark of which is said to be used in dyeing red,
commonly Atis, (Betula.)
 E. विश् to enter, to pervade, Unādi aff. व ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

