	 6. Read, studied, read through.
	 7. Covered.
8. Round.
	 9. Firm, hard.
	 10. Unobstructed, unimpaired.
	 11. Fa-
mons, celebrated.
	 12. Turned.
	 13. Been, existed.
	 n. (-त्तं)
	 1.
Verse, metre.
	 2. Conduct, observance of enjoined practice in
private or social life.
	 3. Practice, profession, means of gaining
a subsistence.
	 4. Procedure, event, occurrence.
	 5. A circle.
	 m.
(-त्तः) A tortoise.
 E. वृत् to be, &c., aff. क्त ।
