वृत्ति|वृत्तिः
वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)
	 1. Livelihood, profession, means of acquiring subsistence.
2. Style or character of dramatic representation, or composition,
considered to be of four sorts, viz:--Kaūsīkī, which exhibits love
or passion; Bhāratī, which appears to implies declamation es-
pecially; Sātwatī, of which the subject is virtue and heroism,
and Ārbhattī, which treats of magic, delusion, wrath and
battle.
	 3. Style in general.
	 4. Gloss, comment, explanation, expo-
sition.
	 5. Being, abiding, staying.
	 6. Seizing, stopping, withhold-
ing, restraining.
	 7. Circumference of a wheel or circle.
	 8. State,
condition.
	 9. Behaviour, action, course of action, conduct.
	 10.
Action, engagement, operation.
	 11. Respectful treatment.
	 12.
Wages, hire.
	 13. Revolving, turning round.
	 14. A complex forma-
tion, (in gram.)
	 15. The connotative power of a word; (these are
three, viz:--अभिधा, लक्षणा and व्यंजना ।)
 E. वृत् to be, aff. क्तिन् ।
