वैकुण्ठ|वैकुंठ|वैकुंठः|वैकुण्ठः
वैकुण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)
	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.
	 2. INDRA.
	 n. (-ण्ठं)
	 1. The para-
dise or world of Vaikuṇṭha or VIṢṆU; its site is variously des-
cribed, either as in the northern ocean, or on the eastern peak of
mount Meru.
	 2. Talc.
 E. विकुण्ठा the wife of ŚUBHRA, and mother
of VIṢṆU, in one form, अण् patronymic aff.: other etymologies
occur, as वि privative, &c. and कुण्ठ said to mean destruction, he
who is indestructible; or वि before the same, explained knowledge
or abode, being omniscient or omnipresent, &c.; again वि various,
and कुण्ठ illusion, aff. अण् ।
