वैष्णव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Relating or belonging to VIṢṆU.
	 m. (-वः)
	 1. A
follower of VIṢṆU.
	 2. One of the modern Hindu sects, (the
VAISHNABAS, the ŚAIVAS and the ŚĀKTAS are the three important
modern Hindu sects.)
	 f. (-वी)
	 1. One of the Mātṛs, the personified
energy or Śaktī of VIṢṆU.
	 2. A name of DURGĀ.
	 3. A flower,
(Clitoria ternatea.)
	 4. Sacred basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)
	 n. (-वं) The
ashes of a burnt offering.
 E. विष्णु VIṢṆU, अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीष् ।
