ing any inherent property.
	 n. (-प्यं)
	 1. An instrument or agent.
	 2.
The thing or substance which may be the site or subject of attri-
butes or inherent properties.
	 3. The subject of an inference, as
fire inferred from the presence of smoke, &c.
	 4. A drug, (Costus
speciosus.)
 E. वि before आप् to pervade, aff. ण्यत् ।
