व्रज|व्रजं|व्रजः
व्रज m. (-जः)
	 1. A cow-pen, a station of cowherds.
	 2. A road.
	 3. A
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">Page701-a+ 60</a>]
flock, a herd, a multitude.
	 4. The district about Āgrā and Mathurā,
the scene of KṚṢṆA'S juvenile adventures.
	 5. An abode.
	 n. (-जं)
Wandering, roaming.
 E. व्रज् to go, aff. घञर्ये-क ।
