व्रात्वता f. (-ता) The condition of one who has lost caste by neglect of the
initiatory observances.
 E. व्रात्य and तल् aff.; also with त्व, व्रात्यत्वं ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यस्तोम|व्रात्यस्तोमः
व्रात्यस्तोम m. (-मः) A particular sacrifice performed to recover the rights
forfeited by an improper delay of the ceremony of investiture. E.
व्रात्य one not invested, &c., स्तोम a sacrifice.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री r. 4th cl. (व्रीयते) To go. r. 9th cl. (व्रिणाति or व्रीणाति) To choose or select.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् r. 4th cl. (व्रीड्यते)
	 1. To be modest, to be bashful or ashamed.
2. To throw, to direct or send.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड mf. (-डः-डा) Shame, bashfulness.
 E. व्रीड् to be ashamed, aff. अच्; fem. aff. अङ् and टाप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडन|व्रीडनं
व्रीडन n. (-नं) Bashfulness, modesty.
 E. व्रीड् to be ashamed, ल्युट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडानत
व्रीडानत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, hanging down the head with shame.
E. व्रीडा, and आनत bowed.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडान्वित
व्रीडान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Modest.
 E. व्रीडा, and अन्वित possessed of.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, modest.
 E. व्रीड्, क्त aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रीसति व्रासयति-ते) To hurt or injure, to kill or wound.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहि|व्रीहिः
व्रीहि m. (-हिः)
	 1. Rice of various kinds: eight principal sorts are enu-
merated by native authorities, but the varieties are more numer-
ous.
	 2. Rice ripening in the rainy season.
 E. व्री to choose, हि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिक|व्रीहिकः
व्रीहिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having or bearing rice.
 E. व्रीहि rice, ठन् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिकाञ्चन|व्रीहिकाञ्चनः
व्रीहिकाञ्चन m. (-नः) A sort of pulse, (Ervum lens or hirsutum, &c.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिन्
व्रीहिन् mfn. (-हि-हिणी-हि) Having rice, (a field, &c.)
 E. व्रीहि rice, इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिभेद|व्रीहिभेदः
व्रीहिभेद m. (-दः) A sort of grain, (Panicum miliaceum.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिमय|व्रीहिमयः
व्रीहिमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made or consisting of rice.
	 m. (-यः) A rice-cake
offered with ghee as an oblation.
 E. व्रीहि rice, and मयट् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिराजिक
व्रीहिराजिक m. (-कः)
	 1. Panic-seed, (Panicum italicum.)
	 2. Another
species, (Panicum miliaceum.)
 E. व्रीहि rice, राजिक shining,
excelling.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीह्यगार|व्रीह्यगारं
व्रीह्यगार n. (-रं) A granary, a shed where rice or other grain is stored.
 E. व्रीहि, अगार a house.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
व्रुड् r. 6th cl. (व्रुडति)
	 1. To cover.
	 2. To heap.
	 3. To sink.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
व्रूस् r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रूसति व्रूसयति-ते) To hurt or kill.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैह|व्रैहः
व्रैह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं) Made of or with rice.
 E. व्रीहि rice, and अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Fit for or sown with rice, (a field, &c.)
 E. व्रीहि
rice, ढक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली r. 9th cl. (व्लिनाति or व्लीनाति)
	 1. To choose or select.
	 2. To hold, to maintain.
	 3. To go.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष्
व्लेक्ष् r. 10th cl. (व्लेक्षयति-ते) To see.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श The thirtieth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet and first of the
three sibilants; it is termed the palatal sibilant, and corresponds
to “Sh” pronounced softly, as in Shun; in the Roman character
it is distinguished by an accent, as Ś.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श m. (-शः)
	 1. A name of ŚIVA.
	 2. A weapon.
	 3. A cutter, a destroyer.
n. Adv. (-शं) or Ind. (शं or शम्) Happy, happily, auspiciously.
E. शी to sleep or शी to pare, &c., aff. ड ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु mfn. (-युः-युः-युं) Happy, prosperous, fortunate.
	 m. (-युः) A sort of
snake.
 E. शम् happily, and युस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंय्य
शंय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Happy, fortunate.
	 f. (-य्या) Knowledge, under-
standing.
 E. शम् happily, and यस् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Fortunate, prosperous.
	 m. (-वः)
	 1. The thunder-
bolt of INDRA.
	 2. The iron head of a pestle.
 E. श good fortune,
and व poss. aff.; also as differently derived, read शम्ब and सम्ब &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवर|शंवरं
शंवर n. (-रं) Water.
 E. शं happily, वृ to choose or cover, aff. अच् or अरप्;
more usually read शम्बर. q. v.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस्(उ)शंसु r. 1st cl. (शसति)
	 1. To praise.
	 2. To hurt.
	 3. To wish.
	 4.
To calumniate.
	 5. To suggest.
	 6. To report, to relate, (with a dat.
or gen. of the person communicated to.) With अभि prefixed, To
accuse wrongfully. With आङ्, 1. To hope.
	 2. To speak.
	 3. To
wish. With प्र, To praise, to flatter; this root and its derivatives
are sometimes read with the palatal sibilant final or शंश, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसन|शंसनं
शंसन n. (-नं)
	 1. The act of reciting.
	 2. Praising.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा f. (-सा)
	 1. Narrating.
	 2. Wish, desire.
	 3. Praise, flattery, eulo-
gium.
 E. शंस् to praise, &c., affs. अङ् and टाप्.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Established, ascertained.
	 2. Calumniated,
falsely accused.
	 3. Said, declared.
	 4. Praised, celebrated.
	 5.
Wished, desired.
 E. शंस् to wish, aff. क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
शंसिन् f. (-नी)
	 1. Saying, indicating.
	 2. Praising, (used at the end of a compound.)
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ m. (-स्ता) An encomiast, a panegyrist, a flatterer.
 E. शंस् to praise,
तृन् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्थ|शंस्थः
शंस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Happy, prosperous, well-faring.
 E. शं happily,
स्था to stay or be, aff. क ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्य|शंस्यः
शंस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)
	 1. Desirable, to be wished.
	 2. Meritorious, to
be praised.
 E. शस् to praise, &c., aff. ण्यत् or क्यप्; also शस्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् r. 4th cl. (शक्यति-ते) (इर ऌ) इरशकॢ r. 5th cl. (शक्नोति)
	 1. To bear
patiently, to endure, to be patient.
	 2. To be able to effect, to be
competent.
	 3. To be powerful, (generally with an inf.) (इ) शकि r.
1st cl. (शङ्कते)
	 1. To think probable, to suspect.
	 2. To fear, to
apprehend. With आङ्, To dread.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक m. (-कः)
	 1. A sovereign, and prince who gives his name to an era,
especially applied to SĀLIVĀHANA.
	 2. A particular caste, the
followers or descendants of ŚAKA or SĀLIVĀHANA.
	 3. A country.
m. plu. (-काः)
	 1. The inhabitants, the Sacæ, the Scythians.
	 2. An
era: see शाक.
 E. शक् to be able, aff. अच् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट mfn. Subst. (-टः-टी-टं) A cart.
	 m. (-टः)
	 1. A Daitya slain by
KṚṢṆA.
	 2. A cart-load.
	 3. A form of military array resembling
a wedge.
	 4. A measure of capacity equal to two thousand Paṇas.
E. शक् to be able, अटन् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटविल|शकटविलः
शकटविल m. (-लः) A gallinule.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटहन्
शकटहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA.
 E. शकट the demon so named, and हन् des-
troyer; also similar compounds, as शकटारि &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाल
शकटाल m. (-लः) The minister of NANDA: also read SAKATĀRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाह्वा
शकटाह्वा f. (-ह्वा) The fourth lunar asterism, called Rohinī, the stars of
which are represented as a cart.
 E. शकट a cart, आह्व appellation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका f. (-का) A small cart, a toy-cart.
 E. कन् added to शकटी ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् n. (-का) Animal-dung; this word has no forms for the first five
cases; according to some this is not a separate word but a substi-
tute for शकृत् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल mn. (-लः-लं) A part, a portion, a piece.
	 n. (-लं)
	 1. Skin.
	 2. Bark.
3. A kind of (black) pigment or die.
	 4. The scales of a fish.
 E. शक्
to be able, कलच् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलित
शकलित f. (-ता) Reduced to fragments.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन् m. (-ली) A fish.
 E. शकल skin or scales, and इनि aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकरण
शकलीकरण n. (-णं) Parting, dividing, cutting or breaking in pieces. E.
शकल, करण making, with च्वि aug.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकृत
शकलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Parted, cut in pieces, wounded,
 E. शकल, कृत made, च्वि aug.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकव
शकव m. (-वः) A goose.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकशकायत्
शकशकायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Rustling, making a noise, (as the leaves
of a tree in the wind.)
 E. शकत् imitative sound, nominal v., शतृ aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकान्तक|शकांतक|शकान्तकः
शकान्तक m. (-कः)
	 1. The prince VIKPAMĀDITYA.
	 2. The name of SĀLI-
VĀHANA.
 E. शक an era or a Scythian, अन्तक destroyer.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकाब्द|शकाब्दः
शकाब्द n. (-ब्दं)
	 1. A year of the Saka era, or era of SĀLIVĀHANA. E.
शक, अब्द a year.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकार|शकारः
शकार m. (-रः)
	 1. A silly brother-in-law of a Rājā.
	 2. The brother of a king's concubine.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकरि
शकरि m. (-रिः) VIKRAMĀDITYA, the celebrated sovereign of Oujein. E.
शक a Saca or Scythian, अरि the foe.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन m. (-नः)
	 1. A bird in general.
	 2. A kind of bird, either the
Indian vulture or the common kite, (Falco cheela;) it is also
applied to the pondicherry eagle, (Falco ponticeriana.)
	 3. A sort
of hymn or song, sung at festivals to solicit or secure lucky
events.
	 n. (-न) Any lucky or inauspicious object or omen.
 E. शक्
to be able, उनन् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञा
शकुनज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) A small house-lizard.
 E. शकुन a bird, and ज्ञ who knows.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञान
शकुनज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of omens.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनि|शकुनिः
शकुनि m. (-निः)
	 1. A bird.
	 2. The maternal uncle of the Kaurava
princes, and counsellor or DURYODHANA.
	 3. One of the astrono-
mical periods called Karaṇas.
	 4. The Indian kite or eagle, (Falco
cheela.)
	 f. (-नी) A hen-sparrow.
 E. शक् to be able, उनि Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिप्रपा
शकुनिप्रपा f. (-पा) A trough or little well for watering birds.
 E. शकुनि a
bird, प्र before पा to drink, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिवाद|शकुनिवादः
शकुनिवाद m. (-दः)
	 1. The sound of a bird.
	 2. The crowing of a cock.
