<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनीश्वर|शकुनीश्वरः
शकुनीश्वर m. (-रः) A name of GARUḌA.
 E. शकुनि a bird, and ईश्वर chief.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुंतः|शकुन्तः
शकुन्त m. (-न्तः)
	 1. A bird.
	 2. A kind of bird, the Indian vulture.
	 3.
Another sort of bird, described as of aquatic habits, perhaps a kind
of maritime or fishing-falcon.
	 4. A sort of insect.
	 5. The blue-jay.
E. शक् to be able, उन्त Unādi aff.; also शकुन, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तक|शकुंतक|शकुंतकः|शकुन्तकः
शकुन्तक m. (-कः) A bird.
	 f. (-न्तिका)
	 1. A kind of bird.
	 2. A locust. E.
कन् added to the last.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तला|शकुंतला
शकुन्तला f. (-ला) The daughter of MENAKĀ, the courtezan of Svarga, by
the sage VISHWĀMITRA, brought up by KANWA the hermit, and
afterwards married to DUSHYANTA, by whom she became the mother
of BHARATA, the sovereign of all India.
 E. शकुन्त a bird, ला to get,
affs. क and टाप्, being born in a solitary forest, and protected by
the birds till found by KANWA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तलात्मज|शकुन्तलात्मजः
शकुन्तलात्मज m. (-जः) BHARATA, the sovereign of India.
 E. शकुन्तला as above, आत्मज the son.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुंतिः|शकुन्तिः
शकुन्ति m. (-न्तिः)
	 1. A bird in general.
	 2. A kind of bird: see शकुन्त, &c.
E. शक् to be able, Unādi aff. उन्ति ।
