शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं) Wicked, depraved, perverse, dishonest.
	 m. (-ठः)
	 1.
An umpire, a mediator, an arbitrator.
	 2. A rogue, a knave.
	 3. A
blockhead, a fool.
	 4. An idler.
	 5. A false husband or lover, one
who pretends affection to one female whilst his heart is fixed on
another.
	 6. Thorn apple, (Dhatura metel.)
	 n. (-ठं)
	 1. A sort of root,
commonly Tagara.
	 2. Saffron.
	 3. Iron.
 E. शठ् to be wicked, aff.
अच् ।
