शतानन्द|शतानंद|शतानन्दः
शतानन्द m. (-न्दः)
	 1. BRAHMĀ.
	 2. VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.
	 3. The car of
VIṢṆU.
	 4. The Muni GAUTAMA, the founder of the logical school
of philosophy.
	 5. The eldest son of GAUTAMA (according to the
Rāmāyaṇa,) and Purohit or religious adviser of JANAKA of MITHILĀ.
E. शत hundred or many, and आनन्द who delights.
