शम्बूक|शंबूक|शंबूकः|शम्बूकः
शम्बूक mf. (-कः-का) A bivalve-shell.
	 m. (-कः)
	 1. A conch-shell.
	 2. A
snail.
	 3. A Śūdra, who had become a devotee in the time of
RĀMACHANDRA, and was slain by him.
	 4. The edge of the frontal
protuberance of the elephant.
	 5. The name of a Daitya.
 E. शम् to
be tranquil, ऊकन् aff. and वुक् augment; also with the vowel short,
शम्बुक, and the final consonant then rejected, शम्बु; it is also
read, शम्बुक्क and with the first vowel long, शाम्बूक, &c.
