शाल्व|शाल्वः
शाल्व m. Plu. (-ल्वाः) The inhabitants of one of the central divisions of
India.
 E. शाल्-व ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)
	 1. Tawny, (of that colour.)
	 2. Relating to the
purification of defilement from the contact or consanguinity of a
corpse, &c.
	 3. Relating to a dead body.
	 m. (-वः)
	 1. Tawny, (the
colour.)
	 2. The young of any animal: see the next.
 E. शव a dead
body, and अण् aff.; or शव् to go, aff. घञ् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
