शावरभेदाख्य
शावरभेदाख्य n. (-ख्यं) Copper.
 E. शावर relating to a low race, भेद class,
and आख्य appellation.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावाशौच
शावाशौच n. (-चं) Impurity from the demise of a relation.
 E. शाव, and अशौच impurity.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Eternal, perpetual.
	 m. (-तः)
	 1. A name of VYĀSA
2. ŚIVA.
	 3. The sun.
	 n. (-तं) Heaven, ether.
	 f. (-ती) The
earth.
 E. शश्वत् perpetually, अण् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतिक
शाश्वतिक f. (-की) Eternal, permanent.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Eating flesh or fish.
 E. शुष्कुली flesh, अण् aff., form irr.: see शौष्कुल ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुलिक|शाष्कुलिकं
शाष्कुलिक n. (-क) A multitude of pies.
 E. शष्कुली a sort of pie, ठक् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास्(उ)शासु r. 2nd cl. (शास्ति)
	 1. To instruct, to inform.
	 2. To order,
to direct, to enact.
	 3. To rule, to govern.
	 4. To correct, to punish.
5. To advise. (शास्ते)
	 1. To wish or desire: with आङ् prefixed,
r. 1st cl. (आशासते) r. 2nd cl. (आशास्ते) To wish well to, to bless.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन n. (-नं)
	 1. An order, an edict, a command.
	 2. A royal grant of
land or of privileges, a charter, &c. usually inscribed on stone or
copper.
	 3. A writing, a deed, a written contract or agreement.
	 4.
A Shāstra or scripture.
	 5. Devotion, or devotional tranquillity, the
government of the passions.
	 6. Governing, ruling, government. E.
शास् to order, to direct, aff. ल्युट् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनपत्र
शासनपत्र n. (-त्रं) A plate of copper, a stone or sheet of paper, &c., on
which an edict or grant is inscribed.
 E. शासन, and पत्र a leaf.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहर|शासनहरः
शासनहर m. (-रः) A royal messenger, one bearing an edict or grant. E.
शासन an edict, and हर who takes.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनीय
शासनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be governed or directed.
 E. शास् to rule,
अनीयर् aff; also शासितव्य and शास्य ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Governed, ruled.
 E. शास् to rule, aff. क्त ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Ordering, commanding, a governor or com-
mander.
 E. शास् to order, तृच् aff. with इट् augment.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्ति|शास्तिः
शास्ति f. (-स्तिः)
	 1. A command, an order.
	 2. Governing, ruling, order-
ing.
	 3. A sceptre.
	 4. Correctre, punishment.
 E. शास् to govern,
aff. क्तिन् or ति Uṇādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ mfn. (-स्ता-स्त्री-स्तृ)
	 1. A ruler, one who rules or governs.
	 2. A
teacher, teaching, instructing.
	 m. (-स्ता) A Buddha or Jina, or the
deified teacher of one or both those sects.
 E. शास् to govern, &c.
aff. तृच्, and the augment omitted.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्र|शास्त्रं
शास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)
	 1. An order or command.
	 2. Scripture, science, insti-
tutes of religion, law or letters, especially considered as of divine
origin or authority: when used singly, it implies works of literature
or science in general, and it is therefore customarily connected with
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">Page716-b+ 60</a>]
some other word to limit its application, as the Vedānta Śhās-
tras, or treatises of philosophical theology; the Dharma-Śhāstras,
books of law, &c.; it is also applied to less important branches of
knowledge, as the Kāvya-Śhāstras, or poetical works; Shilpa-
Śhāstras, works on the mechanical arts; and Kāma-Śhāstras, or
erotic compositions; in the singular number it is also used com-
prehensively to signify the body of all that has been written on
the subject, as Dharma-Śhāstras, the institutes or code of law;
Kāvya-Śhāstra, poetry; Alankāra-Śhāstra, rhetoric, &c.
	 3. A
book in general.
 E. शास् to govern or teach, aff. ष्ट्रन् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकृत्
शास्त्रकृत् m. (-कृत्)
	 1. A Ṛṣi, a holy personage of divine character.
	 2.
An author in general.
 E. शास्त्र a Śhāstra or scripture, &c., and कृत्
the author; the principal compositions in Hindu religion, law,
and literature, being attributed to sanctified and superhuman
personages.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रगण्ड|शास्त्रगंड|शास्त्रगण्डः
शास्त्रगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A general and superficial scholar.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रचक्षुस्
शास्त्रचक्षुस् n. (-क्षुः) Grammar.
 E. शास्त्र science, and चक्षुस् the eye.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञ|शास्त्रज्ञः
शास्त्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Acquainted with the Śhāstras, skilled in the
knowledge of law and religion especially.
 E. शास्त्र a sacred work
and ज्ञ who knows.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञता
शास्त्रज्ञता f. (-ता) Knowledge of the Śhāstras.
 E. शास्त्रज्ञ and तल् aff.; also त्व with शास्त्रज्ञत्वं ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञान
शास्त्रज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge derived from the study of sacred works.
E. शास्त्र, and ज्ञान knowledge.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्त्व
शास्त्रतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The truth or true knowledge taught in sacred works.
E. शास्त्र and तत्त्व truth.
