<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षक|शिक्षकः
शिक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A learner, a teacher.
 E. शिक्ष् to learn, ण्वुल् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षण|शिक्षणं
शिक्षण n. (-णं)
	 1. Learning.
	 2. Teaching, instruction.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षणीय
शिक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be taught or learnt.
 E. शिक्ष् to learn, अनीयर् aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा f. (-क्षा)
	 1. One of the six Vedāṇgas or sciences attached to the
Vedas: the proper pronunciation of the vocal sounds which
occur in them, as explained by PĀṆINI.
	 2. A plant, (Bignonia
Indica.)
	 3. Learning, study, the acquisition of knowledge.
	 4.
Modesty, humility.
 E. शिक्ष् to learn, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाकर|शिक्षाकरः
शिक्षाकर m. (-रः)
	 1. VYĀSA.
	 2. An instructor.
 E. शिक्षा the science of
pronunciation, and कर making.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षानर|शिक्षानरः
शिक्षानर m. (-रः) An epithet of INDRA.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाशक्ति|शिक्षाशक्तिः
शिक्षाशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Dexterity, skill.
 E. शिक्षा discipline, and शक्ति power.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Skilful, clever, conversant.
	 2. Modest,
diffident.
	 3. Disciplined, exercised.
	 4. Tame, trained, (as an
animal.)
	 5. Docile.
	 6. Studied, learned.
 E. शिक्षा studying, इतच् aff.;
or शिक्ष् to study, aff. क्त ।
