शील्
शील् r. 1st cl. (शीलति)
	 1. To meditate, to consider, to reflect profoundly
and abstractedly.
	 2. To worship, to adore. r. 1st and 10th cls.
(शीलति शीलयति-ते)
	 1. To practise, to exercise, (as the memory,
&c.)
	 2. To repeat.
	 3. To honour.
	 4. To visit, to go to. r. 10th cl.
(शीलयति)
	 1. To wear.
	 2. To have or be endowed with.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील|शीलः
शील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)
	 1. Possessed of, endowed with, practising, versed
in, &c.)
	 2. Behaviour, conduct.
	 3. Well-behaved, well-disposed.
mn. (-लः-लं)
	 1. Nature, quality.
	 2. Disposition, inclination.
	 3.
Good conduct or disposition, steady and uniform observance of
law and morals.
	 4. Beauty.
	 m. (-लः) A large snake.
 E. शील् to me-
ditate, to learn, &c., aff. अच्; or शी to sleep, and लक् Unādi aff.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलत्व
शीलत्व n. (-त्वं)
	 1. Disposition, quality.
	 2. Conversancy.
 E. शील, and त्व
added; also with तल्, शीलता ।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलन|शीलनं
शीलन n. (-नं)
	 1. Careful study of the Śhāstras or sacred writings.
	 2.
Serving, honouring.
	 3. Putting on.
 E. शील् to meditate, &c., aff.
ल्युट् ।
