शूद्र|शूद्रः
शूद्र m. (-द्रः) A man of the fourth or servile tribe, said to have sprung
from the feet of BRAHMĀ.
	 f. (-द्रा) A woman of the Śūdra tribe.
f. (-द्री or द्राणी) The wife of Śūdra.
 E. शुच् to purify or cleanse,
Uṇadi aff. रक्, the vowel made long, and च changed to द ।
