शेमुषी
शेमुषी f. (-षी) Understanding, intellect.
 E. शे derived from शीङ् to
sleep, with the aff. विच्, implying ignorance or delusion and मुष् to
steal, to take away, affs. क and ङीष्; or शम् to pacify, (the senses,)
क्कसु participial aff., fem. form, deriv. irr.
