षट्प्रज्ञ|षट्प्रज्ञः
षट्प्रज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)
	 1. A sage, one acquainted with the four objects of human
existence, or virtue, wealth, desire, and final happiness, and with
the nature of the world, and of divine truth.
	 2. A catamite. E.
षष् six, and प्रज्ञ who knows.
