सहस्राक्ष|सहस्राक्षः
सहस्राक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Thousand-eyed; used figuratively, vigilant,
all-perceiving, all-inspecting, all-powerful.
	 m. (-क्षः)
	 1. INDRA.
2. An owl.
	 3. BRAHMĀ.
 E. सहस्र a thousand, and अक्ष the
eye: INDRA having been covered over with marks resem-
bling the female organ, in consequence of a curse of GAUTAMA;
those marks were changed subsequently to eyes by the
relenting saint.
