सारसन|सारसनं
सारसन n. (-नं)
	 1. A woman's zone or girdle, formed of twenty-five
strings.
	 2. A military belt or girdle worn round the waist or chest,
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">Page783-b+ 60</a>]
upon the coat of mail, to bind it to the body.
 E. सार strength, and
षण् to give, aff. अच्, or अस् to diffuse, aff. ल्युट्; also सारशन ।
