सिंहावलोकनन्याय
सिंहावलोकनन्याय m. (-यः) The maxim of the lion's glance; it is used to
denote the connection of a thing with the preceding and the
following, just as the lion constantly pauses and casts his glance
backward and forward.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहासन|सिंहासनं|सिंहासनः
सिंहासन n. (-नं) A throne.
	 m. (-नः) A kind of coitus thus defined:--
“स्वजङ्घाद्वयबाहु च कृत्वा योषापदद्वये ।
स्तनौ धृत्वा रमेत् कामी बन्धः सिहासना मतः ॥”
E. सिंह a lion, (supported by lions, &c. wrought in gold,) and आसन a seat.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहास्य|सिंहास्यः
सिंहास्य m. (-स्यः) A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)
 E. सिंह a lion, आस्य
the face; to which the flowers are compared.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिका
सिंहिका f. (-का) The mother of RĀHU.
 E. सिंही a lioness, कन् aff. of comparison, &c.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिकासूनु|सिंहिकासूनुः
