सित|सितं|सितः
सित mfn. (-तः-ता or ती-तं)
	 1. White.
	 2. Bound, tied.
	 3. Finished, des-
troyed.
	 4. Completed, concluded.
	 5. Known.
	 m. (-तः)
	 1. White,
(the colour.)
	 2. The light-half of a lunar month.
	 3. The planet
VENUS.
	 4. An arrow.
	 n. (-तं)
	 1. Silver.
	 2. Sandal.
	 3. Radish.
f. (-ता)
	 1. Clayed or candied sugar.
	 2. Arabian jasmine.
	 3.
A sort of Clitoria.
	 4. Bent grass with white blossoms.
	 5.
Moon-light.
	 6. Spirituous liquor.
	 7. A handsome or well made
woman.
 E. षि to tie or bind, aff. क्त; or षो to destroy, क्त aff., and इ
substituted for the radical vowel.
