सुधाहर|सुधाहरः
सुधाहर m. (-रः) GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.
 E. सुधा
nectar, and हर who steals; having on one occasion stolen the
moon for the sake of the Amrita which was to be communicated
to the serpent children of KADRU, in consideration of which his
mother VINATĀ was to be released from a state of servitude to
KADRU, the wife, as well as herself, of the sage KAŚYAPA.
