सूक्ष्म|सूक्ष्मं|सूक्ष्मः
सूक्ष्म mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं)
	 1. Little, small.
	 2. Minute, atomic.
	 3. Fine,
delicate.
	 4. Ingenious, subtle.
	 5. Sharp, acute.
	 6. Crafty,
artful.
	 7. Exact, precise, accurate.
	 8. Deteriorated, declined.
m. (-क्ष्मः)
	 1. An atom.
	 2. Clearing-nut plant, (Strychnos pota-
[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">Page799-a+ 60</a>]
torum.)
	 n. (-क्ष्मं)
	 1. The Supreme Soul, the subtle and invisible
spirit that pervades all existence.
	 2. Fraud, cheating.
	 3. Fine
thread, &c.
	 4. A figure of rhetoric, the delicate or subtle
expression of act or intention.
	 5. Subtlety, ingenuity, craft.
	 6.
Minuteness.
	 7. One of the three kinds of power attainable by an
ascetic.
	 f. (-क्ष्मा)
	 1. A kind of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)
	 2.
Small cardamoms.
	 3. A perfume, consisting of a substance in
small grains: see Elabāluka.
 E. सूच् to inform or make known,
मन् Unādi aff., सुक् च नेट् ।
