	 3.
A needle, a piercer, any instrument for perforating.
	 4. A dog.
	 5.
A crow.
	 6. A cat.
	 7. A scoundrel, a villain.
	 8. The manager or
chief actor of a company.
	 9. A Buddha.
	 10. A Siddha.
	 11. A
demon, an imp or goblin.
	 12. A kind of fine rice.
	 f. (-चिका)
	 1.
Indicating, proving.
	 2. Betraying, informing.
 E. सूच् to make
known, ण्वुल् aff.
