सेतु|सेतुः
सेतु m. (-तुः)
	 1. A mound, a bank, a causeway, dyke, an elevated piece of
ground separating fields, and serving, during their inundation in
the rains, for the passage of travellers, &c.
	 2. A bridge.
	 3. A pass,
a defile, a road practised in mountainous countries, and places of
difficult access.
	 4. A land-mark.
	 5. A boundary.
	 6. A barrier, an
obstruction of any kind.
	 7. A fixed rule or law.
	 8. An epithet of
the sacred syllable “Om.” 9. A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)
 E. षि to bind,
तुन् Unādi aff.
