स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमंतकः|स्यमन्तकः
स्यमन्तक m. (-कः) The gem worn by KṚṢṆA. Formerly the gem was
given to SATRĀJIT by the sun, and transferred by him to his
brother PRASENA, from whom it was taken by JĀMBAVAT. After
much fighting it was appropriated by KṚṢṆA.
