हत|हतः
हत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Struck, hurt, killed.
	 2. Destroyed.
	 3. Departed,
lost.
	 4. Ended.
	 5. Deprived of, devoid of.
	 6. Disappointed.
	 7.
Multiplied, (in arithmetic.)
	 n. (-तं)
	 1. Multiplication.
	 2. Hurting,
killing.
 E. हन् to strike or hurt, aff. क्त. It is often used at the
beginning of compounds in the sense of “miserable,” “worthless.”
