1. VIṢṆU, or as considered to be the same deity, with KṚṢṆA.
2. YAMA.
	 3. Air, wind.
	 4. INDRA.
	 5. The moon.
	 6. The sun.
	 7. A
lion.
	 8. A ray of light 9. A horse.
	 10. A parrot.
	 11. An ape.
	 12. A
snake.
	 13. A frog.
	 14. ŚIVA.
	 15. One of the nine VARSHAS into
which the known continent is divided.
	 16. BRAHMĀ.
	 17. Fire.
18. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.
	 19. A goose.
	 20. A peacock.
21. Green, (the colour.)
	 22. Tawny, (the colour.)
	 23. A golden
colour, or yellow.
	 24. A horse of INDRA.
	 25. A name of the poet
BHARTRIHARI.
	 26. A learned man.
 E. हृ to take, to seize, (the
world or men's hearts, &c.,) Unādi aff. इन् ।
