हित|हितं|हितः
हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)
	 1. Suitable, proper, fit, worthy, right, (generally
with a dative.)
	 2. Gone, proceeded.
	 3. Held, taken, seized.
	 4. Put,
placed.
	 5. Advantageous, profitable, salutary, wholesome.
	 6. (In
medicine,) Proper, as diet or menstrua, suitable to the case or
the medicines taken.
	 7. Friendly, affectionate, kind to, (often with
a locative.)
	 8. Useful.
	 m. (-तः)
	 1. A good, a benefit.
	 2. A
benefactor, an adviser.
	 n. (-तं)
	 1. An advantage.
	 2. Anything
proper or suitable.
	 f. (-ता) A causeway, a dike.
 E. धा to have or
hold, क्त aff; or हि to go, &c., क्त aff.
