हिरण्य|हिरण्यं
हिरण्य n. (-ण्य)
	 1. Gold.
	 2. Either of the precious metals, crude bullion,
unwrought gold or silver.
	 3. Silver, crude or wrought.
	 4. Any
precious metal.
	 5. A measure.
	 6. A cowrie.
	 7. Semen virile.
	 8.
Imperishable matter, that which is eternal.
	 9. Thing, substance.
10. Wealth, property.
	 11. The Dhattūra plant.
 E. हृ to take,
Unādi aff. कन्यन्, and किरच् substituted for the radical letters; or
हिरण, यत् aff.
